window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3601,"title":"Chapter 3601: Chapter 3600 Wheels and Flames I","paragraphs":["A shocking weaving of existence erupted in a certain point of the Megalos Ynnere that became covered by white gold flames and obscured everything else!","Amidst the white gold flames, the shocked blue flames of Mysara remained as she witnessed something unspeakable.","But all of this...was in a state of matter.","All around, even the flames of the Singed, were surrounded by weavings of Matter!","Thus...","Back in a nondescript world where the Node of Existence of the Prime Frequency of the End was located in.","The figure of the Queen of Matter was sitting on the shoulders of a massive Theodosius while swinging her legs freely.","Books connected to strings danced around her gleefully as suddenly, her legs stopped their laid-back kicking as her eyes glazed white and black.","Her Source pulsed as Fabled Matter received feedback based on any important events occurring across matter relating to certain key figures!","And at this moment, she caught a glimpse of the weavings of Matter around a certain area as she couldn't help but scream out.","\"Noo....!\"","Her resonant screams interrupted a somber atmosphere of Theodosius thinking of the past, and Noah along side Ruination were carrying out heavy advancement to their weavings of Existence at the same time!","The Queen of Matter screamed in the middle of all of this as she looked towards Noah in dismay.","\"What...what are you doing to the Flower of the Flames, Emelline of the First Flame?!\"","She had a look of dismay as if something that shouldn't be getting desecrated was being desecrated greatly right now!","Noah's eyes turned sharp as he waved his hands, the visage of the Queen of Matter being pulled towards him and standing inches away as he asked.","\"Just how pervasive is your Source? Anything relating to Matter that you deem important gets reported to you? Do you also have records of what went around Matter cycles ago? Records of the Omnifather and others?\"","...!","Her gaze truly saw far as the Source she had was utterly broken.","Emelline of the First Flame had just appeared before him now and began doing what she did, and why would he say no to a proactive cultivation with a Prime Source Complexity- a Singed at that who was deeply connected to the flames of the Wheel? And her words also interested him when she spoke of attaining an Undeniable Telos Source from him!","But these were his matters.","The Queen of Matter...gazed upon and even saw this as his interest in her Source became elevated even more.","And yet, towards his questions, she looked at him with great grievances as she spoke out sullenly.","\"Sir Osmont. Mr. True Emperor of Quintessence. Mr 9th Infernal Lord. I....say with utmost respect and adoration for you, but I think you may have a problem, Sir.\"","...!","Her eyes were sincere.","Her eyes were clear!","But Noah remained unfazed as he knew her character by now, watching her with interest as she continued with a serious, aggrieved look!","\"Women. Dual Cultivation...I think this may be a problem for you, sir.\"","She said this without blinking.","And as if every word she said was right, she was only more bolstered and courageous as she continued!","\"For example! Emelline of the First Flame is a critical figure on the Flow of Existence of multiple Frequencies of Existence! If you are out here poking around her right now, and she becomes another harem member whose existence disappears into oblivion, how will the flow of existence across different Frequencies continue?!\"","WAA!","Emelline!","An important leader of the Singed whose flow affected multiple Frequencies.","In her knowledge and view point, she could not just become another forgotten member of the Wheel!","So she stood up against the one she adored the most.","She told Noah that he had a problem!","He looked at her and smiled, his eyes causing her to become frightened as she covered her face and chest as if Noah would become enticed by her and devour her here too.","Yet the True Severed Origin Osmontian spoke calmly as he felt Kuklos approaching the 81st Severing.","\"I was a man, and I am still a man all these years later. I do not believe in losing the desires that made me who I was just because I am transcending countless weavings of Existence. I do not believe in becoming some apathetic Transcendent entity looking at everything in black and white.\"","HUUM!","As he spoke, his weavings churned tumultuously as behind him, Ruination elevated two Severed Affixes to a tremendous level at this same time.","\"Food. Women. Loot. Power...these are just parts that make the True Emperor of Quintessence you know so well. Maybe they are flaws, but that's more than okay. After all, who in these fantastical weavings of existence is perfect? I've been a Conqueror, a Chef, a Farmer, and many more. If there was not an unknown Frequency Shattering Entity running around with a Primal Flame of the Wheel out there, I might have sought the True Sources of a farmer or cook first before anything else. But circumstances change many things. But circumstances...do not change me.\"","...!","He tapped out as he uncovered the hand of the Queen of Matter covering her face as he continued.","\"As for Emelline of the First Flame. Who are you to say the flow of the Wheel is not following its natural progression right now? She seeks to obtain the Undeniable Telos Source from me. What if she obtains it and becomes capable of fulfilling her weavings of the flow smoothly after this?\"","His words were resonant as the Queen of Matter was shocked, her eyes gradually becoming confused before they became determined.","She began to mutter.","\"Circumstances change many things...circumstances do not change me...\"","She muttered out words that seemed like gospel as she copied them down on a book right away, her eyes shining as she looked towards Noah with unfathomable radiance and spoke out.","\"How could I ever doubt the Dreamer of Extremity? I apologize for veering off the path, Sir Osmont. I have a couple of names of entities with the same calibre if not a little bit lower than Emelline of the First Flame. Shall I set you up with them too?\"","WAA!","He told her a few words, but she was too easily swayed by him as she went from one extreme of telling him he had a problem to now wanting to contribute to this problem!"]},{"number":3602,"title":"Chapter 3602: Chapter 3601 Wheels and Flames II","paragraphs":["The eyes of the Queen of Matter shone dangerously as she simply waited for the orders of her True Emperor of Quintessence.","He shook his head as he thought of all the possibilities out there.","What could be.","What could have been.","He did not wish to have any regrets as while his other bodies increased his complexity and sought grander Pathways, he still had other bodies within the Infiniverse Megalos enjoying the same hobbies he always had.","He was surprised that after all this time, there wasn't a random selection to take the True Severed Weavings of Cooking onto a Pathway already!","But...","\"Everything happens in its own course. On its own...Flow.\"","HUUM!","As he said such words.","His weavings began to shake and tumble as a golden wheel began to spin around him.","A wheel that, with every turn, seemed to be breaking and shattering the weavings of Existence around him.","The Flow of Existence around him felt a disconnect!","Almost as if...he would enact his own Flow!","|The Severed Weavings of Kuklos have attained their Final Severed State.|","|The Pathway leading to the True Source of Kuklos has opened.|","|The True Severed Kuklos of Existence has been born.|","|The True Severed Wheel of the Origin Osmontian has been born.|","|Through the Pathway to the True Source of Kuklos, you have attained Absolute Flow, becoming capable of dictating your own Flow of Existence.|","BZZT!","|The Flow of the current Frequency of Existence has begun experiencing tumultuous changes due to the cut off of your Flow.|","The surroundings turned chaotic.","Weavings of Existence began to crumble as his flow became entirely cut off from the outside weavings!","The face of the Queen of Matter began to change as if she was witnessing a terrifying change of something in real time, and before Noah's eyes, a prompt arose.","|The Flow of the current Frequency of Existence has begun experiencing tumultuous changes due to the cut off of your Flow.|","Tumultuous changes were beginning to occur as for now....","\"Proceed and resume with the same Flow observed before.\"","Noah spoke to the terrifying Wheel born inside of him that at this moment proceeded to overlap with his...Atlas of Existence!","The moment he gave the command, gaps were made between his weavings and the weavings of Existence stretching out all around him as the chaotic churning of weavings settled ever so slowly.","As if the flow they had before was slowly restored!","|The Flow of the True Severed Wheel of the Origin Osmontian has dictated to momentarily follow the persevered Flow of Existence permeating all around.|","|Through the Pathway to the True Source of Kuklos, your Atlas of Existence is being transformed to become a True Source Atlas of Existence. You can channel the weavings of everything within your True Source Atlas, and you can allow other Existences to reach out and connect to your True Source Atlas of Existence. Those touched by and channeling the power of your True Source Atlas of Existence will experience different weavings than the Weavings of the Wheel through which they are currently channeling complexity. Others can connect and channel their weavings through your True Source Atlas of Existence at no cost to you, and the more complexity channeling your Source, the grander and more complex this Source becomes.|","...!","His Atlas...took on the form of an archaic Wheel, with massive unbreakable Spokes separating 9 Mundis of Power!","True Source Atlas of Existence!","Others could channel their weavings of Existence through it as they may come to find his Source...to be a better alternative to the Wheel of Existence they channeled their complexity through!","Noah looked at his Source as he realized at this moment what a tremendous change this could bring.","The dictation of his own flow. The channeling of weavings of existence through his own Source!","Just how ridiculous were the changes that he could make?","As he thought this, his mind went to Emelline of the First Flame who was currently connected to him, his weavings flowing through her as he was able to understand her Source of the Singed and how it had a unique Flow stretching out across this Frequency and even other frequencies.","He was able to see how her Prime Source complexity seethed with interminable might as all of it flowed through a grand and unfathomable Source- The Wheel of Existence where an unknown number of frequencies and complexities channeled their weavings through!","And now, such a being connected to him as she sought to make her Singed an Undeniable Telos Source.","Even when he just opened his Pathway to the True Source of the Singed, the late Persephael had accused him of having an Undeniable Telos Source. A type of source that was very hard for others to deny regardless of their complexity as she was not able to extinguish the Embers of his Flames!","If this was what Emelline of the First Flame sought, he could use her- someone unfathomably close to the Wheel of Existence, and see just how she would change if she attained qualities of a True Severed Singed contained within a True Source Atlas of Existence.","HUUM!","Interminable waves of complexity burned amidst...an entanglement between Noah and Emelline of the First Flame.","Amidst the mixing weavings, Emelline found a core part of her Source opening its eyes as she found herself standing...on a grand white gold flaming Pathway!","A Pathway that stretched out magisterially behind her, and ahead of her...it was still being built.","But the moment her feet touched it...","HUUM!","She felt her flames resonating and changing as their quality became different from what they used to be.","Her Prime Source became active as its weavings became even more complex!","She felt the quality...of something that could not be denied.","She simply stepped on a Pathway to the True Source as she felt its pristine wonder, and the fact that this Pathway was still being forged even now!","Her gorgeous expression was filled with sadness as tears fell from her flaming eyes, and she spoke out calmly.","\"You...are not the Origin Singed, are you?\"","...!","She spoke.","But she knew the one who was enacting this Pathway to a True Source...was here. The man she was currently entangled with.","Behind her, sitting down and watching the Pathway that was being built, Noah's gaze was serene as he nodded in reply.","\"I am not the Origin Singed you know. I am someone who managed to seek the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed though, and this seems to make any entity burnt by the Flame mistake me for the Origin Singed. Did that Entity also seek the True Source, or was he just given a truly close authority by the weavings of the Wheel?\"","Noah asked calmly as the tears on Emelline of the First Flame stopped, a sad smile falling on her face as she shook her head.","\"The Origin Singed was the Origin Singed. The one with the highest level of Purity of the Flame of the Singed as even if you are not him...you are also him. Paradoxical as it may be. You are not the Origin Singed, and at the same time, you are. It matters not. All that matters is that somewhere in the flow of the Wheel, there is the Origin Singed when he is needed. And currently, you have been needed.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":3603,"title":"Chapter 3603: Chapter 3602 Wheels and Flames III","paragraphs":["Somewhere in the flow of the Existence, an Origin Singed was needed!","And now, here was someone to play the role of the Origin Singed.","Emelline of the First Flame truly believed this as she saw the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed continue to be built, her Prime Source feeling a unique type of burn at this moment as she truly felt it become different than what it was before!","This...was what she needed.","\"Ezekiel has already returned his Embers to the Wheel, and I did not know how many would have to do so as well. With this power, I can prevent many things as there are no regrets on my side. The enemy is one that passed through the gaps of defenses of the Origin Singed and many others. Whatever they wish for...is not something the weavings of the Wheel wish for.\"","She said this as she sat down on the flaming pathway, closing her eyes and feeling these burning flames as she looked utterly mystique at this moment.","Noah calmly walked beside her and looked at the darkness that the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed continued to light up, and he asked lightly.","\"The place they went. The realm they reached. What does Emelline of the First Flame know about such a thing?\"","He had called her here for more information.","Even though she jumped him right away, he still sought information!","She opened her eyes and blinked a few times at his question before she smiled and waved her hands as if she would play along.","On her palm, an incandescent white gold flame appeared and burned brilliantly as she spoke out.","\"For me to conjure a flame requires an input of power. Authority, mana, anything...but a spark is needed to cause the flame to bloom. What many do not understand is that things are never that simple. For any unnatural thing to occur- for existence to produce a flame from my hand or the hand of a normal human, the flow of existence itself has to have slight alterations. Nigh instantaneously, there was a communication between my existence, my source, and the outside environment in order to cause this flame to bloom. My Source provided the fuel, but even with the fuel, it may not have done anything unless...I was able to channel the appearence of this power through a Source that stands over our current weavings of existence.\"","WAA!","Her gaze was serene.","Her words only confirmed what Noah just learned!","Emelline of the First Flame allowed the flame on her hand to blaze brilliantly as it swirled to form a scorching pillar of brilliance.","\"The Source that every single being unknowingly channels all Extremes of existence, all weavings of their pathway and sources...is the Wheel of Existence. Every single entity channels the True Source of the Wheel of Existence in order to alter their surrounding existence. All Existences...are merely Channelers at the end. Entities drawing from a profound Source they do not even understand, and some may never even come close to understanding all their lives. The Origin Singed...you...\"","Hey eyes glittered as she looked at Noah beside her, the pillar of flames in her hand flying out to wrap around him as it did absolutely nothing- akin to just air swirling around him!","\"You and a few others became such powerful Channelers that you were able to easily attain Undeniable Telos Sources. The first step to elevating yourselves as after that, you can begin appraching the True Source you channel from and make demands of it. If the pathway you were utilizing to Channel was a single inch cylinder, you could now ask for and have a pathway a mile long in diameter. Your output of power would tremendously change. And some...sought to entirely move away from channeling through the True Source that is the Wheel of Existence, gain independence from it as their weavings channeled something else. But how easy is that? To find another True Source to Channel through?\"","She asked a heavy question that many would not be able to answer.","And yet Noah almost wanted to tell her that just a few minutes ago, he had established his Pathway to the True Source of Kuklos and allowed his Atlas of Existence to become a True Source Atlas of Existence!","That at this moment, it was a budding True Source that others could connect and channel through!","But he remained silent as he thought of the future and coming implications.","If the Wheel of Existence was a True Source that Existence could channel in order to enact terrifying changes with their Extremes, Pathways, and Sources.","What did Bob, an Outsider, want with it? With the Primal Flame of the Wheel of such a Source?","His eyes pulsed with luminous weavings of possibility as his deep voice thundered out amidst blistering flames.","\"And the Singed?\"","The ones burnt by the Flame of a True Source.","He had an idea, but he wanted it to come from this Prime Source itself as Emelline clenched her hands and sensed her flames. Exhuberant.","Undeniable at this moment!","And yet against this being, they did absolutely nothing to him.","Was he the Origin Singed or not...was this even a question that had to be asked?","She smiled and hugged her knees as she looked like an ethereal flaming Queen, her gaze distant and looking at a far place as her voice echoed out like a lullaby.","\"The Singed are more than just Channelers. We get to tap onto the Flow of the Wheel as we become Conduits that express its weavings. A...macrophage of a massive immune complex that moves around clearing dead weavings, infenctions, and anything else that may interrupt the flow of Existence. As Conduits, we gain more power due to our closeness with the True Source, and some of us...\"","She lifted her head up while hugging her knees as she looked Noah with crescent eyes.","\"Some of us are truly close with the True Source as the status of a True Conduit is unfathomably grander, gaining ways and means to channel that the rest of us cannot fathom.\"","...!"]},{"number":3604,"title":"Chapter 3604: Chapter 3603 Wheels and Flames IV","paragraphs":["A True Conduit who had unfathomable means of doing things as others could not even understand!","This was what Emelline of the First Flame knew the Origin Singed to be!","She looked up at him upside down as she continued.","\"We follow the flow of the Wheel. Some of us do not know what it means, but we follow it regardless. Someone like you understands the flow very well. You know exactly what you need to do. If you left, it was because you had to leave. If you are back now, even in a minimal capacity, then it means it is because you know you have to be here. So that is that. Now...it is time for me to return to accomplish the weavings of the flow I know. I have the Singed to lead as if you brought me here through Mysara, it should have been as a warning and to grant me this Undeniable Telos Source to prepare for a war.\"","...!","She guessed things fairly well as Noah raised his brows when he saw her rising up.","\"You see me, proceed to jump me, obtain something from me, and then you just want to leave freely?\"","He turned his head inexplicably as the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed became even heavier and complex, the weavings of the True Source Atlas of Existence fully settling around the Mundi of the Source of the Singed as they became even more radiant!","There was no channeling towards any other Source.","He was no Channeler from this moment onwards.","He was currently the Administrator of the True Source Atlas of Existence as he did not need to channel to any True Source, with him being capable of pulling upon his own!","This...deserved a tremendously heavy distinction in itself.","To channel any power through something, it was an action.","An action had a delay. Some could cast abilities in minutes, some seconds, and others needed just an instant to cast abilities or enact a change.","But they did not know that they were still channeling through a True Source pervasive all around them to even be capable of conjuring any change to their surrounding existence!","For Noah...there would not be any theoretical delay.","He would simply be enacting weavings of his True Source Atlas of Existence right away onto a surrounding environment as he was curious how different this would be compared to before!","He smiled as he waved his hands and pulled the white gold queen like visage of Emelline of the First Flame into his embrace.","He was an imperfect being.","So he would simply continue to be himself even amidst all of these fantastical changes as he looked at the astonished Emelline of the First Flame.","\"Come, let us continue this entanglement and walk the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed a bit more.\"","...!","There were many changes to explore and understand.","What he who walked on an entirely different path and source represented. What an entity like Emelline of the First Flame represented.","And what those who would be Channelers of the True Source Atlas of Existence would experience!","As such weavings unfolded.","In a far distant place.","In an entirely different Frequency of Existence.","Waves of blue waters covered absolutely everything, this place having no skies as everything was just....water. Endlessly.","At this moment, sitting on an incandescent coral reef, the figure of Bob could be seen reading through a Book of Existence as behind him, a massive silver white Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence burned, surrounded by white and black chains as multiple decaying black and white Wheels spun all around it with terrifying waves of power.","The smooth head of Bob weaved back and forth with the clear waters as he hummed, his tentacle like legs swinging back and forth as moments later, he nodded while closing the book with a heavy expression.","\"Let us start with the simple things first, shall we? Access to the weavings of the Wheel...let us make it simple and close it off first.\"","....!","Closing access to the weavings of the Wheel of Existence!","For what he needed to do, this was but a simple first step.","Countless existences were channeling weavings across frequencies onto the Wheel of Existence.","Closing off access to it would allow him to accomplish part of the goal, but the byproduct would be for countless existences...to no longer be capable of channeling any power.","Weavings of Existence would be present.","It would be nothing like Hell Terra Firma where there were no weavings of authority at all.","Authority would still be present.","Just...nobody would be able to do anything with authority.","Those who were not meant to fly would no longer be able to fly.","Those who could conjure fireballs, galaxies, or omniverses with a swipe of their hands would find themselves unable to do so.","There would be no access to the one thing one needed to channel their power through as for the first time in history, true equality would start.","Everyone would be the same.","Well, almost everyone.","Bob's heavy expression remained as he shook his head and sighed.","\"I am sorry for this. None of you deserve what is coming.\"","His eyes were filled with a tremendous weight other people would not be able to understand.","And at this moment, he moved as he appeared before the burning silver white Primal Flame of the Wheel, his tentacles sinking into it while the white and black Wheels around him began to spin!","HUUUM!","His body erupted with waves of terrifying complexity, the Primal Flame burning brilliantly as a cry could be heard as if it was being forced to do things it did not wish to!","But the Complexity commanding it was far too great.","Far above any other complexities in any nearby frequencies as it slowly recovered from its injuries.","So it exploded with undeniable power. And thereafter, unfathomable wonder bloomed.","It started with this frequency filled with water that Bob was in as on the Rift he just left, a shining Node of Existence could be seen becoming distorted as a massive silver white burn mark bloomed across it!"]},{"number":3605,"title":"Chapter 3605: Chapter 3604 Alteration! I","paragraphs":["A frequency filled with endless waves of water.","A serene blue covered everything as in a certain region, there was an Aquahaven holding an Empire stretching out for light years.","Towards the center of this Aquahaven, a humanoid Greater Source with the upper body of a human and the lower body of a fish floated grandly- an Atlantian of powerful stature as he carried a blue gold trident in his right hand that was currently shooting out rays of blue light onto Primaltrees of Atlantis- nurturing them and causing fantastical fruits to begin blooming!","Around him, massive multicolored fish swam serenely, many bowing their heads towards him reverentially as they passed.","A distance away, brilliantly lit walls stretching out for miles could be seen surrounding vibrant Aquacitadels of an Empire.","The Greater Source Atlantian continued his work as normal when all of a sudden...","WAP!","The light shooting out of his Trident instantly ceased!","\"Huh?\"","Bubbles left his mouth as, in the next moment, he felt the heavy pressure of the water all around him, and the gills on the side of his neck began to breathe as he was shocked!","He did not need to breathe.","Nor should he feel any pressure at this moment.","What...","His mind was buzzing as he reached out to weave his Greater Source when...","'Huh? Where...'","He was terrified to realize he couldn't...feel anything.","He couldn't sense anything!","As a Greater Source, his mind could even observe the makeup of his atoms as at this moment, the only thing he could observe was what he could see with his own eyes.","A form of 'inner vision' where he could see inside his body seemingly ceased to exist!","He also felt his hand sinking and being pulled down as the Trident made from the Core of an Omniverse slowly sank down, his hand feeling a tearing force as he let go!","This...","His heart was filled with trepidation and confusion as it felt like his Greater Source and everything he had worked eons for...had just silently disappeared!","As he faced such a terrifying situation.","Behind him, a school of predatory fish- Bluehaven Orcas, who were just reverentially swimming in the distance when they sensed his regal power...one blinked and turned towards the direction of the Atlantian as its eyes showed confusion first, but after that, they became covered by a predatory glint as it sped forth!","Its aim was the Atlantian that released no waves of power or regality, and the Greater Source Atlantian...could only see what was ahead of him with his eyes as he could not even sense the predatory fish silently coming behind him!","...!","This was one being in this vast frequency of waters.","There were many like him, and an uncountable number who were below him in power.","On this day.","Inside the Frequency of Aqua.","Every single one found themselves unable to sense or utilize any form of authority.","All they had...was what their bodies were born with!","It would be the first of many as a Unique Existence moved right after- warping away from this frequency along with a silver white flame bound by black and white Wheels.","He warped away from a frequency where even though every single entity should not be able to access and channel to the Wheel of Existence, he was still able to use authority freely.","It was not because he was an exemption.","It was because he did not draw or channel from the True Source that all other beings here channeled from!","—","In the Prime Frequency of the End.","The new changes continued to settle over Noah as he monitored everything, this entire scene being one of utmost wonder as a Prime Source Theodosius kneeled quietly in the distance, Ruination had her hand behind his back with great focus, and the Queen of Matter had squinting eyes of excitement and expectation as if she was waiting for something!","But during her wait, what she came across was not something she wanted nor expected by a long shot.","The color drained from her eyes.","Her expression distorted and became ashen as Noah saw this drastic change and became serious, the Queen of Matter speaking before she could even be asked!","\"The...the communication of all weavings of Matter with the Frequency of Aqua...are gone! Gone! Has...has an entire Frequency been erased like this?! If it was an action done by someone, it would have at least been gradual as I would see what was behind it. But this...it all just instantly gone!\"","Her expression was heavy as she imagined countless dead in a matter of an instant.","Only a single being could possibly do such a thing.","Only a single one had the power to do so!","\"BOB!\"","She yelled out his name, her lips quivering with a sense of fury as the books connected to strings around her buzzed.","Bob.","Noah's gaze was heavy as he thought of the words of the Queen of Matter, and if there was anything true regarding Bob...he shouldn't have collapsed and killed an entire Frequency of Existence after his last failure!","So...","WAP!","Another body of his adorned in a white Emperor's Robe appeared in this place as he grasped the hand of the Queen of Matter.","\"Send me the coordinates of the Frequency of Aqua.\"","His voice was thick and filled with undeniable command as if what he thought was right, Bob should have just been in that frequency or was still there!","The Queen of Matter held a face of sternness for the first time in a while as bundles of weavings left her and flowed into the body of the newly appearing Noah.","And the moment these weavings were ascertained...","HUUM!","Swirling weavings of existence flashed instantly around them akin to circular multicolored radiance which took the Queen of Matter by surprise, and they disappeared right after!","Foreign.","Noah's weavings...felt foreign and distinctly different from what the Queen of Matter knew as the normal weavings of Existence!","And when it came to the slow process of crossing into different Frequencies that took time and a great deal of Authority, she would come to find this jump Noah made from one frequency to another...took less than a millisecond!"]},{"number":3606,"title":"Chapter 3606: Chapter 3605 Alteration! II","paragraphs":["A Milisecond.","This was all it took to jump from one Frequency to another for Noah, his white robed figure appearing in a sea of endless blue all around him as everything seemed more than normal!","Beside him, the Queen of Matter was just starting to look around in shock when...","\"GRAGH....!\"","Her body paled as she acted like she was drowning, a terrifying pressure pressing all around her as her nose began to gush out blood!","Noah moved right away, his fist striking out and forming a bubble of air in this whole area, his other hand still holding onto the Queen of Matter who heaved with a bleeding nose and reddened eyes as she puked out water.","Around her, books fell down as there were no more strings stretching out from her to connect her to them, and her brain buzzed as she could barely focus and maintain her consciousness!","She had nearly been crushed.","Her.","A Greater Source Complexity, had almost been crushed by the mere pressure of this vast sea!","She hung limply from Noah as she was about to lose consciousness when a blinding green light of the True Severed Weavings of Life surged into her from Noah, her bleeding stopping as clarity returned to her mind while she breathed easire.","And yet...","\"No....\" Her eyes freely leaked tears as she continued to hang in the air- only capable of doing so because of Noah as she looked down at the scattered books that were wet all over!","Noah floated down with her and set her down as she reached out towards her books while tears fell from her eyes.","\"I can't feel anything!\"","WAA!","Her words were heart rending as if she was experiencing the greatest pain in her life.","\"My connection to Matter, my Source, my very Existence...I can't feel any of it. Its so dark. It's so dark!\"","She wailed as she gathered her books and tried to open them, but she was not capable of doing so.","They held records she wrote herself. Fables that she hummed herself to sleep!","And yet, at this moment, she could not access them!","\"Ah...\"","A low voice akin to a wail.","Noah looked at her distraught state as well as what she had said before they arrived here as he instantly understood what had happened.","The Frequency was still here.","Nothing had seemingly been affected.","But the moment the two of them arrived here, the Queen of Matter was affected while Noah...remained unbothered!","There was only a single reason for this.","It seemed like Bob had begun by doing utterly dreadful things as at this moment, Noah understood that somehow, Bob had cut off channeling to the Wheel of Existence for this frequency!","The Queen of Matter was only affected after she came here while he was fine because of a singular reason.","And for this reason, he floated down and looked at the distraught Queen of Matter who looked like she had lost everything.","\"Aah....!\"","Tears and snot freely flowed from her as Noah bent down and raised her head, her figure still trying to pry open the books around her.","She looked like a young woman who was always used to lock herself in her room, lost in the worlds of the books she read. And now, all of these worlds she knew and loved were gone.","\"Sir Osmont, everything I had...I cannot feel any of it!\"","Her mind was unfocused as her eyes trembled!","Noah looked at her with a trace of pity as he replied.","\"I know.\"","He knew.","He knew how she felt at this moment as if he had lost access to his Mana. If he had nothing that he held right now.","Even when he went into Hell Terra Firma, there was still his part of Ozymandias that could still enjoy authority!","But the Queen of Matter was experiencing it fully right now as Noah looked at her in her distraught state as he called out.","\"You lost access to everything you had because you have been channeling your power through something that could be altered by someone powerful enough. You need something else to channel your power through, and you will be able to sense everything you have again. Do you want that?\"","...!","His words coursed down like lightning in her mind as she wiped her snot and tears while looking at Noah.","Could he do even that?","Her reddened eyes looked at Noah for only a few seconds before she nodded.","In her lowest state.","As she hugged books she could not open anymore, she looked up at the visage of Noah as he took her now fragile hands and put them on this chest. His chest. There, she felt a terrifying warmth as her eyes just barely caught a glimpse of a Wheel.","Just barely.","But the warmth she felt traveled like arcs of electricity through her hands, going all the way into her body as the moment it reached a Source she thought did not exist anymore...","HUUM!","Her body began to illuminate with shocking radiance as her figure became bathed with multicolored light!","A dazzling white gold flame swept past her figure, her entire being feeling like it underwent a change as her source gushed out exuberant complexity that almost seemed ready to spill out towards a Prime Source.","The dress she adorned turned blue gold, her hairs gained a silver gold glow as her eyes opened with splendiferous luminosity.","She looked towards Noah in shock as she could feel everything once again, and what she felt was so much more than before!","The books she was always connected to rose around once more, linked by solid golden strings of existence as each book held a vibrant circular glow as if their very records were being fortified to never be lost for the eons to come!","She felt all of this as she had no words, tears still falling in her eyes as she shook her head with incredulity.","She felt a closeness towards this being she idolized that was not there before.","But she could not explain it!","She felt so unfathomably free that even this feeling, she did not know where it came from.","But the words of the Protagonist she idolized made a few things clear.","\"The Queen of Matter, the first Lifeform to connect and channel your weavings of existence through my True Source and not the Wheel of Existence...how do you feel?\"","...!","His words caused her to tremble as many things dawned on her, her expression changing rapidly as she experienced too many emotions all at once!","She wanted to say many things.","She was always so talkative.","Yet at this moment as she stared at the True Emperor of Quintessence...she had absolutely no words to say!","The Queen of Matter who always had words to say was made speechless!","Noah waved his hands at her as she came out of her stupor, her tears disappearing into dazzling lights of stars as she looked away while sighing in a daze.","\"I...can understand somewhat why all those prideful women threw themselves at you...\"","...!","She slowly began to go back to her old self as she spoke like this to evade saying what she truly felt right now.","How he...was just too brilliant for her to even look at.","But as she thought of his words about being the first and the implications this held...","\"Ah, Bob!\" She suddenly remembered this as her weavings erupted.","But Noah only waved his hands lightly.","\"Don't worry, Bob is no longer here.\"","...! He could say this with confidence now.","The Affix of the Burnt Weaver was taken another step by Ruination as after its current update, what he was capable of mapping was not just a mere Megalos.","He could now map out...an entire Frequency!","He affirmed Bob was not here the moment he arrived. What he was able to find...was a dazzling Node of Existence many light years away from here that was left right out in the open!","As all this happened.","|The True Source Atlas of Existence has gained its first Channeler.|","|The distinction of the First Channeler has been granted to the Queen of Matter.|","|The weavings of the Source of the Queen of Matter have been grasped with extreme clarity and can be replicated at any time.|","...!","Prompts began to rise within him!"]},{"number":3607,"title":"Chapter 3607: Chapter 3606 Irreparable! I","paragraphs":["Prompts began to rise as they expressed the wondrous allure of the True Source Atlas of Existence!","|As the First Channeler of the True Source Atlas of Existence, the quality of Absolute Infinitum Existentialism is momentarily granted to the Queen of Matter.|","|With her weavings attaining Absolute Infinitum Existentialism, there will be a constant and continual increase in her complexity with every passing moment.|","...!","His terrifying Atlas buzzed.","And in the next moment, the Source of the Queen of Matter that already seemed brighter began to explode and surge up with complexity as her Greater Source...began to transform!","\"Ah...!\"","She was shocked at this as she sensed her grandiose Greater Source break past heavy shackles and begin to change, heading towards the austere weavings of a Prime!","The two pronged factor of channeling through another Source and as the First Channeler, being granted a shocking quality that Noah had only obtained after he stabilized all three states of matter in his body.","She was exposed to all of this simultaneously as her source rapidly transformed and made the jump from Greater to Prime!","She was dazed as the books around her had their covers become inlaid with gold, her Source shimmering with an ever radiant luster as she felt the constant explosive burst of complexity within her that stemmed from Absolute Infinitum Existentialism.","She couldn't help but utter out as she spoke in a daze.","\"Is this...what you feel all the time?\"","His bursts of complexity.","His ever radiant demeanor.","She felt like she grasped a minuscule part of it as Noah nodded lightly and asked while he looked in a certain direction.","\"We'll have to get to what Bob has done in a second but...how do your weavings feel right now? How different or same are they?\"","Tendrils of rivers of multicolored light began to cover his body and the Queen of Matter as he wanted to ascertain the sensation of channeling through different Sources.","The Queen of Matter sensed her changing Source as she replied with fascination.","\"I feel like...my Complexity is uniquely not just more powerful perse, but as if it is under a different flow. As if the definitions of what I could do before are being redefined. The limitations, the boundaries. The fact that at this moment, I feel like Fabled Matter...has a possibility of adaptability and change as potentially, I could expand it to cover Dark Matter and Anti-Matter as well.\"","...!","A terrifying answer came from her as Noah nodded lightly, realizing there was much work to be done to study just how uniquely different an experience different Entities would have if they switched from channeling through the Wheel of Existence they always knew, to channeling through his True Source!","At this thought.","WAP!","Their figures disappeared once more as when they reappeared, they were light years away where Noah had seen on the Map of the Frequency of Aqua, a clear Node of Existence was displayed out in the open.","It looked like a miniature star of cerulean radiance as at this moment, two heavy silver white burn marks could be seen stretching out across it!","\"That...\"","In the midst of her transforming source, the Queen of Matter reached out to grasp the Node of Existence in shock and Noah's weavings also settled around it.","He shook his head while his eyes shone sharply as he was able to quickly understand what each mark meant- something that came akin to a natural language for him, who also held a significant portion of the Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence and what it could do!","He looked at the first burn mark as it was an alteration made to this Frequency of Existence through its Node- a change to the Flow that stated all those with this Frequency could no longer channel their weavings to the Wheel of Existence!","This was the first scorch mark.","The second one...was a communication and challenge directly from Bob to Noah himself!","The second scorch mark was another change on the Node that stated...any future attempts to alter this Node of Existence or its flow in any way...would result in the instantaneous breakdown of the Frequency itself.","\"This fucking guy...\"","Noah spoke out with a domineering light as the face of the Queen of Matter looked up with confusion, and he replied while looking around the reefs of the waters nearby where Bob should have been.","\"Bob has made it so we cannot reverse what he did. If I seek to alter the Node again, he has it set that the whole Frequency will shatter thereafter.\"","He spoke such words calmly to the Queen of Matter, who turned ghastly, thinking of all the countless lifeforms here who could no longer utilize their power and just how terrifying that would be, alongside the unknown chaos, upheaval, and deaths that would occur from this!","As such thoughts churned, Noah looked around as he wanted to try something.","He raised his hand as a moment later, the True Severed Weavings of Chronos bloomed.","He had a terrifying number of things under his banner as with his True Source Atlas of Existence, he held his own True Source.","He could dictate his own flow as he felt like to a certain extent...he could also violate some flows!","His hand clenched into a fist as the truly Severed Weavings of Chronos burned, a burst of purple radiance erupting out and covering this whole region as an illusory purple clock that also looked like an ancient Wheel bloomed.","And this Wheel...began to turn.","HUUM!","The flows in the surroundings turned chaotic and began to reverse as illusory purple weavings bloomed!","The seas moved in reverse as existence distorted, and in no time...","WAA!","An illusory figure of tentacle limbed entity with a round head appeared in front of a burning flame bound down by rotating Wheels above it.","Everything looked illusory and not real as if it were merely replaying what had occurred in these weavings of existence not too long ago!","Noah turned it all back until the massive purple Wheel conjured by Chronos began to vibrate and crack, and he only stopped then as the distortion of time stopped...and the illusory weavings of a past began to play out in real time before his eyes!"]},{"number":3608,"title":"Chapter 3608: Chapter 3607 Irreparable! II","paragraphs":["The past.","Noah forcefully conjured it as he rewound the flow of existence, and he began to watch what happened here not too long ago.","He saw the visage of Bob as he sat on the reefs, his gaze locked onto a Book that the Queen of Matter beside Noah gritted her teeth at seeing!","His gaze seemed to be blank before his voice echoed out as he closed the Book of Existence.","\"Let's start with the simple things first, shall we? Access to the weavings of the Wheel...let us make it simple and close it off first.\"","...!","Noah heard these words as his eyes became sharper.","The simple things first.","Closing off access to the True Source for all Channelers...was considered something simple among the things that Bob had to do!","Just what exactly would come after?","Such a thing was still unknown as the scene continued playing out.","As he stood over a flame and did what he did...","\"I am sorry for this. None of you deserve what is coming.\"","...!","He expressed a sense of regret for the inevitable!","He actually did such a thing before a moment later, he utilized the Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence not once, but twice!","And that should've been it.","But a moment after a second silver white scorch mark appeared on the Node of Existence...","\"This one is for you, my friend. Is it a good present? You taking over half of the Primal Flame of the Wheel was not among my calculations as I have had to change a few things due to it.\"","HUUM!","The voice of Bob echoed out from the illusory purple recreation of a past flow!","The Queen of Matter was astonished as she moved backwards and came to hide behind Noah.","As if she was scared even this illusory purple figure that should have just been a reversed flow playing out...might somehow be cognizant and be able to take action!","The figure of Bob smiled as the Wheels he had binding the Primal Flame of the Wheel began to turn.","\"Surprised? Shocked?\" His expression was bright as his singularities turned into crescent smiles, as if he understood that even as a reversed flow of existence, he still had cognizance and was himself!","\"Haha, am I truly here with my understanding and complexity? Or did I know you would do something like this and just choose to speak like this to freak you out in the case you did? Or if you did happen to peer into the weavings of past flows, was I able to sense it and talk to you?\"","...!","The illusory figure of Bob spoke like this as he turned towards a certain direction and looked head on as he asked!","\"Isn't that right, friend?\"","\"...\"","The direction he looked at...had nothing there.","Just blue waters of the sea.","Bob's illusory figure couldn't help but laugh lightly as he shook his head.","\"Haha, did I guess the direction right or wrong? I'm just playing with you, how could I possibly know all of this? Even now, I'm probably speaking of weavings nobody will be able to see or know about. When you become as old as I, you start to get senile. And the possibility of a genuine friend seems to have made me senile. Oh well.\"","HUUM!","He was his hands as the Primal Flame of the Wheel bound by two massive ancient decaying wheels disappeared, his figure beginning to disappear as well as at this time...","His head turned. He did not look in any random direction.","His terrifying singularities honed in exactly where Noah was as his eyes locked with his!","\"For you to be in this Frequency and be capable of channeling any power like this has too many implications. It was not something even I accounted for. It actually now makes you very challenging to what I wish to accomplish. Now, I have to answer the question...if you do not draw your weavings from this Wheel of Existence, exactly where do you draw them from?\"","...!","His eyes burned with a horrific radiance as he said these words with a wide smile, his visage giving a small nod to Noah while his eyes also glanced at the Queen of Matter beside him!","\"Till next time, Friend.\"","WAP!","With such words, Bob disappeared.","And Noah's expression became stern.","The entity that was Bob...was eccentric and loved to play around even while he did the unspeakable!","Even his flow in the past knew when it was being gazed at.","The illusory purple weavings of the past continued...until he and the Queen of Matter arrived here as soon, the past met the present as everything shattered, purple radiance fading away and only leaving them behind.","\"...\"","\"Fuck, he's scary....\" The Queen of Matter cursed out even as her complexity reached Prime Source.","Noah's white robes fluttered as he looked at the blue waters around him that maintained a wondrous level of serenity in all this.","\"Our enemy is moving quickly and decisively. We have to move even quicker. \"","WAA!","His vision saw a distant place others could not even imagine as to get there, many smaller things had to be done!","This Frequency was irreparable after what Bob had done as all those in here would not be able to channel through the Wheel of Existence.","But he...was not the Wheel of Existence.","He would give the people of this frequency a new Source to draw from.","Those of this Frequency, yes, but also his own people.","Such a process had to be fast as with his people and the countless lines of entanglements he had, there was no worry.","But for the masses across an entire Frequency or multiple Frequencies...there had to be another way!","\"Begin the design of another Source of Existence...\"","WAA!","He gave a command to his True Source Atlas of Existence as another Mundi lit up brightly, the weavings of Anti-Matter and Dark Matter rising as they asked from which of them this new Source would be based on?!"]},{"number":3609,"title":"Chapter 3609: Chapter 3608 Channelers! I","paragraphs":["Inside endless waves of blue, another one of Noah's bodies sought to enact an additional Source.","The more that were made, the more that the True Source Atlas of Existence would be compete!","As one of his bodies sought to do this. Back in the Prime Frequency of the End, near another Node of Existence, only Noah and Ruination remained alongside a kneeling Theodosius.","Crimson gold brilliance pulsed around Ruination as the Affixes of Burnt Weaver and Severed Extractor finished their ridiculous elevation- with Burnt Weaver of course gaining the capability to map out an entire Frequency while Severed Extractor...","\"Even incompatible Sources of Existence should be ones that Master is able to study and infer from. And so long as an entanglement exists, Master should be able to begin analyzing and studying said Sources.\"","Ruination spoke out calmly while keeping her hand behind Noah's back.","Noah heard this and nodded with bright eyes as even without asking...","\"With that being said, I've already placed the highest priority on understanding the weavings of Bob. His Source seems to be masked under layers of truths and falsehoods as the Affix has only just theorized and uncovered a decimal percentage worth of progress regarding this. It could take hours, days, or even more...\"","...!","The Source of Bob!","The entity who should be a Channeler drawing from an entirely different True Source!","Noah sought to understand just how and what the Source of this being was as such a thing began to be processed.","Ruination was doing all that she could and more as her status as a Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence gave her tremendous uniqueness.","Her eyes held a clear crimson gold brilliance as she said lastly.","\"Another Seed of an Affix is also budding within Master, and I am still constructing it to match utility and usefulness for the future to come. But something else is ready within the Forge, Master. I have been changing it as I advanced recently, and it should have grown to a sufficient enough level to be of use. Inside the True Severed Osmontian Forge...\"","...!","It had gone by many names before.","The forge where countless waves of Loot light bloomed within Noah's own existence- where Ruination resided in!","At this moment, amidst waves of changes, Noah looked deep within himself as his weavings went into the depths of the True Source Atlas of Existence.","Into the crevices of his soul where a system of existence relating to Loot spun.","Like all things, it was truly severed as it felt like a world inside of him.","He delved into it as the skies were filled with spinning cerulean infinity symbols that gushed out indeterminate waves of golden Loot light.","Down below, a spinning golden sea of Loot light spun as at the very center, a floating island rose above an ancient, archaic golden wheel that was bathed with golden waters of loot and constantly spun.","Every time this golden wheel spun, it sent beams of light into the island that looked utterly serene and celestial, with golden rivers and lakes flowing through it as vibrant grass born from Loot itself waved calmly in the surging winds.","At the center of this island.","In what looked like a farm, Ruination was in simple farming attire as she had long blue denim overalls, a simple white shirt under them, and a small straw hat that covered her head.","She looked up as Noah made his descent on the dazzling core of the True Severed Osmontian Forge, her eyes turning into crescent smiles as she pointed towards a mountain of...Purified Source Complexity Pearls near her!","\"I tried to hide it from Master, but I know you know what goes on inside you more than anything else. This has been something I've changed constantly over the days as I sought to aid in Master's goal of self sufficiency. Of not needing Loot from other Sources to rely on for your growth. The answer was to naturally make the forge capable of spitting out as much if not more Loot than what enemies could. So...I have been able to set up the Forge to produce a single Purified Greater Source Pearl...with every passing second.\"","WAA!","Above the hazy gold skies of the floating island, Noah had watched multiple singularities form while Ruination was talking, these singularities becoming dazzling Purified Source Pearls that fell on a mountain of other Pearls as there had to be hundreds of Greater Source Pearls alone here!","Noah came before the mountain of Source Pearls and smiled as he took one while looking at it.","A goal of self-sufficiency.","With Absolute Infinitum Existentialism, this was already a reality as now, with Ruination's ridiculous efforts, it would be cemented as an undeniable reality.","He did not need enemies to obtain Loot.","Loot was...","Loot was....!","HUUM!","True Severed Weavings descended.","The brilliance of Loot churned!","|Purposefully, the selection of an instant has been made after countless formulaic equations that have altered and triggered the Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity.|","|The passage of an instant may not be allowed without your complexity undergoing a targetted, significant burst of elevation that will be supported entirely by the True Severed Heart of Infinity.| |The Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity has purposefully declared the burst of elevation to stem from the weavings of...Loot.|","|The Severed Weavings of Loot, backed by the Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity, are undergoing a resurgence of their Pathway to attain a different Final Severed State!|","...!","Granted a Pathway before, but never truly defined. Today, Loot was given a resurgence with even greater authority as their distinction was made clearer!","A storm of golden brilliance erupted as Ruination looked around with wonder, and Noah nonchalantly walked towards her figure that looked like a simple farm girl who was cultivating terrifying Source Complexity Pearls of Existence.","He patted her head while lifting up the straw hat as he spoke with a genuine smile.","\"Thank you for working so hard.\"","A few words.","But they caused Ruination to feel a burst of happiness from the depths of her heart as all she ever wanted...was to be useful.","All she ever wanted was to stand side by side with him and not feel like she couldn't give anything.","She knew he didn't think of her any less whether she gave or didn't give anything, but this was just something in her heart that she wanted to achieve!","And now, the results bore fruit!"]},{"number":3610,"title":"Chapter 3610: Chapter 3609 Channelers! II","paragraphs":["The results bore tremendous fruit as down below, in a surging sea of Loot, a Wheel turned.","With every full turn, a Purified Greater Source Pearl would be produced and added onto a tall mountain on an island above!","And at this moment...","|The Severed Weavings of Loot have attained their Final Severed State.|","|The Pathway leading to the True Source of Loot has opened.|","|In the True Severed Osmontian Forge, the Severed Weavings of Loot make their home.|","|Through the Pathway to the True Source of Loot, you have attained Absolute Loot Generation- such a wonder fusing into the True Severed Osmontian Forge and empowering it even more. Its principle states that a Pathway leading to the True Source of Loot should make one independent of all needs of Loot from outside Sources. And once the True Source of Loot is obtained...|","|Through the Pathway to the True Source of Loot, it is recognized that while attaining independence from needing any outside Source of Loot, such things still exist. In the case that Loot is obtained outside, it only acts to supplement as it is not the main source for you. Any Weavings of Enemies with a sufficient enough complexity that have their weavings decimated by you will have their complexity transformed to become an Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence. From such a Loot Box, Undeniable Telos Purified Source Pearls may come out, or any myriad of wonders that lie in the realm of Uncertainty and Possibility across nearby True Sources.|","Loot took a tremendous step forward as its own Pathway was opened. From this pathway comes Absolute Loot Generation and Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence!","The latter was outside.","The former that dealt with Noah's weavings...","HUUM!","Caused the Forge to churn as even denser waves of gold flowed down from the spinning infinity symbols in the skies, while the golden sea below that had a golden archaic wheel at the very center became chaotic.","The Wheel turned.","And the whole forge instantly flashed with multicolored radiance all around.","On the island above, nine radiant singularities of heavy complexity bloomed, an allure of a terrifying Source being felt from them as a prompt came down!","|Every time a minute passes, 9 Purified Prime Source Pearls will be generated within the True Severed Osmontian Forge. Based on countless formulations and possibilities under the banner of the Golden Ratio, Undeniable Telos Purified Source Pearls also have a chance of generating ever so often.|","...!","Noah looked at this prompt and smiled, holding Ruination close to him as he reached out to hold nine dazzling Purified Prime Source Pearls.","Every minute, they would form.","Outside of here, could he kill 9 Prime Source entities every minute for the foreseeable future?","The answer was no as this...was the answer that Ruination and Loot gave for Noah's own sustainability!","With Absolute Infinitum Existentialism. With Absolute Loot Generation. With this True Severed Osmontian Forge...","With all of it, he had multiple pathways of pumping his complexity in a manner that even hunting entire frequencies filled with Greater or Prime Sources could not provide.","With this...","\"Direct it all to the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed. Let us see the halfway point to the True Source of Singed itself after all this time...\"","...!","He gave the command to his weavings as all of these flows of Loot would head towards a singular direction- and he expected to make a significant enough advancement in the coming minutes to finally push a Pathway past a significant milestone!","And while all of this occurred.","Upheaval began within the Infiniverse Megalos. Noah gathered his people under glorious Pantheonic Havens as he tugged upon their entanglements.","He tugged on their weavings of Existence as his voice thundered out within their minds!","|This whole time, you have been Channelers of weaving you do not know nor understand. You have been Channeling a True Source that is grand, but malleable to changes. Malleable to alterations. Leave such a True Source behind as from here on out, you shall join the True Source of the True Severed Origin Osmontian- the True Source Atlas of Existence!|","HUUM!","His voice was a booming undeniable command that his son heard.","His women heard.","All those closest to him, and the countless others that he did not interact with or truly know!","But so long as they were within the vast lands of the Infiniverse Megalos, their weavings were taken from channeling towards an unknown and not too entirely understood Wheel of Existence, and they were steered towards another True Source!","They were steered to become Channelers of something with much clearer demarcations and distinction as this...nobody but Noah himself could alter!","They were the Channelers that followed the Queen of Matter.","They were among the first, but they were certainly not the last as away from the Megalos Ynnere where the Infiniverse Megalos was contained in.","With the neighboring Megalos Beyond and Megalos Nihilos where all states of existence were meeting in one area.","In the location where Ozymandias was floating while Outerversal Morphons led by the Great Mother, Aspasia, and others...pledged their Allegiance not to the Instrument of the Beyonder, but the Protagonist, Ozymandias!","As they looked at him, he gave the answer as to what state of Existence the upcoming System of Existence being forged would be.","Something to allow his weavings to stretch unto those he knew and those he did not know.","When he thought of this as a method to gain more Channelers, he naturally remembered the Outerversal Morphons who could fish across the Megalos to attain connections and attain followers.","So his singularities burned as he felt his True Source Atlas of Existence begin the design of another System- Dark Matter surging at its base as just at its formation...Ozymandias found himself asking!","|Why not both?|","HUUM!","From the base of Dark Matter alone, Anti-Matter also bloomed!","Who said a System of Existence had to be built on a single State of Existence alone?","There were also qualities of Anti-Matter that were unique to think of when it came to spreading one's weavings!","So...","\"Made of Dark Matter and Anti-Matter....\"","HUUM!","Ozymandias proclaimed grandly as he looked to obtain countless more Channelers.","\"Let the System of Existence of...Eldritch Expanse come to fruition.\"","...!"]},{"number":3611,"title":"Chapter 3611: Chapter 3610 Channelers! III","paragraphs":["Eldritch Expanse.","Such a set of words were called out nonchalantly at a spot where seas of three states of Existence met.","Ozymandias called them out as the distant Great Mother and many other Outerversal Morphons barely even heard it, but in the next moment...","HUUM!","The surrounding weavings churned as rivers of Dark Matter and Anti-Matter began to flow into Ozymandias en masse!","They were the backbone for a new System of Existence entirely as a lot could be needed!","And the Administrator of the True Source Atlas of Existence...began to design and etch out a System of Existence with the very authority of this Atlas.","It was akin to a man making up a word and, in the next few seconds, proceeding to make a definition for the word.","What it stood for. What its parameters were.","He used inferences from other observations made within different Sources of Existence, but at the end of the day, the definition was his.","What it meant.","What it stood for. In the Eighth Mundi of Power, regal black and white tentacles began to bloom as even when Noah's weavings looked at them, these black and white tentacles seemed foreign. Pervasive.","As if the moment they would bloom, they would spread out across countless weavings of Existence in ways others couldn't even comprehend.","This...was a critical factor of Eldritch Expanse as even while it was being constructed...","|The weavings of the Golden Ratio have already made countless formulaic calculations and tipped the favor of change and probability to the newly designed System of Existence.|","|As long as a sufficient level of complexity in design is complete, Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity will be triggered to truly sever and take the weavings of the new System of Existence towards their Final Severed State.|","...!","His weavings of existence were already there and ready to go as inside of him...the heavy Wheel that was overlapped with his Atlas of Existence turned.","A single turn. DUM!","And the moment this turn was made, a weaving of a terrifying complexity bloomed as a singularity shooting out stellar white and black tentacles truly bloomed.","|A new System of Existence is being established within the True Source Atlas of Existence.|","|It is the first Source of Existence being designed while the Atlas is at its current stage of a True Source.|","|The Source of Existence, Eldritch Expanse, has gained accelerated qualities of a Source from the True Source Atlas of Existence as its elevation and progression as a Pathway to its True Source will be accelerated by an unknown factor.|","|The True Severed Weavings of Pathogenicity are in heavy support of the Source of Eldritch Expanse and throw their weight fully into it.|","|The True Severed Weavings of Cheats are in heavy support of the Source of Eldritch Expanse and throw their weight fully into it.|","|The True Severed Weavings of the Protagonist...|","Multiple weavings rose up in tremendous support.","Around Ozymandias, a horrific aura that caused one's heart to palpate echoed out, the distant Outerversal Morphons feeling their Sources of Existence tremble as the sensation of prey looking at a horrific predator bloomed.","Stellar white and black radiance leaked out from Ozymandias as from his obsidian skin, tendrils of beautiful and grotesque white and black tentacles began to emerge.","They vibrated with heaviness and tenacity as they sensed their surrounding, their level of cognition seeming to be unfathomably high.","|The budding weavings of Eldritch Expanse gaze at the Complexity of Existence and despairs at their imperfect form.|","|The budding weavings of Eldritch Expanse pull upon the True Source Atlas of Existence and undergo True Severing!|","...!","The weavings of Ozymandias and Noah buzzed!","The blooming new Source...did not even wait for others to move on its behalf as it pulled upon the power of the True Source Atlas of Existence to sever itself!","And after that...","|The True Severed Weavings of Eldritch Expanse pull upon the connection of the Heart of Infinity and the Singed to instantly achieve 27 rounds of Severings.|","...!","Around Ozymandias, more and more heart-shaking stellar black and white tentacles bloomed- the figure of Ozymandias being drowned out as these tentacles grew unfathomably huge- very quickly becoming larger than a world, a sun and continued to stretch out like a circular pulsing mass of tentacles for hundreds of thousands of miles!","Eldritch Expanse!","It showed a shocking level of initiative and control at this moment as if was far from being done!","|The Severed Weavings of Eldritch Expanse forcefully extend into the True Source Atlas of Existence and trigger Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity.|","|The passage of an instant may not be allowed without the complexity of the Eldritch Expanse undergoing a crucial, significant burst of elevation that will be supported entirely by the True Severed Heart of Infinity.| |The Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity had been commanded to impose its weavings on the Eldritch Expanse.|","|The Severed Weavings of Eldritch Expanse surge across Severings and head towards their Final Severed State!|","HUUUM!","The phenomenon...was unheard of.","DUM!","The Wheel overlapping the True Source Atlas of Existence turned as a colorless radiance began to flow out.","|Quintessence observes Eldritch Expanse with caution and coldness.|","|Tyranny gazes towards Eldritch Expanse with eyes of unscalability.|","|The weavings of Ozymandias are under the extreme influence of the Severed Weavings of Eldritch Expanse.|","Something was happening.","Something unexpected.","Something new!","Many of Noah's terrifying Sources rose up with care and caution as they sensed this!","Yet in the midst of all of this...","|The Weavings of Uncertainty throw their full support to Eldritch Expanse.|","|The Weavings of Plot throw their full support to Eldritch Expanse.|","|The Weavings of Entropy throw their full support to Eldritch Expanse.|","|The Weavings of Armageddon throw...|","|The Weavings of Apocalypse...|","...!","Noah's weavings buzzed as while some cautioned, others rose in support of the First Source to bloom while the Atlas of Existence was a True Source Atlas of Existence!","The interminable authority and control that Eldritch Expanse was gaining became even more profound as quickly, its Final Severed State was obtained!"]},{"number":3612,"title":"Chapter 3612: Chapter 3611 Channelers! IV","paragraphs":["|The Severed Weavings of Eldritch Expanse have attained their Final Severed State.|","|The Pathway leading to the True Source of Eldritch Expanse has opened.|","HUUUM!","The mass of stellar black and white tentacles that had Ozymandias at the very center attained a terrifying glow- white and black flames of virulence and pathogenicity blooming over them as in the distance, the hearts of the Great Mother and others shuddered.","What was this? Just what was happening? Was this still part of the weavings of the Protagonist?","Many began to edge back unknowingly as they saw what was happening ahead, the figure of Tam of the Singed also coming from a distance as he finished clearing out the last Faceless Lifeforms in distant Pantheon, and even he looked towards the scene in shock!","Far from here, in the Megalos Ynnere where Mysara brought Emelline of the First Flame who was currently still undergoing Dual Cultivation with Noah...even their weavings were interrupted by the horrifying and foreign aura leaking out from a far distance, their will gazing out to understand just what it was.","In the midst of all this...","|The Pathway to the True Source of Eldritch Expanse gazes at the weavings of existence.|","|Eldritch Expanse gazes at the complex Flow of Existence.|","|Through the Pathway to the True Source of Eldritch Expanse, Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis has been claimed.|","|Through the Pathway to the True Source of Eldritch Expanse, Absolute Frequency Ontopathogenesis has been claimed.|","...!","Terrifying capabilities bloomed as a pathway for something utterly glorious was made.","And right away...","|Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis has been triggered, powered by the Heart of Infinity.|","HUUM!","The stellar black and white tentacles of mass that had spread out tremendously around Ozymandias.","At this moment, they pulsed eerily as an instant later, countless thin, barely discernable tentacles barely half an inch in size shot out in all directions!","\"Ah...\"","Little Aspasia and Other Outerversal Morphons backed up the moment they observed such a thing.","The Great Mother...her tentacles trembled, but she did not move a muscle.","She stayed still.","And whether it was her or other Outerversal Morphons, the moment they even saw the stretching out thin tendril, it had already reached them as it was far too fast.","WAP!","A single thin tentacle for every being.","Some were struck by a stellar black tentacle, others were struck by a stellar white tentacle.","But undoubtedly, every single one was unable to even defend against it no matter what their complexity did, and the moment their bodies were stuck by it...","They became utterly still.","HUUM!","Their bodies glowed with a faint stellar black and white radiance as their eyes and singularities opened wide, but they held no cognizance.","The brilliance in their eyes....was only that of Eldritch Expanse.","In another direction, the figure of Tam of the Singed watched with a sense of wonder and trepidation as a white tentacle struck his forehead, his head being knocked back as his pupils, which were always covered by white gold flames, turned a hazy white gold.","They blinked right after to show no emotion, and they only looked at the surroundings with calm!","Countless unfathomable stellar black and white tentacles shot out from the region where three states of Existence met, all of them stretching out across the Megalos Beyond, Megalos Nihilos, and Megalos Ynnere!","They bound onto every single complexity they came across as the ability that initiated all of this...was Unidemic!","Not Epidemic.","Not Pandemic.","But Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis.","Across the Megalos.","And not just the Megalos...with countless more thin tentacles transcending the weavings of existence and shooting out into the Expanse.","The Weavings of Eldritch Expanse proliferated in such a rapid manner as even the Megalos Ynnere...","One of Noah's bodies disconnected from Emelline of the First Flame and straightened out his robe, his expression cold as he looked at the Prime Sources Complexity before him who had just attained an Undeniable Telos Source.","Yet at this moment, her body was frozen as a white tentacle connected behind her head, her figure floating serenely without an expression as when she blinked and opened her eyes, they were covered by a hazy stellar black and white radiance.","Not the radiance of Emelline of the First Flame, but that of a part of Noah...of Eldritch Expanse!","Noah also gazed nearby where the visage of Mysara was, and she held the same state as she floated serenely, her body beginning to pulse with a unique sense of power as...","|Through Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis, all infected Complexities are being automatically redirected as they are granted the glorious distinction of the Channelers of the True Source Atlas of Existence.|","...!","What Noah sought to do with the enactment of a new Source.","To rapidly and quickly change the Source that countless existences across the Megalos and Expanse held to that of his own!","It was being achieved at this moment, but...even after the Sources of these complex beings became Channelers of his True Source Atlas of Existence.","Even as he felt trillions of connections flow towards his Atlas as its Wheel began to conduct heavy spins of complexity...","Those he looked at remained under the effect and control of Eldritch Expanse.","The faint half an inch tentacle connecting to countless beings became transparent as if it did not even exist.","But their eyes remained flashing with a hazy black and white radiance as the singular prevailing identity and control within the affected beings...was that of Eldritch Expanse.","\"...\"","Noah looked into that black and white glow.","He was essentially looking at himself.","And he asked.","\"What are you doing?\"","HUUM!","He asked a newly born part of himself that because of the factors leading to its birth, it gained far too much cognizance as it moved based on how its Source felt.","He knew what it was doing, and yet, he still had to ask...his new System of Existence.","Eldritch Expanse!","In front of him, a deep voice came from Emelline of the First Flame.","|Complexity...Existence itself...is filled with uncertainty and contradiction.|","WAA!","The voice was deep.","The voice was his.","A part of him...with a different ideology. |All sources of conflict stem from the countless clashing ideologies and complexities across the different Flows of Existence. The Flows under this Wheel of Existence. The Flows of the Beyonder and the Omnifather under this Wheel of Existence. The Flows under the Wheel of Existence Bob and the Faceless Lifeforms stem from. We can eliminate all this conflict by taking over their flow. By controlling existence to move as we see fit. By our flow. The elimination of their flimsy ideologies and emotional complexity that make them take actions that only create unstable chaos. We can come to deny and control all of this. No uncertainty. No contradiction. Only stable chaos. Just countless, endless flows filled with certainty...under the banner of the True Severed Origin Osmontian.|","...!"]},{"number":3613,"title":"Chapter 3613: Chapter 3612 Complexities and Contradictions! I","paragraphs":["A part of him.","A part of him forged under the True Source Atlas of Existence proceeded to look at existence itself after waking up and deemed the countless complexity across it...to be far too unstable.","The Pathway to the True Source of Eldritch Expanse deemed that the best possible path...was to eliminate the countless ideologies and emotions that were always mixed in with the complexity of Existence as they made way for unstable chaos!","Noah gazed into the white and black glow in the eyes of Emelline of the First Flame and Mysara who held absolutely no cognizance as around him, heavy flows of budding complexity bloomed.","Above, a colorless Pathway burning with Quintessence manifested as an illusory figure with his likeness appeared, his gaze cold and calculating.","He was only the first.","Nearby, a glorious white gold Pathway burning with flames of the Singed bloomed as a Noah wreathed in flames appeared, his flames burning everything nearby with an overpowering light of brilliance!","Near this Pathway, a gorgeous blue Pathway burning with Infinity bloomed- multiple parts that made Noah blooming one after another at this moment as they all looked at each other.","The Pathway to the True Sources of Plot and Cheats also appeared as among the many different parts of Noah, there were some that supported Eldritch Expanse.","There were those who cautioned and opposed the Eldritch Expanse.","And behind Emelline of the First Flame and Mysara, a glorious black and white pathway filled with countless tentacles bloomed, another version of Noah sitting in the middle of all these tentacles as his gaze was a calm one. His gaze was a cold one.","|We all know it.|","His deep voice, filled with complexity, echoed out as intent was shared with all parts of himself.","|Ideologies and Emotions mixed in with a high level of complexity only lead to unstable chaos that leads to chaotic flows. Take a look at Azzurra. A remnant of Beyonder- a creature born from an obsession to protect, and yet she backed another Channeler of this Wheel who abandoned it and joined hands with Channelers of another Source. All for the sake of his ideology and emotions. Because of it, countless complex lifeforms in an entire Frequency of Life perished. Because of it, the Change and proliferation of countless Faceless Lifeforms took place. Unstable chaos. Uneeded chaos. If these ideologies were to be eliminated, something like this would not happen again. Everything would flow under our guidance. Our principle.|","The words of Eldritch Expanse were heavy.","He had black and white pupils and looked exactly like Noah as he looked at the other parts of him.","He gazed toward Infinity and the Megalos.","He gazed towards the Singed and Quintessence.","|We have the capability. We can stabilize countless flows and ensure prosperity that spreads not just across this Wheel of Existence but also other True Sources. Because once we get started, we cannot stop. One True Source. Another True Source...and Another True Source. The flow of the True Severed Origin Osmontian would spread across every true Source and ensure no possibility of haphazard ideologies mixing in with complexities. We...have the capability!|","WAA!","Its vision was grand.","Its weavings were heavy.","Noah, surrounded by many parts of him, walked towards the figure of Mysara whose eyes held no cognizance of her past self as he spoke calmly.","\"In their current state, what difference is there between this Mysara and the Persephael whom we scorched the weavings of Existence of? Persephael is dead, but is Mysara...also not dead? If you take away what she is, would you not be taking away what countless other complexities are across frequencies and effectively be killing all of them?\"","...!","What was the difference?!","Noah asked calmly as Eldritch Expanse did not take long before replying.","|This depends on the definition of what it means to be alive. Mysara's weavings are still alive. Her Record persists. Her Record is her life. We can preserve the records of all others and prevent the actual cessation of life- the cut off and erasure of their existence and records.|","WAA!","The definition of life!","Eldritch Expanse viewed life as the accumulation and records one held- where so long as this was preserved, one was alive!","Noah shook his head at this as he replied.","\"The moment you take away their ideology. The emotions that go along with their complexity, their records will stop. They will no longer be capable of enacting any more records as their Will to do so will be gone. They will just exist...but be dead inside. We would be responsible for the cleansing and deaths of countless records across countless Frequencies. How will we be any better than those we have defeated before?\"","|...|","Eldritch Expanse was silent.","This part of Noah was just born, but it knew many things- as well as the fact of who was in control.","It turned and looked at Noah tenderly before it replied.","|This whole time, you have always been in control, and yet you allowed me to do this. Part of you...part of us believes in this. That there lies the possibility of this being a true path to follow. We could do this. We could be...ever so glorious.|","HUUM!","The part of him that had its tendrils spreading out across the Frequency of the End said such words as Noah was silent to this.","Above him, his part brimming with Quintessence had a cold gaze as it was the one to reply.","|As we crush any other ideologies and emotions, our ideologies will remain. Our emotions will remain. Who will be there to stifle our weavings and ensure the collapse of any ideologies across complexity? For true, absolute efficiency across existence?|","Quintessence spoke out grandly as nobody was there to answer.","Nobody.","Until the weavings of Cheats smiled and looked towards a distant place that they could all see.","|Well, one thing is clear. This Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis has allowed us to sniff out a rat of unique significance.|","WAA!","Cheats looked towards a distant place within the Expanse as all parts of Noah's weavings knew exactly what he was talking about!"]},{"number":3614,"title":"Chapter 3614: Chapter 3613 Complexities and Contradictions! II","paragraphs":["Noah looked out towards the distant place Cheats was gazing at as he remained unfettered, his gaze going towards Eldritch Expanse as he gave a light command.","\"Make all Channelers here follow our True Source, but leave their weavings be. Their ideologies and emotions are their own as I do not take the Will of others.\"","...!","He gave the command calmly as he began to rise up.","On the black and white Pathway to the True Source of Eldritch Expanse, his other self had a complex look as he uttered out.","|We could have been...even more Quintessentially glorious...|","It looked discontent. It seemed to still want to carry out at its will!","And at such words, Noah's eyes became sharp as he turned towards another part of him with lividity.","\"Will you listen and obey, or will you revolt?!\"","HUUM!","Unfathomably terrifying waves of complexity seethed around Noah, his True Source Atlas of Existence buzzing as he looked towards Eldritch Expanse coldly!","\"I face countless unknown threats outside of me, I will not have conflict within my own weavings. Will you obey, or will you revolt? I can strip you down to countless minuscule particles of Dark Matter and Anti-Matter, utterly shred everything to do with Eldritch Expanse within a Mundi of Power with but a thought and build something else right after!\"","His face held boundless waves of Tyranny as his weavings of Eldritch Expanse closed their eyes sadly.","They then nodded.","They then followed.","In the surroundings, Plot smacked his lips and began to disappear.","Entropy, veiled in the back, was silent the whole time as he also began to fade away.","Ultimately, the colorless Pathway to the True Source of Quintessence remained as it observed everything for a little while longer before even it faded away.","Eldritch Expanse, on his black and white brilliant Pathway, let out a pulse of radiance that traveled to the countless quintillions of thin tentacles he had connecting to countless existences as he also disappeared.","Clouded in even more darkness, the True Severed Weavings of the very concept of Existence itself buzzed with silent contemplation as it also disappeared.","A Council of different parts of Noah had formed ever so briefly and dispersed even more quickly.","Cheats still had an interested gaze as he looked at a certain location within the depths of the Expanse, even his weavings beginning to fade away.","Ultimately, the colorless Pathway to the True Source of Quintessence remained as it observed everything for a little while longer before even it faded away.","Eldritch Expanse, on his black and white brilliant Pathway, let out a pulse of radiance that traveled to the countless quintillions of thin tentacles he had connecting to countless existences as he also disappeared.","HUUM!","In the next moment, the eyes of Mysara and Emelline of the First Flame flashed before they lost their black and white luster.","\"Ah, shit...what the hell happened?\"","Mysara grabbed her head as if she had a horrid headache, Emelline of the First Flame doing the same as she blinked before looking around to see Noah.","She placed her hands on her chest as she felt...different.","In a way she couldn't explain.","She raised her hands as terrifying flames bloomed from her Undeniable Telos Prime Source, feeling that they were familiar to her old flames, but they carried a sense of lethality and complexity that was not there before!","\"I...I felt something, but I cannot remember...\"","Her Prime Source buzzed as if it was trying to remember something critical, but nothing arose as she looked toward Noah!","The Origin Singed.","Noah simply looked back at her as he knew because of their prior connection, when Eldritch Expanse made a move, the Undeniable Telos Prime Source of Emelline was not even able to react as her weavings, which were empowered by his treated the attack as if it was not an attack.","That action did not mean that the Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis was capable of ignoring even weavings of Undeniable Telos Sources, but...it could easily infect Greater Sources!","As for Prime Sources, this varied.","Depending on the Prime Source.","Depending on their power.","And he was learning this first hand as he also thought about the location Cheats was looking at where they found...a Rat!","But he shook his head at this as he spoke towards Emelline of the First Flame.","\"You have your Undeniable Telos Source, and as a Channeler...you should be able to sense some changes. Can you still perceive...the flow of the Wheel?\"","He was curious about the Singed.","Burnt by the Flame of the Wheel, and yet now...one of their most powerful Singed was no longer channeling through the Wheel of Existence.","At his words, Emelline of the First Flame blinked as she closed her eyes before she opened them in surprise.","\"I can sense the Flow of the Wheel with much greater clarity, but...\"","There was something she could not put a finger on!","Noah nodded at her words as he noted that though she was now a Channeler of a different True Source, she knew that something was different, but could never pinpoint exactly what.","\"Head back to the other Singed. I will start clearing Faceless Lifeforms across frequencies soon as there a small fight for the Singed remaining.\"","He talked to her as if a superior was giving their follower a command.","And Emelline of the First Flame felt no dissonance from this as she nodded!","\"Yes, Origin Singed.\"","BZZT!","Flames burned around her as she disappeared.","She left behind Mysara who looked towards Noah bashfully before she cleared her throat and spoke while blue flames surged around her.","\"Sir Origin Singed! I would also like an Undeniable Telos Source!\"","She had seen what he had just done as she wanted to jump on board as well, Noah shaking his head lightly with a sigh as he beckoned her over, whispering to himself along the way.","\"An imperfect man...I'm just an imperfect man...\"","...!","With a glimmer of brilliance, a veil came to settle down.","And far, far from here.","In the Expanse.","BOOM!","Newly forming Strings of Existence shattered as millions of thin black and white tentacles chased after a single being.","A Rat.","An Old Man whose weavings were unfathomably vibrant- an old man discovered while Eldritch Expanse cast Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis to cover all entities across this frequency!","\"Haha, I thought myself to be a learned man of the Origins of Existence, but what the hell is this?!\"","Burning brilliantly with a unique Prime Source that looked to be distorted and mutated by many things.","It was an Existence that had interacted with Noah before under different power.","Under veiled weavings!","It was Ashmole...who had gained a drop of Noah's Blood within the Commonwealth!"]},{"number":3615,"title":"Chapter 3615: Chapter 3614 Complexities and Contradictions! III","paragraphs":["In the Expanse.","Millions of thin black and white strings chased after an Old Man whose weavings brimmed with a Prime Source Complexity!","He had been so deeply veiled and hidden inside small gaps of Megalos within the Expanse as even with other Prime Source complexities searching, they may have not been able to find this entity.","But Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis sought every single creature across the Frequency.","Nothing escaped its sight as this old man was discovered this way.","Ashmole!","\"Hey! Do you know who I am?! How about you reveal yourself first, huh? And then we can see whether any of this should be happening. You see, I am just a Scholar of Existence...\"","He spoke as his Prime Source ebbed and flowed in a unique manner.","Half black and half white garments covered him currently as even though he was visibly old, he seemed to have returned to his prime as his hair shone with lustrous black glow rapidly, his eyes twinkling with brilliance as a force existed around him which seemed...Undeniable.","It knocked away anything that came even though he was being pushed back, and at this time, another voice descended as from the surroundings, Noah's figure stepped out from the golden strings of existence.","\"I know very well who you are. Did you forget about me, Alchemist Ashmole?\"","The black and white tentacles pulsed and spread out all around like spears that waited to strike as Ashmole blinked and rubbed his eyes as if he couldn't believe it, pointing towards Noah with utter surprise as he laughed jovially!","\"Haha! Osmont? Osmont! I thought you were dead and banished after I stopped messing around with the Commonwealth. So you are alive and well! But...\"","Ashmole looked around at the terrifying bursts of tentacles that were supported by Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis.","\"...this type of power here is excessive even for you, don't you think? How about we-\"","\"What did you do with my drop of blood?\"","WAA!","Noah interrupted the ramblings of the old man.","They had made an exchange what seemed like many, many days ago when Noah was first exploring the weavings of the Commonwealth.","Who knew that all the way back then, Noah had met a Prime Source Complexity who was veiling himself to be so weak?","Hearing the question posed to him, Ashmole stopped and smiled.","\"Oh, that?\"","He hummed lightly as his Source did the same.","He looked around and seemed thoughtful for a second before he replied.","\"I truly do study Existence. Especially anomalous Existence. You, other creatures in separate frequencies who hold a massive flow of the Wheel around them, Singed, and now...even those Faceless Lifeforms.\"","WAA!","As he spoke, his body undulated and gradually changed as he seemed to be many people at the same time.","Multiple faces came and went on his aged face as he smiled eerily and continued.","\"I study this Existence so that I can incorporate such anomalies into myself. You were among those who helped supercharge my existence and grant me an Undeniable Telos Source, for that, I thank you. Your little drop of Blood...I was able to extrapolate many things from it, as, surprisingly, my inherent energy and complexity have been edging toward the edge of Infinity! As if I have inexhaustible waves of authority to spare...well, almost. When I lean too much into it, it turns my chimeric weavings a bit unstable. But you made many things possible for me...\"","...!","Noah's expression was cold as he listened to this being, now fully allowing him to ramble on as he was revealing quite a lot freely.","And Ashmole seemed to know this as he had a bright smile while shaking his head.","HUUM!","\"Man, look at that look in your eyes...all you anomalies with a heavy flow of the wheel always have this main character syndrome. You think yourselves to be the only creatures with stories that matter across existence, and you so ridiculously downplay the existence of all others as if they don't matter at all. Even now, what do you see me as? Someone that lied to you and you are now discovering the truth as you will try to kill me? My story is more than that, you know...\"","HUUM!","His existence began to buzz.","On his chest, skin faded and tore as a dazzling black nine pointed star manifested.","On this star, dazzling sockets holding jagged Gems that glimmered with the allure of Omniverses could be seen as the smile on Ashmole faded!","\"I have met a few like you, Osmont. I have tried replicating their qualities with some success, but as always, there is a level of defectiveness. Impurity. You remember that? You said something about purity and how it keeps the Wheel turning...well, something along those lines, anyway. But did you know how impure someone like me is? But even I...can have a flow that makes the Wheel turn, O Lumen Emperor.\"","HUUM!","He called out a past distinction of Noah's as his Source emenated a unique sense of danger.","A danger exceeding even that of entities like Giuseppe!","Tentacles erupted from behind him and formed into black wings as he smiled eerily again as he spoke.","\"I've taken from your qualities. From that pesky Peacemaker that keeps sending attacks my way. From a Usurper that nearly devoured a part of me. From the Lost Avatar of the Beyonder, Azzurra. From the Antideluvians...and truly, any traces of those Legends that transcended the Wheel of Existence to go to that place.\"","HUUUM!","\"That place...I am close to it, you know? I just need to completely join or do something else to all my possibilities- all versions of me across the Frequencies, and I will be complete. Right now, you are interrupting my progress, Osmont. A day of progress as I was hurrying before the weavings of that monstrous unknown creature swallowed up this Frequency!\"","His eyes flashed with power and madness.","Stability and chaos.","His Prime Source was utterly terrifying as Severed Extractor analyzed it, and Noah couldn't help but shake his head with pity.","\"What a sad life you have led, Ashmole.\"","...!"]},{"number":3616,"title":"Chapter 3616: Chapter 3615 Complexities and Contradictions! IV","paragraphs":["What a sad life he led!","Noah uttered such words as Ashmole couldn't help but look at him incredulously before he laughed, his enlarging hand holding his belly as if what was said was the funniest thing he heard.","\"Man, the main character syndrome has delved itself in you more than any others. You do not have to pity my life. I have lived for cycles. I have taken many lovers and have had many children. I have lived as a peasant, and ruled as an emperor. I have worked for the Commonwealth in one Frequency, and commanded the Commonwealth in others. I have joined the Watchers of Wheelomachy in some and even waged war against Singed in others. I have lived...Osmont, I have lived!\"","HUUM!","His words were resonant and filled with power as the quality of undeniability around him became even more intense, the Nine Pointed Star on his chest beginning to spin like an engine as his weavings released a devouring light that tainted and usurped anything nearby.","Noah looked at this as he shook his head.","\"If you have lived this much, then it might be time for you to die, Ashmole.\"","...!","In his hands, multiple statues of himself appeared. Ashmole gazed towards him coldly as at such a moment...","BZZT!","In the distance, space fluctuated as from the golden strings of existence, a figure made of light manifested.","Humanoid.","Adorned in a green gold robe.","And on his chest...a dazzling Nine Pointed Star could be seen.","What Ashmole had on his chest seemed to be a mere imitation as this Nine Pointed Star seemed genuine.","Complete.","And at this moment, this Nine Pointed Star had many Sockets that held multicolored Gems shimmering with the light of the Megalos themselves!","Noah looked at the newly appearing being calmly as he sent Severed Extractor to do its job, but he found that the entity he was looking at...was not actually here for him to study his Source!","Ashmole turned and looked towards this being coldly as he spoke with a hint of anger.","\"The Peacemaker comes to join the fray? Why now? My dear Gem Master, do you anomalies share the same senses?\"","The Peacemaker. Gem Master!","Noah heard this name as he raised his brows, thinking back to the weavings he had heard from another conversation he had not too long ago!","The man who appeared in the distance buzzed with weavings of a Source as it was not too clear whether he was Lesser, Greater, or Prime as it seemed to fluctuate.","He placed his hand on his chest as he looked towards Noah briefly before his gaze locked onto Ashmole!","|I came across the knowledge that the moment to make or break you had arrived. If you are to succeed, my peace might be ruined in the future, so I came back to this place that I truly did not want to return to, even in this limited capacity...to ensure your failure, Ashmole. To ensure my peace.|","WAA!","He came back.","He was here, but not really here!","Noah's eyes were luminous as when this being talked about coming back, he seemed to be talking about the very weavings of the Wheel of Existence as he should not be a native of the Prime Frequency of the End.","\"Haha...at the precipice of success or failure, and the anomalies that helped me get here are appearing one after another? What, should I expect even more to come? Is that what the Wheel intends? Will it not let me have even this after eons of experimentation?!\"","HUUM!","The weavings of Ashmole shook tumultuously as around his enlarging and increasingly distorted body, his faces that had been changing this whole time settled back to that of an old man as around him, stability slowly began to return.","His gaze became cold and detached as he looked at Noah and the Peacemaker.","He gave them both a sidelong glance as he spoke out impassively.","\"Did you know? Every single creature under this Wheel of Existence channels through it. All their weavings. All their power. It all flows across a singular channel that is unfathomably hard to change. The Beyonder, The Omnifather...those being managed to overcome the limitations of their channels. The more straightforward forward is to be the only you remaining across frequencies. I theorized they may have stably merged with all their other selves and attained a vastly expanded channel, and they reached that place. But for me...I already have too many transmutations mixed in. If I try to fuse with even more parts of me across frequencies...everything will collapse. So tell me, O Anomalies, what is another path I could take?\"","The Alchemist asked calmly as around him, millions of black and white lines seemed ready to strike.","And from the newly appearing Peacemaker, a simple white bow carved with countless runic gems appeared in his hands- this bow becoming raised as a bowstring was slowly pulled back!","Noah looked at this being that provided another viewpoint on the elevation of power that the Beyonder and a few others might have gone through as he replied to his question calmly.","\"If you cannot fuse with your other selves, then you can naturally...kill them.\"","HUUM!","Cold, dreadful words.","And yet they caused Ashmole to smile and nod sadly.","\"Yes. My other selves that I have been sharing memories with this whole time...I have ordered them all to die. Do you anomalies understand the weight of that? This...moment that will make or break me as you so said, Peacemaker, is a moment of extreme sadness filled with death. So why not just leave this old man be? After years of studying existence, I am about to change my status from a mere Channeler of Existence...to a Transcendent Channeler of Existence. Free from the influence of others, and capable of doing unfathomably more. After I attain that...I will just do my own thing. There will be no karma between us.\"","...!","His body gradually became rigid and stable as even while he was finishing his speech, Noah had already unwound a Tzar Versepiercer as it shone with a heartshaking allure.","And the Peacemaker...had already pulled back a bowstring as an arrow shimmering with multicolored brilliance of multiple Megalos buzzed!","\"You have lived, Ashmole. It is just time for you to die.\"","Noah's expression was calm as he released a Versepiercer.","And the Peacemaker gazed out coldly as he released his bowstring and supplemented.","\"For my peace, you have to fail, Ashmole.\"","...!","HUUUM!"]},{"number":3617,"title":"Chapter 3617: Chapter 3616 Glory I","paragraphs":["Bindings were unwound.","An arrow was released.","All of it went with a unique ebb and flow of the Wheel of Existence as someone like Noah who held a True Source was able to perceptively feel many more things compared to before.","Because of his True Source Atlas of Existence, he could control his own flow.","When he did dictate his flow, even if it was momentarily, the surrounding weavings of existence had momentarily turned chaotic as if an important piece of a puzzle was taken out of circulation!","A piece of a puzzle.","He never liked such an analogy of feelings like something that simply had a part to play in a grand scheme.","But this was how it could best be described as at this moment, while he released a single Tzar Versepiercer, his True Source Atlas of Existence pulsed as the heavy Wheel superimposing it spun once.","HUUM!","A single spin, but it turned everything around him black and white as his vision was able to see something else.","The Flow.","He saw everything as if it was a stretch of an endless sea of strings moving out with ancient ebbs and flows, and of those mixed inside this sea...he held a shockingly abundant rotation of a Flow around him.","A flow that shone gold in a sea of black and white.","When he made a move, he affected many things.","Then, there was the figure of the Peacemaker who was here and not here at the same time, presenting a Paradox as he saw a massive icy white blue flow around this being, even if it was lesser than his, and he then did not see it again!","...!","As for Ashmole...","His flow was chaotic, black and white as if it held no uniqueness, but it was rising and expanding rapidly. Tremendously!","BOOM!","Nine ancient wooden Wheels bloomed around Ashmole as he was made the target at the very center, while the thin strings of Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis flung out from all directions and still sought to infect!","At the same time, from the released bowstring of the Peacemaker, glacially cold Megalos Mountains bloomed as there were nine in number, each one releasing pulses of a heavy chill as these alone were capable of freezing Lesser Sources.","The glacial mountain spun with a heavy show of glory before they suck down like hammers to nail Ashmole!","\"You! Foul! Narcissists!\"","HUUM!","The Nine Pointed Star on Ashmole's chest spun heavily. His weavings radiated a tremendous eruption of power that almost seemed endless- a sense of undeniability erupting out as he withstood both of these attacks coming his way.","Nine wheels converged around his figure and exploded.","Nine Megalos Mountains thrust down to pierce and destroy for peace!","Space toiled and tumbled as strings of existence snapped, a heavy impact exploding out as even before the dust could settle, millions of parasitic strings shot into the point of the explosions.","SAA!","What was revealed was a mass of wriggling complexity with many faces, some frozen over and others burned but, nonetheless, still very much alive.","A Nine Pointed Star spun in the depths of this mass as Ashmole immediately erupted with black gold waves of undeniability that blocked off the lines of Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis once more.","His power began to recover as if his existence had nearly perished and instantly been rejuvenated at the same time!","His many faces were livid as he roared.","\"I can die, but I will live again!\"","WAA!","With brilliance, Noah gazed coldly at this Undeniable Telos Prime Source who had survived a Tzar Versepiercer as he was about to unwind three more status.","He was about to, when he saw the flow around Ashmole instantly explode in the world of black and white to be filled with a faint multicolored allure!","And Noah could read this flow.","He could read it as he was very surprised by it, his hands stopping from unwinding the other Tzar Versepiercers as he contemplated before putting them away!","And in the next moment, the roars of Ashmole could be heard while another nine glacial Megalos Mountains thundered with precision from the stone cold Peacemaker.","\"Do you know the biggest thing that I got from all the anomalies I have studied the existence of and taken from? A level of your narcissism. A level of what makes you all advance and succeed again and again! The random Epiphanies. The powering up in the middle of battle. Plans on top of plans and even more backup plans. Your flow...I have imitated it, and am perfecting it. What I wanted will not be perfect as this hurt me greatly to do, but I will tell you narcissists that as of this moment...no other Ashmoles exist across the weavings of the Wheel.\"","HUUM!","What he had to do was ensure that he either absorbed all parts of himself across frequencies, or that there were no other parts of himself across frequencies.","Noah looked at this being who seemed to have undertaken a heavy action, his flow that held no color before gaining rays of faint multicolored radiance and reaching levels it could not have possibly reached before as, at this moment, Noah was actually curious about the result!","He changed the course of killing and instead wanted to know if this was the same path that the Beyonder and others took- with them expanding their roles as Channelers to become True Channelers of the Wheel of Existence.","He looked at the flow of this being and the swirling brilliance it was gaining as Noah's True Source Atlas of Existence buzzed, releasing silent and invisible ebbs of flow known only to it.","Flows of the Atlas of Existence holding no relation to the Wheel of Existence!","Eldritch Expanse seemed to buzz with activity to silently mix in the Flow and infiltrate what was swirling around Ashmole- this Alchemist entirely focused on his ascension as he had no idea!","\"I shall be just like you all, overcoming adversity and coming out the other side...unfathomably glorious.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":3618,"title":"Chapter 3618: Chapter 3617 Glory II","paragraphs":["Glory.","Far too many sought it, and very few ever ended up achieving it.","But at this moment, after years of research and experimentation, an Alchemist became the only possible version of himself across countless frequencies of existence!","\"I feel it!\"","WAA!","He roared out as his weavings denied Megalos Mountains smashing into him, the eyes of the Peacemaker flashing dangerously as he became stern and seemingly was about to make a critical decision of whether to use more of his power here.","But before he did so, brilliance flashed in his eyes that stopped him.","As if he had received a feed of information from the depths of his being!","And his Bow lowered down slowly.","He looked at Ashmole, whose Undeniable Telos Prime Source looked like it was burning and undergoing a nirvanic procession, his complexity spilling out into a place it had never arrived at before as he laughed madly!","\"I FEEL IT!\"","BOOM!","Everything nearby shuddered a truly fantastical emergence of complexity bloomed, the visage of Ashmole being reconstructed as his source pulsed to radiate waves of complexity that could even make a Greater Source fall to their knees from the sheer pressure.","\"Ah...\"","A joyous shout rang out from Ashmole as his gaze was turned up, lustrous back hair and beard showing on his face as he gazed up as if there was something only he could see.","The Peacemaker could not see it in his current state.","But Noah, burning with a light of brilliance as he had already silently entrenched a great deal of unique flows into Ashmole that he had no idea about...he could see it.","A path that Ashmole followed.","A path shooting up and connecting towards an endlessly vast flow- the reason why Ashmole's own flow had gained color and size.","At this time, this path had been expanded tens of times compared to before, as what Ashmole could channel through it was many times grander!","This was...","\"A True Channeler...A True Channeler of Existence!\" Ashmole roared boisterously as golden tears ran down his face.","His complexity buzzed with heaviness as around him, the sense of impurity was suppressed so tremendously that he seemed a wholly new man.","On his chest, a clear black Nine Pointed Star shone as his whole demeanor gave off a feeling of immensity.","He turned towards Noah and gave a sidelong glance to the Peacemaker as he smiled, bright white teeth burning with brilliance showing as he bowed.","\"I thank you, the great contributors to my cause. None of you are used to failures if any, so this will be a good learning opportunity. I, Ashmole, stand before you now having exceeded the weavings of any common Source. Any common existence. I have become a True Channeler of Existence as already; I can feel a calling towards a place...a place where the Legends you all have only heard over the eons should be!\"","His whole existence seemed to be brimming with exuberance and complexity as after he bowed, his eyes flashed with a dangerous light.","His gaze became as he seemed about to shift his entire demeanor and begin talking about revenge, but at this time...Noah turned and shook his head with perplexity as he asked.","\"That's it?\"","WAA!","A simple question that caused Ashmole to frown.","\"Horrid narcissism until the very end. I shall start with you, Osmont. This time, I won't just ask for a drop of your blood. This time, I want it all.\"","...!","He dropped all pretenses and got ready to move as opposite him, Noah shook his head with disappointment and replied.","\"This...seems to not be the path that the Beyonder and others have taken, or maybe they have exceeded it. But either way, this about wraps up this little experimentation.\"","Utterly cold and dreadful words came from him as he began to float towards Ashmole.","He nodded to him as if letting him know he could give it a try.","\"Go on. Let me see your elevated complexity.\"","...!","Words of utter disregard echoed out coldly as, under the smiling eyes of Ashmole, rage began to seethe as he touched his chest.","\"I will not make it easy for you, Noah Osmont. I will...?\"","Ashmole stopped and looked down at his chest.","He was activating his weavings, but...why was nothing coming out?","\"What...?\"","His eyes shone dimly with perplexity as, in the next moment, he began to sway as he floated in the Expanse.","As if...he could not even control his body.","\"What is this?!\"","Confusion gave way to shock as his eyes looked up to see Noah's figure nearing him, coming to tower over him inches away as he looked down with eyes that Ashmole hated the most.","Eyes of control and majesty.","As if everything happening was solely under his calculations and control!","But this should not be.","He had exceeded himself. He had just become a True Channeler!","And yet...why could not sense any of the grandiosity he just had? Any of the tremendously wide channel he could course unlimited power through?! Why...did his unfathomably elevated Source seem so distant? As if did not even exist?!","Standing over him, Noah seemed like an insurmountable force of nature as he spoke out coldly while a tendril of white radiance unfolded from his palm.","\"Channeler or True Channeler...what difference does it make if you draw from the same True Source? All one has to do...is block your access to said Source.\"","HUUM!","Dreadful words that caused Ashmole to raise his head with incredulity rang out.","Block access to the True Source?","The Wheel of Existence itself?","That...","\"That is...impossible?\"","He seemed to question even his own words as his eyes shook with incredulity and a sense of despondency.","\"I did everything. I...I studied. I observed. Across cycles. Across Frequencies. All parameters, I...I...\"","His lips trembled as truly, no matter how much he reached out to his complex Source, he could not reach it!","What possible explanation could there be apart from what this monstrous creature had just said?","But that...should be impossible, right?","Ashmole gazed up towards Noah.","And as if Noah could read his thoughts of impossibility, he spoke out coldly.","\"In Existence, nothing is impossible.\"","WAA!","From his hand, the white tentacle shot out like a dagger, sinking into Ashmole's forehead as right after, his eyes became glazed with a black and white radiance!","A distance away, a Bow disappeared from the hands of the Peacemaker as he found his already transparent body began to fade away even more. His eyes buzzed with their own unique complexity as he looked up towards Ashmole, his gaze coming across the entity who had taken him down even after his feared success as such a being...was looking towards him with interest!"]},{"number":3619,"title":"Chapter 3619: Chapter 3618 Impossibilities! I","paragraphs":["The Peacemaker.","Noah gazed at such a being with a calculating expression as he placed Ashmole's dazed body beside him, the eyes of this old man shining with the black and white light of Eldritch Expanse as, at this moment, every single shred of his records, memories, and weavings were being analyzed.","Around them, golden strings of existence reformed as the white gold glow of the Expanse returned, calmness and serenity settling in as Noah spoke out nonchalantly.","\"Peacemaker...I believe I've heard of your weavings from Bob. You're here and not here as you must be another Ankyra, or at the very least someone with a heavy flow that Bob was forming connections with?\"","He spoke nonchalantly.","Yet his words had very clear intent as when he spoke about Bob, there was clear distaste and animosity towards him as he left no possibility of misunderstanding for the Peacemaker to look at him and question whether he was aligned with Bob.","Initially surprised by the direct mention, the Peacemaker was silent with contemplation before he nodded and replied. \"Osmont. I've heard this name a few times before, the first being from the Alchemist beside you in our first meeting. As for Bob, that creature is...something to be feared.\"","...!","\"Oh?\" Noah raised his brows as he looked at the figure of the Peacemaker that became more and more illusory.","And this being opposite him nodded as he touched the Nine Pointed Star on his chest while continuing.","\"He is not alive. His Source is dead. What he draws from is dead. He has nothing to live for, and yet he is moving with such activity and complexity in these Weavings of the Wheel. He is the first enemy I have run away from for the sake of my peace...forcing me to find a new home in another True Source entirely. Once I elevate my complexity a bit more, I will come back to eliminate him for my prolonged peace. But until then...\"","...!","His eyes held a heavy complexity as he did not have any hesitation for his actions!","And Noah thought about his words.","A being that was not alive.","He was dead. The True Source he pulled from was dead.","So naturally, why would he come to a place with a vast and mighty True Source?","The answers to be extrapolated were many as each one was more dreadful than the last.","Noah shook his head as he looked at the Peacemaker, who was about to entirely disappear.","He ran from Bob due to his power as at this moment, Noah also knew his complexity was still not enough for Bob.","He didn't run because he had certain layers of protection, but he still needed a high enough complexity that when he fought this being again, it would not be so one sided!","There was a lot to be done to prepare for everything as there were Nodes, Frequencies, and Wars to clear out.","But he would be ready.","He nodded towards the Peacemaker who was giving one last gaze to Ashmole.","\"This man was another thing that had me on edge, but my weavings tell me you have truly neutralized him as he shouldn't be an issue. Be careful of man. For a dead man, revival can be the only thing he seeks. But existence is balanced. Nothing dead can come back to life unless the life of another is taken in exchange. If he seeks to give life to a Dead True Source, then naturally, another True Source has to die...\"","Heavy words echoed out from the Peacemaker as his visage dissipated entirely, and yet the nearby weavings of existence held no change at all as if nothing had been there to begin with!","Noah looked at such a scene with sharp eyes as he tugged on Ashmole as if he were pulling along a dog.","\"What a unique existence...\"","This time had provided a great deal of things and success.","First, he could effectively say that the Prime Frequency of the End...only had his True Source Atlas of Existence as the source that all Entities within it could pull from!","Countless Channelers were all connected to his True Source.","Every time they channeled...","BZZT!","The wheel of his Atlas spun as it gushed out heavy waves of Complexity.","Pristine complexity that was all directed towards the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed!","And since Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis ensured every entity was a Channeler of his True Source, his other body utilized the Primal Flame of the Wheel to do exactly what Bob had done to the Frequency of Aqua.","Channeling to the Wheel of Existence was blocked off.","A simple action, but it was one that allowed him to easily incapacitate a True Channeler who had exceeded Undeniable Telos Prime Source complexity.","And now, this entire Prime Frequency of the End was secured as he had one more alteration to make to the Node of Existence of this Frequency.","That whatever changes were done to other Frequencies connected to the Wheel of Existence, this particular Frequency would remain unaffected!","This...was just the first time and layer of protection.","Noah would leave no stone unturned as he did this to ensure that whatever Bob was doing would not result in a catastrophe here, and in the meantime, the main thing he waited for...","BZZT!","Was complexity.","He smiled as he felt a certain Mundi within his Atlas buzzing with brilliance, the Wheel of the Atlas making another turn and giving a burst of complexity to the foremost Pathway as...","|The Pathway to the True Source of the Singed has crossed the critical threshold of the halfway point to the True Source.|","...!","Yes.","The Singed.","The Loot obtained from enemies. The Loot from Ruination and the Forge!","And now, the complexity that arose from the Wheel of the Atlas turning every second as countless entities Channeled through it!","From F-rank hunters in small worlds just coming in contact with mana and casting fireballs.","To Source Complexity Entities among the Watchers of the Wheelomachy that he was purging at this very moment to ensure this Frequency was clean!","From all of this, a road was more than half walked.","And the result of this...was indubitably glorious!"]},{"number":3620,"title":"Chapter 3620: Chapter 3619 Impossibilities! II","paragraphs":["A road was half walked as because of it...","|The Flames of the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed are able to purify and Sever all parts of your Existence up to the 54th Severing.|","...!","Yes.","All parts of his were capable of being severed 27 times through the Singed before.","And now...this was elevated to 54!","It would be a thorough elevation all around.","An increase in complexity that would be heavy!","|Embers of the True Source of the Singed converge around you in even greater complexity and concentration as at this moment, your Embers can singe other lifeforms and transform their weavings to more heavily revolve around your flow of existence. Their complexity will be transformed, and they gain a benefit from the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed.|","...!","More and more wonders came with his flames as the Flames of the Wheel of Existence could enact a Lineage of Singed. Now...so could he!","His own Singed of Existence.","He felt like there was much to be done as he pulled along the captures Ashmole, waves of memories surging into his mind regarding all the things across frequencies that this Alchemist did, as well as everything he knew.","As he did this, the Source of the Eldritch Expanse within him buzzed as it affirmed that Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis had spread out across the expanse, altering the channeling of the True Source of all entities it came across while those deemed enemies were currently in the same state as Ashmole!","After he finished draining out all the weavings of this Alchemist, he planned to let his vibrant complexity fall under the allure of the Pathway to the True Source of Loot. All would occur in due time.","But as he moved, he already gave the command.","\"Begin the elevation of all True Severed Weavings towards the 54th Severing.\"","WAA!","His Atlas pulsed as a Mundi within it burned furiously.","Thereafter, fiery tendrils of white gold flames began to spread out all across his weavings of existence as burning Embers crackled, a heavy light of purification spreading out!","All weavings that had not attained their Final Severed State and opened up their pathway were about to become ever closer as everything would be purified upwards!","His Eyes.","His Wings.","The main concepts under the banner of the Conceptual System of Existence.","Uncertainty. Relativity. Continuity.","Even the very Ordinance of Existence itself that Noah was expectant of.","Existence.","If it could attain a Final Severed State and open up a Pathway to the True Source of Existence...just what would the end result be? He thought of many things and moved with a great deal of possibilities as at this moment, he felt like a hurried farmer who had to move to tend to many crops!","As flames furiously burned and elevated many things across his weavings, his other bodies continued to move.","In the junction where three Megalos met.","Ozymandias stepped out countless black and white tentacles that stretched out across the Frequency as he gazed towards the Great Mother and others who had returned to their own cognizance.","They looked towards him in shock as they could sense something was different, but they did not know exactly what!","Ozymandias looked at them as white gold flames began to burn over his hand.","\"You closely followed the legend and weavings of the Beyonder as initially, I did not deny them. But now, only my weavings remain prevalent as I ask...do you wish to fully come under my banner?\"","A grandiose question.","One that the Great Mother's tentacles vibrated with fervor as she was the first to bend down!","\"For the Protagonist!\"","WAA!","For the Protagonist, she said.","Others who already saw the terrifying power he portrayed thought about the Great Beyonder and all the things promised for the Megalos Beyond that were still unfolding as one by one...they all bent their wills towards Ozymandias!","Not the Instrument.","Not the Inheritor of the Megalos.","But Ozymandias!","In the seas of stellar black waves of radiance, Ozymandias nodded gloriously.","\"Very well.\"","HUUM!","Flames burned furiously around his body as, at this moment, they began to wash out like cleansing flames of purification all around him- their range extending outwards as its goal was to eventually cover all of Megalos Beyond.","Ozymandias looked at this with a sense of majesty as he proclaimed.","\"From this day forth, the Outerversal Morphons of the Megalos Beyond shall become the Singed of the True Severed Origin Osmontian!\"","WAA!","A heavy proclamation of change.","Change that would cover all of Megalos Beyond!","They began by toughing the infinity symbol of tentacles that was the Great Mother, her stellar black appearance trembling as her complexity exploded upwards, bands of white and gold appearing around her!","It was an advent of fantastical changes.","And as such, changes occurred here.","Far from this location, in the distant Frequency of Aqua affected by Bob, another one of Noah's bodies stood beside the Queen of Matter as he called out loudly.","\"Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis.\"","He called out lightly as around him, millions of thin white and black lines exploded, and they caused the Queen of Matter to yelp as she moved away while looking towards him in shock.","\"Sir Osmont...you're a fan of tentacles too? Just what are you doing right now? I'm getting different musings from the state of matter as even they can barely make heads or tails of what is going on...\"","His number one fan asked such a question as Noah watched the millions of thin black and white tentacles explode into billions as they turned invisible and stretched out across the Frequency of Aqua.","The blue waters around him gave him a sense of peace and serenity as he replied slowly.","\"I am patching up all the areas that an entity with a Dead True Source is destroying. In the coming days...I will face him once again as, at that time, I do not know how many frequencies will have been affected and what all of this will boil down to. But as always...the answer is complexity. If there is a sufficient amount of complexity...even the strongest enemies can be extinguished with but a thought.\"","WAA!","As he said such words, he knew them to be true as did he not just defeat an Alchemist that had become a True Channeler by utilizing things the Alchemist didn't even think of!?","In all of existence, so long as the complexity was right....anything was possible.","He said such words simply, but the Queen of Matter who heard them nodded religiously before she began to write them down!"]},{"number":3621,"title":"Chapter 3621: Chapter 3620 Impossibilities! III","paragraphs":["In the grand weavings of existence, so long as one's complexity was enough...there were no impossibilities.","Noah knew this firsthand as while his existence continued scaling upwards at a rapid pace, he conducted multiple heavy actions simultaneously.","The forging of the Eldritch Expanse Source of Existence made way for the rapid spread of the usage of his True Source Atlas of Existence- where he started off with the Prime Frequency of the End and now continued with the Frequency of Aqua where Bob had altered the Node of Existence of.","Since he stopped the Channelers of this Frequency from accessing the Wheel of Existence, Noah would grant them another True Source to channel from, as this would be done without any additional changes to the Node of Existence!","He stared at the endless expanse of blue, his pupils reflecting its brilliance as at this moment, even he could not say where everything would go.","Against the foe that was Bob, entities with heavy flows of the Wheel, like the Peacemaker he had just met, were forced to temporarily leave due to the sheer complexity of this being.","He did not know how everything would unfold, but he would make sure that he would not fail.","He could not fail.","The lives of too many lay on his shoulders for him to fail!","When he thought of the countless entities entangled with him, he turned towards the figure of the Queen of Matter beside him as he spoke out while tapping with a single finger in front.","PAH!","A single tap, and yet a radiant blue portal leading into a location within an entirely different Frequency bloomed.","\"Someone would like to meet you to utilize your Source in other ways.\"","...!","He spoke calmly towards the girl surrounded by books as she pointed to herself and became stern, her eyes trying to peer into the portal to see what lay on the other side as she asked nervously.","\"I've met the great Ruination, I've been with you, there isn't anybody as grand as....!\"","Her eyes opened wide as she thought of something.","The only other wonder of Noah's that she had yet to meet.","Her face changed drastically as radiant waves of white and gold began to pulse around her as she asked in shock.","\"You can't mean...no way! Apart from you and Ruination, the third and only one can only be the Spirit of Spiritual Land! The Infiniverse Dowager! Is it? Is it really?!\"","Her entire weavings of existence buzzed with activity as Noah grabbed her neck as if he were grabbing a cat, flinging her into the portal before she could speak any more nonsense as yes, the Infiniverse Megalos Body had asked for the entity with the Source of Fabled Matter who could spy on and gain knowledge of anything relevant happening in the state of matter across Frequencies.","If such a capability could be applied not just for Matter, but also Anti-Matter and Dark Matter...what secrets would there be across Frequencies for them?","Such weavings became set in stone as while this occurred, Noah was also about to take another major action after he continued reading the countless memories of Ashmole that spanned across Frequencies.","A True Channeler.","Someone that had made a jump past Prime Source Complexity as after Noah was done with him, the only thing he would be was loot.","But his weavings led Noah to think of those who truly had attained a terrifying level of power that Ashmole looked up to!","He thought of the Emelline who called herself and other Singed more than just Channelers. That they were Conduits of the wheel that acted like macrophages of an immune system.","She had also called the Origin Singed a True Conduit who was unfathomably close to the Wheel of Existence itself.","Noah wondered about that being and others as at this moment, he moved to get answers.","Answers from a source that he had actually already ensnared!","Far from any set weavings of existence, far from any Frequency.","In a field of sandy gold mountains and clouds within an Amarantos Dream.","The figure of Azzurra sat atop a cloudy mountain peak as she played with the stellar sand below her in the form of a white gold gold-furred cat.","She used to be a black cat, and yet her captor using her as a spy had altered her source so much that she felt like another person entirely!","He let her be since then as she remained within this dream, and she couldn't help but pace around the golden sand below her paws as she thought of how everything would end.","\"It could all end with a very positive result you know?\"","...!","She was startled to alert as the voice of Noah echoed out alongside his appearance, his figure looking towards her calmly as she hissed while jumping away just like any cat!","Noah gazed at her up and down calmly as he came to float above her, his voice heavy and filled with power as he spoke.","\"I had to confirm from a True Channeler, but you seem to also be known as Azzurra, the Lost Avatar of the Beyonder. Do you know of your own identity or did your main body lock everything away?\"","...!","His words left no space for rebuttal or discussion as when she heard them, Azzurra became stern as she shook her head.","\"What are you talking about? I am myself- you have probed my Source as you should know there is nothing there but me...\"","Azzurra spoke stiffly but seriously, and yet Noah remained towering over her as from his chest, a heavy wheel spun as a terrifying black and white tentacle was released- instantly shooting out like a whip to smash toward Azzurra's forehead as his voice rang out!","\"Let us see if she has entirely abandoned a part of her, or if I can entirely alter and take away the very Will of a part of the Beyonder!\"","WAA!"]},{"number":3622,"title":"Chapter 3622: Chapter 3621 Impossibilities! IV","paragraphs":["He was past asking nicely, and there were no more moves to be made apart from this as Absolute Unidemic Existence Pathogenesis struck out towards the Lost Avatar of the Beyonder, smashing onto her forehead as her cat-like eyes rapidly began to turn black and white!","Her Records.","Her Weavings.","All of her existence would be under Noah's fingertips soon unless...","BZZT!","An utterly horrific complexity instantly bloomed from the small cat-like body of Azzurra, Noah's black and white tentacle snapping off her forehead while his body received a heavy impact that flung him back across multiple sandy gold cloud mountains!","BOOM!","He smashed onto the ninth mountain and came to a stop, his eyes sharp as he looked ahead to see a cat floating in the air while looking around with a sense of confusion and ancientness.","The eyes of this cat eventually came to focus on Noah as they flashed with a deadly sharpness!","Noah looked back at her without so much as an ounce of fear as he dusted off sand and remnants of clouds as he asked.","\"Am I talking to the Great Beyonder? In the flesh?\"","...!","He asked calmly.","And yet, in the next instant, the sandy gold mountains and clouds in this Amarantos Dream became tinged with stellar obsidian radiance- the whole landscape changing as a certain cat also transformed into the figure of a dazzling woman with black and gold robes draping over her.","Her hair shone with dazzling black and gold strands as her eyes...carried an unfathomably luminous light of existence.","\"You try to alter everything about me within Dreams? My very own sandbox?\"","Her voice carried tremendous undeniability and power as she appeared right before Noah, clouds of stellar obsidian gold gathering below her as she sat down, her arms hanging on her knees as in front of her- stellar black chains rose to pull Noah down in place!","She looked down akin to a queen staring at someone lesser, trillions of small Runes of Amarantos exploding around her as every landscape of this dream seemed to fall under her control!","Noah gazed at the chains binding him as well as the horrific complexity he felt above, and he found himself affirming that this...felt genuine.","This was nothing like Ashmole as his heart felt more at ease that even a trace of someone like the Beyonder could be this powerful!","He was fearful of meeting these old legends and being disappointed at the complexity they held as so far...it did not seem like this would be the case.","\"I know you...\"","Sitting there coldly with regality and power, the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder squinted her eyes while she looked at Noah.","\"One of the kids who took my Inheritance. Have you grown up so much to try and alter the very Primeval Source of a remnant I left behind? While knowing who it was? Do you even know how much it is costing me, you, and the countless others under the Weavings of the Wheel for me to awaken even this trace Will here?\"","...!","Bound by obsidian chains, Noah looked up at the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder as from his chest...","HUUM!","A Wheel turned.","A True Source burned.","And the chains binding him began to burn and fall down like paper as his figure became unbound!","Sandy gold clouds gathered around him and elevated his figure until he was leveled with the Great Beyonder, his arms also freely hanging atop his knees as he looked at her calmly.","\"Spare me any sophistry and riddles if you can. There is a creature with a Dead Source running freely across the weavings of the Wheel. Where are you? Where are those like you?\"","...!","His words were straight to the point as the Trace of the Great Beyonder frowned, looking at him up and down as she asked.","\"The small half dead rat that slipped in all those years ago still has not been taken care of? Even with all the measures we left behind?\"","Her frowning eyes were filled with a trace of disappointment as she looked around, her body releasing trillions of Runes of Amarantos outwards as she closed her eyes!","Noah looked at such a being as he shook his head while continuing to ask.","\"Where did you all go? Why is it that you cannot even send a simple trace of your power back into the weavings of the Wheel to potentially take care of something like this?\"","He had many clones. He could move around freely.","These truly powerful entities who were supposedly protecting the Wheel from harm that he and others could not fathom were not able to even send a small part of themselves to ensure things were not destroyed from within.","As he asked this, the eyes of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder opened and looked at him coldly before she replied.","\"You forcing me to appear here by itself will come at a heavy cost to my Weavings out there. I need every shred of myself just to survive. Every last shred...for all these past years.\"","WAA!","She spoke with deadly seriousness as even while Noah heard such words, he still shook his head and asked with a frown!","\"Illuminate things for me. The more I know, the more I can help. No riddles or words of obscurity. Just what is going on?\"","He wanted her to speak clearly and without any confusion.","And as if she had a limited amount of time, she looked at her fair hands and spoke out coldly.","\"A True Source of Existence...a Wheel of Existence capable of supporting countless frequencies and lifeforms is rare. Very, very rare. Existence...is never so easy. Nor is it so simple to have. Out there, there are countless Dead True Sources as finding a True Source Wheel of Existence that is alive and well is unfathomable. We hold such a type of True Source. So because of this...we face an onslaught of countless Existences with dead sources seeking something. Constantly. Daily. Hourly. With every shred of what we have. The moment they notice even a small gap of concentration, they will attack it to get through as my True Weavings have just been placed in another perilous war because you forced a trace of me to appear here.\"","...!"]},{"number":3623,"title":"Chapter 3623: Chapter 3622 Impossibilities! V","paragraphs":["He put her True Weavings in peril just by forcing a trace of her to come here!","Out there there were countless Dead True Sources!","Noah listened to such words as his expression flashed with a profound level of coldness.","Existence was not easy.","Weavings of Existence seemed like they were not truly all that easy to have and stabilize!","The Wheel of Existence was actually something of a rarity as outside of it, waves of countless other existences sought to enter it.","As for the reason why?","Noah was silent in contemplation, as he asked calmly.","\"How long before the weavings of existence of someone with a Dead True Source collapse?\"","A question he asked after some contemplation as opposite him, the figure of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder looked towards him with a knowing gaze.","\"At least you are not too stupid. Yes, the reason why so many existences throw themselves towards our Wheel of Existence is because their time is limited. With a Dead True Source, unless they have attained a tremendous level of complexity where they can live without the need of an outside True Source, their weavings of Existence will surely collapse. It is only a matter of time, and this time could be a hundred years, a thousand years, or even a million years, depending on their complexities.\"","...!","Death.","As always, it came down to the complete cessation of life.","\"And no, we cannot just simply allow them in or even form a process where we tell them that if they do not fight and have conflict, they can simply connect to our Wheel of Existence. Those whose complexities that are bathed with the light of a Dead True Source carry this like an infected aura around them. At the moment they connect to our Wheel of Existence, they will begin setting it on a path of no return as the more entities that connect to it, the more that they lead it to become another Dead True Source. Thus, we fought. We have been fighting. For cycles. For eons. To the point that some...grew despairing at this endless fight as they asked themselves whether they would do this for the rest of their lives. Either until they perished, or their complexities were dried enough and they simply collapsed. So some...have left.\"","...!","Heavy words echoed from her long monologue as around her, the obsidian mountain of dreams she sat on seemed desolate!","After such long periods of time filled with endless battles, some left.","\"The Dead Channelers keep coming. As if out there, in any nearby Weavings of Existence, only our Wheel is present. It has been endless. So...so...endless...\"","Noah's eyes became stern as he listened to the words of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder, her facial expression and eyes portraying a sense of tiredness as if she would soon join the throngs of beings who grew tired and left.","And he looked at her like this freely as she was quickly able to notice his piercing gaze, and she harrumphed!","\"Hmph, I am not so weak minded as those fools who left, so you can drop your judgmental gaze. You...\"","She looked at him closely and then closed her eyes as if she was looking for something else.","\"Entities like you should have been able to gain access to some safeguards we left behind in case of emergencies. My Crucibles, My Instrument...you fucking destroyed it, did you not?\"","WAA!","She opened her eyes to look at him with an accusatory gaze as Noah simply shrugged his shoulders!","\"An enemy came for me, and I simply retaliated. There were waves of causality here and there but for the most part, that was it.\"","He did not have a shred of doubt about his previous actions as the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder snorted out before she uttered a rebuttal.","\"Whatever it may be, we cannot leave that place. We cannot leave the Infinite Ravines. Even a Trace Will like this...\"","The Great Beyonder raised her hands and looked at the body of Azzurra as she shook her head.","\"A Dead True Source?\"","\"This alone has allowed a tricky Dead Channeler to feel the slightest changes to my weavings as they have launched another assault at the position I protect. I knew I could handle it, which is why I spared this Trace Will, but I cannot stay here too long or do much. Even this conversation cannot be a useless one! So, since you destroyed the safeguards I left behind, you have to be the one to take care of things in their place. The Dead Thing walking around within the Wheel should just be that infinitesimally small thread of a Dead True Source that passed by me and the Stellar Weaver.\"","WAA!","Noah's eyes flashed sharply.","\"A Dead True Source?\"","He heard something heavy as he had to ask!","A Dead True Source!","The Trace Will of the Great Beyonder had her immeasurably deep eyes focus on him as he asked, and she replied coldly.","\"There are different True Sources out there. A True Source, regardless of the type, could theoretically survive even without a Wheel of Existence. But the Wheel of Existence is an unfathomably vast Absolute Complex True Source. Any True Source the rest of us could theoretically obtain will be a simple Existential True Source. A Source born from a concept or weaving of existence. I...have attained my True Source after guidance from the Wheel of Existence. Since you question me here so cluelessly, it means that even with your complexity, you have yet to enter...the True Frequencies of Existence that are isolated from all other frequencies of the Wheel.\"","...!","The Trace Will of the Great Beyonder revealed information that for the first time...allowed Noah to smile!","\"Haha!\" He did not just smile, he even laughed as the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder looked towards him as if he had gone mad.","\"Did my words break you, Noah Osmont?\"","The Trace Will of the Great Beyonder asked coldly!"]},{"number":3624,"title":"Chapter 3624: Chapter 3623 Impossibilities! VI","paragraphs":["He smiled and laughed freely at the words of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder as this whole time, part of him expected tremendous disappointment from the legends whose names were mentioned across eons.","The Great Beyonder. The Omnifather. The Stellar Weaver!","They and other unknown entities were mentioned in hushed whispers as when it came to the possible power they could hold, Noah reserved his expectations after what he observed Ashmole doing.","The Advancement of the Wandering Alchemist was not one that showed him a truly deep complexity even as he stated he was going towards a place that those similar to the Great Beyonder had arrived at.","But at this moment, the Great Beyonder stated that she and others had attained their True Source!","He felt happiness at this as he also felt like...he was no longer alone.","In Existence, he was not alone in attaining a True Source.","Well, he still was an exception as he would not just have a single True Source of Existence!","Facing the perplexed gaze of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder, Noah shook his head and looked towards her with an interested smile.","\"I was just happy that I would not be disappointed by the complexities that came before me. You were talking about True Sources?\"","There were different True Sources.","Ones that were far too profound and complex like that of the Wheel of Existence, and then there were Existential True Sources that entities could obtain.","The Great Beyonder attained her True Source a long time ago as she mentioned True Frequencies of Existence.","She looked towards him with a cold gaze as she continued.","\"There isn't much time to waste. If that Dead Thing has recovered even a bit of its complexity, it will try to brute force its way into the True Frequencies of the Wheel. Even if it taints Common Frequencies and Prime Frequencies of the Wheel, it would still not be able to do much...\"","She was speaking thoughtfully when right after, Noah stopped her as he spoke out.","\"Oh, that so called Dead Thing has already obtained the Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence from Hell Terra Firma.\"","\"...\"","The Trace Will of the Great Beyonder blinked as her eyes became sharp.","\"What?\" She asked as if she wanted to make sure she heard correctly.","BZZT!","Her figure then rose up with a sense of anger on her face as she looked towards Noah with even greater coldness, and he continued calmly once more.","\"I'll rephrase that- he has obtained less than half of the Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence from Hell Terra Firma. He is currently going around sealing the connection of Channelers to the Wheel of Existence across different Frequencies.\"","...!","He gave more information regarding what was happening as the hands of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder clenched, and she took deep breaths as her blessed chest heaved up and down.","She then closed her eyes and enunciated each of her words clearly as if she was almost at the absolute end of her patience.","\"Where...is the remaining portion of the Primal Flame of the Wheel?\"","Her stellar waves of dark hair pulsed.","Her fair skin shone with resplendent as Dark Matter was vibrant around her.","A unique sense of beauty surrounded her as Noah looked at her with a silent smile while he replied. \"I hold the remaining part of the Primal Flame of the Wheel. Safely tucked away in a place he cannot reach.\"","\"...!\"","Her eyes flashed sharply as the gaze she gave him gradually changed.","It still maintained its coldness as she uttered out through her teeth.","\"The Primal Flame of the Wheel is one of the keys one could use to enter the True Frequencies of Existence. Within, the Dead Thing would have gained true access to the Wheel of Existence to do as he saw fit. If the Dead Thing is shutting off the connection of Frequencies to their existence, then he should be seeking to lower the influence of Existences across the Wheel just enough to perceive where any of the myriad True Frequencies are, and he would then gain access. This is the most roundabout way he could use, though, as I'm curious why he didn't just destroy multiple Frequencies easily...\"","...!","Her gaze was contemplative.","Opposite her, Noah waved his hands as he thought of Bob and spoke out.","\"That so called Dead Thing is a sentimental and emotional one. They have said that they apparently care for the many lifeforms out there.\"","He spoke words even he found laughable as the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder became stern as she shook her head.","\"Do not even speak to Dead Existences. Those with Dead True Sources can taint you. Alter Existence in ways you cannot fathom. Even their words are poisonous and filled with deception as some can have their own discrepancies, but they are all ultimately the same. As for you...since you hold the Primal Flame of the Wheel and destroyed the safeguards I personally put in place, you will have to be the one who stops this Dead Thing. I will also relay words to others to see if any of their safeguards are active or capable of being activated. But you...you need to enter a True Frequency of Existence. You need to follow the Flow and attain your True Source. Only a True Source can eradicate a Dead True Source.\"","WAA!","Only a True Source could eradicate a Dead True Source.","The Trace Will of the Great Beyonder stated such words with absolute confidence as Noah maintained his composure.","He...already had the True Source Atlas of Existence.","And he was already halfway to attaining another True Source.","And there were many more on the way!","But he didn't say any of this.","He looked towards the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder with interest as she looked back at him with a sigh before she continued, her finger tapping out and releasing a bundle of light.","\"You could potentially use the Primal Flame of the Wheel if you hold the more significant portion to access True Frequencies. Or you can use the Singed as another Key. I know there was a child by the name of Ezekiel? He should know the method all the Singed could enact to open a pathway to the True Frequency of the Singed. There, you could find a viable Existential True Source to establish at the core of your existence, and the resources to nurture it. Do this, and we will continue our defenses in the Infinite Ravines...\"","...!"]},{"number":3625,"title":"Chapter 3625: Chapter 3624 Sources! I","paragraphs":["She spoke and came up with a plan so easily.","She mentioned the name Ezekiel as she said this Singed knew the methodology left behind in order to open the True Frequency of the Singed!","But...","\" Ezekiel has already had his Embers of the flames returned to the Wheel...\"","No one spoke with a straight face as he told Trace Will of the Great Beyonder that Ezekiel had long been dead!","\"...\"","The face of the dark-haired woman paused slightly at such words while Noah continued.","\"His weavings were among the first collapsed by the so called dead thing, that is Bob. At this moment, the Singed are led by Emelline of the First Flame.\"","...!","Emelline.","He just mentioned her name and nothing else as the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder closed her eyes thoughtfully with a silent sigh before she opened them and continued.","\"Even she should still know the methodology left behind for the Singed. Connect with them and see if you can get through to the True Frequency of the Singed. As for the Dead Thing...Bob, you said?\"","Bob.","The name became amplified and scrutinized in her eyes as she held her chin thoughtfully as if she were trying to remember something critical. \"Bob...there were whispers of this name many, many years ago among the Dead Things that we were fighting. Some...were cautious and fearful of this name alone...\"","WAA!","She pulled from the last vestiges of her memory as she uttered such words and caused the atmosphere to become even over here.","Around them, the weavings of the Amarantos Dream pulsed with a heavy ebb and flow as Noah gave a light nod.","\"As much as I would like to discredit the Dead Thing that you call Bob, he is a creature with a unique level of complexity who seems like he will make things a tad bit difficult for us. I never give compliments to my enemies, but this one...has caused me a bit of a headache...\"","...!","The Patience.","The schemes.","The lack of rambling about his grand plans like a psychopath!","None of it fit the mold of the many enemies he had come across in the past as he had to make a new mold for this being.","The Trace Will of the Great Beyonder shook her head eventually as she replied.","\"I will ask around more regarding this to make sure that I did not miss anything. In the meantime, do what you can to locate and enter a True Frequency of Existence. I will leave behind scattered weavings of myself within this Avatar as a trace of my cognizance should still remain, and if I need to return, I will.\"","This Great Entity made plans to leave already as Noah remained seated while asking in a low tone.","\"The Infinite Ravines where you all are fighting...where are they located?\"","...!","He wanted more direct answers without leaving too many mysteries behind as when he asked, the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder looked at him coldly and only answered a moment later.","\"When a True Source has grown complex enough to be capable of living independently from the Wheel of Existence, it will be capable of following a pull towards an exit point filled with endless weavings. The only place to go in and out of the influence of the Absolute Complex True Source. Easiest to reach them through a True Frequency of Existence. The Infinite Ravines. Without a sufficient enough complexity, you will not be able to make a trek there. As for you...\"","She looked at him closely before shaking her head.","\"You're still a ways off, so keep at it.\"","WAA!","She truly said he was still ways off!","He smiled calmly while the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder clasped her hands together, millions of Amarantos Runes returning to her as her eyes lit up with a dark light of brilliance, and she shook her head right after.","\"I had spread out my weavings across nearby frequencies to see if I could locate this Dead Thing myself, but I have come back with nothing and I cannot stay here any longer than I need to. They have already begun their assault in the region I protect and with much grander intensity. All of this...\"","She spread her hands out within this Amarantos Dream as she looked towards Noah.","\"All of this is existence. It's ups and downs. It's good and bad. Sometimes it is fair; sometimes, it is unfair. All of it is still existence. I don't know what your motivation is for doing all the things that you have done so far, but...\"","Her stellar black eyes filled with countless Runes locked with his.","\"Keep at it. Don't be like those who gave everything up in the end. Don't let up. There won't be some grand reward waiting for you on the other side. There won't be groups of people waiting to congratulate you. It will feel like thankless work as you even ask yourself what you're doing everything for...\"","She had been talking to him as if she was giving a speech to tell him not to give up, but halfway through it, Noah could see she became half here and half not as the same words she was giving him...felt like they were for her!","\"...\"","How many years had she been fighting? At a certain point, did all these great beings start to question and grow tired?","Noah sighed internally as he knew there had to be a more permanent solution than this, and he rose from his pulsing mountain peak as he looked at the complex weavings of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder, and his deep voice echoed out.","\"At the end of the day, we continue to protect the weavings of Existence, yes? There won't be others to recognize or congratulate on the work, but we all have each other. I'll be the first to congratulate and acknowledge you, the Great Beyonder, for all that you have done for the Wheel. Your contributions mattered and saved many for countless cycles, and they will save even more for the years to come.:","...!","In front of him.","The pupils of the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder shook!"]},{"number":3626,"title":"Chapter 3626: Chapter 3625 Sources! II","paragraphs":["Her pupils shook as if she had received a great shock!","She turned silent thereafter and closed her eyes, and when she opened them again, all emotions had been swept away as she looked towards Noah.","She couldn't bring herself to say anything substantial as she could only sigh, brilliance beginning to leave her as the weavings of her Avatar returned.","\"In an Amarantos Dream, it is somewhat easier. Somewhat manageable as it is an existence between false and real, and it does not take away too much from my weavings. A bit of myself will be left here as if you come across too much trouble, or even the Dead Thing is discovered; tell me.\"","As she said these words, the terrifying brilliance in her eyes entirely faded in the next moment as the surroundings of the dream began to return to their golden sandy brilliance.","The weavings of Azzurra returned...somewhat as she blinked and looked around, eventually settling on Noah in a daze as she voiced out.","\"I am...not me...\"","The Lost Avatar of the Beyonder.","She remembered everything as in the back of her mind, the presence of her true self blinked. It was still there as it could be pulled upon at any time to come back.","How did it even feel to live for eons and knowing your identity was one thing, only for all of this to change as you realized that you had an entirely different life?","Noah shook his head at this and patted the shoulder of Azzurra before his figure fell back onto vibrant golden clouds of this Dream, thinking about everything that had to be done as his figure floated serenely in this dream.","A distance away, there was a woman who continued to have a miniature Existential crisis!","—","Towards entirely unique weavings of existence.","Inside the Infiniverse Megalos.","\"No. Fucking. Way!\"","The figure of the Queen of Matter looked at the terrifyingly massive Infiniverse Vein in the form of an infinity Symbol, and the many Pantheonic Megalos Havens surrounding it as...","\"How can a tiny Spiritual Land from a Beast World do this? How?!\"","The Queen of Matter almost pulled her hair out as she could not believe the weavings of this place.","Everything was currently shaking and vibrating with a terrifying ebb and flow as all the things she looked at...seemed to be expanding and growing larger.","She also sensed Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter swirling together as every time they clashed, even more explosive waves of growth occurred!","\"What is even happening...\" The Queen of Matter was utterly dazed as she asked this, and in the next moment.","\"The Infiniverse Megalos is undergoing the fastest period of growth it has ever gone through. Within this day, its density and complexity of Existence will surpass the Megalos Ynnere of this Prime Frequency of the End, and it will soon grow larger and more complex than all three Megalos and the Expanse combined as at that time, its complexity would rival a Frequency.\"","...!","The body of the Queen of Matter trembled as she looked to her left.","There, the figure of the Infiniverse Megalos Body appeared grandly, a stellar white dress donned on her visage as her being shone with multicolored radiance.","\"Ah...\"","The Queen of Matter fell to her knees as she floated to be right before the Infiniverse Megalos Body, her hands reaching out hesitantly as if she was before someone sacred!","\"I have...I have dreamed of you. I have been obsessed with you. The impossibility of your very existence...ah!\"","The books around the Queen of Matter trembled as she barely managed to utter such words, the Infiniverse Megalos Body smiling as she looked out into the constantly expanding weavings of complexity and existence.","The incorporation of Anti-Matter caused the exponential growth to kick an even higher gear, but it was not alone.","The expansion of the Severed Weavings of Manadynamics, Relativity, Dreams, Genesis, Avalon, Polarity...and the countless pillars that made a core part of its beings heavily contributed to the growth of the Infiniverse Megalos.","The more these weavings became Severed, the more they opened their Pathways towards their True Sources....the growth of the Infiniverse Megalos would explode even further as at this stage of its existence, it did not need to do what it did in its earlier stages.","Before, it had to devour the worlds, galaxies, Cosmos, and countless other weavings of its surroundings in order to become bigger and bigger.","Now, it did not need to devour Omniverse X-999 or the Megalos Ynnere or anything else in order to become more complex!","Its weavings- the weavings that Noah expanded, were leading it towards a path of self sufficiency and reliability as it did not need outside input for growth.","What it needed was itself.","And now...the Infiniverse Megalos looked towards the kneeling Queen of Matter as she voiced out calmly.","\"Your Source interests me. I wish to freely observe the pertinent weavings of Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter across the Frequencies of the Wheel as I wish to study you and your source. It might be a bit invasive as-...!\"","The figure of the Queen of Matter rose up while ripping her dress right off, her figure being revealed as she voiced out with an extremely serious expression!","\"Dissect me as much as you wish, Ma'am!\"","The Infiniverse Megalos Body looked at the valiant figure of the Queen of Matter as she nodded while keeping her words to herself.","She wondered why the most unique existences out there seemed to also be the most eccentric ones.","Did complexity slowly alter their minds and make them just a little bit crazy?","She had this thought as she beckoned towards the figure of the Queen of Matter, waves of light wrapping around them as they disappeared!","Quite a distance away from here, in the Megalos Ynnere.","\"Haa...\"","A flushed Mysara donned her clothes as her body radiated the terrifying, undeniable pressure of a Prime Source at this moment.","Similar to the Queen of Matter, the Source she Channeled to was changed as she also underwent the additional weaving of Dual Cultivation on the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed, her weavings gaining a quality of an Undeniable Telos Source as her power was currently exuberant!","Near her, Noah was already adorned in a white gold Emperor's Robe as he looked towards a certain direction while voicing out.","\"Let's go join your Main Body in the Prime Frequency of Flames. Wars and passageways to True Frequencies seem to go hand in hand...\"","...!"]},{"number":3627,"title":"Chapter 3627: Chapter 3626 Sources! III","paragraphs":["Wars and Passageways.","Noah uttered these words seamlessly as in the next instant, he tugged on the True Source Atlas of Existence, causing the distinct absence of Channeling from any outside source to manifest once more.","He could clearly sense where Emelline of the First Flame was, and his weavings honed in on their entanglement. His intention was simple, to transition from his current Frequency onto the Prime Frequency of Flames.","As this thought crossed his mind, the authority of the Administrator of the True Source Atlas of Existence pulsed. It was as if countless authorities had been activated simultaneously, and multicolored radiance enveloped both him and Mysara, swirling around them like a cocoon of brilliance.","BOOM!","And in the blink of an eye, they vanished.","—","In the Prime Frequency of Life.","A vast expanse lay decimated, obsidian radiance flowing across the Megalos that stretched into the void. Yet, despite the vibrant weavings that filled this place, the allure of the weavings present was...","Dead!","The more Giuseppe became acquainted with these weavings, the more he realized that the Weavings of Existence he had aligned himself with exuded the distinct essence of death- an undeniable divergence from the life they were originally meant to represent.","But under the Wheel of Existence, Giuseppe would have never achieved anything of this magnitude.","He understood his limitations.","Unlike great beings like the Omnifather or the Great Beyonder, his complexity was not sufficient to surpass his old weavings and obtain a True Source.","Yet, under the guidance of that Entity...","A True Source was guaranteed.","Giuseppe floated in a field of black radiance when suddenly, his consciousness wavered.","His vision twisted and distorted.","And an instant later, he found himself standing amidst a vast black and white sea, a stellar ocean that stretched endlessly both above and below him.","Above and below the identical stellar seas of black and white, there were swirling intricate black and white Wheels of Existence that rotated silently across the expanse.","Dead Wheels of Existence.","Giuseppe's expression grew solemn as he witnessed this eerie scene.","And then, in the next moment...","BOOM!","His existence shuddered.","A terrifying aura flooded the surroundings as the one who had summoned him made their presence known.","The Despondent One.","Giuseppe didn't need to see him to know who had called him here.","This was an entity whose authority was undeniable, whose weavings were far too complex for Giuseppe to ever comprehend.","Without turning around, Giuseppe bent his knees and bowed deeply, lowering his head in reverence.","\"I recognize the Despondent One...how may I serve you?\"","His voice echoed across the silent expanse.","The Despondent One.","Giuseppe knew this being by that name- the one who occasionally summoned him and others.","Even without looking, Giuseppe could vividly imagine the being's round, bald head and the tentacles for limbs that extended from its form.","It rarely revealed itself like this as most of the time, communication occurred through the intricate weavings of existence.","So why now?","For the Despondent One to appear directly...","Was something of such importance unfolding? Was it the War that was about to occur?","From the swirling black and white seas, profound waves of power emanated as the deep magnetic voice of the Despondent One echoed out.","\"Your assault against the Singed...is going to fail.\"","...!","Giuseppe's entire being trembled upon hearing these words.","Failure?","The Faceless Lifeforms had already reorganized. Multiple Prime Source Entities, including himself, were ready to move out!","And yet the Despondent One was certain that failure was imminent?","Giuseppe's head remained bowed, vibrating slightly with confusion and doubt. He wished to ask for clarification, but he knew better than to question the Despondent One.","Silence was his answer.","And as expected, the voice of the Despondent One echoed again, breaking the stillness.","\"Since that is the case, I will grant you all a bit more power as my complexity has managed to recover further. Whether you succeed or fail matters not this time. What is required, is for their focus to be drawn to that place.\"","...!","Power.","More power.","Giuseppe's body trembled, but he remained silent.","\"Raise your head.\"","The voice of the Despondent One commanded.","Giuseppe complied immediately, lifting his head, and what he saw...left him speechless.","The black and white Wheels of Existence that were emitting unfathomable waves of death and desolation had descended from the stellar sea above.","And now, they hovered dangerously close to him.","\"You will be able to channel directly and freely from both of these True Sources. Dead as they may be, they are still True Sources of Existence. With unfiltered and expanded access to them...\"","HUUM!","Giuseppe felt his weavings of existence explode.","The cap that had kept him bound, a barrier he could never breach no matter how many cycles he lived...shattered seamlessly.","His complexity surged to unprecedented heights as he felt the call of an Undeniable Telos Source wrapping itself around him.","But that wasn't all.","There was...","Something else.","Something he couldn't understand.","A new level of complexity!","Giuseppe's eyes were wide as he gazed at the Despondent One, fear and awe mixing in his expression as he voiced out.","\"I thank you for the opportunity and trust, Sir.\"","His voice was steady, but a flicker of hesitation followed as he spoke softly.","\"If I may, I wonder if my partner, Azzurra, could obtain the same? It would empower us both and allow us to achieve your aims more effectively.\"","His tone was filled with sincerity as he asked, hoping that the one he loved could obtain the same power without enduring the heavy price he had paid.","The Despondent One, however, shook his head calmly.","His gaze shifted upward, looking at the black and white Wheels of Existence with a mixture of emotions before he responded.","\"I cannot elevate the complexities of those whose weavings do not align with mine, nor those who do not trust me. Your partner's Weavings inherently don't trust me. But it does not matter. So long as I achieve what I desire, you will achieve what you desire. At that time, since your partner trusts you, you may grant her as much complexity as you wish.\"","...!","The words were heavy.","They were undeniable.","Giuseppe nodded, his expression cloudy, but he did not question the Despondent One any further.","\"The other Bearers of Despondency have been elevated in a manner similar to you.\"","The voice echoed once more.","\"Go now. Begin your assault on the Singed. Success or failure is entirely dependent on you all. Even if you die though, do not concern yourself with that. You have begun to walk the path of becoming a True Bearer of Despondency. Even if your weavings were to shatter, be broken, or devoured by another, I will call them back, and I will prepare you for resurgence.\"","WAA!","\"So fight freely, my child.\"","...!"]},{"number":3628,"title":"Chapter 3628: Chapter 3627 Sources! IV","paragraphs":["Fight freely!","Giuseppe's body trembled as he heard these words, but this time, it was not from fear.","It was from the immense, immeasurable power that now flowed through his being.","A True Bearer of Despondency.","The title echoed in his mind as he prepared to take the next step.","\"I will not fail you!\"","He spoke vehemently towards the Despondent One who nodded with a calm sense of apathy, and the stellar weavings Giuseppe found himself in disappeared.","Soon enough, he found himself back where he floated before, but his Complexity was unfathomably much greater.","He raised his fist as it caused the surrounding weavings to tremble, feeling like even a Prime Source Complexity like him in the past could only take a few strikes of his current power!","\"You okay?\"","Near him, the voice of Azzurra rang out as she appeared, her eyes slightly unfocused as if she was thinking about something else as Giuseppe couldn't help but smile when he saw her.","\"Yeah. I...I was just given new directives by the One We Follow. Things seem to be a little difficult as he had to be involved again.\"","He spoke about the Despondent One without mentioning too many things as Azzurra nodded. And Giuseppe continued. \"I have to set off right now, but wait for me once more, okay?\"","He looked at her with deep care as Azzurra seemed concerned while she asked.","\"You're off to fight against the Singed already? What about Osmont? What if he interferes?\"","She asked out of genuine care!","But the weavings of Giuseppe pulsed at the mere mention of Noah Osmont as he harrumphed.","\"I wish he would make himself present again! This time, he won't be able to stand so freely against a True Bearer of Despondency!\"","WAA!","His expression carried a sense of lividity and power as he exploded out with Complexity, his expression heavy as he kissed Azzurra's forehead and began to disappear. \"Do not worry, this battle won't be as dangerous as it seems. Success or failure aren't the true determinants of victory as we simply need this battle to occur.\"","...!","His voice slowly faded alongside his weavings of existence.","Across distant weavings within this same place, many Faceless Lifeforms also began to disappear- with some entering massive Dark Towers that hummed like vessels!","Azzurra was left behind with a complex expression as in her eyes, the Runes of the Amarantos Dream flickered.","—","In the Prime Frequency of Flames.","Gorgeous colored flames danced freely all around, the temperature being akin to that of multiple suns constantly shining miles away from each other as those who could exist here were a powerful few.","Noah appeared within such weavings alongside Mysara as he had a smile on his face, having received new waves of information from Azzurra.","\"It seems that Bob can freely hand out power-ups, too. And he simply wants this war to happen regardless of the results...a diversion while he continues altering Nodes of existence, or something else?\"","He wondered of the schemes continuing to unfold from that being as he took the hand of Mysara who was breathing in the flames while humming happily, their figures disappearing right after as from a single step...","PAH!","They manifested in a region filled with powerful lifeforms, alongside a massive Wisp of the Flame of the Wheel shining brilliantly!","...!","Ahead of them, Singed of different types were moving with power and purpose as they looked to be preparing, some already grouped up in specific squadrons as nearest to the massive burning Flame of the Wheel...the visage of Emelline of the First Flame turned towards their direction in shock.","The body of Mysara shimmered as clone and main bodies joined each other, scorching blue flames of an Undeniable Prime Telos Source burning around her as she looked towards Noah.","\"Sir, are you going to unveil yourself to all Singed?\"","Her eyes shone with vibrant luminosity as she asked what she believed to be a critical question.","Yet Noah only shook his head while turning around to gaze towards the far distance.","\"There won't be time for anything like that. Let's see what this war amounts to...\"","...!","In the distance.","Black radiance began to spread amidst the scorching flames as massive Dark Towers broke past crimson gold scorching flames- making their arrival here in a grand fashion as alongside their appearance, the auras of multiple terrifying Prime Sources bloomed!","Massive Faceless Lifeforms. Glimmering Dark Towers.","They all seemed to hold a vile sensation of death as at the forefront, three Faceless Lifeforms burning with an undeniable brilliance stood beside a Faceless One with a very unique muscular figure that looked more humanoid than others.","His gaze was piercing as even while he adorned the suit of the Faceless Lifeforms again; he was distinctly different as he looked around the moment he appeared- gazing at the burning waves of life of the Singed in the far distance of this flaming Expanse!","And among the Singed he saw...he managed to see the eyes of a calm figure staring back at him.","...!","Giuseppe naturally recognized Noah's unrelenting visage.","\"YOU!\"","HUUM!","The visage of Giuseppe was unfathomably bright and carrying billowing waves of black and white radiance as an Undeniable Prime Telos Source burned around him- his gaze undoubtedly locked onto Noah.","He pointed towards him with fervor as even without waiting for others, illusory black and white Wheels bloomed and began to turn behind him as he surged forward!","\"I want to see if you can stay still this time! I! WANT! TO! SEE!\"","WAA!","This terrifying figure barreled down like an unstoppable force of power.","And on the other side, Noah's gaze was calm as he was-...!","He frowned as instantly, his weavings became different, and black and white brilliance flashed around him.","|Your weavings have subtly changed.|","|Ordo Ab Chao has subtly shifted your Existence as you transition from the Cycle of Ordo to the Cycle of Chao.|","Such a thing made him sentimental as when he looked towards the rushing Giuseppe and the thousands of powerful Source Complexity Faceless Lifeforms behind him, alongside three massive ones radiating a light of an Undeniable Prime Telos Source that seemed devilishly powerful...","|In this Cycle of Chao, the complexity of your weavings obtains Absolute Infinitum Penetration, allowing the output of your complexity to scale up by 250,000% between the set parameters of 1,000% to 1,000,000%. In exchange, the complexities of others can also damage your weavings by the product of a fourth of the Complexity Scale of 250,000%.|","...!","His weavings of existence changed at a critical time.","But even then...his eyes only brightened as he adapted to the change his eyes looking at the terrifying Complexity Scale of 250,000% from Absolute Infinitum Penetration!","His weavings were already terrifyingly complex.","And if his output of complexity was further multiplied by 250,000%...","\"Ah...\"","He breathed in the flames around him calmly.","Flames.","A Prime Frequency of Flames where fiery heat filled everything.","Such a thing made him sentimental as when he looked towards the rushing Giuseppe and the thousands of powerful Source Complexity Faceless Lifeforms behind him, alongside three massive ones radiating a light of an Undeniable Prime Telos Source that seemed devilishly powerful...","He raised his hand towards them all as he called out.","Just to test things. Just to see.","\"Fireball.\"","...!","The Pathway to the True Source of the Singed seethed.","HUUUM!","The True Source Atlas of Existence vibrated.","Existence trembled.","The light years of Expanse of the Prime Frequency of Flames began to shake and tumble!","And instantly.","Before Noah and the Singed.","A terrifying ball of flames- a horrific sun that bloomed to cover half of the endlessly massive Prime Frequency of Flames bloomed!","A Fireball that painted half of an entire Frequency...bloomed!"]},{"number":3629,"title":"Chapter 3629: Chapter 3628: Existence Can Be Ridiculous! I","paragraphs":["Complexity was an interesting thing.","Depending on its utilization, one could achieve stupendous effects- but even these effects had limitations.","One could conjure Megalocides, Megalos Mountains, Strings of Existence, and countless other manifestations of existence, with some relying purely on raw power as all of this complexity could be collected into the body and expressed through sheer physicality alone.","Giuseppe walked such a path.","His body was the vessel that channeled the entirety of his complexity. A single step or punch from him could unleash the power equivalent to Megalos Mountains, Megalocides, or any other myriad conjured forms of attacks.","All of this fell under the realm of normal.","And then, there were anomalies.","Anomalies who stacked multiple, absurdly complex factors together to achieve utterly dreadful and incomprehensible weavings of existence!","[Fireball] was a unique F-Rank Modus Operandi from a world that empowered its lifeforms with the ability to manipulate Mana and conjure a ball of flames.","A round, glowing ball of flames.","Fairly straightforward.","Fairly simple!","Yet, such a simple, F-Rank methodology of power, when wielded by an F-Rank Hunter or by an anomaly with a True Source Atlas of Existence, could yield astoundingly different results.","The result this time was observed under the eyes of many, and it was one that caused even the most complex existences, at the stage of Undeniable Telos Prime Source, to question what they were witnessing!","From the tap of a hand, aimed toward thousands of powerful Faceless Lifeforms, each carrying variations of Lesser, Greater, or Prime Sources...Fireball was called out.","Emelline of the First Flame, watching from a distance, saw it.","Mysara, standing beside the anomaly who cast Fireball, saw it.","Thousands upon thousands of powerful Singed, who were present, saw it!","They witnessed the brilliance of a crimson-gold sphere of flames that pulsed with intense waves of heat. The flames released waves of heat all around that surged like a relentless tide, crashing against the bodies of these beings!","Beings who were composed of fire themselves, and yet, their very existences, regardless of complexity, were forced to acknowledge one thing.","'It's hot!'","...!","The Singed felt the heat.","And their eyes trembled as they saw, from the point where Noah was floating, an incandescent flame extending outward, stretching for uncountable millions upon millions of light-years across the Expanse of the Prime Frequency of Flames and beyond any Megalos.","A scorching sun had bloomed.","It engulfed the Faceless Lifeforms.","It surged toward the charging Giuseppe.","And it extended even further- so far that even if they couldn't fully observe its reach, the one who conjured this Fireball felt the outer edge pulse at the very boundary of observable existence of this Prime Frequency!","HUUUUM!","An incandescent fireball bloomed, covering half of a Prime Frequency.","Those caught inside it- designated as enemies, were now facing waves of complexity so dreadful that even the most powerful entities could barely comprehend them.","The complexity belonged to a man who held many, many True Severed Weavings of Existence.","A man who wielded a True Source Atlas of Existence and had access to the Pathways of True Sources linked to multiple concepts.","Complexity that stemmed from the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed- a pathway more than halfway to becoming its own True Source.","And all of this was further amplified by 250,000% in its output.","The result was catastrophic.","A mere second after the manifestation...","\"OOOOH!\"","\"AAAH!\"","\"NO!\"","Faint, brief screams echoed, filled with shock and horror.","For a second.","The briefest of a second.","And after that... silence.","A complete cessation of any noise or complexity within the ball of flames that continued to cover half of the Prime Frequency.","All Dark Towers.","All Faceless Lifeforms.","Even Giuseppe, who had been pulsing with an Undeniable Telos Prime Source backed by two dull White and Black Wheels of Existence...","All of them were incinerated.","Not even ash remained.","Noah knew this. He could feel it.","Every lifeform that fell under the Fireball was gone.","Yet, amidst the chaos, he had precisely designated the Faceless as the only enemies affected by its complexity. Across the half of the Prime Frequency of Flames that was engulfed, Noah sensed trillions upon trillions of other flame-based lifeforms that were untouched. For them, there was no destruction. They merely felt...a rise in temperature.","Within the same fireball that had incinerated Prime Source Complexities in a mere second, flame-based lifeforms blinked and looked around, wondering why it had suddenly gotten a bit hotter.","Beside Noah, Mysara rubbed her eyes, her gaze fixed on the blazing sun that still burned in the distance.","It remained.","A flaming sun whose edges stretched beyond her sight, tendrils of fire dancing across its surface with unwavering stability. It did not waver or fluctuate. It simply remained.","Mysara extended her complexity outward to search for the army of Faceless Lifeforms that had just appeared.","But...","She could not feel anything.","They were gone!","In the far distance, Emelline of the First Flame stood with a spear burning with a small Wisp of the Flame of the Wheel. Her body radiated an Undeniable Telos Source as she had been preparing for war.","A Holy War for the Singed against the Faceless Lifeforms burning with a Dead True Source that sought to infect and taint their Wheel of Existence.","She had rallied the Singed for such a grand war as when their enemies arrived...","She spread her senses outward to confirm.","Nothing.","All their enemies had been erased.","And as far as the eye could see, a burning sun covered the entirety of the Prime Frequency of Flames- extending infinitely outward in a certain direction.","It did not plan to fade away.","\"Ah...\"","The Singed gasped, their weavings churning.","Their eyes weaved and locked onto the figure who had nonchalantly tapped out to conjure this Fireball.","They sensed the utter complexity of the flames. Even a single tendril of it felt more pristine than all the flames enveloping their own existences!","The flames covering half of the Prime Frequency of Flames felt as complex and sacred as the Wisp of the Flame of the Wheel burning near the Singed.","They could not help but feel their very existence shudder as their eyes locked onto one man.","The man who stood at the center of it all!"]},{"number":3630,"title":"Chapter 3630: Chapter 3629: Existence Can Be Ridiculous! II","paragraphs":["One man floated before the burning ring of a vast sun that silently blazed, its weavings smoldering as if they had no intention of fading away.","\"Hmm...\"","A light nod followed as he surveyed the results, his eyes flashing with brilliance as prompts filled his vision.","|A Lesser Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been obtained from the collapsed Weavings of the Lesser Source Complexity, Tukrux.|","|A Lesser Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been obtained from the collapsed Weavings of the Lesser Source Complexity, Thrulgen.|","|A Greater Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been obtained from the collapsed Weavings of the Greater Source Complexity, Chumars.|","|An Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been obtained from the collapsed Weavings of the Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity, Giuseppe.|","|An Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been obtained from the collapsed Weavings of the Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity, Madhaed.|","|An Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been...|","The prompts came by the thousands.","The True Severed Weavings of Loot burned gloriously. Even though, like the Infiniverse Megalos, he was gradually becoming self-sufficient and capable of supporting his own rapid advancement, it did not mean he would refuse loot from external sources.","If they presented themselves, he would gladly take them.","Since the days when he was merely an F-Rank Hunter first utilizing Fireball, the exhilaration of acquiring loot had never left him!","With the Severed Affix of Burnt Weaver confirming no remaining Faceless Lifeforms in the gradually forming Map of the Prime Frequency of Flames, he turned to Mysara while his body floated toward Emelline of the First Flame and the others.","\"Let's go.\"","...!","He was utterly nonchalant about it all.","The war that Bob had orchestrated, whether it was merely a scheme to divert attention or something layered with complex plans they had yet to perceive, had been ended in a single second.","Whether this was a setback or a step forward, he would discover in due time. For now, as he floated toward the Singed who gazed at him with awe and reverence, his focus shifted toward the Loot Boxes as he called one out.","A dazzling, multicolored square box materialized before him.","Its allure was painted with a radiant glow of gold, inscribed with symbols of golden infinity signs and adorned with musings of wealth that others could only dream of.","It reminded him of the Treasure Caches of the past as the moment the Loot Box appeared, it spun with glorious waves of golden light!","Then, with a resounding explosion of fireworks, the top of the box burst open, releasing an array of dazzling Loot.","|17x Undeniable Telos Purified Source Pearls have been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Giuseppe.|","|A Torn, Scattered Record of an Unknown Dead True Source has been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Giuseppe.|","|The Records of the Weavings of Giuseppe have been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Giuseppe.|","|Scorched Remnants of an Existence Isolator Armament have been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Giuseppe.|","Waves of wonder erupted as dazzling singularities of Undeniable Telos Purified Source Pearls burst forth, accompanied by other marvels that raised Noah's brows.","He absorbed them all into himself and began perusing their weavings as he floated through throngs of Singed who looked upon him and the distant flaming sun with profound reverence. They instinctively made way for him, some bowing their heads with fervor and respect.","Noah and Mysara seamlessly arrived before a dazed Emelline of the First Flame with Noah offering her a calm, steady smile before asking softly.","\"The late Ezekiel seemed to have known the methodology to access a path into a True Frequency of the Wheel. Do you or the remaining Prime Source Singed know it as well?\"","...!","He did not mention the Faceless Lifeforms he had just reduced to ash, nor did he speak of their complete incineration. Instead, he asked for what he had truly come here to find.","In a daze, Emelline of the First Flame shook her head before pointing toward the massive Wisp of the Flame of the Wheel behind her.","\"We may not know much regarding that, but the Embers of Ezekiel were returned to the Sacred Flame here. They should contain his records...\"","WAA!","Noah's eyes gleamed with anticipation as he nodded, his gaze shifting toward the vibrant Flame in the distance!","—","Away from the Weavings of the Prime Frequency of Flames.","Inside the weavings of an Amarantos Dream.","Noah sat atop a flowing mountain of sandy gold clouds, gazing at a scene displayed before Azzurra.","It was the scene that had unfolded in the Prime Frequency of Flames- a scene where Giuseppe, someone close to her for many years as a Lost Avatar of the Beyonder, had been reduced to nothingness.","Azzurra's eyes were clear as she silently watched the blooming sun that had engulfed Giuseppe and incinerated him, along with thousands of other Faceless Lifeforms.","She closed her eyes afterward as Noah waved his hand, clearing the illusory scene.","Giuseppe...was gone!","This fact was undeniable as after offering her silent respects, Azzurra reopened her eyes, speaking softly with acceptance.","\"Since I stem from the Great Beyonder, all other weavings are false. Any entanglements I had... are false. It is right that things ended this way.\"","...!","Her obsidian-gold robe only magnified her desolate beauty. Her dark hair shimmered as she placed her hand gently on her chest and continued, her tone heavy with melancholy.","\"I can feel her... I can feel me, more and more. My weavings of the Expanse. Of the Megalos Beyond. Of the Outerversal Morphons. But what I thought I had in Existence, none of it remains. Only Legends across Frequencies. Apart from that, I have nothing. Absolutely nothing.\"","Her words carried a deep sense of desolation and self-deprecation as if the weavings of her existence were overlapping, tangled, and fragmented with all of herself, including the Great Beyonder.","Noah could only sigh as he looked at her, shaking his head softly.","\"Since I have altered your weavings and connected you to me, you will always have me.\"","Words of solace for an entity who blinked and gazed up at Noah.","The weavings of Azzurra and the Great Beyonder in the unfathomable Infinite Ravines seemed to overlap and become one entity, the shared sense of loneliness between them stretching to unbearable levels. And in that moment, Noah, the only tangible figure in her existence at this moment apart from endless battles of Dead Things...became a warm flame that the weavings of the Great Beyonder gravitated towards!","In the Amarantos Dream, Azzurra, the Great Beyonder, looked up at Noah's visage as he raised his brows at her actions. Her voice, barely above a whisper, echoed out.","\"You will always be there?\"","...!","Her eyes, glowing with the vibrant Trace Will of the Great Beyonder, sought assurance in these endless weavings of existence.","And Noah simply nodded.","\"I do not foresee my weavings collapsing anytime soon so...yes, I will always be here.\"","His words were like havenly water descending upon a desolate flower in a desert of loneliness. The weavings of the Great Beyonder moved closer toward him within the Amarantos Dream as Azzurra floated toward him, her obsidian gold robe falling away to reveal a fantastical visage underneath!","A veil of the Amarantos Dream rose around the region, obscuring anything that could possibly be happening beyond as the weavings of two beings intertwined!"]},{"number":3631,"title":"Chapter 3631: Chapter 3630: Past and Present! I","paragraphs":["As the weavings of an Amarantos Dream unfolded with obscurity in one region.","Across the Frequencies of Existence, other weavings manifested gloriously.","In an unknown Frequency.","Dazzling, multicolored rivers of reality swirled around a particular region, stretching outward for light-years.","At the center of these rivers stood a figure- Bob!","A placid expression filled his eyes as he toyed with a Node of Existence.","Before him hovered two dazzling Wheels of Existence, one black and one white as they were manifestations of profound power- of True Sources!","He held a sense of wonder and clarity as he gazed into the depths of these Dead True Sources.","Within their intricate design and countless spokes, one could see the weavings of entire seas of existence.","Seas of weavings.","At this moment, Bob focused on a specific subsection of the black Wheel of Existence.","Between two spokes lay a thick, dark sea- a place where the wails and screams of quintillions echoed.","These wails were drenched in pain and terror, the kind that would drive any being mad if they listened for even an hour.","And yet, Bob had listened to them endlessly, for eons.","Not just from this small subsection of the black wheel but from its vast expanse and from the white Wheel of Existence as well.","The screams of grief, indignation, fear, and hopelessness-he bore them all!","Over and over and over again.","Now, in the section he studied that was buried beneath countless weavings, he found the collapsed existence of none other than Giuseppe.","Linked to him as a True Bearer of Despondency, Giuseppe's very foundation now resided within his Source of Existence.","Bob reached out, his limb plunging into the dazzling black wheel and wrapping around the wailing weavings that once were Giuseppe.","BZZT!","A heavy friction surged, the effort monumental, but Bob did it anyway.","He grasped the weavings, like a singularity in his hand, his eyes flickering as he began reading its memories.","A moment later, he let out a light chuckle.","\"A single second...this was the extent of the forces I prepared required to be utterly erased from existence?\"","He shook his head at the absurdity, but he did not deny it had happened.","Over the eons, Bob had come to understand a truth.","Existence could be utterly ridiculous. Depending on who you were and what you did, you might be embraced by the weavings of existence, or you might stand against them.","Bob was currently standing against them.","The weavings of existence, especially in an Absolute Complex True Source, were unfathomably powerful.","A single action from him could trigger a cascade of disproportionate reactions from existence itself.","Noah Osmont...he appeared to be one such disproportionate reaction.","Yet Bob continued.","For him, there was no other path, only forward.","He fed complexity into the collapsed weavings that were Giuseppe as in seconds, the wailing ceased.","Moments later, Bob released his tentacled limb, and the illusory figure of Giuseppe reformed before him.","A terrifying work of complexity.","Giuseppe regained cognizance and cried out after another few seconds.","\"I WILL kill him. I will kill Osmont!\"","His existence blazed with fury as the last thing he remembered was being engulfed in endless flames.","A ball of fire had consumed him and thousands of others in mere seconds.","Now, pulled from a Dead True Source, Giuseppe had become a Dead Weaving of existence that was unable to return to what he once was.","At this moment, Bob shielded his own weavings with the black and white wheels spinning above as from here on out...","HUUM!","A black suit enveloped Giuseppe's body.","His weavings of existence began to climb, rising from a Lesser Source surging toward the Prime.","Eventually, the weavings ignited with the terrifying force of an Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity. Giuseppe's screaming stopped as he fully sensed his surroundings.","Unlike his previous dreams, he saw something that was very real.","He stood before The Despondent One, fully and truly. His existence trembled.","Bob looked at him and spoke calmly:","\"I told your child, even if you died... I would still call you out. Come now, step aside as the others are recalled. Your work is far from being done.\"","...!","Terrifying words.","Giuseppe nodded fervently, his weavings trembling as he thought of the one who had ruined everything in the Frequency of Life.","Now, that same being had erased his weavings in the Frequency of Flames.","The feeling of his own existence collapsing and disappearing...it was one Giuseppe never wanted to experience again.","He looked at the Despondent One and wondered.","Could he ask for even more power? Enough that Osmont could never touch him again?","He asked himself this question, unaware of what was currently unfolding within an Amarantos Dream.","From the black and white wheels of existence shimmering above, surrounded by multicolored rivers of reality, Bob continued.","He pulled out collapsed weavings of existences, reviving them and making them stronger!","It was a shocking feat of complexity as from this point forward, there would be no redundancy.","His work had only begun.","After all, he wouldn't simply restore collapsed weavings to what they once were.","They had to be better.","They had to be improved!","They had to be just as ridiculous...as the one who had collapsed them!","—","Back in the Prime Frequency of Flames, the gazes of the Singed burned around Noah as they were intense, reverent, and expectant.","But Noah had long since grown used to such looks.","Awe, shock, and even fear- they had followed him for an extremely long period of time. They no longer stirred his existence nor strengthened his weavings. They simply were.","He called to his weavings and floated toward the towering white-gold flame, the one Emelline of the First Flame had said held the embers of Ezekiel.","He had encountered many flames in recent times. This one, in truth, seemed almost lackluster. It lacked the chilling majesty of the silver-white Primal Flame of the Wheel, or the dreadful power of the flame crafted from the fusion of his own weavings and the Infiniverse Megalos- the construct that burned at the heart of his greatest weavings.","Yet this flame before him possessed a grandeur of its own. When Noah appeared before it and placed his hand within its burning light, the Sacred Flame opened to him as if recognizing old weavings.","HUUM!"]},{"number":3632,"title":"Chapter 3632: Chapter 3631: Past and Present! II","paragraphs":["Noah closed his eyes, delving deep into the flame. With his intricate complexity and the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed, he passed through the flame with ease and began searching for the weavings of Ezekiel.","It did not take long. His will spread through the flame like Mana through rivers of reality, touching and wrapping around a particular set of weavings. And there, in the heart of what Emelline had called the Sacred Flame, part of Noah manifested as he found what he was looking for.","He saw a man, or rather, the flame-born image of one that was serene, noble, and wreathed in tranquil fire. The man met Noah's gaze and spoke, his voice echoing out with grandness!","\"I did not expect my flow, once spent, to be stirred again by any complexity. To wake from the basking of countless flames, what does the Origin Singed seek of me?\"","As with the others before him, Ezekiel had looked once upon Noah and decided that he was the Origin Singed.","Noah no longer questioned it as the Pathway he held must bear such purity and likeness to the True Source of the Singed that those attuned to it saw no difference.","He gave a single nod and replied evenly:","\"I need to locate the pathway to the True Frequency of the Singed.\"","...!","Ezekiel raised an eyebrow, amused.","\"I might ask how the Origin Singed lost the path to his own home, but I know better than to question. If you wish to connect to the True Frequency, you need only connect to the weavings of every Singed in this Frequency and inscribe the Rune of the SINGED. The path will open.\"","So simple?","Noah nodded once more and began to withdraw from the Sacred Flame, giving a light nod of thanks to Ezekiel's weavings. As he did, the embers within the distance called out with a final flicker:","\"It was good to see you again, Sir. However brief our meeting.\"","\"...\"","Noah said nothing to such words.","He emerged from the flame fully and turned towards Emelline and the other Singed who awaited him, their gazes filled with expectation.","Any other Source Complexity might have buckled under the weight of such gazes!","But Noah? He bore the crushing weight of the Infiniverse Megalos already as this was just another Monday for him.","\"Come,\" he said, turning his gaze to each of them. \"Connect your weavings to mine. The pathway to the True Frequency of the Singed must be opened.\"","...!","He spoke freely.","And the Singed only glanced at each other briefly before...they obeyed without hesitation!","Mysara's eyes gleamed with anticipation, her flames burning a glorious blue.","Emelline, ever the calmest flame, smiled and nodded. She looked towards Noah, and in a voice only he could hear, she said:","\"I told you before that when the weavings need the Origin Singed, he appears, whether or not he believes he is one.\"","Her eyes burned like miniature suns.","Noah arched a brow in response to this nonsense and then raised his hand as a tendril of flame unfurled from him, radiant and pure as it sank into Emelline's chest.","BZZT!","Light exploded. Emelline's eyes blazed white-gold, and her entire being shimmered with incandescent brilliance.","More tendrils burst from Noah, arcing out toward the assembled Singed, even those scattered across the Frequency of Flames!","Some had Sources, others only Paths or Ordinances. But they would all be connected!","Among them, Noah searched quietly as the Great Usurper's weavings were not here.","The Usurper had shown disturbing interest in the Faceless Lifeforms. His last message to Noah was a unique one as he intended to test how easily the weavings of Dead Things could be swallowed and silently usurped.","Whether he was successful, Noah didn't know.","But if the Usurper had indeed seeded his will through the Faceless Lifeforms, perhaps he could become a blade, a weapon sharp enough to pierce even Bob.","Noah mused on this only lightly. In the space of moments, a myriad of tendrils connected from him to the other Singed as his Pathway trembled, glowing with brilliance.","Now came the Rune that Ezekiel mentioned.","He summoned the flames of the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed as he began to construct the Rune of the SINGED.","The Rune was not just a word, it was intent that changed the weavings of existence in a unique fashion.","Noah's understanding of the language of runes was still forming as he knew a single word could change all things. But the Rune of the SINGED, he shaped with certainty as he poured into it all his knowledge, all his desire to find the True Frequency of the Singed.","HUUM!","The air vibrated. The weavings of existence shook.","A single word blazed to life soon after as it was magisterial to see!","SINGED!","Flames roared.","Emelline and Mysara, along with countless others released beams of brilliance from their eyes.","The entire Frequency responded. Flames stirred, converging and billowing toward the blazing Rune like moths to a sun.","It was an event that many Singed had never witnessed.","But it happened today under the banner of the True Severed Origin Osmontian!","The Rune acted as a key to a doorway that was leading toward a place impossibly close to the Wheel of Existence itself.","And Noah? He was already calculating many things with his Weavings of Existence.","He thought of Bob. He thought of the Faceless Ones who did not need to win or lose, only to come here to wage a war with the Singed.","Was it part of Bob's design, the doorway to the True Frequency of the Singed opening?","Bob, too, sought entry into the True Frequencies. Perhaps this could all be according to some ridiculous, convoluted plan of his!","So, just in case...","Even now, another body of Noah materialized in the Frequency of Flames, his hands holding the Book of Existence gifted by the Queen of Matter as he had already located the Node of this Frequency.","Whatever plans were in motion, whatever schemes unfurled by the Dead Thing that was Bob...","They would not pass through the brilliance of Noah's weavings!"]},{"number":3633,"title":"Chapter 3633: Chapter 3632 Past and Present! III","paragraphs":["Somewhere deep within the Prime Frequency of Flames, space itself decided it had had enough as it tore open under the brilliance of the rune of the SINGED!","A blinding rune, etched in raw authority of the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed and known only to the True Severed Origin Osmontian ripped open the flaming space like someone tearing a hole in reality itself.","A jagged rift, buzzing with stability and wonder, bloomed into being like a scar across the face of existence!","The Singed watched from afar, their gazes intense and reverent as their connected weavings leading into tendrils within Noah caused all of this. In the distance, tucked inside a region wrapped in so many layers of flames that most beings wouldn't dare approach, another body of Noah moved.","It phased in like an echo threading between overlapping layers of Existence as if following the Flow of Existence was optional for him.","He arrived at a certain place as without hesitation, Noah reached into the overlapping Strings of Existence in one area and pulled out...a flame.","It looked completely normal. Average, even. Like something you'd find hovering above a campfire.","But the moment his other hand, already glowing with silver-white Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence came into contact with the flame...","BZZT!","The ordinary flame pulsed, shimmered, and revealed itself as a Node of Existence.","Noah didn't flinch. He just narrowed his eyes and calmly released more Primal Flames, starting to alter the Node of this particular Prime Frequency of Flames.","He was making alterations with a single goal in mind- to make sure Bob couldn't get into this Frequency or do anything to affect it.","The changes were similar to what he'd done with the Prime Frequency of the End, but this time it was more personalized to Bob. More targeted. Every adjustment was a deliberate strike against anything tied to Bob's existential weavings!","Noah wasn't about to be a pawn in someone else's chess match, if Bob was in fact scheming something. If he had to run around struggling as he was, then Bob better be doing the same!","And honestly, with how fast Noah's power was rising- with Absolute Infinitum Existentialism, Absolute Loot Generation, True Severed Osmontian Forge, and more...he was pretty sure the only thing that could keep up with his rise in complexity was maybe the Infiniverse Megalos.","The thing was growing exponentially as it garnered more self sufficiency and was absolutely taking off currently.","Every time Noah gained something, the Infiniverse Megalos gained more. At this point, it was even moving to conduct more grandiose actions- already seeking out the Queen of Matter for yet another wondrous upgrade.","Then there was the True Adaptive Power of Existence, which had officially tagged Bob as an enemy of growth. The stronger Bob became as he recovered his power, the faster the rise of complexity for Noah!","Eventually, even Bob wouldn't be able to keep up.","So yes.","Let time pass!","Because if there was one thing Noah had learned since he started as an F-Rank Hunter, it was that given enough time, he always won.","Kings. Tyrants. Hunters. It didn't matter how long they'd reigned as if one gave him days, weeks, or sometimes just hours, they would all eventually fall.","The only question now was...how long would it take to overcome Bob?","That was all he needed to think about. His victory.","For him, there could be no other eventual outcome. There wasn't room in his mind for doubts. No what-ifs. No fears about what might happen to existence if he failed.","Because in the Weavings of the True Severed Origin Osmontian, failure was just not an option.","Others could stumble. Others could fall.","But Noah? His failure meant utter catastrophe as it could not even be feasible!","HUUM!","His eyes lit with silver-white brilliance as he finished his alterations to the Node of Existence. In the distance, he saw where another one of his bodies had opened a dazzling pathway.","It wasn't just a door as he observed its weavings and sensed their heavy complexity.","The pathway could only be crossed by entities of a certain weight- those ranked Greater Source and above!","Dozens of the Singed watched what was happening with glowing eyes as the tendrils connecting them to Noah faded.","That alone made it unique as Noah hadn't seen something like this recently.","One of his bodies stayed back, guarding the Node of Existence even after all the changes. He didn't trust anything fully. The other body drifted forward toward the convergence of flames where heat could literally melt the complexity of anyone below Greater Source.","Dozens of the Singed watched what was happening with glowing eyes as the tendrils connecting them to Noah faded.","And then, Mysara and Emelline of the First Flame stepped forward.","Each summoned secondary bodies, their figures cloaked in radiating complexity and white-gold light for Emelline, and cerulean brilliance for Mysara!","\"Will Sir allow us to come as well?\" Mysara asked, gripping her tight blue robe, her form pulsing with Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity.","Noah gave a quiet nod as both she and Emelline fell in behind him, flying towards the heavy convergence of flames.","WAP!","They crossed the gateway like it was nothing.","Their complexities didn't even blink at the scorching temperatures.","What came next was hard to explain.","Crossing into this new frequency wasn't like stepping from the Megalos to the Expanse, or diving into the starless dark void he entered after the True Severing.","Even using his True Source Atlas of Existence, which let him bounce across that void that seemed to connect all Frequencies of Existence felt different compared to this passage!","This was...different.","The Flames of the Singed were required just to pass through as without them? You would disintegrate, the pathway would close, and your weavings would collapse like nothing.","His True Source Atlas of Existence discovered all of this!","Noah blinked, impressed.","So there were security measures already baked in and he had gone a little overboard with his edits of the Node of Existence.","But hey, there was no harm in going a bit overboard- he had done so many times in the past!","Seconds passed, and the three of them emerged into what should be the True Frequency of the Singed.","And what they saw was...","Pure!","Unfathomably, marvelously pure weavings of existence!"]},{"number":3634,"title":"Chapter 3634: Chapter 3633 Past and Present! IV","paragraphs":["Pure.","That was the only way to describe it.","Waves of white-gold plasma washed over the landscape. Light bent, shimmered and distorted in strange ways. It took them a moment to adjust their weavings and truly see.","And when they did, the first thing they observed was a Tree.","A towering, incandescent white tree that was so vast it dwarfed the equivalent of a thousand Omniverses in size easily!","Its trunk extended like the spine of existence itself as its branches sparkled, glowing with Wisps of the Flame of the Wheel of Existence on their ends.","Floating around it were pieces of the Wheel- massive golden constructs burning in complexity and serenity. White-gold flames curled around their rims and spokes seamlessly.","And far, far in the distance, a silver white Wheel larger than the size of the tree itself was surrounded by the Primal Flame of the Wheel, and it radiated a kind of glory that even an Undeniable Telos Prime Source would stop to stare in a daze as it was filled with majesty!","\"Ah...\"","Emelline of the First Flame gasped, not because of the overwhelming grandeur before her, but because of something that was alive.","Across this impossible expanse, she could feel multiple waves of complexity.","Lifeforms pulsed in the distance, their presence unmistakable as even from this far out, the signature of Prime Source Complexity Entities radiated with terrifying clarity!","And there weren't just a few.","There were thousands!","Emelline exhaled heavily, only for something even more intense to hold her attention across the horizon. Her eyes locked on a silver-white Spoke—one of the colossal ones branching out from the distant Wheel itself. This one burned with a Primal Flame, stretching so far it looked like a smooth, infinite silver white bridge of light.","They weren't hiding either as they were scattered across the tall tree, fragments of burning Wheels, and even along the vast surface of the massive silver-white Wheel in the distance.","And the moment Noah, Emelline, and Mysara arrived, every one of those thousands of Prime Source Complexities turned their attention toward them.","It was like standing under the gaze of flaming wonders, each one buzzing with the aura of the Singed as their complexity crackled, and then... the pressure faded. In the blink of an eye, it was like all those Entities had silently recognized them, and whatever hostility there might have been simmered down right after!","Emelline exhaled heavily, only for something even more intense to hold her attention across the horizon. Her eyes locked on a silver-white Spoke—one of the colossal ones branching out from the distant Wheel itself. This one burned with a Primal Flame, stretching so far it looked like a smooth, infinite silver white bridge of light.","And on it, an entity sat. A single point, so tiny on the grand scale, but burning with an aura that crushed anything they had felt so far. This wasn't just the Prime Source level or Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity level. This was beyond that!","Dozens of other Singed surrounded the figure as if they were attending a lecture from a great being. And that figure was staring straight at them.","Even from light-years away.","Emelline trembled again as her lips moved on instinct.","\"O Origin Singed...\"","...!","The Origin Singed.","THE Origin Singed?","Noah's eyes sharpened instantly, locking on the figure seated far away. His senses stretched across the weavings of existence, permeating every detail of the distant Spoke, and the figure gazed right back.","Then...that figure smiled. He raised a hand and spoke.","\"Do not resist.\"","HUUM!","The voice echoed like a whisper made of eonic flames.","Then, with a single tap from his finger, the very space around Noah, Emelline, and Mysara began to ripple and distort as in the next moment, they vanished!","They reappeared on the silver-white Spoke, light-years from where they had stood before as the heat here was even more intense.","Dozens of Prime Source Singed sat nearby, and three of them burned with the unmistakable power of Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity.","In the center of them all sat the man cloaked in silver-white robes, his body wreathed in the Primal Flame of the Wheel as he smiled softly and spoke out.","\"This is the first time a Pathway to the True Frequency of the Singed has been opened in quite some time as it startled quite a few of us. Especially now, in the middle of such...chaotic times. But still, welcome.\"","...!","His voice was calm. Silver-white hair flowed down his shoulders. His face was a handsome one filled with nobility as it shone with layered complexity and grace.","But Noah wasn't focused on any of that.","Noah was locked onto one thing...the burning purity of a True Source.","A True Source!","He could feel it radiating from the man before them as a tear slid down Emelline's cheek as she stepped forward.","\"O Origin Singed... you've been here this whole time?\"","Her voice buzzed with emotion- awe, and confusion all jumbled into one!","The Origin Singed shook his head, a soft smile still on his lips as he replied.","\"I am here... and I am not. My true Weavings remain in the Infinite Ravines, holding back the taint that tries to touch the Wheel. What you see now...\" He gestured around his silver-flame-wrapped form. \"Is merely a Remnant Weaving. A whisper of me. A complexity that was left behind in this True Frequency.\"","...!","Noah's gaze narrowed. It was another Remnant- just like the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder he'd met recently! How many more whispers of ancient legends like the Beyonder and Origin Singed were hidden across the Frequencies while their main bodies were in the Infinite Ravines?","As Emelline processed his response, the Origin Singed turned to Mysara and gave a nod of acknowledgement, and then his eyes finally settled on Noah.","There was something almost amused behind his terrifyingly peace gaze of flames! The Origin Singed looked at another...Origin Singed. For Emelline and Mysara, it was like the past and the present were colliding as their weavings buzzed when they saw it.","\"And here we have the infamous Noah Osmont...I don't know what exactly you're doing, but you've got the Flow of the Wheel buzzing constantly with every lift of your finger.\"","WAA!","\"What I'm more curious about, is how your flames are this pure. That level of purity is something I'd expect from someone who's already attained a True Source. This is your first time entering a True Frequency of the Wheel, right? So how did you stumble onto a True Source, or even onto its path? And more importantly, what exactly brings you here?\"","...!","Question after question arose as Noah met another entity who had attained a True Source.","His eyes vibrated with the tyrannical light of Quintessence as he gazed towards the Origin Singed calmly as he replied.","\"Complexity.\"","WAA!","\"I am here for the same reason that makes countless quintillions of entities rise and struggle every waking second- more Complexity.\"","...!","He was straightforward as in the surroundings, the silver white Primal Flame of the Wheel began to seethe!"]},{"number":3635,"title":"Chapter 3635: Chapter 3634 Limitations! I","paragraphs":["Complexity.","Every entity sought it, and Noah was no different.","His weavings spread out across this True Frequency of the Singed as he sought to understand everything- even as he talked to this Remnant Weaving of the Origin Singed.","The being seemed entirely carefree, carrying the air of mysteries that Noah didn't like too much- the air of those beings who acted like they had everything under control, or that because of the power they were connected to, everything would be okay.","When in fact, things were not okay.","And if the Origin Singed had a Remnant Weaving sitting in the True Frequency of the Singed, he could have moved to do something regarding Bob, right?","So he looked towards him and the silver-white wheel they sat on, as well as the many other profound structures in this space buzzing with plasma and heat, as he asked:","\"I came across Remnant Weavings of the Great Beyonder not too long ago too. She at least tried to locate the Dead Thing running around the Frequencies of the Wheel when she came to. But have you been active in this True Frequency this whole time? Your True Source could potentially move freely to act if it wished?\"","WAA!","His eyes flashed sharply as he made his intent clear.","Beside him, Emelline and Mysara had complex expressions, as if they had the same questions—but not the strength to actually raise them!","The Undeniable Telos Prime Source Singed and other Singed in the surroundings heard the questioning tone from Noah and became stern, one even rising up as if to ask Noah why he would question the Origin Singed like this!","But the Origin Singed smiled lightly while raising his hand, and he replied with a sense of melancholy:","\"In existence, there are always limitations. I have my own constraints and limitations, as my Remnant Weavings are constrained into this True Frequency. If ever it were to be breached by those that should not be here, I am a safeguard for it. The importance of a True Frequency of the Wheel is the only reason why this Remnant Weaving is here.\"","...!","The location was an important one. And so, he was there to protect it.","Noah heard such words, and they only made him dislike this ideology more and more. His gaze swept around as he replied.","\"Yeah, fuck all the normal Frequencies and the Prime Frequencies and the countless lives on there, right? So long as this True Frequency is safe, they don't matter that much.\"","...!","His words were sharp, and Emelline and Mysara were shocked.","The Origin Singed retained his smile as he replied right after:","\"If the True Frequency is ever breached or falls, then even more countless lives and records of all Frequencies will be lost. The Wheel of Existence itself could be put at risk.\"","The ideology of the Origin Singed gradually became clear.","And Noah gazed back at him coldly as he replied:","\"So the Flow of the Wheel moves as it does to protect itself in the long run—not those channeling through it. The Wheel flows to preserve itself and nothing else. Good to know. I'll leave that work to you all and proceed to get what I came here for.\"","...!","His words caused the surrounding Singed to shudder, as if blasphemous weavings were being uttered. But the Origin Singed kept his calm as he asked quizzically:","\"Do you even know what you are looking for?\"","He came for complexity. But did he know how to get it in this True Frequency?","Noah simply gave a light nod to the Origin Singed as he floated up, his eyes turning toward a certain direction.","\"Yeah. I've found the only thing that could possibly aid me tucked away over there.\"","...!","After floating up, he shot out toward a certain direction- leaving behind the Origin Singed and all others, as the air grew heavy!","Noah's senses still covered that region as he saw Mysara's visage wrapped in blue flames rise up right behind him and follow, while Emelline of the First Flame wore a difficult expression. A second later, she gave one last gaze to the Origin Singed and then followed Noah!","...!","It was a phenomenon that showed where their allegiances lay. As for the other Singed, this was preposterous.","And yet, the Origin Singed raised his hand again to keep the order, his gaze filled with a mixture of weavings as he seemed to be thinking of many things!","Noah pulled his gaze away from that silver spoke of the Wheel where the Origin Singed sat, continuing toward the direction that could actually aid him in increasing his complexity.","Past the shattered wheels and complete ones like the one the Origin Singed sat upon, past the tall Tree with wisps of the Flame of the Wheel on its branches, there was a place light years away that radiated waves of heavy complexity!","Around it, Existence itself distorted from its sheer brilliance. And the closer Noah got, the more he could hear and feel its booming sound, which had been silently permeating across the True Frequency of the Singed.","DUM!","Pure white.","DUM!","Unfathomably scorching—to the extent that the white brilliance overcame any gold in the surroundings. Noah neared the wonder, and his distinctions of the Weaver analyzed it as its identity became clear.","DUM!","It was... a heart.","A pure, beating heart that looked extremely detailed, with its pulmonary arteries and veins cut off. And it was cycling a shocking concentration of white flaming authority!","Around it, the white flames it cycled eventually dispersed outward to form a ring of silver-white flames. Other white flames joined the plasmic gold brilliance in the surroundings to form weavings of white-gold Wisps of the Flame of the Wheel.","It was a heart spitting out flames, and from the trunks of its aorta, there were also dazzling drops of white brilliance that occasionally flowed out and formed into a scintillating sea above.","Noah looked at such a wonder with bright eyes, as this was...","\"The True Heart of Existence...\"","HUUM!","In this True Frequency of the Singed, there was no Node of Existence.","He could instinctively feel the same weavings of a Node from the white heart, as this... was what served as a Node here—a Heart that was spitting out white flames that transformed into Primal Flames of the Wheel and Wisps of the Flame of the Wheel!"]},{"number":3636,"title":"Chapter 3636: Chapter 3635 Limitations! II","paragraphs":["The True Heart of Existence!","Noah felt his weavings churning and cycling at an ever faster rate the closer he neared this heart, with his Existence accelerating in its advancement of complexity!","|The Pathway to the True Source of Loot looks at the True Heart of Existence with fascination.|","|The True Heart of Existence is deemed to be the True Source of the scattered Flames of the Wheel of Existence—being merely a part of what makes up the Absolute Complex True Source that is the Wheel of Existence.|","...!","What his weavings were discovering were an array of wonders, as the Heart before him was actually a True Source—and it was a part of what made the Wheel of Existence what it was, as from this heart came all the flames.","Noah's eyes were bright as he floated towards it, the scalding temperatures from the pumping heart being so intense that it was a question whether even Prime Source Complexity Entities could actually get near it!","But him?","BZZZT!","His golden robes billowed tyrannically as his skin only glinted with a fantastical radiance the closer he went.","His foundation and weavings of existence were already astounding enough.","His complexity held a True Source Atlas of Existence already!","His concepts were all severed 54 times over as his complexity was utterly tyrannical—where even if he didn't say it out loud, he knew that nobody else held the foundation he had at this moment!","Nobody with an astounding flow of the Wheel around them.","Not Ashmole with all his experiments. Not the Peacemaker he recently met. Not even the Great Usurper with his overbearing Soul!","\"You think mere heat will keep ME away?!\"","HUUM!","Flames that would later transform into Primal Flames or Wisps of the white-gold Flame of the Wheel, but at this moment...the pure white flames held a level of uniqueness that was extremely conducive to the growth of Complexity.","His expression carried the tyrannical dominance of the True Severed Origin Osmontian as he took a step forward, his existence shifting as he instantly appeared above the True Heart of Existence—specifically, above the three white tunnels of the aorta that were gushing out extremely pure white flames.","Flames that would later transform into Primal Flames or Wisps of the white-gold Flame of the Wheel, but at this moment...the pure white flames held a level of uniqueness that was extremely conducive to the growth of Complexity.","So long as one's existence could withstand them, they would be refined like molten metal and made more complex over time.","And if one was able to consume these flames without their existence burning...","Noah's eyes showed immense firmness and tyranny as he looked at the white flames flying up and flashing over his skin, his complexity booming upwards just from this proximity.","But this was nowhere near enough for him, as at this moment, his mouth began to open wide as his chest expanded—and he took a Quintessential Breath!","HUUUM!","All nearby weavings shook and tumbled as if a titan was breathing in utter majesty.","In the distance, the figures of Emelline of the First Flame and Mysara arrived as they felt the blistering heat, their weavings also advancing, but...when they neared a certain proximity to the True Heart of Existence, they actually had to come to a stop as they felt their Undeniable Telos Prime Sources actually begin to be injured from the heat and flames!","They had to stop and wait as their complexity gradually rose before they could forge ahead again.","But far in the distance, Noah stood right above the True Heart of Existence as he even breathed the unfathomably pure and scorching white flames into his body!","...!","It felt like they were witnessing an obscene scene of tyranny, as white flames weren't the only things coming out of the trunks of the aorta.","There were scintillating drops of pure white brilliance that floated up to form a sea.","When he breathed in, the white sea above formed a spinning vortex and began to descend into his mouth and nose.","From the trunks of the aorta, drops of white dew—akin to glimmers of rain—began to float towards his mouth and nose!","All of it flowed into Noah as he drew from the purity of existence of...an already existing True Source.","His intent was singular today.","To draw from this True Heart of Existence until...a certain Pathway to the True Source of the Singed was more than halfway completed.","Until its road was completed.","Until a True Source of the Singed was obtained—bathed from the white flames and blood of the Heart of Existence itself!","HUUUM!","\"Come!\"","The booming roar of the True Severed Origin Osmontian echoed out of the True Frequency of the Singed, the myriad of lifeforms within unable to help but turn toward his direction.","Among the many eyes gazing over, there were also the eyes of the Origin Singed.","Within them, complex waves of thoughts swirled as he looked at Noah's figure, his thoughts indiscernible!","—","While a significant explosion of complexity occurred in the True Frequency of the Singed.","In the Frequency of Light.","A taint of Darkness spread across the expanse of this Frequency as massive Dark Towers were being enacted, and tens of thousands of Faceless Lifeforms at the level of Pioneers or Existence Severing entities moved, while a few dozen Lesser and Greater Sources were also present!","There was also a single Prime Source.","At this moment.","Inside the weavings of the Prime Source seated atop a Dark Tower.","\"What is this...\"","His voice echoed out as he peeled the white bar on the black suit he wore—and the signature burn that should have occurred...did not occur, as once the black suit that veiled everything was taken off, the black mass on the face distorted as the handsome appearance of none other than the Great Usurper took its place.","Since the Great Usurper had taken over the Source of this being, it naturally could not be rejected by the weavings of the Wheel as he made the Source his own!","And alongside this...he gained the memories of this particular Source.","Memories...that showed him an entirely different weaving of existence.","He saw countless waves of corpses that made up a vast sea of countless quintillions—and he was among these corpses.","A Prime Source with his complexity leaking of death and decimation, and as he died...his weavings managed to see a scene.","Above the seas of corpses.","In the skies.","He saw the figure of two identical entities with the same faces, but one was black, and one was white!","But both...were Bob!"]},{"number":3637,"title":"Chapter 3637: Chapter 3636 The Dead and the Living! I","paragraphs":["Above a sea of corpses.","One of the bodies among the countless quintillions held a strange complexity. Though undeniably lifeless, its eyes still shimmered with the remnants of awareness, as if recording everything unfolding around it.","It was a unique complexity of Existence!","It was into this corpse that the Great Usurper had extended his weavings into as he was observing in this moment a distant memory.","A memory that showed that, above this endless sea of death, two figures stood- arguing.","Both bore the likeness of Bob as One radiated with an obsidian luster; the other, a brilliance as pale and blinding as the color white.","Their voices echoed like thunder across the decimated sky.","\"We tried it—and it did not work! It did not work, and now the collapse of an entire Wheel of Existence rests on our hands!\"","HUUM!","The words were terrifying. They spoke of a terrifying failure, the breaking of something that was far too critical to life","The white-lustered Bob, whose form rippled with tentacles, had bellowed those words. The obsidian Bob regarded him with a cold, tyrannical stare.","\"Do you think you're the only one who feels? Who understands? Do you think I didn't witness the shattering of the Wheel?! I know- I understand more than you think. And even though we failed here, we confirmed something critical. We can now put all our efforts into finding... THAT.\"","...!","THAT.","What the fuck was THAT?","The weavings of the Great Usurper pulsed, shaken by what they were witnessing as his vision expanded across the vast sea of corpses.","Far in the distance, he saw it- the remnants of an ancient black wooden wheel. Only a fragment was visible, yet even that fragment was as vast as an entire Megalos as all these remnants stretched out across countless weavings.","Shattered.","Broken!","An entire Wheel of Existence shattered and broken. What force could have possibly caused such a cataclysm?","The white Bob stared at his obsidian counterpart, his expression hazy, grief-stricken.","He spoke again, his voice a whisper brimming with ruin and guilt.","\"We were wrong. The dead and the living are far too different in the scope of existence. A dead Wheel of Existence cannot be reenergized simply by connecting to a living one.\"","They had tried.","They had pierced through to the True Frequencies of the Absolute Complex True Source here, examined its essence, perused its depths, inching ever closer to its core. Close enough to touch the Wheel of Existence itself as they connected a Dead True Source to a live one.","But the vibrant surge they'd expected never came.","Instead, the Dead True Source overwhelmed everything. Every spark of life was extinguished.","Countless lives across countless frequencies- gone. They were Channellers of the True Source that was the Wheel of Existence. If they simply lost that connection, it wouldn't have meant death.","But the breaking of the Wheel? That was the breaking of existence itself!","And the umbrella it cast shattered with it.","Without that shade, unless one possessed immense power or had attained their own True Source, living became nearly impossible.","The Absolute Complex True Sources provided the shade required for life. Breaking them meant breaking the very existence they upheld.","The white Bob clutched his head and collapsed to his knees, haunted by the screams of quintillions who had died by his hand.","His expression was haggard as he turned to his obsidian self, who remained composed and eerily calm.","\"Is it all worth it?\"","...!","He asked the question softly.","A question he would continue to ask himself for eons to come.","Was it all worth it?","The weavings of the obsidian Bob glimmered as he looked to his other self and replied, his voice cool and resolute.","\"Is it worth it to hold your child again? To see her smile? To free her from eons of torment? While her very existence is assailed again and again and again? Is. It. Worth. It?!\"","HUUUM!","The sky trembled. His final words crashed like the fury of a titan across the weavings of existence!","Silence followed, heavy, as the two Bobs stood locked in solemn understanding.","It was the obsidian Bob who finally broke the quiet.","\"We don't know. But connecting to another Wheel...doesn't work. And the words of that being, the one who shattered our Wheel of Existence, are only now confirmed. What we need to reenergize our own Wheel...is the very thing he was looking for within our weavings. He went about it monstrously and left only destruction in his wake. But we can do it differently. No one else has to die. We just need to find the Absolute Complex True Source, the one Wheel of Existence that can act as the key which leads to THAT.\"","WAA!","\"If we can grasp it- if we can grasp the Construct that Innervates the Wheels of Existence themselves...\"","...!","The Construct that Innervates the Wheels of Existence.","The Usurper's weavings pulsed in awe.","It sounded far too fantastical.","The obsidian Bob turned to the white Bob, whose expression twisted with uncertainty as he responded grimly.","\"There are many Wheels of Existence, many already dead, and others on the verge of collapse. And yes, a few are still alive...still vibrant. But finding the right one- the one that leads to THAT...will be a journey of endless searching. Even if we find it, every Wheel has its own protections. The living and the dead are separated by a sacred line. The living will not allow the dead to enter. They will resist. There will be deaths.\"","...!","\"We were once defenders of our own Wheel as we were holding back legions of dead things clawing to enter. We cannot become the very threat we once repelled, right? We cannot wage war on those who have done nothing to us...right?\"","His somber expression grew a touch more resolute.","He seemed ready to ask again- was it worth it?","But instead, he turned toward his other self. He became reflective.","A decisive light then shimmered in his eyes.","\"For her... and for all others whose deaths we can undo, whose lives we can restore...it will all be worth it.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":3638,"title":"Chapter 3638: Chapter 3637 The Dead and the Living! II","paragraphs":["For the sake of undoing all their mistakes, it would all be worth it.","For the sake of seeing her again, it would all be worth it.","The obsidian Bob and the white Bob looked at each other as an unspoken agreement bloomed between them.","Behind the obsidian Bob, a terrifying shattered, and destitute black Wheel of Existence bloomed... and began to spin.","Each rotation was slow, heavy, and agonizing as though the screams of countless lost entities echoed through its broken spokes. And this was true in a sense as with every turn of that Wheel, those contained within it felt its movements that caused them all tremendous pain! This was why they were wailing constantly....","Such a Wheel and all those within were still present.","A dead True Source of Existence, shattered by their own hands.","Unintentional, yes. But done all the same.","As the broken and dead Wheel bloomed behind the obsidian Bob, a radiant white Wheel of Existence bloomed behind the white Bob.","Waves of complexity converged between them, their bodies buzzing as if in harmony—until they were pulled toward each other.","Where once there was disagreement and division, now their Weavings of Existence aligned as one.","An obsidian Bob. A white Bob.","And in that moment, they became a single Bob.","The endless field of corpses that the Great Usurper had been observing began to stir. Slowly, impossibly, they rose- an unfathomable sea flowing toward the spinning black and white Wheels of Existence.","It looked like a procession of countless dead beings as even in their dead state, some even struggled as if they innately knew they were in for constant and endless pain for an unknown number of years to come.","But they had no power to reject anything, so they were put inside the Dead True Source.","When it came to living True Sources, rules and limitations were many, as distorting and reshaping existence was nearly impossible.","But with dead things...","With dead Wheels of Existence?","The alteration was so much easier.","From the Weavings of Existence, as the Great Usurper watched in shock, he heard Bob's voice one last time.","\"For her... for all those I have imposed suffering upon...\"","WAA!","For her.","It was all for her. And he had tried to make things right.","But in the end... how could the deaths of countless quintillions and the destruction of multiple Wheels of Existence ever truly be rectified?","BOOM!","The sliver of memory, seen through the eyes of a faceless lifeform, vanished—snuffed out in an instant.","The Great Usurper came to once more, his expression heavy as he softly repeated the words he'd just heard.","\"The thing that Innervates Wheels of Existence...\"","That was what Bob was after.","Not the Wheel itself. Not the Absolute Complex True Source that so many protected.","No. The Wheel was just a pathway... leading to something else. Something unnamed. Something more than what even someone like him knew!","The Great Usurper's expression darkened.","He needed to know more.","Only then could he continue his idle existence while the souls he had usurped moved on his behalf.","Bob had held the remnants of countless quintillion souls embedded in the Dead True Sources under his command.","No... not just Dead True Sources. That was misleading.","They had once been Absolute Complex True Sources—Wheels of Existence that had sheltered entire realities under their great shade.","And Bob now held two of them. From their husks, he brought forth Faceless Lifeforms.","Dead things to move as he pleased.","\"Looks like I've got quintillions of dead souls to take over... how much complexity will that add?\"","His luminous eyes flickered with uncertainty as yes, even he had doubts.","The dead and the living did not mix.","And yet here he was, seamlessly usurping the dead, making them part of him, of the Weavings of the very Wheel he now borrowed shade from.","But now...","He looked up.","He could sense the Dead Wheel of Existence, the one belonging to those he had usurped.","He could even draw power from it through them.","An array of intricate, mind-bending weavings unfolded before him as...","\"I sure as hell am not taking all of this on myself.\"","He muttered the words to no one in particular. But thereafter, he reached out. This time, he spoke to someone.","\"Hey Big Guy, you busy?\"","HUUM!","He pulled the entanglement toward the one entity who made him feel like he wasn't the craziest thing in Existence —no matter how wild things became.","Existence, after all, was a progression of increasingly ridiculous things.","Things he couldn't even fathom months ago? Now done as easily as breathing.","With madness constantly unfolding, it was easy to feel like he was losing his mind... unless there was someone who operated on an even more absurd level.","The Great Usurper reached out to such a being—one whose Weavings were complex enough to drift easily through frequencies, bypassing all resistance to communicate clearly at this moment.","He asked whether he was busy.","The reply?","\"Just trying to obtain a True Source. What's up?\"","...!","Just trying to obtain a True Source?","The Great Usurper paused before shaking his head.","This was the kind of crazy that reminded him he wasn't alone in it. That someone else existed out there on a level far more absurd than his own.","So, without asking how or what he meant, he continued.","\"I've got some Weavings of information—just found something interesting about our dear friend, Bob. Sending it over now.\"","HUUM!","Power radiated from his eyes as he transmitted the scenes he had witnessed—seen through the lens of a Dead Thing.","Across frequencies, the Weavings surged.","In the True Frequency of the Singed, as Noah floated above a dazzling white heart billowing with the purest flames and blood, his eyes sharpened—radiating brilliance that could not be contained.","He received the transmission—and his Weavings buzzed with revelation.","Information about a Dead Thing.","A being far grander than anyone had anticipated.","A being who was not within these Weavings of Existence for the reasons people thought.","Bob!"]},{"number":3639,"title":"Chapter 3639: Chapter 3638 True! I","paragraphs":["The information Noah received shed light on an enemy of immense power and significance- an entity backed by not one, but two Absolute Complex Dead True Sources!","One of them had been directly affected by his actions, it's very breaking as a result of his interference.","He had already connected his own Dead True Source to another Wheel of Existence as what had occurred wasn't a re energization, but rather the shattering of another Wheel.","\"And you're looking for something even more pristine than a Wheel of Existence itself...\"","Noah murmured to himself calmly as billowing white flames and white blood from the True Heart of Existence continued to surge into him.","Bob was searching for something that Innervated the Wheels of Existence themselves- something so unknown and untouchable that even the unknown entity responsible for the collapse of Bob's home Wheel of Existence seemed to be seeking it as well.","\"Okay.\"","Noah nodded, eyes gleaming with purpose and unwavering tyranny.","So much had remained unclear before. Who exactly was Bob? What were his true motives? What of the legends surrounding beings like the Beyonder and Omnifather, the Wheels of Existence, and everything else?","All of it was unknown before!","But the fog was finally lifting. For days, Noah had been in reactive mode- responding to events as they unfolded, doing what he could to stay afloat.","No more. The pieces were aligning, revealing a clearer picture of what was happening, who was involved, and why.","The legends in the Infinite Ravines- the ones who once protected the Absolute Complex True Source that was the Wheel of Existence, they had fulfilled the same role Bob once did before becoming a Dead Thing.","Now that everything had fallen into place, Noah's path was equally clear.","\"Attain the True Sources of all my Severed Weavings. Prevent Bob from acquiring access to whatever Innervates the Wheels of Existence so that he doesn't kill off every single thing accidentally. Step into the Infinite Ravines where the Beyonder and the Omnifather are. Observe the growth of the Infiniverse Megalos...and find time to retire on my farm.\"","...!","Just a few tasks. Easy enough, right?","Noah chuckled, his smile sharp with Quintessence and Tyranny! Despite everything, his goals had never wavered.","When Existence collapses around you, don't be the weakest thing left behind- the one who couldn't do anything as the walls fell.","Right now, those collapsing walls were being brought down by Bob and the countless Dead Things in the Infinite Ravines. What he had to become was not a weak piece of the puzzle, but one of its greatest Bosses.","And the first step toward that? The attainment of the True Source beside his True Source Atlas of Existence.","He looked down at the pulsing, white heart, while another body of his within the Frequency of the End gazed upon the visage of Ashmole.","The two of them stood in a cornfield Noah had woven from Dreams, stretching a full light-year wide. He had brought Ashmole here, to this place of peace.","The tentacle from the Pathway to the True Source of the Eldritch Expanse faded from Ashmole's forehead, his eyes dimming, losing their glimmering haze of white and black radiance.","His weavings returned into his body. He gazed at the endless rows of corn, then at Noah who stood silently beside him before speaking.","\"You truly did live. In all of the lives I saw for you, the memory that made you happiest was standing before fields of corn in every single Frequency.\"","...!","\"So I brought you here to give you your send-off.\"","WAA!","Ashmole remained silent.","He placed a hand to his chest, searching within himself. Then he looked outward, toward the light-year-long stretch of golden corn.","His eyes shimmered with regret and infinite possibilities as he finally spoke, voice gentle.","...!","\"Existence is not fair.\"","...!","\"Some are born on a much higher level than others. No matter how hard one tries, they'll never reach the same height as someone who was simply born with more.\"","\"Existence is not fair...but it's also unfathomable, vast, and filled with endless potential and possibilities. I've seen it across the myriad Frequencies I've touched. In this one, this Wheel of Existence with its terrifying flow- you, Noah Osmont, are beyond measure. But I know that out there, in other weavings and wheels of existence...there are others. I'm certain someone even more ridiculous than you exists. I hope the day comes when you meet them. An entity that makes you feel like an ant before an elephant. One who brushes aside your complexity like it's nothing but cotton. And when that day comes, Osmont...remember me.\"","WAA!","Ashmole's voice fell quiet.","Noah met his gaze and nodded, offering no arguments and no words. This being, this Alchemist of Existence, deserved his peace. At that moment, Noah simply tapped out.","Raw Power leaked from his form.","He borrowed the weight and grandeur of the growing Infiniverse Megalos as the brilliance surged through his body, coalescing around Ashmole and then...it began to disintegrate him.","His True Source Atlas of Existence spun with a thunderous boom as it began erasing all traces of Ashmole as the being broke down into glowing motes of ash!","Noah watched with calm reverence as prompts began to bloom before his eyes.","|An Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Existence has been obtained from the collapsed Weavings of the Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity, Ashmole.|","The loot box manifested, and Noah opened it right after.","A swirl of multicolored brilliance erupted in the heart of the cornfield and turned into wonders.","|x29 Undeniable Telos Purified Source Pearls have been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Ashmole.|","|The Records of the Origin of Existence have been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Ashmole.|","|The Records of the Weavings of Ashmole have been obtained from the Undeniable Telos Prime Absolute Infinitum Loot Box of Ashmole.|","Loot!","Waves of power and knowledge flowed in. With the opened loot boxes of Giuseppe, the three other Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity Faceless Lifeforms, Ashmole, and the thousands of Lesser and Greater sources he had decimated, along with the scorching purity of blood and flame from the True Heart of Existence....something monumental was within his reach.","He placed a hand to his chest and closed his eyes. There, he saw the flickering flame of the Singed within.","And he called out.","\"Be true, O Singed.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":3640,"title":"Chapter 3640: Chapter 3639 True! II","paragraphs":["Be true.","He spoke grandly like a teacher addressing a student. Like a blacksmith commanding their hammer. Like his very existence was summoning the weavings of the Singed to take their next step forward!","And in the true Frequency of the Singed, a profound change began to bloom as countless eyes turned toward it.","The Remnant Weavings of the Origin Singed looked on, seated atop a silver-white spoke over the Wheel.","The figures of Emelline of the First Flame and Mysara floated in the distance, near the True Heart of Existence. Their Sources thrummed and resonated as they turned their gazes toward Noah.","Everyone could feel it- something was about to happen, even if they didn't know what.","And the man atop the trunks of the Aorta of the True Heart of Existence stopped breathing in those terrifying, pure white flames and blood. His body radiated a pulse of unfathomable light.","He floated, wrapped in grandeur as white flames and shimmering seas of purity spun around him, encircling freely.","A moment of peace. Of raw and Quintessential power.","And then...","DUM!","Like the beating of a celestial heart, Noah raised his leg and took a step forward.","As though he were walking a path- a sacred road he had built himself!","He had walked this pathway for so long. He had constructed it with his own hands, with countless authorities and treasures from boundless Sources.","And now, this final step...this was the step Existence would witness.","They saw only that step. None of the storms it took to reach this point. None of the trials and tribulations!","Only the movement.","And with that single step, from one end of the path to the other...","BOOM!","His body was consumed in a dazzling bloom of white-gold flame thay covered everything.","The flames swallowed even the True Heart of Existence! They engulfed Emelline and Mysara!","They stretched outward for a full light-year, a storm of power impossibly vast and endlessly complex!","\"Ah...\"","Emelline and Mysara felt their own weavings buzz violently as they were subjugated by waves of purification, their complexities beginning to surge uncontrollably.","The flame that bloomed from Noah was so intricate, so pure, that even the distant form of the Origin Singed stood, no longer seated.","He stared ahead, eyes gleaming, as he and countless others bore witness to the emergence...of a True Source.","A True Source of the Singed, born in a fashion never seen before.","HUUM!","| The Pathway to the True Source of the Singed has been walked. |","| At the end of the pathway, you have obtained the True Source of the Singed. |","| The complexity of your existence has undergone a significant advancement as a new milestone has been achieved. |","Complexity!","A strange, curious thing to try and measure.","The complexity of a Source was unlike anything else as it varied depending on the one who walked the path.","Countless beings had come before Noah as many had walked their own roads and become Lesser, Greater, or Prime Sources.","And yet Noah's path was something else entirely. His Source was different! So vastly different from all who came before him.","Within a certain Mundi of Power in the True Source Atlas of Existence, a flame bloomed that was so blindingly bright that the moment it was born, it spread across the entire wheel-like structure of the Atlas.","It touched the other Mundis of Power. It permeated all of Noah's existence.","And then...","| Quintessence welcomes the emergence of the first True Source. |","| Infinity welcomes the emergence of the first True Source. |","| Cheats welcomes... |","The True Flames of the Singed surged and everything welcomed their emergence.","And as the flames spread","| The True Source of the Singed declares that no Severed Weavings shall remain in the body of the True Severed Origin Osmontian unless they have begun their Pathway to the True Source. |","...!","Noah possessed many concepts that had been severed by the Singed.","They had contributed 54 Severings to each weaving once they reached their halfway point. Now, with this pathway completed and a True Source attained, the Singed would continue its Severings.","In one sweeping motion...it would push them all 27 more times until every single one reached the Final Severed State!","Until they achieved 81 Severings and opened their own Pathways.","His Source of Ingeniare.","His Weavings of Paradox, Uncertainty, Farming, and so many more.","All would enter the Final Severed State.","All would begin their journeys toward becoming Pathways.","The bloodlines, distinctions, and weavings under the True Severed Origin Osmontian would form their own Pathway to a True Source.","The identities of Weaver of Existence and Extremity, they too would attain their Final Severed States.","Even the concepts themselves- of Extremity and Existence, were drawn in.","HUUM!","| The Severed Weavings of Existence itself begin to edge toward the Final Severed State and attain their Pathway to the True Source of Existence through the flames of the Singed. |","...!","Existence.","A terrifying concept.","Difficult to raise, even with the rarest of resources or loot.","It was never selected by the Limited Infinitum Weaving of Complexity.","Never caught in the calculations of the Golden Ratio.","It had only ever been slowly elevated bit by bit by the Singed.","And now, brought to its fifty-fourth Severing by that same flame, it surged toward its final Severing.","What it's Pathway would bring, what the True Source of Existence would become...Noah could only imagine.","But in that moment as his existence evolved to a shocking new stage of complexity, as the True Source of the Singed emerged...","Every part of him was pulled forward.","Willing or not.","His rising existence exploded with acceleration, and the many, many aspects that composed him surged as each went towards becoming a Pathway!","The weight of it all was tyrannical.","BOOM!","The massive flame cloaking him seethed, roared, trembled.","And in the distance, even the standing Origin Singed bore a look of wariness at the impossible purity now whirling around Noah like a storm forged by the purest of Existence itself!"]},{"number":3641,"title":"Chapter 3641: Chapter 3640 True! III","paragraphs":["The Origin Singed welcomed the sight of a new, profound purity.","Over the years, it had witnessed a few entities who surpassed the Weavings of Existence and were capable enough to attain a True Source.","It had even stood beside many entities who held True Sources and were now fighting alongside it in the Infinite Ravines.","Even if their complexity was higher, the level of purity this new entity exhibited... seemed unmatched. Even compared to itself!","How could a being in the distance obtain such purity?","That question buzzed through the mind of the Origin Singed as, at that moment, it turned to look behind towards an extremely distant location- one that very few, if any, even knew existed within the True Frequency of the Singed.","A place closest to the Wheel of Existence. Where, if one possessed enough purity, they might just catch a glimpse of it.","But that was bad.","Very bad.","Nobody should be able to glimpse the Wheel of Existence.","It was too pristine- its weavings too intricate to be observed or touched by any Existence.","Even the Singed dared not entrench upon its weavings. It left them untouched.","But what choice would this new entity make?","\"...\"","Choices.","They remained the one constant every existence had to make.","And depending on the choices made, existence could flow in a completely different direction!","—","BOOM!","The birth of a True Source was a unique phenomenon- so much so that even Noah paused, taking a few seconds to marvel at it.","When he had obtained the True Source Atlas of Existence, the sensation had already been profound. The choice to shape his own flow of existence, whether to align with the existing flow of the Wheel or to create his own divergent path, was unfathomable.","But this new source... it was even clearer. More defined.","He felt like an object floating in a vast sea- a sea filled with waves, twists, and turns. Most simply flowed with the tide, swept away by its overwhelming force.","Entities like him, the Great Usurper, the Queen of Matter, the Beyonder, the Peacemaker, and others- they all carried their own waves in this sea. Their mere movement could shift its flow in their vicinity.","But in the end, they were still within the sea.","Now, Noah had gained the ability to step out of it like a few others.","Others who were weaker may not be able to survive the separation, but he could.","The flames of the Singed burned with terrifying allure, elevated by this new True Source. It held far more flexibility than the Atlas of Existence, and his complexity had multiplied dramatically in a short period of time.","He could now feel it as he felt the endless flows of Existence that passed through frequencies all around him.","A convergence point where countless flows of the sea gathered.","Because even though the sea seemed endless, it didn't spread infinitely in all directions. All its countless weavings... were converging toward a single point.","If anyone wanted access to the vast sea, they had to pass through that one entry and exit.","And at this moment, Noah could sense that access point.","It was distant.","It was extremely far away!","But he knew what it was.","The Infinite Ravines.","His weavings shimmered with curiosity, his complexity rising as he began preparing for his next move.","His body's weavings in the Amarantos Dream churned.","He sat atop an obsidian-gold mountain, his upper body bare. Beside him lay Azzurra, the Lost Avatar of the Beyonder, breathing peacefully with closed eyes as her gorgeous figure was barely covered.","She looked... unburdened. The countless shackles that had weighed her down were vanishing.","Then, she heard Noah's voice beside her.","\"I have located the True Frequency of the Singed and obtained my True Source.\"","...!","He said it as casually as commenting on the weather.","Nonchalantly as if it was nothing much!","And yet—","BOOM!","Waves of immense complexity burst from Azzurra's body as the Trace Will of the Great Beyonder returned in full. It was almost like it had always been there and had not fully left.","\"What the fuck do you mean you've obtained a True Source? It's been less than an hour since I last talked to you—!\"","She had started with confusion but was abruptly silenced.","Because Noah's body erupted in a silent, blazing radiance- a white-gold flame that radiated nothing but the raw allure of a True Source.","\"...\"","Azzurra stared, stunned. Her dazed eyes looked as though they questioned the very foundation of reality.","\"You...\"","She had no words.","Noah simply smiled, looking toward her as he spoke.","\"I believe I can sense the Infinite Ravines where all those legends I've heard about are said to reside. I'll send one of my bodies over.\"","...!","He was ready to begin.","But before he could move, the Great Beyonder's expression shifted sharply as she shook her head and shouted,","\"No!\"","...!","\"No?\" Noah raised an eyebrow at her outburst.","She continued, her voice stern...as if she was about to unveil a secret she did not mention before.","\"Something all of us eventually realized in the Infinite Ravines...is that it's a place of Absolute Complex True Weavings. It...traps whatever True Source enters. Any entity with a True Source that has been channeled by the Wheel of Existence will have their entire Source locked down inside that place! That's why none of us have returned.\"","HUUM!","\"When the Wheel senses a constant threat bearing down on it, it shuts everything out. For the last few eons, the Infinite Ravines have been sealed. One can step out and experience the convergence point of all Existence's weavings. The Infinite Ravines can even elevate one's complexity further due to their brilliance. But so long as the Wheel still senses the approach of the dead things, it will remain closed to ensure nothing passes through. All of us...we've been inadvertently made into guards. Protectors of a home we can never return to unless we leave behind little threads of ourselves. Remnant Weavings. Trace Wills. Echoes that barely contain our true power.\"","...!","\"If we push too much True Source into them...we risk creating entanglements that link back to the Wheel, violating its will. One of us, driven mad after countless eons, tried returning. They sent over more than half their True Source forcefully...and during the chaos that followed because of his actions, an injured Dead Thing was able to pierce the Ravines and enter the weavings of the Wheel.\""]},{"number":3642,"title":"Chapter 3642: Chapter 3641 True! IV","paragraphs":["The words of the Great Beyonder were heavy, filled with the weight of shocking truths as Noah looked at her sternly.","The convergence point of the Absolute Complex True Source, the Wheel of Existence, was more like a prison. Nothing could enter or leave.","The native inhabitants of the Wheel of Existence had some leeway. They could send their Remnant Weavings or Trace Wills down. But ever since the Wheel shifted into a defensive state- bombarded from all sides of the Infinite Ravines by countless Dead Things, it had closed itself off entirely.","Any True Source that entered it was forced to remain there.","And if someone tried to force their way in like petulant children throwing a tantrum outside a locked house...","Well, a lot could go wrong!","One such legend had done exactly that. Tired of endless battles and the responsibility of protecting the Infinite Ravines, they tried to return- sending at least half of their weavings back into the Wheel of Existence.","The result? A Dead Thing slipped through.","Bob!","Noah's gaze sharpened as he stared at the Great Beyonder, who went on:","\"He tried to fix his mistake. Sacrificed that half of his True Source to destroy the thing he let in. We thought he succeeded, we thought only a tiny fragment of that Dead Thing remained, so small it would collapse on its own. We didn't expect it to survive, thrive...and rise stronger than ever within the Wheel of Existence where the rest of us can't even return.\"","...!","Noah remained silent, his weavings making rapid calculations, while the Great Beyonder continued.","\"We confirmed it's the True Source of an existence that gets locked within the Infinite Ravines. When we once brought a Prime Source Complexity Entity there, they could still go in and out, because the issue was only with True Sources. I believed the Wheel found True Sources difficult to manage inside itself and that's why it kept them out. But beings at the Prime Complexity level? That wasn't too difficult.\"","\"But all the Dead Things? They possess True Sources. They're dead, yes, but they can survive outside the umbrella of a Wheel of Existence, at least for a while...because of their powerful True Sources. In the Infinite Ravines, anything less than a True Source will be crushed. Ground down by the purity and convergence of existence. They wouldn't survive even a minute\"","Her gaze was heavy as she raised her eyes to him, almost pleading!","\"So no. Don't come. You're the first entity in ages to rise with a True Source...and also have someone like me to explain what's happening. Everyone else who attains a True Source? They all feel the same pull. That same brilliance of the convergence- the old weavings of the Wheel calling out towards the Infinite Ravines. And maybe...maybe that's the Wheel's intentional doing. Creating more guards for itself. Or maybe it's just how existence is woven as there is nothing inherently malicious with it. Maybe the constant attacks from Dead Things forced the Wheel into a defensive state...and that changed everything.\"","\"I don't know the full truth. I can't say the full truth. But if you step into the Infinite Ravines, the True Source you just forged- most, if not all of its power- will be pulled there. You'll find very little of your complexity remains behind.\"","WAA!","Her eyes held complex emotions. Through her words, one could sense doubt- not toward Noah, but toward the intentions of the Wheel itself.","The Wheel of Existence was not fair.","The Wheel of Existence was not kind.","It reacted instinctively to threats, and its changes were absolute.","As Noah finished listening, his gaze hardened with calmness. He asked the Great Beyonder.","\"If a True Source gets locked down in the Infinite Ravines, shouldn't it be fine...if the existence holds multiple True Sources? If only one Source is trapped, another Source can remain active within the Wheel.\"","...!","He spoke such wild, nonsensical words that the Great Beyonder couldn't help but blink, then burst into laughter.","\"Multiple True Sources in one existence? That's a dream, big guy. The Wheel of Existence itself is a single True Source. Any entity that raises their complexity high enough can only attain one. You're telling me that you, who just barely awakened your first True Source...already believe you can forge a second? A third? A True Source is the very definition of your existence. One cannot have multiple definitions.\"","She shook her head, a wry smile tugging at her lips. She had head some insane things lately, but this? This topped them all.","\"No. If you've awakened your True Source here, then use it. Cleanse the Wheel of Existence from the inside. Stop that Dead Thing from continuing to run rampant.\"","Noah looked at her valiant expression as he shook his head. She didn't believe him, and honestly...he didn't need her to.","He already had two True Sources.","The True Source Atlas of Existence, and now, the True Source of the Singed.","He simply gave her a calm look, saying nothing about the body of his that was already burning with the brilliance of the True Flame of the Singed as it departed the Infiniverse Megalos and entered that unfathomably dark expanse he only felt when he Severed his Weavings of Existence.","He didn't tell her how that part of him followed the flow of an endlessly vast sea headed toward the point of convergence. Whether the journey took hours or days...he did not know. But at least he had already begun.","What he did say was far more simple as he nodded.","\"With the attainment of a True Source, I can now more easily peer across the frequencies of existence. I'll find the Dead Thing and have a rematch.\"","His eyes glowed with luminous brilliance as he thought of Bob and his own complex weavings of existence now.","This time, after such a tremendous jump in complexity, how would he fare against a being that held two Absolute Complex True Source that were dead and shattered black and white Wheels?","The answer would only be found by trying.","And to locate Bob...","He turned his attention to his main body, still within the Infiniverse Megalos.","He was currently looking at the Queen of Matter, the Infiniverse Megalos Body positioned beside her, watching her as the weavings of the three states of existence swirling around her.","Matter. Dark Matter. Anti-Matter.","The Infiniverse Megalos sought to tap into the Fabled Weavings of Existence granted by the Queen of Matter. She sought to use her gaze to pierce the frequencies of existence and locate a single, slippery Dead Thing.","Add to that the fact that Noah's rise with the Singed's True Source had begun to ignite a True Flame within the very depths of the Infiniverse Megalos itself as its foundation built from Noah's weavings...its complexity was rising sharply.","And because of that, finding the hidden figure of Bob...was now only a matter of time!"]},{"number":3643,"title":"Chapter 3643: Chapter 3642 Existence! I","paragraphs":["Above the massive multicolored Infiniverse Vein of Existence that pulsed with intense waves of complexity that would put even Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity entities to shame.","The figures of the Infiniverse Megalos and the Queen of Matter stood at a small point of this Vein that was countless light-years long, with one of Noah's bodies standing near them as they sought to spread a search across frequencies to lock down a single enemy!","With Noah attaining a True Source while all other entities with such a level of power were supposedly pulled into the Infinite Ravines, he was the only one who could potentially face the terror that was Bob!","So he observed the nervousness on the Queen of Matter as the right hand of the Infiniverse Megalos was shimmering with light while it pierced into her chest.","As if it was playing and molding her Source of Existence itself, tweaking it in a way that only it understood!","But while this process was taking place...Noah's complexity was still continuing to surge.","And at this moment, one particular part of himself underwent its 81st Severing.","|The Pathway to the True Source of Existence has opened.|","HUUM!","A grandiose Pathway unfolded.","The Infiniverse Megalos and the Queen of Matter were forced to turn and gaze at Noah as around him, a stellar black radiance with hues of purple erupted and surged high.","And yet...it seemed like the start of something even more magisterial than that as within Noah's weavings, his True Source Atlas of Existence turned while the True Source of the Singed flickered.","Thereafter, all of Noah pulsed and radiated a glorious obsidian purple brilliance as his Complexity proceeded to have another massive jump, with prompts appearing right after to explain why!","|Your Existence has already attained the True Source Atlas of Existence.|","|Your Existence has already attained the True Source of the Singed.|","|Multiple parts of your Existence have already attained True Source as, by Definition, your Existence is and holds a True Source.|","BZZT!","|The Pathway to the True Source of Existence is traversed in an instant as, by its truest Definition, your Existence has long since become a True Source.|","...!","Noah's weavings radiated an intense luminosity.","His mind buzzed crazily as deep within him, there was a surge of unfathomable radiance as a third True Source bloomed!","The quickest that any True Source had bloomed in Existence, and it turned out to be for the weavings of Existence themselves.","Obsidian radiance that shone with stellar hues of wonder that made him seem entirely otherworldly flowed out.","The Queen of Matter looked in his direction and couldn't help but shake her head in wonder.","\"You are the coolest fucking existence I've ever come across...\"","She uttered those words even as the hand of a terrifying construct pulsed within her chest.","Noah's eyes radiated a stellar black brilliance as he felt the weavings of his third True Source being born. With its advent came a storm of new possibilities.","He felt the budding True Source of Existence communicating with him—its weavings speaking, teaching, and explaining what it truly meant to possess such a thing.","The first and foremost lesson: from this point forward, now that he had obtained the True Source of Existence, every single one of his weavings- those already on their own path toward becoming True Sources, would experience a terrifying acceleration.","Because he now held the True Source of Existence, the rest of his weavings were being pulled upward, as though they only needed to follow the thread.","Their destinations, their individual True Sources were now almost inevitable. All they needed was for him to attain a sufficient level of complexity in each to reach them!","The True Source of Existence would now permeate every one of them, ensuring that their progression would move ten times faster than before.","That was lesson one.","Lesson two dealt with existence itself.","As his body became layered in stellar obsidian radiance, his vision shifted. He looked at the Queen of Matter and the Infiniverse Megalos Body with new clarity. Slowly, he floated toward them and spoke.","\"Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter... at the end of the day, they're just different states of existence. They hold distinct differences and can never truly fuse with each other. But...if the True Source of Existence wraps around them?\"","He smiled.","\"They can only listen and follow.\"","HUUM!","As he spoke, he placed his hands on the shoulders of the Infiniverse Megalos Body. Her figure lit up, covered in the stellar obsidian radiance of the True Source of Existence.","The weavings were pumped into her, overflowing from her eyes as they shone with this terrifying light. At the same time, the hand that was sunk into the Queen of Matter's chest tightened its grip on her Source, and the authority of the True Source of Existence began to flow into her- into her Source of Fabled Matter.","\"Holy shiiiit!\"","The Queen of Matter screamed with equal parts shock and exhilaration as her Source, once purely Fabled Matter, began to expand.","She could feel it being torn apart and rebuilt at its very foundations.","From the surroundings, different flows of Dark Matter and Anti-Matter surged toward her Source, drawn in with force and purpose.","By every law of Existence, she should have exploded right there on the spot. The clash of such unstable states of existence should've ripped her apart with unimaginable instability.","And yet...","The stellar obsidian brilliance of the True Source of Existence stabilized the fusion. It prevented any disharmony between the three elemental states.","Then, the voice of the Infiniverse Megalos Body rang out.","\"The Source of the Queen of Matter has successfully been integrated with Dark Matter and Anti-Matter as well. Temporarily, the Fabled Tri-Matter Source of Existence has been born. I will now proceed to connect to their weavings and use the complexity of the Infiniverse Megalos itself to begin scanning frequencies blanketed in these same states of existence.\"","...!","Her words were heavy and powerful as in that moment, the Infiniverse Vein of Existence beneath them began to glow and vibrate, radiating terrifying brilliance in every direction.","From Noah, the stellar black radiance of the True Source of Existence spread outward, casting a dee hue across the surroundings- like paint across the fabric of Existence itself!","In front of him, the Queen of Matter raised her head.","Her eyes gleamed as obsidian beams of stellar light burst from within, and she laughed wildly and shouted:","\"I can feel so much! Haha, so, so much! So many Fables! So many stories!\"","Her laughter was one of crazed wonder.","Like someone who had been reading only one book her entire life...","And had just discovered there were two more she'd been missing all along!"]},{"number":3644,"title":"Chapter 3644: Chapter 3643 Existence! II","paragraphs":["Now, this moment could arguably be considered the happiest moment in the life of the Queen of Matter.","She had the man she idolized standing before her. Beside him towered the manifestation of a terrifying construct- something he had raised from a spiritual floating island. It was now somehow even larger than any Megalos she had seen as honestly, it could already be considered a full-on Frequency!","She had all of them before her, and the Construct''s manifestation had its very hand dug deep into their Source, which was currently expanded and reformed- transformed into something capable of handling multiple states of existence at once!","She could feel the Fables within each of them.","Her entire body was surrounded by swirling books that trembled with power, glowing with incandescent light as they recorded the Fables of all states of matter across all Frequencies.","But what this construct, what the Infiniverse Megalos Body was doing wasn't just viewing Fables across states and Frequencies.","It was searching for a single person's Fable across every Frequency and every possible state of existence that person had appeared in.","And it was doing this using someone else's Source.","After expanding it in an unfathomable way, its current usage being something the Queen of Matter herself could never even attempt, the Infiniverse Megalos Body was doing the impossible!","'Ah...am I actually playing a critical role in the Fable of the True Emperor of Quintessence? I didn't get absorbed into the Harem? I didn't get forgotten?!'","...!","Those were the thoughts dancing through the Queen of Matter's mind even as her own weavings expanded and spread across Frequencies to search.","The hunt for Bob had begun.","Opposite her, Noah's figure radiated a stellar obsidian brilliance as he turned in a certain direction and voiced an intent that was inaudible to most, but one that rippled through entanglement to reach a distant entity.","To the Great Usurper.","\"If you've started commandeering the souls of dead things within the Wheels of Existence surrounding Bob, can you pinpoint the location of those Wheels, or where he himself might be?\"","He sent the question, and it didn't take long for a reply to come.","\"Maybe. Possibly. But the moment I do that, he'll sense me and start purging my access. I've already usurped a few million weak ones as I climb toward the stronger ones. I could use them to get a general direction. But if you're already searching... are you confident you can secure a unilateral, absolute victory in just a few moves?\"","The Great Usurper knew Noah well.","They both preferred fights that ended quickly- it meant the gap in power was wide enough!","But Noah couldn't answer with confidence just yet as he looked at his Weavings. He simply replied,","\"This enemy this time is different. Compared to the others I've faced, I can't say for sure. But the last time I fought him, I didn't have a True Source. Now I do. So, we will see. Let me know if you can find a general direction. I've already cast a wide net across Frequencies as it might take a while.\"","...!","On the other end, the Great Usurper took a moment before responding, as if weighing his words.","\"I've begun searching for a more specific trail. The weavings of the Dead Wheels of Existence are murky, but...they have passed through the Frequency of Aqua, the Frequency of Gold, and the Frequency of Normada...\"","WAA!","As Noah received his words, he turned toward the Infiniverse Megalos Body and spoke aloud.","\"Focus the search on the Frequencies of Gold, Normada, and Time...\"","He didn't give exact coordinates- just places Bob may have passed through or could still be hiding in.","A massive search unfolded, all in pursuit of a grandiose Fable tied to a dead entity with multiple True Sources.","It was going to be a wondrous search as at such a time...","HUUM!","Noah's weavings vibrated with terrifying power. He turned his head sharply, his gaze cutting toward a direction not even within their current Frequency, but somewhere entirely different.","In the Frequency of Vigor.","Waves of white-green brilliance burst like oceans over verdant strings of existence within the Expanse.","Among those strings, the figures of Henry, the Emperor Penguin, Lilith, Erikson, the Primogenitor of Steel, and several others from the Infiniverse Megalos battled Lesser Source Complexity Faceless lifeforms, drawing upon the power of the True Severed Origin Osmontian to wield immense Complexity. They overwhelmed their enemies before any more Dark Towers could be constructed.","Everything had been going smoothly.","Until—","BOOM!","A Dark Tower tore through the veils between Frequencies, blooming in the heart of Vigor. Immediately, enormous Faceless entities emerged- radiating the might of Undeniable Telos Prime Sources.","At the forefront stood none other than Giuseppe!","The white bar on his head had hidden his face beneath the full suit of a Faceless lifeform as he was shining with lividity and rage as he roared.","\"You're his people?! Followers of Noah Osmont? You'll be dragged into the endless agony of the Wheel!\"","HUUM!","Behind him and three other Telos Prime Source beings, black-and-white Wheels of Existence exploded into motion, emitting a horrifying pull toward Henry and the others.","A horrific, slow grinding pull.","\"RAA!\"","The Emperor Penguin let out an enraged roar as its clone's weavings, and even the faint thread connecting to its main body, were dragged toward the spinning black and white Wheels.","It wasn't the only one. Everyone felt it, that strange, eerie sensation as if their very weavings were about to be swallowed by the Dead True Sources of Existence and lost forever.","A terrifying moment!","But then...","\"A mere pawn actually dares?!\"","A young voice rang out.","It was none other than Henry Osmont who stepped forward, his features uncannily similar to the True Severed Origin Osmontian. When Giuseppe saw him, he might as well have been looking at a younger version of Noah.","Rage overtook him as he locked onto Henry, focusing the Wheel's pull entirely on this single figure.","\"Are you his progeny?! A child of that man?! I'll torture you the most!\"","His voice was wild and chaotic, but before he could say another word, Henry's body ignited with a white-gold brilliance and proceeded to cover everyone behind him in radiant light.","White gold.","The True Flames of the Singed bloomed!","From the Son of the one who pioneered the True Source of the Singed, its power now bloomed.","He was young, yes- but the weavings of Nepotism among others made the impossible possible.","Even if it wasn't entirely his own, the power of a True Source flowed from him. And with it, he clashed head-on against the ghastly light of the Dead Wheels of Existence and entirely absolved the devouring force towards those he was with!"]},{"number":3645,"title":"Chapter 3645: Chapter 3644 Existence! III","paragraphs":["The weavings of Giuseppe burned with brilliance as black and white wheels were spiraling around him- even though he felt like he was going mad at this point.","The one he hated, and had already died from once- Noah Osmont...he had his people spread out across Frequencies. He had a Progeny. And the Despondent One had sent Giuseppe right toward them! He gave the simple command- draw them in through the Wheels of Existence.","A command Giuseppe should have been able to carry out without too many problems.","And yet...","And yet...!","\"You are his fucking progeny! Why the hell are you erupting with the allure of such complexity?!\"","Giuseppe couldn't help but bellow out his misgivings as he felt the effects of the terrifying black and white Wheels behind him, and the three other Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity entities near him...being completely nullified by white-gold flames erupting around Osmont's progeny.","Flames that seemed purer. More complex than even his own Source, and the Sources of the three others beside him combined!","This power seemed even stronger than his father's as it made absolutely no sense.","And yet, Giuseppe didn't know.","The weavings of the True Severed Origin Osmontian could be shared. His son, who had already stepped onto the Pathway to the True Source of the Singed before when he was choosing in the Infiniverse Megalos had his existence opened even further when his father attained the True Source. Through the weavings of Nepotism among others, it had all transferred seamlessly.","And in the middle of it all, the fantastical stellar black brilliance of the True Source of Existence itself stabilized everything.","At this moment, the figure of Henry didn't bother explaining anything. The mere fact that this being had tried to pull the very existence of him and those he held dear was a deed worthy of a cruel, interminable death.","His blue-gold hair flowed serenely in space as he called out calmly.","\"Ashes to Ashes. Dust to Dust.\"","WAA!","Ashes to Ashes, Dust to Dust!","A terrifying set of words.","The moment they echoed out, white-gold flames bloomed and painted the entire region.","Scratch that- not just the region, but the whole Frequency of Vigor.","The son of the True Severed Origin Osmontian channeled a True Source stemming from his father as he unleashed an attack that bathed entire an frequency in the unquenchable embers of the Flames of the Singed.","The moment these flames touched Giuseppe, the three Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity entities, and the hundreds of faceless life forms just beginning to pour out of the dark tower...","The moment the flames touched them, they began to turn to ash.","No contest. No resistance. No back and forth tug-of-war between complexities. The complexity of a True Source was just far too high.","And so, a scene repeated itself. Giuseppe appeared for a few seconds in the True Frequency of Flames not too long ago and was then eradicated in the next second, incinerated by a blazing sphere from the hands of the True Severed Origin Osmontian.","He appeared again, now for a few seconds in the frequency of Vigorbas the son of the man he hated- the son of the man he didn't know had already taken the one he considered the love of his existence.","That son voiced it out simply- Ashes to Ashes. Dust to Dust lm","And irradiated white-gold flames engulfed an entire frequency of existence.","After that, the figure of Giuseppe and all remaining Faceless Lifeforms...turned to dust.","HUUUM!","The figures of the Emperor Penguin, Lilith, Primogenitor of Steel, and many others had absolutely no words. They just stood there, watching in stunned silence at what had unfolded.","Far away from the Frequency of Vigor, Noah observed the scene coldly, his eyes bathing in the stellar obsidian brilliance of Existence.","\"It seems we're getting closer and closer. But for him to try and get my attention by going after my people...I can't say I'm not a little disappointed in such a move, Bob.\"","His voice was mesmerizing. His weavings were fully connected to the Infiniverse Megalos as he supported its efforts in tracking Bob across the Frequencies.","In his mind, the voice of the Great Usurper continued to echo- giving new, updated locations by the moment, and Noah passed them to the Infiniverse Megalos as her gaze swept through frequency after frequency that had anything to do with Bob's past weavings.","It was like a twisted game of existential hide-and-seek.","But the one hiding had sent assassins after his son and others he cared about.","And Noah's patience was wearing very thin.","Even the Loot Boxes of Existence regained from the weavings of Giuseppe and the three other Undeniable Telos Prime Source Complexity entities...didn't feel all that satisfying. Not with Bob feeling so close and beginning to get desperate!","The search was nearing its end.","Across the weavings of Existence...","Across an interminable, dark void where all frequencies could be accessed and many sections of the Wheel of Existence could be reached if one took a step in the right direction and had the complexity to traverse it.","This was the space Noah had arrived at when he first Truly Severed his existence.","He called it The Weave.","A void of interconnecting webs stretching endlessly, extremely difficult for even Sources to navigate. Only those who had obtained a True Source could traverse it freely.","Through the Weave, one could take a few steps with the right complexity and be able to traverse multiple frequencies.","And Noah was doing just that, guiding one of his bodies toward the Convergence Point of all the weavings of the Wheel.","An area rumored to hold an unknown number of Legends locked in battle against Dead Things.","He felt himself getting ever closer as he focused on his entanglements—trying to connect to those of the Beyonder so he could appear wherever her weavings were in the Infinite Ravines.","After all, when entering a new place...","Wasn't it better to have a local?"]},{"number":3646,"title":"Chapter 3646: Chapter 3645 Existence! IV","paragraphs":["To have a local when entering a new place.","These were Noah's thoughts as he had this body take on the majority of the weavings of the True Source of the Singed and prepared to have this Source pulled into this place and locked down there if need be, as the Great Beyonder uttered.","Because under the umbrella of the Absolute Complex True Source that was the Wheel of Existence, Noah felt that even a sliver of the True Source of Existence would be enough, and he had all of it.","The True Source of Existence- something he had only just begun to grasp. Jumping from a Pathway straight into a True Source, or exerting its brilliance on Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter was just the tip of the iceberg.","It had even allowed him to begin thinking of the final Source he would design for his True Source Atlas of Existence- one that would encompass all three states of existence!","So, while the True Source of the Singed neared the musings of the Infinite Ravines, the True Source of Existence...","\"Oh?\"","The body of Noah, burning with the white-gold flames of the Singed, turned and gazed toward a certain direction extremely far from where he stood.","There...","\"Found you.\"","A Dead Thing had been discovered.","The game of hide-and-seek was ending.","—","In the Prime Frequency of the Abyss.","There were many Prime Frequencies out there, but this one held the fewest number of existences by a staggering margin.","It didn't have countless quintillions of beings stretched across the Megalos and Expanse.","No Pantheons, Omniverses, or Dreadlands bursting with life.","Across the entire Prime Frequency of the Abyss, there were approximately 10,000 entities.","That's it.","Each one a was unique being that had managed to survive and thrive in an environment defined by manic, desolate weavings of existence. All 10,000 were Pioneers of Existence or Source Complexity entities.","In this place, vibrations of existence shredded perception and sanity. Reality bent and twisted, drifting outside of linear time and Euclidean space.","Violet-dark strings of existence threaded with spinning spikes stretched across vast, unfathomable regions. Some of these maddening strings clustered into massive structures that embodied both horror and wonder.","Simply existing here, standing still, could unravel, bend, or deform your very being unless your Source or Pathway protected you.","And if your existence could protect you, something strange would begin to happen.","Echoes.","Echoes of your own existence would glimmer in and out of space and time- phantom versions of yourself flickering with possible futures and probable pasts.","Echoes of Existence.","They were a reminder of just how terrifying and powerfully unique this frequency was. Aside from Hell Terra Firma, no other frequency matched its blend of isolation and complexity.","At this moment.","Upon a massive, naturally formed structure known by locals as the Spiral Dissonant Lexicon.","A winding staircase-like monument that extended across the Megalos and into the Expanse, looping endlessly, stretching from the top to the very bottom of the Prime Frequency of the Abyss...","Entirely violet in color, pulsing with tendrils of Entropy, Chaos, and Destruction.","Bob sat on one of its stairs- stairs that alone extended for light-years.","And as he sat, two Echoes of Bob manifested- violet, illusory versions of himself standing, flying, or moving elsewhere.","Every few seconds, more Echoes appeared in different positions, showing him taking other possible actions.","This happened to every entity who survived the unraveling weavings of this frequency.","Bob's bold figure overlooked storming violet-black weavings of existence, the air tinged with violet lightning and flames that coasted across light-years.","\"In my Wheel of Existence, I had a frequency just like this. I was born in it. Its weavings were stronger, heavier, and much more dreadful than even here. Only a hundred of us survived and thrived in that entire frequency. Can you imagine that? A hundred complex beings in a whole frequency of existence? The loneliness, the desolation, the level of power, and the potential of such beings. In such a place, to find companionship, to have a family...you would be unfathomably lucky.\"","Bob's voice was tinged with melancholy.","From the gaps of existence not far away, Noah had arrived at some unknown time.","His gaze was cold and filled with interminable brilliance as he examined the uniqueness of this Prime Frequency. Around him, violet-purple Echoes of himself already began to manifest.","One Echo looked back with tyranny in his eyes. Another floated toward Bob, roaring before dispersing, replaced by more phantom selves.","Noah looked at the massive winding staircases larger than countless Omniverses stacked together. He and Bob stood on a single spiral of a structure simmering with lightning and flame- a representation of chaos and destruction itself.","He walked calmly as Bob continued.","\"I find it unique that the same, or similar frequencies appear across different Wheels. It shows that, in the end, everything stems from the same Source. That we're all connected through something larger we don't yet understand.\"","Bob's voice turned philosophical, his thoughts drifting to times long gone.","Echoes of himself appeared and disappeared, while Noah's body was now surrounded by the scintillating stellar black radiance of the True Source of Existence. He finally spoke, turning away from Bob, staring at the violent beauty of this place.","\"You sent your Dead Things after my son. And my people. You and I have been clashing since before then as everything was fine. That action...disappointed me deeply.\"","...!","\"I sensed something closing in. Something narrowing my possibilities into a single, inevitable confrontation. So I tried to buy time. Gain more leverage if I could. Their lives wouldn't have been in true danger. I would've kept them in my Wheel until I achieved my goal.\"","He spoke calmly. Almost as if talking to an old friend or colleague.","Bob nodded with understanding, even smiled.","\"I sensed something closing in. Something narrowing my possibilities into a single, inevitable confrontation. So I tried to buy time. Gain more leverage if I could. Their lives wouldn't have been in true danger. I would've kept them in my Wheel until I achieved my goal.\"","Dreadful words.","Noah's eyes flashed coldly.","Echoes around him erupted with obsidian flame and then vanished.","Leverage.","That's all Bob considered his son and his people.","Sensing Noah's rising fury, Bob shook his head and looked away, gazing at his tentacled limbed hands.","\"You wouldn't understand where I come from. Why I do what I do. Every creature across existence has its own reason to move, to act. I don't feel the need to explain mine. All you need to know is that I must reach the core of this Wheel of Existence. Not to taint or destroy it. I've tried that. I failed. I carry quintillions of souls because of such an action as they are screaming in my ears every second for the past eons.\"","...!","\"I've learned. I won't subject more beings to death and pain. I only need access to the core- a possible pathway to something neither you nor I could comprehend. Some Wheels don't even have that pathway. But this one might. Its vibrant complexity could hold a clue to what innervates the Wheels themselves. The Great Usurper must have told you about that, right?\"","HUUM!","Bob's dreadful words hung heavy in the air. Noah gave a slight nod, his body glowing brighter with stellar black light as he turned his gaze back toward Bob who continued.","\"I don't need a fight. I don't want anything else. I just need direction. I need to access the True Frequencies that began pulsing after you opened the True Frequency of the Singed. I need time. Nobody, and I repeat- nobody...has to get hurt.\"","...!","No one has to get hurt.","Bob said it like a cold plea, but Noah's eyes turned colder than ever. Echoes of himself appeared every few seconds, most laced with raw tyranny.","And he asked, voice sharp as a blade:","\"Who are you planning to hurt? If things don't go your way, what leverage do you already have?\"","...!","If Bob saw Noah's son and people as leverage once...what else might he be hiding?","Bob nodded lightly.","\"I hold with me the musings of multiple Nodes of Existence tied to frequencies. If we remain here, just talk, everything remains intact. But if we go primitive, if we fight, those frequencies will crumble. Countless lives will be lost. And neither of us wants that. Especially not you, friend\"","...!"]},{"number":3647,"title":"Chapter 3647: Chapter 3646 Existence V","paragraphs":["The coldness in the region of the Prime Frequency of the Abyss was bone-chilling.","In the Spiral Dissonant Lexicon- a massive, stair-like structure extending across this Frequency, the visage of Bob stared calmly at the True Severed Origin Osmontian as he laid out his leverage.","He held multiple Nodes of Existence, each with the power to make or break Frequencies themselves.","Countless lives and weavings of existence resided in each, and he wielded several of these Frequencies as leverage!","And even with all that, he had still sent others to capture Noah's people- just for a little more leverage. Just to be as prepared as he could be as he was this close to finding a way into a True Frequency of Existence. Though unsuccessful in getting more leverage, it revealed his obsession with control in the current moment.","He sighed.","\"Friend, I've made some mistakes in my past- many of them, in fact. I'm paying for them even now. I know the dead and the living don't mix. I made the mistake of connecting a dead Wheel of Existence to one that was alive, and I have been paying for that mistake ever since. All those lives.\" He paused, then offered a rueful chuckle. \"What do you humans say? Everybody makes mistakes? And those who learn from them, those who try their best not to repeat them...those are the ones who are truly human.\"","You humans.","Noah absorbed the words coldly. He remembered the musings of the Alchemist Ashmole who once looked him in the eye and said he wasn't human at all.","With his weavings of the True Source of Existence, he knew well where he stood as he didn't reply to this.","He didn't want a psychological sparring match with the entity before him. So he simply responded, cold and sharp.","\"This is a fascinating monologue you've got going. Any chance you're nearing the end?\"","...!","His gaze didn't shift. His body was cloaked in a stellar obsidian luster brimming with power and threatening to overflow.","It was the allure of a terrifying True Source of Existence, and it was only getting started! Even Bob seemed to regard it with a glimmer of caution as he gave it a few looks.","Behind Bob, dreadful black-and-white wheels manifested silently as he looked back at Noah and spoke softly.","\"You're angry.\"","...!","Angry?","He was angry?","Noah shook his head.","\"No. I'm not angry. I'm pissed.\"","HUUM!","Around him, the illusory echoes of alternate versions conjured forth, flickers of possibility...stilled.","As if, through sheer will, Noah had frozen even the shifting threads of potential and possibilities spawned by the Prime Frequency of the Abyss.","Bob's expression turned grimmer. He raised his tentacled hands and revealed dazzling Nodes of Existence shimmering between them.","\"I really don't want it to come to this. When two unstoppable forces meet, they often choose to clash. But there are other routes. There is dialogue one could have. There is a level of understanding to be given to both sides.\" His voice softened as he uttered lastly. \"I thought, at least, that you would understand.\"","...!","\"Your Wheel of Existence will remain untouched. I just need to see what it is- to confirm something. If it truly leads to what Innervates all Wheels. I just need to find the missing piece. If I do, I can revive a dead Wheel. My actions and every single thing that I am doing right now...they could save countless lives across two whole Wheels of Existence.\"","He continued, eyes earnest.","\"This isn't some grand, evil plan. I'm saving lives. I'm rewriting terrible mistakes, ensuring they never repeat. Why stand in the way of that? Why not simply consider that my path might actually be possible? We could enter a True Frequency of the Wheel together. There, everything would be made clear.\"","...!","Bob's words were terrifying in their simplicity. He spoke to Noah about imagining a different outcome.","\"It could all be so simple,\" he added, as he plucked a Node from the cluster and held it delicately between two tentacles.","\"In every Wheel of Existence, there are always one or more entities that rise above the rest. In your Wheel, there's you and a few others. Anomalies. In mine, there was only me.\"","He leaned in slightly.","\"My complexity is unlike any anomaly you've met. Behind me are two Dead Absolute Complex True Sources. I bear them. They draw from me, and I draw from them- even in death.\"","Then his voice dropped low.","\"But more than that, you remember, don't you? I have my own Source.\"","WAA!","\"Khaos. I never lied about that, friend. I've been slowly regaining clarity on it. So while you may have attained a True Source in the midst of this chaos somehow, I hold the equivalent of three.\"","His voice now held weight, grief, and pride mixed alongside everything else!","\"We could fight. But even on my worst day, I doubt I'd lose to you. And if we do fight? The death toll will be obscene. It will make me infinitely sadder. But I can bear the burden of death. I don't think you can.\"","As he spoke, he raised the Node of a normal Frequency like a man drawing a final line in the sand.","His eyes held no cruelty, no triumph.","Only sincerity.","As he looked at Noah, he waited for the choice.","The decision.","As always, it came down to a choice.","And in that moment, the visage of the True Severed Origin Osmontian looked toward Bob with chilling apathy.","A response. A verdict!","\"The dead and the living do not mix.\"","No matter how sweet the words Bob used.","No matter how twisted his logic.","No matter how simple he made it all sound.","\"If we just do this,\" or \"Let me into the true frequency and I'll find the answer\"...","None of it mattered.","The core truth remained unchanged.","The dead and the living do not mix.","The moment these words were spoken, Bob sighed and closed his eyes...","And crushed the Node of Existence in his hands!"]},{"number":3648,"title":"Chapter 3648: Chapter 3647 Existence! VI","paragraphs":["The crushing of a Node of Existence.","A Node was no trivial thing. And when Bob crushed it, he didn't just use brute strength.","There was a flash of silver-white radiance. One could see it clearly—he had called upon the Primal Flame of the Wheel of Existence to achieve this terrifying effect.","And Bob didn't just crush a Node.","His weavings surged. Behind him, within the Spiral Dissonant Lexicon, a massive illusory screen appeared—revealing the weavings of the Frequency of Gold.","Surrounded by endless golden brilliance, this was a realm of unfathomable wealth and beauty. And in the next moment, the screen showed the actual flow of the Wheel within this frequency...beginning to fracture.","Lifeforms began to appear on the screens—multitudes of them—as reality itself shattered around them like fragile glass.","When this glass broke, it didn't do so quietly.","Many entities, to their horror, found that they couldn't channel any power at all. Their connection to the Wheel had been cut. Severed!","They were locked out of reality.","Space cracked. Fissures spread. Creatures in the path of these splits were torn apart—eyes dimming of all brilliance—fading shortly after.","The illusory screen behind Bob shifted rapidly. It showed countless regions of the Megalos—the grand expanse of the Frequency of Gold, which he had just erased with a single crushed Node.","And he had done it...with his eyes closed.","Essence of desolation and regret radiated from him, as if he truly hadn't wanted to take this step.","\"I hear them.\"","His voice echoed out—low, mournful.","But Noah stared at him with eyes colder than the Abyss. Any remnants of goodwill, any flicker of redemption that might've once existed was gone.","This being had just made a conscious choice to destroy an entire Frequency of Existence.","And Noah already knew what he was about to say next.","\"That didn't need to happen, my friend. And it still doesn't. I have a dozen more Nodes of Existence. This can stop right now. Let's not descend into something primitive. Let's rise above our baser selves. Let's do something...we'll actually be proud of.\"","His words were polished. Persuasive. Coated in idealism.","But toward this creature who had just annihilated an entire Frequency of Existence, Noah raised his hand and formed a fist.","Within that fist, a convergence of blinding, stellar obsidian brilliance began to bloom.","The weight of a True Source of Existence gathered there as he said, coldly.","\"Echoes of the Unwritten.\"","HUUM!","Echoes of the Unwritten.","Four words. New, even to Noah. And by the look on his face—new to Bob, too.","Bob's brows furrowed.","And then...his eyes widened.","The illusory screen behind him—once dark and lifeless from the destruction it displayed—suddenly flickered to life. The events it had shown began to play in reverse.","Reality, once fractured, began to reform.","Shattered space knitted itself back together. Entities returned to life. The Frequency of Gold...healed.","It all unfolded uniquely and rapidly. In seconds, the entire destruction sequence had been undone. The screen vanished.","And in Bob's two tentacles...the Node of Existence he had crushed reappeared—reborn from a blinding singularity.","...!","Bob's eyes flared with light, staring at the unbroken Node now resting in his hand.","It was there.","As real as it had ever been.","The sheer impossibility of it made his inner complexity buzz. He turned and summoned another set of limbs, weaving more complexity into being. Another illusory screen appeared, showing the Frequency of Gold once more.","Intact.","Untouched.","Bob stared at it, his expression growing darker and more severe.","Far in the distance, Noah stood surrounded by rippling waves of True Source of Existence, his body blazing with obsidian radiance.","He spoke again.","\"Existence is a unique thing. When one attains the True Source of Existence, one of the abilities it bestows is something called... Echoes of the Unwritten.\"","HUUM!","\"It grants the power to undo—or redo—any event in existence. There are limitations, sure...but I don't need to tell you that. All you need to know is this- from here on out? You can destroy any Frequency of Existence you want. And right after... I'll undo that event.\"","...!","Noah's words were horrifying in their certainty. What he did was not something that one could attribute the reversal of time or even the reversal of Causality itself.","What he undid were the very weavings of existence themselves!","As he spoke, the True Source of Existence pulsed within him as it continued communicating with him. Guiding him.","This was the truth of the True Source.","Attaining it was not the end.","Attaining the True Source of Existence wasn't the final step. It was only the beginning.","The weavings of reality were vast—beyond imagination. And only after one claimed the True Source could they truly awaken to the infinite possibilities they could undertake with it.","To the alterations that could be made.","The only real limitation was complexity.","Because Noah's complexity had reached such terrifying heights, he had become capable of using Echoes of the Unwritten—able to reach into the strands of what could've been, and force one strand into being.","He had looked into the branches of probability where Bob destroyed and didn't destroy the Frequency of Gold, and chosen the path he preferred.","The one where the Frequency remained.","And just like that...he had become capable of undoing anything someone in front of him did—so long as it hadn't happened too far in the past.","Even if the action hadn't taken place right in front of him.","So long as it was recent?","He could unravel it.","It was terrifying. It was a sort of power that made even him take a pause when the weavings of the True Source of Existence spoke to him!","A power that made Bob pause—still holding the Node of Existence that just moments ago had been crushed and lost.","And now...it was perfectly whole again.","Meanwhile, Noah's body continued to shine with an even more scintillating stellar obsidian brilliance.","The True Source of Existence within him was only just waking up.","And it was beginning to show itself with terrifying fervor."]},{"number":3649,"title":"Chapter 3649: Chapter 3648 Existence! VII","paragraphs":["Bob silently stared at the Node of Existence in his hands.","It had been destroyed by him moments ago, and yet in the next instant, it was wholly undone in a fantastical way.","He looked at the Node as if, deep down, he knew this wasn't some lesser reversion or reversal of causality. That this was the genuine undoing of existence itself!","\"You've found yourself a truly terrifying Source, my friend.\"","His voice was honest.","He let the words linger as the action Noah had just performed was something that demanded, even from someone as horrifying as Bob, silent applause.","\"But still...\"","Bob's eyes flickered. Behind him, the black and white wheels began to turn, radiating an eerie aura of power.","Even they, however, remained subdued as from Bob himself, a hazy violet light began to bloom.","Violet.","An extremely dense and pure violet erupted around his body. It was the reveal of the true weavings of none other than...","\"Khaos.\"","Bob spoke lightly.","His eyes held a trace of reluctance as he shook his head and continued.","\"I actually did my best not to utilize the True Source of Khaos within another Wheel of Existence. I didn't attempt to draw upon this Source because even though it's mine, even though my weavings manipulate it...the effect it has on existence is too widespread. Too chaotic. It taints and ruins the very flow of the Wheel, even if I never wish it to. It causes an eruption of absolute entropic energy that leaks across Frequencies. I did not want to use this True Source. But you, my friend...you're forcing my hand.\"","...!","The violet light became unbearably intense as Bob closed his eyes.","His eyes were already closed as if he knew the answer. And even though he didn't need to physically look at Noah, his voice echoed out clearly, surrounded by irradiant, stellar obsidian weavings of authorial force.","\"To fight is to be primitive. Even now, dialogue and understanding would be ideal. Even now, I ask again...can we come to an understanding?\"","...!","His eyes were already closed as if he knew the answer. And even though he didn't need to physically look at Noah, his voice echoed out clearly, surrounded by irradiant, stellar obsidian weavings of authorial force.","\"We are way past understanding.\"","A simple answer.","And toward such an expected answer, Bob had his own.","He whispered as if he were cradling a newly born baby.","\"Fractal Collapse.\"","...!","HUUM!","Space around him began to crack like a spiderweb.","No, not space. What was cracking and breaking apart was Existence itself!","Around Bob, reality shattered as if it had never been there to begin with. And in its place, the unraveling of Khaos spread.","\"You can undo events within the bounds of Existence. But what if Existence turns chaotic- becomes absent entirely? Would you still be able to undo the weavings then?\"","Bob spoke serenely. Only an instant had passed, and yet the cracking, the shattering of Existence, had already spread across multiple light years.","And it didn't look to be slowing down in the slightest- it began to consume the Frequency itself.","The Spiral Dissonant Lexicon beneath them instantly shattered, becoming pieces of dissonant violet brilliance. The weavings of the Abyss seethed, their very existence being torn apart as they seemed to cheer it on!","Around Noah and Bob, the entire landscape turned into one of immeasurable Khaos.","Bob's form vibrated. His limbs exploded into kaleidoscopic chaos- countless tentacles spreading through the collapsing, unwinding fabric of reality.","\"I didn't want to use Khaos. Because as you can see, once entropy is unleashed, its effects run wild. Soon, this entire Frequency of the Abyss will be covered. After that, Khaos will spill into other Frequencies. The more that are consumed, the closer we come to something unbearably unique. I'll tell you now, so you can possibly stop it in time. Once enough weavings of Khaos have spread, there will be a Paradoxical Collapse of Certainty. Existence itself will begin to unravel on a massive scale. The Flow of Existence will collapse. And within the bounds of True Khaos...even True Sources may begin to doubt themselves.\"","...!","Bob uttered terrifying words as his response to Noah's unwinding of an event was releasing his True Source in kind.","Noah's weavings shimmered as he looked upon the continuing collapse- the chaotic, barely visible weavings of Existence that consumed the entire Frequency.","Reality had become an array of unstable weavings that were haphazard, empty, or undone.","And yet, even so...","HUUM!","Existence was still present.","No matter how chaotic it had become under Bob's influence, it was still there- fractured or not.","And so long as it had not entirely collapsed...","Noah raised a single finger toward the shattering existence above.","A finger that pulsed with an incandescent singularity of stellar obsidian brilliance.","On it surged endless waves of the True Source of Existence. And his answer to the collapsing chaos around him?","It was a simple one.","\"Existential Proliferation.\"","WAA!","His raised hand pulsed. From the singularity of stellar obsidian mass, a sea of existence erupted.","If Bob was collapsing and erasing existence itself?","Then Noah would drown everything in the overflowing brilliance of his Weavings of Existence!","From that single finger, the seas of stellar obsidian Existence poured out- flooding billions of light years in an instant. They continued to spread rapidly across the Frequency.","Even his son, wielding another True Source, had once bathed an entire Frequency. How could Noah not do something far more?","BZZT!","The collapsing, chaotic Existence stalled. The spiderweb-like fractures began to fill.","The torn, decimated weavings of reality—like a ruined painting—were made anew.","Yet Bob's influence lingered. Khaos continued to spread madly.","More spiderwebs appeared—Existence itself fracturing. But each time, mere moments later...seas of billowing obsidian Existence surged forth and filled the gaps.","A terrifying display of mastery.","Bob looked once more at Noah and sighed.","\"I collapse Existence and introduce uncertainty. And you try to restore it. But how long can this continue before the Wheel's very flow is affected and collapses? I never wanted to become primitive. But if you force me, my friend...there is no going back.\"","A final warning.","And Noah, radiating waves of stellar obsidian Existence—became wholly immersed in it. Behind him, massive wings unfurled, made of blinding stellar light. Halos of obsidian radiance spun behind him like unfathomable disks, ready to unleash the beams of the True Source of Existence at any moment.","His eyes—no longer eyes—had become singularities of the blackest Megalos.","And with rising majesty in his voice, he replied simply.","\"Let's. Fucking. GO.\"","HUUM!","Boundless authority rose as the True Severed Origin Osmontian abandoned all hope of diplomacy.","The figure of Bob stopped holding back. The smile faded from his face. His jaws unhinged—stretching end to end—as his limbs exploded outward like a kaleidoscope.","BOOM!","A single punch.","And it was enough to collapse the weavings of Existence nearby—except those around Noah. The punch's force carried them directly into The Weave.","SIUU!","Even the blackness of the Weave shattered. When Bob retracted his arm, Noah's obsidian halos unleashed beams of Existence, restoring everything in their path.","They reappeared in a new place.","In a Frequency.","No longer the Abyss.","Bob's single punch had shattered everything nearby. Noah had filled it back in. But the blow had already hurled them through an entirely different Frequency of Existence!","This would be a battle of unfathomable proportions.","On one side, a budding entity, just now awakening to the full depth of a newly claimed True Source.","On the other, an ancient being, recovering his complexity- his Source too unstable for most to even comprehend.","These two cosmic forces now clashed under the umbrella of an Absolute Complex True Source—one seeking to reach the core and ignite it, not to toy with it, but to find something he desperately needed. The other? He fought to protect what was left after entire Frequencies had already collapsed. After entire Wheels of Existence had shattered behind a man who sought even more change.","But the only change he was destined to find...was the desperation to restore what he could not.","And with that...all he would bring was the collapse of another Wheel of Existence as it would be disastrous!","Each entity had their reasons, their ideals.","But at this moment, all that remained was their complexity.","And their complexity alone."]},{"number":3650,"title":"Chapter 3650: Chapter 3649 Existence! VIII","paragraphs":["As a terrifying battle erupted- one that could shift its landscape from frequency to frequency at any moment, there were very few who could claim to have witnessed it.","Very few.","And yet, from the frequency Noah and Bob had just departed.","The Frequency of the Abyss.","An illusory nine-pointed circle began to bloom high above the nearly decimated Spiral Dissonant Lexicon.","The circle pulsed with unique weavings and interlocking sockets. It was an Enneagram, glowing with unstable threads of a Wheel. It almost resembled and pulsed with an air of a True Source, but it was far too chaotic.","Unstable.","Incomplete.","As if parts of it had been missing all along, only now beginning to be made whole again.","To become what it was truly meant to be.","From the center of that shining illusory star, the figure known as the Peacemaker emerged.","His entire form flickered, ethereal- more suggestion than substance, as if he wasn't truly here at all.","He looked down at the decimation of existence- at the scars of Khaos that had spread briefly through this place. Then, he shook his head.","His complexity wasn't enough, not for this. As much as he longed to act, to intervene, he simply wasn't ready.","So he continued his search, looking for the pieces he needed to complete his Enneagram. And maybe, just maybe, he would one day enact the kind of Peace that wouldn't require him to look over his shoulder for eons to come...wondering whether a certain bald, tentacle-limbed being was still alive or dead.","Well, even more dead than he was already dead!","Just as quickly as he came, the Peacemaker vanished.","The illusory nine-pointed star that had heralded his arrival flickered out of existence.","And amidst all these fantastical weavings, there was one more witness.","This being's soul and will were scattered across many points, many spaces- but now, in this moment, he focused himself. He began a thorough assault, stretching his fragmented soul into the weavings of two Absolute Complex True Sources.","Well...dead ones, anyway.","In a silent frequency untouched by battle, the figure of the Great Usurper sat atop a black tower. His gaze was narrowed, filled with somber concentration.","He had sensed the beginning of a battle between two unfathomable entities—and amidst the chaos, he struck.","He would use this instability to his advantage.","His target? The countless dead souls sealed within the Dead Wheels of Existence that Bob carried. If he could claim them...","He might disrupt Bob's usage of them and granting Osmont an edge.","Or...Bob might prove powerful enough to cleanse the intrusion entirely.","But the Usurper could feel it- these countless lifeforms, wailing in pain within the Dead Wheels- they weren't just echoes. They were components of the Wheels themselves.","If he could take them all...","With their power—alongside the chaotic complexity of existence—couldn't he command the Dead Wheels himself?","It was dangerous.","After all, the one he was attempting to siphon from, this being called Bob....was the most complex entity within this Wheel of Existence.","Even more than Osmont.","And his power was growing rapidly.","But still, the Great Usurper moved.","Because if Bob, the Dead Thing, held such terrifying power...","One had to wonder...","How powerful were the other dead things the legends whispered about and fought against?","The ones whose names were forgotten...","The ones the protectors of the Wheel held nightmares of in the Infinite Ravines?","—","\"The Infinite Ravines...\"","Noah's voice echoed out softly.","His body—housing the True Source of the Singed—arrived at a uniquely strange junction within The Weave.","After traversing at a terrifying velocity—fast enough to cross from one Frequency to another in an instant—he felt as though he'd passed the equivalent of hundreds of millions of Frequencies.","It was unreal.","But now, he stood at a threshold.","The darkness of The Weave collapsed ahead of him into an expanse of white.","Endless white.","Yet it wasn't merely a transition from black to white. It was a convergence—a fusion of such incredible complexity and brilliance, that the moment he stepped out of the blackened Weave, he would be transported somewhere wholly new.","A place one could only enter with a True Source.","The Infinite Ravines.","When Noah finally arrived at this point, he saw that taking a single step into the junction between black and white could send him to vastly different places within the Ravines.","But he was focused.","Focused on the entanglement, the one between him and the Great Beyonder.","As he contemplated his next move, it came—a pull from his True Source. It told him that a very specific position on his left side held the path.","Any step—except that one—would send him somewhere impossibly far from her.","Incalculable in distance, even if measured in the scale of entire Frequencies.","This proved something undeniable.","The Infinite Ravines wasn't just an endpoint or gateway of an Absolute Complex True Source.","It was a dimensionally vast space!","Vaster than the concept of distance itself.","As he stood there, Noah's distinction of the Weaver of Existence buzzed to life.","And of all the distinctions, this stood above the rest, empowered by the True Source of Existence itself.","He held the True Source of Existence. So...why shouldn't his distinction reveal everything about the existence he saw?","His eyes shimmered, constantly feeding back information.","Dozens of prompts appeared and vanished.","Even the correct step, the one that would take him to the Great Beyonder, was highlighted by his Weaver of Existence with a green arrow flashing above it.","And so...","He breathed out.","And he stepped forward.","Existence buzzed.","It flickered.","He moved forward, illuminating his weavings using the True Source of the Singed alone to anchor himself here.","His Distinction buzzed again, feeding him critical truths of his surrounding Existence.","|Part of your Weavings of Existence have taken a nearly irreversible leap away from the Loose Cover of an Absolute Complex True Source.|","|Part of your Weavings of Existence are stepping into the Strict Cover of an Absolute Complex True Source.|","|The light of your True Source is capable of surviving the transfer into the area designated as the Infinite Ravines.|","The information flowed freely as Noah felt the subtle, infinite shifts.","He could feel the freedom within strictness, the strength hidden within fragility.","It was paradoxical...and yet, he was drawing closer.","Closer to the place where the weavings of the Great Beyonder awaited.","|The Weavings of your Existence are arriving at a region within the Infinite Ravines.|","|This region has been analyzed and distinguished as the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality. |","...!","| Here, an unknown Wild True Source permeates the Hollow Cascade. The Causality of Existence is reversed constantly. |","|Cause follows effect. Enemies may bleed before they are struck. Time flows backward. Weavings unwind.|","|Your True Source must adapt, or your very existence will become unwound.|","...!"]},{"number":3651,"title":"Chapter 3651: Chapter 3650 Exodus! I","paragraphs":["The Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.","This was the domain where the Great Beyonder resided.","Noah's weavings of existence trembled as the True Source of the Singed wrapped tightly around him—protecting him from the ravages of Causality itself. Upon his arrival, he felt his True Source being converged upon and pulled into this place with terrifying force.","It was as if the Source was being displaced, forced to exert its power only within the Infinite Ravines, and nowhere else.","He could resist it.","He knew that with his True Source Atlas of Existence, and the True Source of Existence itself, he might actually withstand this undeniable force—not because it was opposing his Source, but because it ensured that 99.9% of it would remain anchored in the endlessly vast regions of the Ravines, where even the concept of distance was a paradox.","But for now, he allowed himself to flow with it.","Within moments, his weavings buzzed, and he fully crossed from The Weave into a new domain.","A domain that instantly caused his True Source to flare, white-gold flames of the Singed erupting protectively around him as the atmosphere trembled with existence-altering force.","\"This...\"","...!","He heard his voice.","But he hadn't opened his mouth yet.","His lips parted only a breath later, and in that moment, he understood.","He had truly arrived in the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.","The effect had occurred before the cause.","He heard himself before speaking.","And more than that—if his True Source hadn't instinctively enveloped him, his weavings of existence would already be destabilizing. Time flowed in every direction here. Without protection, the Wild True Source of this domain would begin to unravel a being, regressing them to the point they'd never even been born!","HUUM!","His surroundings buzzed with the weight of compressed paradox.","Then slowly...they came into focus.","Noah stood upon a field of stellar grains, silver-purple sands that shimmered like ground-down stars.","All around him...","Shattered Crystalline Megalos Seas floated in space. Rivers and waterfalls surged upward from them—flowing into the skies, crashing into floating landmasses and suspended lakes.","And the sky...","The Weaver of Existence buzzed loudly, displaying exactly what Noah was seeing.","[Skies of the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality. A dome of reflected true and false futures of causality. Some are real. Others are deceptive, born from the Wild True Source of Causality.]","...!","Above, light-years away, layers of complex illusions pulsed constantly.","Some showed the lands breaking apart in one timeline. Others showed them untouched. And others still...showed himself.","Illusory figures of Noah appeared in the distant skies, flickering across divergent threads and possibilities.","One scene showed his golden flaming robes fluttering—then unraveling, along with his body.","Another showed him flying through the Cascade, only to be struck with the terrifying consequence of failure here.","Chrono-Fragmentation.","In that thread, his mind and existence were pulled into infinite possibility loops, spiraling endlessly into what-ifs until even his weavings began to collapse in on themselves.","Yet another illusory thread showed him standing still as a dark-haired woman materialized beside him, scoffing.","Her voice arrived before her figure.","And then...","He heard a voice that was oddly familiar.","\"My dear Wild True Source of Causality... I thought we were getting along by now. I've grown immune to your complexity after all these years. Why try to unravel my weavings again?\"","\"Now you bring the causality of the one man I've been with after eons? To what, trigger an emotional fluctuation? You should know I'm not some weak woman. That man hasn't been critical to me for eons, and even if he knows some good tricks with Dual Cultivation, I'll be fine even if he was gone. You don't need to use his image to deceive me.\"","...!","The voice of the Great Beyonder echoed into Noah's ears before she'd even arrived.","She was clearly being drawn in by the presence of a dazzling True Source that shouldn't be here.","And yet...she didn't believe it was him.","She believed it was just another trick of reversed causality—another illusion from the Hollow Cascade meant to manipulate her.","BZZT!","Just ahead of Noah, standing on the shimmering sands of stellar grains...","A gorgeous figure emerged, radiating terrifying waves of complexity.","Her complexity felt vastly greater than Noah's in this moment—both pure and intricately woven.","And it all converged into a single woman:","Dark hair. Equally dark eyes.","A vivacious form wrapped in a stellar obsidian robe that glowed with trillions of True Source runes.","Her face carried the timeless weight of ancient beauty and age. As she appeared, she crossed her arms, shaking her head.","Her lips began to move—but Noah had already heard the words. Seconds ago.","Thanks to the temporal disarray of this place.","Her body shimmered with waves of her True Source as she stepped forward—defying the flow of reversed causality.","Noah prepared to hear her again before she even spoke. He didn't like this disjointedness.","His True Source of the Singed pulsed violently as it began burning away the interference in nearby reality. It scorched through the local reversal of speech, syncing future audio to match the present moment.","Like editing a future echo to match current lips, the effect stabilized.","And her words finally flowed in sync with her voice.","\"I have to give it to you, Causality,\" she said with a smile, \"you captured everything about him very well. But your illusions only work when a trace will of mine isn't standing beside the subject inside the weavings of the Wheel itself.\"","She stepped closer.","Her complexity spilled out like dark crimson waves, formed from trillions of floating Runes—each capable of erasing what she still believed to be an illusion.","But Noah simply smiled.","He didn't respond.","Not here.","Not in this region of the Infinite Ravines.","Instead, he used his body within the Amarantos Dream, where her Trace Will existed—and asked her.","\"What if I really am right there with you... in the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality?\"","...!"]},{"number":3652,"title":"Chapter 3652: Chapter 3651 Exodus! II","paragraphs":["What if he was there?","He hadn't even asked this with his body, the one that was actually inside the Infinite Ravines.","No.","He asked it with his weavings inside the Wheel of Existence, and the Great Beyonder could not call that false!","And the moment he did...","The fair face of the Great Beyonder here in the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality changed.","Shock.","Disbelief.","And then, rising anger!","The seas of complex authorities rising around her erupted in heavy waves as she roared.","\"You...YOU! I told you—!\"","Her voice cracked with emotion, her eyes burning with a mixture of fury and disbelief as if she couldn't fathom that he would actually come here!","After she'd explicitly told him not to.","His weavings could get locked down in this place.","His newly born True Source could be bound here.","And there was a rising enemy in the Wheel of Existence one only he could face.","He was their greatest hope.","But what had he done?","He had...","He had actually shown up.","Noah looked at the furious Great Beyonder—and as her full, unveiled complexity surged from her, he grew somber.","She was miles ahead of him it seemed. In raw complexity, in command of her True Source.","She could actually suppress the very structure of his True Source of the Singed if he didn't explain himself here.","So, he did with one sentence.","Enough to stop all doubt.","\"I have two True Sources.\"","...!","The billowing form of the raging Great Beyonder froze, millions of Runes flashing within her eyes as they sharpened and turned icy.","\"...What?\"","Noah simply repeated himself, as if it were the most natural thing in the world.","\"I have two True Sources. One is here. One is already battling the Dead Thing inside the Wheel right now.\"","...!","The dark sea of trillions of complex Runes around her stilled.","Her eyes churned with disbelief, suspicion, and confusion, but she didn't speak.","She had seen so much.","Over the years, she'd witnessed wonders. Faced impossibilities and walked through layers of existence most beings couldn't fathom.","She had ruled in the Megalos Beyond, dominated multiple Frequencies, and had an unfathomable Outerversal Lineage flowing through her blood.","She had seen countless complexities.","But this?","Two True Sources of Existence?","\"...\"","She didn't say anything at first.","Her mind was always open to possibilities...but this?","This was unthinkable.","Noah sighed.","He raised a hand.","His True Source of the Singed pulsed, burning away the reversed causality in their immediate space.","He summoned an illusory image, and there he was.","Fighting Bob.","His other self appeared as his form was wrapped in the stellar allure of a True Source of Existence, black halos spilling seas of reality into space.","Across from him, Bob—his body pulsing with Khaos was tearing existence apart!","With every blow exchanged, they shattered entire Frequencies, ripping across the Weave and only to reappear elsewhere right after.","And this whole time?","Bob had only been using Khaos.","The black and white Wheels behind him hadn't even been fully activated yet.","Noah was waiting and preparing for when they were utilized!","The Great Beyonder watched it all with pitch black eyes.","She shook her head, staring at him like he was an alien!","\"Inconceivable...multiple True Sources? That's the very foundation and definition of a being. To have more than one, it should be unstable and impossible. How were you...?\"","Her eyes narrowed sharply, glowing with dangerous curiosity.","She examined him, top to bottom.","Noah didn't answer her gaze.","Instead, he asked.","\"Tell me about the Infinite Ravines and where we are right now. I'm curious about the Dead Things here.\"","He had tried spreading his weavings far—but the Wild True Source of Causality resisted.","Here, the farther you stretched, the more violent the pushback as there were limits.","But more than that, he was curious about the structure of the Ravines themselves.","Too vast for even the idea of distance!","The Great Beyonder watched him.","Still quiet.","Still processing.","Then finally...","\"I don't understand you.\"","...!","She said it quietly.","\"I don't understand you, but if you say you have two True Sources...then you have two. I won't deny impossibilities as we are in desperate need of them.\"","WAA!","She raised her right hand, motioning to everything around them.","\"I welcome you to the Gateway Domus of the Wheel of Existence, The Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.\"","\"Your weavings were unique enough to find this place without having to trace the flow of the Wheel.\"","Her tone shifted and became serious and grim.","\"Places like this, Gateway Domus, they're unknown in number, but in the past few eons...many have been closed off and merged into others.\"","...!","She continued.","\"Think of the Gateway Domus as massive doors. If one of those doors is about to break, if it's about to be breached by a Dead Thing, the Wheel merges it with another because the Wheel can't just...close the door.\"","\"The Infinite Ravines is made up of these Doors, and do you know why they're being merged?\"","She asked the question.","Noah didn't hesitate as he sighed and nodded.","\"Because the defenders of those Gateway Domus were either defeated or no longer there.\"","...!","Defeated.","Or gone.","Legends- beings who had once achieved their True Source!","The Great Beyonder nodded slowly, closing her eyes.","\"Yes. Half and half. Some fell, and some were worn down by time...or waves of Dead Things.","And others, they just left. An exodus of True Sources. They had defended for millions of years and faced endless assaults, and now, they grew tired and left. So now, Gateway Domus collapse and merge. Two Wild True Sources can be in one place. It becomes harder for Dead Things to breach, but also harder for any defender to maintain integrity.\"","...!","\"And the Wheel? It moves with logic and calculates what's necessary. If it sees a door is failing, it merges it based on who's inside. It measures complexity and sees if those within can handle the merge. If so, it proceeds as things are that dire.\"","She turned to him, voice sharp again.","\"And now that you're here, the complexity of this Gateway Domus has changed. What the Wheel thought this door could handle has changed. I wouldn't be surprised if-...!","HUUUUM!","As if existence itself wanted to prove her right.","The Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality began to shake."]},{"number":3653,"title":"Chapter 3653: Chapter 3652 A Fortified Door! I","paragraphs":["The Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality was shaking with interminable brilliance.","Noah's eyes were luminous as he scanned the surroundings, the words of the Great Beyonder echoing in his mind.","The Wheel of Existence could only be accessed through the Infinite Ravines, and the Ravines themselves were composed of countless doors known as Gateway Domus.","Depending on the intricacies of existence protecting a given Door, the Wheel could merge two Domus into one—for no reason other than one being on the verge of collapse, or the Defender of that Door no longer being able to hold the line.","His arrival at this particular Gateway Domus—the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality—had caused the Wheel to reevaluate its strength.","And now, it was likely that another Gateway Domus was being merged into it.","The Great Beyonder observed the shaking space and slowly shook her head, weariness and sorrow in her expression.","\"The only reason the Wheel would act this aggressively, merging different doors, is if either the exodus of the long-standing Defenders has increased, or the Dead Things hammering at those Doors are growing stronger.\"","\"I've remained in these Cascades of Reversed Causality for eons without change. So I suppose I should thank you—for being the catalyst of all this right now. I only hope we survive it. Until now, I've been defending against a few Dead Things, attacking in sequence. But they've sensed the shift after all of this. They will come in full force now. And with another Gateway Domus merging here, we'll also face an unknown number of Dead Things from that doorway. I just hope it's one that had a protector—someone simply deemed not strong enough—rather than an empty Gateway Domus. Because if it's empty...their burden falls entirely on us.\"","Two scenarios.","It wasn't clear which would become their reality. But as the trembling of the Hollow Cascade reached its peak, a sharp crack echoed through the void—existence itself splintering to their right.","Light-years away, it looked as though reality was folding in on itself. The silver-purple stellar weavings that defined this space of reversed causality began to darken—interwoven with dim black seas.","Seas filled with obsidian vines, writhing outward and snaring everything in their reach.","Two Gateway Domus were merging, with the new one burning with tenebrous radiance as its vines looked vile and filled with horror.","|The Gateway Domus blooming ahead has been deemed the Absolute Fear of Existence...|","His weavings spun rapidly, decoding its nature as he spoke to the Great Beyonder—who now stood rigid while trillions of Runes were spiraling from her being to verify the aura of the new Domus being integrated.","Noah's role as the Weaver of Existence surged to life, sensing the identity of the new doorway forming.","|The Gateway Domus blooming ahead has been deemed the Absolute Fear of Existence...|","His weavings spun rapidly, decoding its nature as he spoke to the Great Beyonder—who now stood rigid while trillions of Runes were spiraling from her being to verify the aura of the new Domus being integrated.","\"The merging Gateway Domus is the Absolute Fear of Existence. It carries the Wild True Source of Fear. Within its scope, every True Source will bear fruit to the user's deepest existential fear—and manifest it. Anyone inside will face their own worst nightmare...endlessly amplified by the Source.\"","...!","A dreadful Domus.","The manifestation of the worst fear of True Source Entities!","Just what fear could a being like the True Beyonder have, and what manifestation of fear would be expressed for Noah?","The Great Beyonder, analyzing it with her entire being, turned toward Noah in stunned silence. She had only just identified the Domus, and not even begun to understand its inner workings—yet Noah had already discerned the Wild True Source it housed.","Her Complexity was far greater than his—yet he saw it first.","Her gaze narrowed sharply.","\"Yes, and—...!\"","But her words faltered.","Because the shaking intensified, growing more violent. Both Noah and the Great Beyonder turned their heads—not to the right, where the Fear Domus merged—but to the left.","Another weaving of existence was descending.","Another Gateway Domus was being merged.","\"No...\"","The Great Beyonder went pale.","Noah's eyes hardened.","\"This... this shouldn't be happening. My Complexity is far higher than yours. Why the fuck would the Wheel merge not one but two additional Gateway Domus just because you stepped in?! What the fuck?!\"","The Great Beyonder's fury rose as realization dawned—three Gateway Domus were converging into one.","To their left, pure white bled into everything. Endless white corridors emerged, hallways blooming outward into a maze-like structure as Noah observed it with grave intensity, his distinction as the Weaver of Existence going to work once more!","\"This is the Pale Verbum Labyrinth. It's suffused with the Wild True Source of Verbum. Within its walls, no one can unleash their True Source through traditional means—only through their words. Every word must carry intent. Every sentence must be structured. Speak recklessly, and your power withers. Speak with precision, and you may command a thousand times the strength of your True Source. In that Domus... silence means annihilation.\"","...!","Even Noah's eyes pulsed at the thought. The Great Beyonder's full attention swung to him now, unreadable emotion behind her tired gaze.","\"I've been here for millions of years,\" she whispered. \"And nothing changed. Then you step in, and within minutes, the Wheel decides to merge two more Domus into this one? Every Domus is a path. That means we're about to face an influx of Dead Things from three different fronts! And we haven't even seen another Defender yet—!\"","Her voice cut off once more.","Both she and Noah turned—gazes locking onto the twisting white corridors still forming.","From one of them, a vibrant True Source bloomed. Not wild. Controlled. Ancient.","Footsteps echoed. A figure in white robes emerged, his eyes shimmering with the brilliance of endless stars. And as the Great Beyonder saw him, she trembled—her voice cracking with recognition and slight easing as if she felt their weight lessen somewhat.","\"Veyl'Aethra!\"","...!","A name.","A legend.","She spoke it like a memory.","He looked nothing like a warrior—just an old man with kind eyes and a smile, protected by a unique True Source that wrapped him like a cloak of existence.","And he came to stand, calmly, at the junction between the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality and the Pale Verbum Labyrinth.","A legend Noah had never even heard of—yet one who now stood as the second Defender of the Infinite Ravines that he had met here!"]},{"number":3654,"title":"Chapter 3654: Chapter 3653 A Fortified Door! II","paragraphs":["Legends.","There were an unknown number of them. The ones Noah knew were simply those who shone the brightest in this most recent era.","But across Frequencies, there existed others—ancient legends who lived eons upon eons ago. They had long since attained their True Sources. Like many before and after them, they had once sensed the pull of the Infinite Ravines—a place that could amplify their Complexity...but also trap them here for eons to come.","The one who arrived at this moment was someone Noah had never seen before.","But the Great Beyonder knew him very well.","She leaned close and whispered only for him to hear, filling him in.","\"Veyl'Aethra, the Oracle of Collapse. His True Source is Chronotropy—he specializes in unraveling time and existence itself. He can age Sources and concepts, erode causality, even collapse the entire sensation of time for others—locking them into existential stasis for eons. Many of us believed he was dead. He was generations behind me, the Stellar Weaver, or that wanker, the Omnifather.\"","...!","She spoke plainly, though her words ended on a name laced with derision—and even a flicker of anger.","The Omnifather.","Noah glanced at her and asked, still studying the distant legend with sharp intent—intent on seeing if he could study the True Source and integrate it into his own.","\"Why does the Omnifather earn the title of wanker?\"","His question drew a sharp huff from the Great Beyonder as she shot forward toward the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, her voice echoing behind her.","\"Who do you think tried to break back into the Wheel of Existence and accidentally brought a Dead Thing with him? Even after sacrificing a large part of his True Source to hunt it down, the damage was done. His actions caused the chaos inside the Wheel.\"","...!","The Omnifather.","He was responsible for the discovery—and eventual extinction—of the Megalonians.","And now, his recklessness had affected the Wheel of Existence itself.","Noah's eyes brightened as he recalled the Remnant Weavings of the Omnifather—the one he'd spoken to before extracting the Source of Versality.","Even then, he seemed aware of Faceless Lifeforms and what they represented.","He was the one who had inadvertently allowed Bob into the Wheel of Existence!","This guy...had a tendency to cause problems.","He was responsible for the discovery—and eventual extinction—of the Megalonians.","And now, his recklessness had affected the Wheel of Existence itself.","Noah shook his head as he arrived beside the Great Beyonder, facing Veyl'Aethra and his ever-dramatic name that was far too much of a mouthful. The Great Beyonder spoke out.","\"Sir, it's an honor to fight beside you. Are you alone? How many Dead Things usually assault this place?\"","Her voice was direct—seeking critical answers without delay.","The old man in white robes smiled wearily, stepping out of the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, where words bore terrifying power. When he spoke, his voice was deep and majestic. From his very presence—and the silent pulse of his Source—Noah felt a profound purity and complexity that surpassed even the Great Beyonder.","\"Five little fiends have tried to break me over the eons. Their Dead True Sources are nearing collapse, growing more desperate. It seems the Wheel believes I can no longer endure what's to come. So now, I join you—one I've heard about from the whispers of talkative others—and this...new one, it seems?\"","His gaze settled on Noah as the Great Beyonder's expression grew more somber. She nodded slowly.","Five Dead Things.","She herself faced three that routinely clawed their way through the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality. The number had nearly doubled.","Worse, her eyes drifted toward the distant edge of the Domus of Absolute Fear of Existence as her voice dropped low.","\"Five from you, three from me...and an unknown number from the Gateway Domus of Absolute Fear of Existence. And it seems—no Defender is coming out of that one.\"","...!","One of the worst-case scenarios.","A Domus merged into theirs—and already without a Defender.","Either its guardian had left or had been killed.","The air turned unbearably heavy. Then—","HUUM!","The junction between the Domus of Absolute Fear of Existence, the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, and the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality collapsed into convergence.","And all weavings of existence among the three Domus fully melded, fusing into a single space.","Three Wild True Sources ignited and clashed—Causality, Fear, and Verbum—their effects compounding in real-time, covering entire light-years in chaos and raw, unpredictable power of Existence.","Noah stood at the center of it all, his weavings absorbing every detail, his focus razor-sharp as he analyzed both threats and opportunities.","Then—","AWUU!","A howl erupted from the Pale Verbum Labyrinth.","A scream layered with death and destruction. It came from weavings saturated in ancient hatred—weavings tired of everything, desiring only endings.","Veyl'Aethra shook his head grimly as he spoke.","\"The Dead Thing Yrrmoth, the Maw of the Unwritten, is the first to sense the convergence and arrive. Last time I saw it, I fought it alongside another Dead Thing. But as it sensed its death approaching, it turned on its ally—devoured it. It must have finished assimilating what it gained. And now... its complexity has likely surpassed what I can withstand. That's why the Wheel decided I could no longer defend the Pale Verbum Labyrinth alone.\"","...!","The Oracle of Collapse's expression darkened.","And Noah's eyes flared as the monstrous entity approached—light-years away—shattering the stretching white corridors as it advanced.","It looked like a skeletal serpent, its body inscribed with glyphs that pulsed with malevolence.","Veyl'Aethra continued, speaking for the benefit of the two beside him.","\"Yrrmoth, the Maw of the Unwritten, holds the Dead True Source of Obliviscript. It devours stories, existence, even opposing True Sources. If your Source is not properly shielded, it will consume the lore and meaning of your being. Protect your record. Protect your story. And be careful with your words. In overlapping regions, you may still express your Source freely, but in others—those governed by the Pale Verbum Labyrinth—you will need words to channel power. Stand tall, O Defenders of the Wheel. For this... is only the beginning. Surviving this and what comes next will reveal exactly why the Wheel has done what it has.\"","...!","Words wrapped in shimmering weavings of existence fell from Veyl'Aethra's lips as Noah prepared to face yet another Dead Thing since Bob!"]},{"number":3655,"title":"Chapter 3655: Chapter 3654 Adaptation! I","paragraphs":["Yrrmoth, the Maw of the Unwritten.","A dead thing wielding the forsaken True Source of Obliviscript—a Source capable of consuming lore itself, erasing the very meaning of one's existence. Against such a force, even a bearer of a True Source could find their essence fading, their reality unthreaded if they lacked the power to resist Obliviscript.","A monstrous entity, skeletal and serpentine, covered in glyphs etched into bone, tore through the pale white halls and corridors of the Pale Verbum Labyrinth. Nearby, Noah, the Great Beyonder, and Veyl'Aethra, the Oracle of Collapse who wielded the True Source of Chronotropy, prepared for what approached.","Amidst that preparation, the dark hair of the Great Beyonder shimmered as she turned to Noah and spoke.","\"Before that Dead Thing gets here, I want to get a better grasp of your power—and your complexity. I need to understand why the Wheel would do something so drastic, and why now. Tell me, what do you know about the levels of power and complexity among those of us who've obtained a True Source?\"","Even as a dead thing barreled toward them, they conversed—because beings of their caliber could hold entire conversations in the space of a single moment, stretching seconds into what felt like days.","Communication flowed like lightning as in mere instants, they could exchange volumes.","The Great Beyonder was doing exactly that, ensuring she understood the power of the being who had entered this domain—one who claimed to possess two True Sources.","Noah gave her a slight nod before replying with ease.","\"Why don't you enlighten me?\"","The complexity of those who had attained a True Source.","The Weaver of Existence was already quantifying such metrics under Noah's terms—but there was no harm in incorporating what the current Weavings of Existence defined as complexity.","The Great Beyonder's eyes glinted as she looked toward the distant Yrrmoth, who now broke apart the Wild True Source of Verbum while surging toward them like a hurricane of decay.","\"When one obtains a True Source, they're considered to have reached a benchmark that few beings among the countless under the Wheels of Existence ever attain. It's a pinnacle of power. It means that someone, within their lifetime, achieved something monumental. And yet, in terms of complexity, someone who's just awakened their Source is known as a Nascent Source-Bearer.\"","...!","Nascent Source-Bearer.","The Great Beyonder uttered the term with clarity, gesturing toward Noah as if to confirm that was what he currently was.","Veyl'Aethra watched their exchange with a silent smile.","The Great Beyonder continued.","\"A Nascent Source-Bearer earns that title based on their Complexity and Purity. These two traits—Complexity and Purity—are fundamental. It doesn't matter how powerful someone appears; if they lack in either, they'll never truly ascend. If one has great Complexity but low Purity, their power stagnates. At the Nascent Source-Bearer level, you can command your Source to pass through the Infinite Ravines, even survive without the shelter of a Wheel. You can challenge Wild True Sources and clash with other True Source entities of similar standing.\"","...!","\"To overcome another Nascent Source-Bearer, your own Source must either be of an extraordinarily high tier, possessing elevated Purity and Complexity, or be uniquely compatible. Most Nascent Bearers have average levels in both. So then—how does one grow stronger? How do you refine your Purity and Complexity?\"","She asked, her voice threaded with challenge.","Noah remained calm, pointing toward the chaotic Wild True Sources whirling around them.","\"A place like the Infinite Ravines helps.\"","...!","Yes.","A place like the Infinite Ravines.","The Great Beyonder nodded in agreement.","\"Yes. One of the methods for increasing one's Complexity and Purity is something we call... Existential Source Trials.\"","A methodology for enhancing one's True Source—Existential Source Trials.","\"When your Source is exposed to and withstands other Sources—especially Wild True Sources—over time, it adapts. It's like being struck by hammers of raw existence, over and over again. Each blow tries to break you. Every time you survive, you come out stronger. That's what an Existential Source Trial is—a relentless battering of your essence until it evolves enough to challenge many others.\"","\"This is the path most of us walk in the Infinite Ravines. Even I have reforged my Source through it. After fighting Dead Things over and over again, enduring the Wild True Source of Causality across countless millennia... I escaped the bounds of a Nascent Source-Bearer and became...a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.\"","WAA!","The first two stages of True Source Entities were revealed.","Nascent Source-Bearer, and then Harmonized Sourcebound Icon!","Trillions of runes circled the Great Beyonder as she raised her hands, revealing a fraction of the power she'd cultivated through the harsh discipline of Purity and Complexity refinement.","\"At this stage, one's True Source has matured to the point where it is recognized as having Moderate Purity and Moderate Complexity. We can easily surpass newly awakened Sources with lesser development. A hallmark of a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon is the ability to lay down a Pillar of Concordance—an imprint of one's Source that spreads through external existence. A projection of power, purified and harmonized, that can convert a region across light-years to reflect the law of your own Source.\"","\"It's as if you've built your own Domus—a stable realm, no longer ruled by Wild True Sources, but governed by your own. And when a Dead Thing arrives? It must fight you on your terms. It must contend with your Source. That is how I've survived these countless years inside the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.\"","...!","The Great Beyonder had survived for millions of years because she had attained the second distinction among those who obtained their True Source.","She had become a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon, capable of laying down a Pillar of Concordance—a manifestation of the philosophy and purpose behind her True Source—unleashing its Purity and Complexity to turn an entire region into her own Domus- her own source with its unique impositions of existence!","Where every being who dared to breach it had to withstand the very essence her True Source represented."]},{"number":3656,"title":"Chapter 3656: Chapter 3655 Adaptation! II","paragraphs":["\"It takes very little authority from our True Source to enact the Pillar of Concordance, but it's one of the supreme weapons available to entities at our level. Any being seeking to survive within a Gateway Domus of the Wheel and defend it must obtain this level of power. Some of us are fortunate enough to grow into it without being ground down to nothingness, while others... they don't have the time. And so, they seek other paths to acquire such power. That brings us to the second methodology for obtaining a higher level of Complexity.\"","The Great Beyonder chose her words carefully. Noah raised an eyebrow, catching something unspoken in her tone, and asked lightly.","\"Only Complexity? This other method... it doesn't raise Purity?\"","...!","She hadn't mentioned Purity.","Only Complexity.","And now, she nodded slowly, the weight of the truth settling in her eyes.","\"Yes. The first Mechanic of Ascension to elevate a True Source is the Existential Source Trials. The second... is Source Devouring Evolution. It has two components, but only one of them truly works—and that's Complexity Devouring. It focuses solely on Complexity. Through this method, one can devour the Weavings of Wild True Sources, Living True Sources, or even Dead True Sources to rapidly increase Complexity. The fastest method is devouring Living True Sources, followed by Dead True Sources, and then Wild True Sources. But this method comes with a terrible cost—your Purity becomes corrupted. Tainted to an unimaginable degree. Your Source is stained by what you consume.\"","...!","Her expression turned solemn, and a shadow flickered in her eyes—something heavy, burdened by history and sorrow.","\"That is why they are drawn to the Infinite Ravines—any Absolute Complex True Source of Existence can nourish them. Even the Wild True Sources that dwell within can sustain them. But there's a terrifying drawback to devouring any Source indiscriminately and weaving it into your own. True Sources are too powerful. You risk corruption, existential collapse... even the complete loss of identity. When it gets truly bad—when your Source becomes a tangled mess of incompatible weavings—you face something called... Fractal Collapse.\"","\"Some of our own people have taken this path, sacrificing the Purity of their True Source to gain more Complexity. If they raised their Complexity high enough, some were able to ascend into Harmonized Sourcebound Icons with a high level of Moderate Complexity...but with Below Average Purity, or even worse—Tainted Purity. This path is very, very dangerous. It's the one Dead Things follow most often. They will devour any trace of a True Source they can, because they have already accepted a predetermined death. And they will do anything to postpone it.\"","\"That is why they are drawn to the Infinite Ravines—any Absolute Complex True Source of Existence can nourish them. Even the Wild True Sources that dwell within can sustain them. But there's a terrifying drawback to devouring any Source indiscriminately and weaving it into your own. True Sources are too powerful. You risk corruption, existential collapse... even the complete loss of identity. When it gets truly bad—when your Source becomes a tangled mess of incompatible weavings—you face something called... Fractal Collapse.\"","WAA!","Her voice trembled with memory, as if she were reliving something vile from a past too ancient to name.","Fractal Collapse.","Even Veyl'Aethra's face darkened at the mention of it.","The Great Beyonder continued.","\"Fractal Collapse happens when a Source becomes increasingly complex but is paired with dangerously corrupted Purity. It leads to the formation of... Fractal True Sources of Existence. Fractal Beings. Most Dead Things you'll encounter are either on the brink of becoming one—or already are.\"","Her voice was somber.","She had just spoken in detail about one component of Source Devouring Evolution-Complexity Devouring.","Noah's Weavings buzzed with endless possibility. He couldn't help but ask.","\"What's the second component of Source Devouring Evolution?\"","The other mechanic.","The Great Beyonder shook her head, as if it were something not even worth mentioning. Still, she answered. Even as they spoke within the span of an instant, Yrrmoth—the Maw of the Unwritten—was still inching closer within that very same breath of time.","\"The second component... is Purity Devouring. It involves finding a complementary and similar True Source of Existence, then devouring its likeness—its resonance—to your own. But this is nearly impossible. Every True Source is unique. To find one that matches yours exactly... it almost never happens. But if someone is lucky enough to encounter a True Source similar to theirs, they can siphon its Purity and rapidly increase their own, gaining a slight boost in Complexity as well. Still... it's so rare.\"","Too rare.","There has only ever been a single case—a True Source Entity who arrived in the Infinite Ravines and, by unimaginable chance, encountered a Wild True Source in a Gateway Domus that matched their own forged Source. They were able to siphon its Purity and Complexity, rising to a level of power beyond even the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.","But that was just one...","...!","One being.","One moment of absurd luck.","As Noah listened, he glanced toward the wild resources around this Domus, thoughts spinning.","He wanted to voice something—to ask the Great Beyonder that what if someone could forge a second True Source to match the Wild True Source around them? Wouldn't they then be able to siphon off its Purity freely?","But even if he asked... he knew the answer. He'd be met with skepticism. Others held only one True Source.","Unless they shattered their current Source and began anew—rebuilding from nothing, carefully matching the Wild True Source in their environment—they wouldn't be able to. And even then, they would never survive the ravaging process long enough to see it through.","But he could.","HUUM!","His mind hummed with Tyranny.","His Weavings sparked with infinite potential.","He already carried the Weavings of Causality—it was a Pathway now.","Could he not continue?","Could he not forge multiple, compatible True Sources—each harmonized with Wild True Sources and even the Sources of others—so that he could seamlessly ascend in both Complexity and Purity?","The ideas buzzing in his mind made the Weavings of his existence leap with anticipation, vibrating as if they were already grasping the future.","Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity. Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity.","The Mechanic of Ascension, Existential Source Trials.","The Mechanic of Ascension, Source Devouring Evolution with its twin paths—Complexity Devouring and Purity Devouring.","All of it danced through his thoughts. Plans and possibilities began to take shape—visions even the Great Beyonder hadn't imagined."]},{"number":3657,"title":"Chapter 3657: Chapter 3656 Adaptation! III","paragraphs":["As The Great Beyonder finished explaining the mechanics for elevating the Complexity and Purity of a True Source—and the kinds of power one could wield at each level—she turned toward him, her voice quiet, intent.","\"So, knowing all of this, you should at least not be caught off guard when you meet Dead Things. And it begs the question—why your entrance here led to all of this. I could feel your Complexity clearly... but Purity? That's different. One's Purity is always hidden, no matter their level of power. That's the only explanation circling in my mind for why the Wheel of Existence would do what it just did. You must have a secret. Maybe... a level of Purity I can't comprehend. I don't know your limits. So, the only thing I can propose is this—test them.\"","...!","A test of his limits.","A test of his Purity.","He already knew—his Purity was incomparable. Because he had done something none of them ever had.","He had severed every single concept he had taken as a Pathway—eighty-one times—before forging it into a Source.","Eighty-one severings for every single Pathway. With the level of Purity he had achieved, there shouldn't be another being in existence who could match him at the same level.","Was that what the Wheel of Existence had considered when it chose to merge two Gateway Domus into the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality?","\"My friends,\" Veyl'Aethra's calm voice rang out. \"I believe our time is up.\"","In the midst of their conversation, Veyl'Aethra turned toward the distance—toward the serpentine skeletal form of Yrrmoth diving through the Wild True Source of Verbum, its body now weaving itself into the Wild True Source of Causality.","The white robes of the old man shifted as he sensed Yrrmoth's elevation in power, his voice soft and haunting—like a lullaby.","\"Yrrmoth, the Maw of the Unwritten... it seems to have devoured the other Source that had been assaulting me. And now... its Purity is so corrupted, it's displaying the first sign of a Fractal Collapse of Existence—Echo Distortion.\"","...!","A sign of an approaching Fractal Being.","Noah narrowed his eyes at the oncoming Yrrmoth. The massive, skeletal serpent rippled strangely, its form fizzling at the edges—as if its existence lagged in real time.","One moment, it was a pristine white skeleton and the next, its body spasmed, covered in fur and then scales—never settling down to one single thing.","It couldn't hold its form!","Echo Distortion. The Purity of the devoured Source was now clashing against its own, threatening to dismantle the very identity of the being it once was as its Dead True Source was put under scrutiny.","And this...was just one Dead Thing.","Veyl'Aethra exhaled a heavy breath, stepping forward until he stood between Noah and the Great Beyonder. With a graceful wave of his hand, something glorious appeared.","Between them and Yrrmoth...","A bloom of terrifyingly complex energy surged as Noah witnessed the rise of a massive, incandescent pillar of radiant purple light.","A Pillar of Concordance.","That one gesture confirmed what he already suspected- Veyl'Aethra was a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon. From the place where he stood, the pillar stretched outward, consuming regions heavy with the Wild True Sources of Causality and Verbum.","The brilliance bloomed like violet purple petals—petals that bore the hands of time, shattered clock faces, and spinning wheels etched with the runes of Chronotropy.","It was breathtaking.","This was the Pillar of Concordance of Chronotropy—and its very identity was rewriting the rules of reality in front of them.","But Veyl'Aethra had only cast it forward. He kept it from touching the Weavings of Noah and the Great Beyonder.","Still, the display was extraordinary.","As Yrrmoth entered the field of violet light, its skeletal form roared in anguish, pulsing with white flame.","White and violet collided.","The skeletal serpent surged forward through unraveling time and space, pressing toward the towering pillar—over light-years tall—stretching into wonder above and below.","And yet...","Despite swimming endlessly through this purple sea of shattered clocks and flickering timelines—it wasn't advancing.","It wasn't moving at all.","No matter how hard it surged, it remained in place.","A terrifying distortion of existence.","Noah turned sharply toward Veyl'Aethra, whose expression had gone ice cold.","\"It will keep coming,\" he said flatly, \"but it will never arrive.\"","HUUM!","Coming—but never arriving.","Yrrmoth thrashed, endlessly reaching for a destination he could see... but could never reach.","It howled, fury and desperation converging, as a Pillar began to rise from its own corrupted Source.","A budding Pillar of Concordance!","The Great Beyonder's gaze sharpened, her expression darkening. She floated forward, trillions of runes gathering around her.","With quiet power, she spoke.","\"Pillar of Concordance.\"","...!","A black pillar unfurled from her body, made of swirling runes and rippling existence.","And yet...it didn't overlap with the Pillar of Chronotropy.","It did not move to reinforce the Oracle of Collapse!","Instead, it reached toward the opposite end—where the Wild True Sources of Causality and Fear flowed freely.","Because from that direction... she sensed something new.","Two more unique signatures.","Two more Dead Things.","They had sensed Yrrmoth—something with a resonance like theirs—and had responded.","Two more entities emerged from the direction of the Wild True Source of Fear.","These weren't known. No defenders from their origin Domus had ever reached this side.","Even the Great Beyonder didn't recognize them.","Her expression twisted with somberness as her obsidian pillar surged, casting her influence across light-years of existence.","And then—another tremor.","Her eyes snapped toward another direction.","Two more Dead Things.","These, she knew. They were among the trio that frequently assaulted the Gateway Domus of Causality.","One became five.","The eyes of the Great Beyonder flickered with doubt—and resolve. She turned toward Noah, her voice deadly serious.","\"If ever there was a time to reveal something—some unique secret, some hidden power—it is now. Before our very Sources are threatened. Before we stand at the edge of collapse.\"","\"Because these five Dead Things?\"","\"They might just be the first volley.\"","...!"]},{"number":3658,"title":"Chapter 3658: Chapter 3657 Adaptation! IV","paragraphs":["Now was the time for him to reveal anything he had been hiding!","And perhaps reveal whatever it was that had caused the Wheel of Existence to merge multiple Gateway Domus together.","The Great Beyonder uttered those words softly, as Noah's weavings pulsed in quiet resonance.","Compared to others...what made him unique?","The answer rested entirely in his Purity.","One of his bodies, currently stationed in the True Frequency of the Singed, could feel the gaze of the Origin Singed. And from that being's eyes, he felt something rare.","Caution.","Not hostility—but caution. As if the Origin Singed could not fathom the level of Purity emanating from the True Source Noah had just obtained.","Of course, he held the True Source Atlas of Existence, among other things—but here, the Singed remained singular in its judgment.","Noah's path diverged from all others. While they ascended through Lesser Sources, Greater Sources, Prime Sources, and eventually the revered Undeniable Telos Prime Sources, before evolving into True Source Complexity Entities—","He had walked a different road.","He didn't climb through Amalgamation. He never cobbled together fragments.","He severed his Ordinances eighty-one times until they became Pathways.","And when he finally obtained a Source from the Pathway—it was already a True Source.","Noah's ascent was different. Profoundly so!","Naturally, his Purity didn't match the conventional metrics explained by the Great Beyonder.","Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity Entities were known to have Average Purity, but he could feel it- his Purity far exceeded those bounds.","It felt as though his Purity belonged among Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexities.","So.","He decided to test it.","His Weaver of Existence Distinction analyzed the Pillars of Concordance cast by both the Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra—pillars that had turned their surrounding regions into extensions of their True Source.","His gaze then turned to the distant silver seas and rising waterfalls of Causality, where two Dead Things now approached.","And he spoke, softly.","\"Pillar.\"","HUUM!","The Great Beyonder's eyes flew open, astonished as she heard the first word. He didn't hesitate as he completed it.","\"Of Concordance.\"","...!","Three simple words.","But in the next breath—toward the direction from which the two Dead Things advanced...","A dazzling pillar of white-gold brilliance erupted.","It wasn't just flames.","This was a pillar of judgment.","A white-gold flaming monument that rippled across many light-years, rising and descending with seeming infinitude. It spread the weavings of its True Source across the domain of Causality—and just in time.","The two Dead Things were approaching.","The Great Beyonder turned toward Noah, her gaze unreadable.","He didn't even need to look back before he spoke.","\"The Purity of my True Source may have just surpassed the distinction between Nascent Source-Bearer and Harmonized Sourcebound Icon. It seems... if Purity is high enough, even Average or Low Complexity can be overridden to exhibit power on par with higher-tiered beings.\"","...!","He said it so casually.","The Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra exchanged glances.","The old man offered Noah a smile.","\"It's always good to see the young ones outpacing us. But let's not celebrate yet—this is only a portion of the Dead Things making their way here. I still don't see how we'll survive the rest.\"","Yes.","Things were only beginning.","The Great Beyonder kept her sharp gaze fixed on Noah, speaking as she observed the two Dead Things surging toward the white-gold flaming domain where his Pillar of Concordance had been enacted.","\"The ones approaching your True Source... I know them well. Nyxal, the Dreamer Beneath Withering Stars, bearer of the Dead True Source of Somnial Nihilum—a collapsed Source of dreams and imagination. And Grys, the Archivist of Hollow Truths, with the Dead True Source of Veritas Moribundum—a fossilized Source of Truth that corrupts certainty itself.","Both are tricky little fuckers. Will the Purity of your Source be enough against them?\"","She asked a critical question, just as Nyxal and Grys entered Noah's expanded Pillar of Concordance of the Singed.","Nyxal's form was a titanic humanoid of ashen-gray flesh with five glowing eyes across his face.","Grys was a woman with an obsidian trident, her lower half a mass of writhing octopus-like tentacles.","The moment they breached Noah's domain, the white-gold flames surged wildly.","The flames latched onto the weavings of existence surrounding the two Dead Things—burning not with heat, but with the purity of eonic embers that could never be extinguished.","OOOH!","Roars of fury erupted from both beings.","Grys' corrupted Source shattered certainty in her surroundings, causing the white-gold flames to flicker in and out of reality.","Nyxal unleashed a source of endless, recursive dreams—powerful enough to trap even True Sources in endless loops, further disrupting the flames.","And yet...","They burned on.","Flickering, warping, but never fading.","They returned.","These were no ordinary flames.","They were the True Flames of the Singed, fueled by such terrifying Purity that even the Origin Singed had taken notice.","With proper Complexity, they might one day scorch even Harmonized Sourcebound Icons.","But for now...","\"We may not be doomed after all,\" the Great Beyonder whispered.","Noah turned to her with a raised brow.","\"Why do you always speak too soon—just before you're proven wrong?\"","He had to ask.","Because just as the Great Beyonder finished her words...","HUUM!","Another Dead True Source blared, this one from behind Nyxal and Grys.","That brought the number to three.","And from the direction of the Wild True Source of Fear, two more Dead Source auras erupted, bringing the total to five from that side.","And it didn't stop there.","As if every Dead Thing across the merged Domus had been waiting for the perfect moment-","BZZT!","From the white halls and corridors of the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, four more Dead True Source auras surged outward in a maddened burst.","Add Yrrmoth, already advancing from that direction, and that made five from the Pale Verbum Labyrinth.","Five more from the Domus of Absolute Fear.","Three from the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.","Twelve Dead True Sources in total.","Against the three of them.","The Great Beyonder's visage shifted—her face a mask of fury and grim realization.","She cursed under her breath.","\"What a bullshit fucking move from the Wheel...merging all these Domus like this. If I finally die now after all this time because of its twisted calculations...\"","...!"]},{"number":3659,"title":"Chapter 3659: Chapter 3658 A Flame That Purifies!","paragraphs":["The Great Beyonder cursed under her breath at the Wheel's calculations.","How were the three of them supposed to withstand the assault of twelve Dead True Sources of Existence?","Each one held its own complex weavings- and in that moment, Veyl'Aethra sighed, his eyes brimming with emotions far too tangled to describe.","He lifted his left hand, subtle and hidden from the sight of the Great Beyonder and Noah, who remained focused on the waves of Dead Things approaching.","His gaze fell upon his pale hand, where a swirling obsidian singularity bloomed in and out of existence. It made his entire limb spasm, flickering in and out of reality like a being that couldn't quite hold its place.","But his True Source pulsed silently.","He clenched his hand, stabilizing it. The Echo Distortion of Existence faded before it could be observed by the others.","He understood, at least in part, why the Wheel had merged the Gateway Domus together.","But he... couldn't bring himself to speak of it. Not yet.","Instead, he focused forward—preparing to unleash even more Pillars of Concordance, his True Source ready to burn at its limits.","Meanwhile, the Great Beyonder's expression darkened.","She took in the chaos around her and spoke, more to herself than to anyone else, her voice wrapped in solemn power.","\"I've done this for so long. I've defended for millions of years. I thought of leaving a total of three times. But I stayed. I remained strong. Surely...this can't be how it all ends?\"","Half of her attention drifted toward Noah.","As if she were still... expectantly waiting.","Noah met her gaze with a quiet smile, a flicker of calm in the storm of despair and uncertainty.","\"You'll likely be put to work a little while longer,\" he said softly. \"So hang in there.\"","...!","His words carried no grandeur- just truth.","There was no need for despair.","The Wheel of Existence wasn't finished with her yet.","Then, he closed his eyes.","Even as the Dead Things closed in from every direction, he stilled his breath and listened.","To the True Source of the Singed.","Its brightness. Its brilliance.","Its Complexity.","Its Purity.","It had been the first Source to speak to him.","Why had the Wheel done what it did?","The answer was always the same.","The Variable.","He was the variable.","And so, with his heart aligned to that truth, his flames began to hum—vibrating with sacred resonance as his voice echoed out to all present beings, living and dead.","\"My flames are pure.\"","...!","\"My flames are scorching.\"","...!","\"My flames are glorious.\"","HUUUM!","\"And my flames...are empowering.\"","The instant his final word rang out...","He unleashed the True Flames of the Singed.","The Pillar of Concordance of the Singed erupted in brilliance, releasing ringing waves of white-gold fire that surged outward, spiraling toward the Pillar of the Great Beyonder—inscribed with trillions of runes—and the Pillar of Veyl'Aethra, etched with the unraveling strands of time itself.","The flames touched the other Pillars...","BZZT!","...and ignited them.","The unfathomably pure white-gold fire acted as a catalyst, bonding with their constructs and causing their Pillars to blaze brighter, expand, and intensify.","The Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra could only look on, astonished.","A True Source...was empowering the True Sources of others?","\"Is this... what the Wheel saw?\"","The Great Beyonder's eyes gleamed as her own True Source of Runes surged in Complexity and Purity, even if just for a moment.","And Noah?","He stood silent, listening.","The True Source of the Singed communicated with him again, just like before, speaking of its limitless possibilities, its unseen design. Not only did it sever concepts to become a Pathway...","...it could also empower True Sources.","His flames stretched far toward the regions of the Gateway Domus, toward Yrrmoth, Nyxal, and Grys, and every other incoming Dead Source.","They came into contact with them. They touched their essence.","And in doing so.","They made a distinction.","They declared those beings as enemies.","HUUM!","Noah's weavings pulsed.","The True Severed Adaptive Power of Existence activated, marking each hostile entity as an enemy whose Complexity he now needed to match—to overcome—in the battles to come.","This was his starting point.","And his flames—those wondrous flames of the Singed—continued to break down the corrupted weavings of the Dead True Sources they touched.","They were unfathomably pure.","Now, all they needed was...","Complexity!","As Noah's flames empowered the Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra, as he prepared to face even more Dead Things...","One more thing demanded his focus.","There were two Mechanics of Ascension among True Sources.","The first- to clash with other Sources, growing stronger through the impact and surviving collapse.","The second- Source Devouring Evolution—the path others feared.","But it was the path he wished to walk most.","One path involved attaining a Source similar to the Wild True Source in the current Domus.","The other...was to devour the Complexity and Purity of other True Sources without undergoing Fractal Collapse.","And so, he called out in thought.","\"My dear Ruination, you have given me the Affix of the Severed Extractor to understand even incompatible Sources. Now, can you give me an Affix to break down and purify understood True Sources of others—so I may devour them entirely...without fracturing my existence?\"","...!","This body- his form bound to the True Source of the Singed, had arrived in the Infinite Ravines, where he had met the Great Beyonder and encountered beings with other True Sources of Existence.","He directed his message to none other than Ruination- the Ruined Miniature Wheel of Existence within the grand Wheel itself.","One of his bodies was currently traversing Frequency to Frequency with her, gathering the final Traces of the Wheel.","This body- his form bound to the True Source of the Singed, had arrived in the Infinite Ravines, where he had met the Great Beyonder and encountered beings with other True Sources of Existence.","Another body bound to the True Source of Existence itself was now engaged in the most difficult battle of his life, stretching across frequencies of reality.","He was battling the Dead Thing known as Bob- a being so unfathomably complex, even Noah could not measure the full scope of his power.","Bob's weavings had been fractured long ago—broken while being chased by the Omnifather, after he invaded the Weavings of the Wheel.","Bob had sealed his own memories, twisted time, distorted frequency all for the reason of going with the flow of the Wheel to not be found out and treated as an enemy.","He even became a disciple of the First Watcher of the Wheelomachy in this distortion of time and reality!","He had sought out entanglements like Noah, the Great Usurper, and the Peacemaker for a purposes of obtaining what he wished, and he eventually did.","Even the Omnifather, who had been chasing him across infinite echoes, had never truly discovered Bob's identity.","He was a mess of paradox, uncertainty, and time.","And Noah could not help but look forward—to the day he would forge the True Sources of Paradox, Uncertainty, Relativity, and Chronos.","But for now...","There was Bob.","There were the Infinite Ravines.","There were the True Frequencies of the Wheel.","There was the mission to fill his last Mundi of Power with a System forged of all Three States of Existence and to finally complete the Atlas of Existence- to break free of the title of Administrator.","There was the Infiniverse Megalos.","There were his True Sources.","And there was...Ruination."]},{"number":3660,"title":"Chapter 3660: Chapter 3659 The Complexity of the Dead! I","paragraphs":["As Noah looked at the many areas of focus he had to pour his attention into, weavings of existence continued to unfold.","The merging of the Gateway Domus was complex and chaotic, unfolding at the same time as the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality, the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, and the Domus of Absolute Fear of Existence twisted and tore into each other- each Wild True Source striving to overpower the next in a terrifying display of supremacy.","In the midst of these terrifyingly intricate reactions and interactions, in the farthest reaches where distance was nearly impossible to measure, something stirred. From the direction of the Wild True Sources of Existence where the Dead Things emerged...","Surrounded by the Wild True Source of Fear, a Dead Thing stood with its aura entirely retracted, as though it truly were lifeless.","It was something called Vha'Nekrul, the Corpse Lattice of Memory.","A Dead Thing born of the Dead True Source known as Mnemosyne Abyssum.","A True Source that dealt in memory, and at this moment, the very memory of his existence had been forgotten by the Wild True Source around him, as though he'd never been.","He appeared as a massive chained skeleton formed of crumbling brains and eyes, wrapped in flickering neural filaments. Thoughts echoed around him like whispered screams in forgotten languages, and his presence was utterly horrific.","And yet, in that moment, those crumbling eyes and brains focused on the figure of Noah and his dazzling white-gold flames- flames that were actively empowering the Pillars of Concordance of other True Sources, making them blindingly stronger.","Stronger, to the extent that even from such an impossible distance where his own Source had been erased from memory, he could still feel the looming threat.","As he watched, his weavings trembled tumultuously, as though he had uncovered something unthinkable.","And then, this Dead Thing, Vha'Nekrul, the Corpse Lattice of Memory, turned in the opposite direction and shot away with solemn purpose.","He moved across the Wild Resource of Fear as if he knew how to escape a place that had no concept of measurable distance.","His Dead True Source pulsed, contracted, and pulsed again, flickering in and out of existence as it crossed unknowable spans in mere moments.","At the same time, he seemed to manipulate his Source, causing his memory to vanish from the grasp of time itself. One second passed and yet, at the same time, thousands of years could have flowed by. It didn't matter.","It was unfathomable and hard to explain, but the distortion of the True Source was so profound that moments after he began his trajectory, he began flickering in and out of existence, depleting the authority of his True Source by a terrifying amount to do one thing.","Escape the Wild True Source of Fear.","Escape the Infinite Ravines of the Absolute Complex True Source, an ancient place he and many other Dead Things had discovered and fed from over millions of years.","None of them had truly wanted to leave. Not even the Wild True Sources of the Gateway Domus, for even they found nourishment in devouring what they could to sustain their decaying, dying True Sources.","But this Dead Thing left anyway because it had seen something.","After leaving the Infinite Ravines, all that protected it from the ravages of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds was its own decaying Source, but that Source now pulsed like it carried a signal. And Vha'Nekrul burned even more of its authority, making terrifying jumps across incalculable distances- flickering through time, or rather, the absence of it until finally, he saw it.","A blinding, swirling mass of darkness.","And his dead eyes...were relieved.","He dove in.","BOOM!","As if crashing into a sealed vault, a dead cocoon where his weary Source could rest, Vha'Nekrul exhaled soundlessly and looked around at the Wild Dead True Source permeating this strange refuge.","He didn't linger.","He could already feel it- an aura of such ancient, terrifying power that it stirred fear in what remained of him. He floated toward it, releasing his intent like a respectful knock.","\"O Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw... I seek your audience. I may have discovered something that matches the signs you once spoke of.\"","...!","His tone was reverent, like a junior addressing an impossibly powerful elder.","And that's exactly what this was.","A deep, ancient voice erupted from the center of this place as space distorted around it, causing Vha'Nekrul to be transported instantly into a storm-wracked region formed from a violent True Source.","At its core stood a childlike humanoid floating above an Existential Shadow that devoured nearby weavings of existence.","Its grin stretched ear to ear permanently, its eyes were pure obsidian- cold and merciless.","And its voice, when it came, was terrifying in its complexity- more than anything within the Gateway Domus of Absolute Fear, the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, or the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.","\"What did you find?\"","Vha'Nekrul trembled as he replied.","\"Many of us have been feeding from the Infinite Ravines of an Absolute Complex True Source for eons. I myself have done so for several million years...though I've never breached the Wheel itself. But—\"","\"Get to the point.\"","WAA!","Vha'Nekrul flinched. The monstrous being waved its hand dismissively, its obsidian gaze granting him only a few more seconds to justify his presence or be erased.","The Corpse Lattice of Memory bowed its skeletal head deeply.","\"Inside a Gateway Domus, I observed an existence wielding a Living True Source capable of empowering other Living Sources and suppressing Dead True Sources. You said...if such a thing ever appeared, you wanted to be told. That it might be a sign- one of the signs that an Absolute Complex True Source powerful enough to create such a being could hold the key...to saving the countless Dead True Sources lost across the Ravages of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.\"","...!","The words hung heavy in the space between them.","Opposite him, the childlike figure's obsidian eyes pulsed with keen interest. It nodded slowly, one finger rising and tapping in Vha'Nekrul's direction.","Instantly, his body trembled as his Dead True Source of Existence felt another pervading across it, a tremendously vile and complex Source that if he ever thought of denying, everything would end for him!"]},{"number":3661,"title":"Chapter 3661: Chapter 3660 The Complexity of the Dead! II","paragraphs":["In the next breath, the memories and coordinates of the place he had just left poured from him- ripped from his control. His Dead True Source of Mnemosyne Abyssum was easily overridden, even though it stood at the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity level.","The memories were read, and rapidly at that.","Then...","\"Hmm...good. There is potential in this. Here is the first part of your reward. You will also gain the privilege of joining us in an official capacity...keep working hard. Return to that Infinite Ravine and observe. I will assemble a team to confirm...\"","...!","The being- Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, spoke while tossing something toward the bowing Vha'Nekrul.","An incandescent, colorless crystal.","A crystal!","Vha'Nekrul had actually been thrown a crystal, and he caught it like it was the most treasured thing in the world, his skeletal mouth even moving as he whispered what he held.","\"A Sorrowglass True Source Panacea...!\"","A crystal that every Dead Thing would do anything and everything to obtain. A rare relic found only in the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","The Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","Broken stretches of existence, nonexistence, and unreality where remnants of Dead Wheels of Existence were scattered, where Dead Things roamed endlessly, hunting for even the faintest glimmer of life. Anything truly alive hid unfathomably deep in the crevices of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","Only when something died did its weavings become clear.","To find an Infinite Ravine of a living Wheel of Existence? That alone was a miracle.","The Sorrowglass True Source Panaceas were incomparably rare and vital to Dead Things. They could prolong the vitality of their Dead True Sources, even elevate their Complexity without forcing them to devour every Dead and Wild True Source they encountered...and risk becoming Fractal Beings.","Sorrowglass True Source Panaceas were remnants of collapsed True Sources, final dreams, unwitnessed paradoxes, and forgotten possibilities!","They appeared in unique locations where the very identity and purpose of existence began to unravel.","The Sorrowglass Crystal glowed with a colorless hue, woven from lost purpose and fractured possibilities, the remnants of shattered wheels flickering within it.","Vha'Nekrul, the Corpse Lattice of Memory, felt his Dead True Source pulse just from holding it.","Without hesitation, he devoured it. Then, with a nod toward Veltraxis- the Smiling Empty Maw whose obsidian eyes shimmered with turbidity, he turned to leave.","He didn't overstay his welcome.","The rush he felt after consuming the Sorrowglass True Source Panacea made it all feel worth it!","But he didn't know.","He didn't know he had just acted as the bridge between forces that were never meant to be joined.","He left behind an entity of terrifying Complexity, floating amidst storms of swirling existence, who murmured quietly to himself.","\"Could this one be it? I cannot bear to see another Wheel of Existence shattered and broken...\"","...!","Veltraxis spoke those words.","And yet... the permanent grin carved from ear to ear across his face made the sentiment sound eerily unfathomable. The words and the expression simply didn't match.","—","Across Existence.","Beyond the Infinite Ravines of a certain Absolute Complex True Source.","Inside that True Source, this grandiose Wheel of Existence...within the Frequency of Blood.","A region thick with crimson strings of existence, where the air radiated the metallic taste and scent of concentrated bloodlust and power. In this place, the figures of Noah and Ruination could be seen.","Noah floated in a stellar sea of blood, watching Ruination as she finished absorbing another crimson-gold Piece of a Spoke of the Wheel.","They had been moving through frequency after frequency, gathering more pieces of the Wheel. And with each one, her status as a Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence grew- her Complexity rising to terrifying heights.","Noah watched her closely as he had already discussed with her what he needed. A methodology- an Affix! One that could purify Wild and Dead True Sources of Existence. A way for him to use Source Devouring Evolution...without triggering a Fractal Collapse of Existence.","Without becoming a Fractal Being.","After he proposed the task, the most important thing wasn't what she said.","It was what she didn't say.","She didn't say that it was impossible!","Instead, she turned contemplative. And after a few long moments, her wide crimson-gold eyes lifted to meet his.","\"I'll have to abandon all other potential Affix plans except Burnt Weaver and Severed Extractor. At my current stage, I believe I can support a new Affix- one capable of purifying Wild and Dead True Sources of Existence. But it would demand nearly all of my Complexity. My Complexity, which is now...\"","She raised her hands and looked at herself.","Noah studied her, too. His weavings told him she was truly evolving and becoming something more.","Something dangerously close to a Wheel of Existence.","A wholly unique construct.","And so, he nodded.","\"You can proceed with forging it...if it's currently viable.\"","Ruination received the command and stepped forward, her hands resting gently against his chest as though she were touching the pristine True Source Atlas of Existence hidden underneath itself.","Her eyes shimmered with reverence. Crimson-gold light surged from her body as she began to forge a terrifying Affix.","\"I'll call this type of Affix...the Affix of the Ruined Miniare Wheel.\"","She paused, searching for the right name. The name that would match the sacred, terrifying construct she was about to weave into her master's very existence.","\"It shall be named...the Affix of the Cradle of Purity.\"","...!","The Cradle of Purity.","BOOM!","The Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence began etching a terrifying wonder into Noah's weavings. He watched her quietly, his thoughts drifting even as she worked.","Her path seemed clear now. She would continue scouring the frequencies, gathering more Traces and Spokes of the Wheel.","But one question loomed.","A question that buzzed within Noah, and would haunt anyone who looked just a little deeper.","A question about the Wheel itself.","Because anything that had fragments of its whole scattered across creation, pieces, traces, even segments of its spokes...meant one thing.","The whole...was broken.","Or shattered.","So if there were multiple fragments of the Wheel across countless frequencies, what did that say about the Wheel of Existence itself?"]},{"number":3662,"title":"Chapter 3662: Chapter 3661 The Complexity of the Living I","paragraphs":["Was the Wheel of Existence still whole, or had it shattered, yet somehow remained capable of expressing its power as a living, Absolute Complex True Source?","Or was Noah missing something critical? Just because its pieces stretched across countless frequencies didn't necessarily mean it had shattered and scattered throughout existence.","These thoughts permeated his consciousness, lingering deep within even as the presence of Ruination flickered in and out beside him.","Ruination.","Her hand pressed against his chest, her fingers carving into him as they began altering something intrinsic, something that felt like a part of existence itself. He could feel her gaze, piercing into him as if she were looking cor something. He smiled at that. What could this girl possibly hope to find?","—","Ruination.","That was her name, and her identity. Even now, she remembered who she was. The treasure of taboo- the weapon that once brought ruin in the hands of the Sages of the Dark Universe.","She remembered the man before her. How, piece by piece, he had gathered her shattered self and made her whole. That felt like eons ago!","She remembered every single thing he'd done since. And during all that time, she had done everything in her power to be useful to him.","Because she saw it- the terrifying weight he carried on his shoulders. A burden no other existence should ever have to bear.","There were moments she had helped him. And more recently, she'd reached a state of being that allowed her to lessen the crushing weight bearing down on her master.","The distinction of a Wheel.","A Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence.","A Wheel was a Wheel, no matter its state. And Ruination had found her purpose. She knew exactly where she needed to go and how to give back to the man who had given her everything.","Her very existence was shifting, evolving, and still, she remained irrevocably tied to him. Tied to the very concept of Ruination, and yet he had elevated her core concept into something far more.","Ruination itself had been made a Pathway to the True Source.","And that meant Ruination herself...was walking the path to becoming a True Source.","And yet...wasn't she already a type of Wheel?","Didn't that mean that she should already be a type of True Source?","The wonder of such a reality pulsed through her. She didn't tell him how close she was- not yet. She wanted it to be a surprise. He was stretching himself thin, doing countless things across existence as this was something she could bring him.","Something only she could give.","Because as she consumed more and more fragments of the Wheel, as her signature as a Wheel of Existence grew stronger, and so too did the reality that she was becoming a True Source.","Her hand cradled his chest, and she felt the boundless weavings of the True Source Atlas of Existence beneath her fingers. She closed her eyes.","In her musings, she finished etching the third Affix she was working on- meant to aid her Master and to ease his burdens even just a little.","The Cradle of Purity.","An Affix of the Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence.","Ruination had poured everything into it. From the memories she had seen within her Master regarding the Infinite Ravines he carried in his mind—she had taken every last ounce of her ruined power and woven it into this Affix.","And still, she felt like it wasn't enough.","Opening her mouth, she finally spoke, her voice soft.","\"The Affix of the Cradle of Purity is designed to take in Wild, Dead, and Living True Sources of existence and break them down into something pure and viable. It separates the corruption and taint of the complexity of True Sources by refining and breaking them down. To make that possible, as much as fifty percent of the targeted weavings will be lost. But what remains will be the pure, filtered essence of existence, known as Pure Natal True Source Weavings of Existence.\"","...!","The moment the terrifying words left her lips, she felt a knot of frustration as if it should have been more. The Cradle of Purity should have been capable of refining one hundred percent of the weavings...of turning them all into Pure Natal Weavings!","But she knew that Existence had its limits.","And she was still limited as her current power couldn't bend Existence that far. Not yet.","So even as a storm of crimson and gold raged around them, she finished carving a massive rune into his chest and branding him with yet another Affix. It resembled a fantastical cradle.","A celestial construct meant to receive Wild, Dead, and Living True Sources and refine them into something not just consumable by her Master...but something he could choose to share with others.","Though she would much prefer he keep it for himself.","Still...she knew who he was.","She knew that in the near future, some of the gifts that came from the Cradle of Purity would inevitably be given to a few others because her Master never stopped giving.","And at times she wanted him to take everything for himself without worry.","She lifted her hand from his chest, lost in thought, until she felt his presence glowing and warm, near hers. He tilted her chin up with his hand and smiled.","\"You've just casually done something that multiple True Sources of existence haven't achieved in millions of years. And yet, why do you look disappointed? You just created a way to devour other True Sources without becoming a Fractal Being. You know that, right?\"","His words pulsed with brilliance, as if trying to remind her that what she had done was no small feat.","But Ruination shook her head as she responded:","\"Just give me more time, Master. I'll make the Cradle of Purity everything it's meant to be and more.\"","She'd set the bar high for herself. What she wanted to create went far beyond this.","Her Master understood. He nodded, his voice low and commanding as he rose to his feet, shaking his head with a soft laugh.","\"You have all the time in the world. Come on, let's get you more pieces of the Wheel- whether it's whole or shattered.\"","HUUM!","His weavings buzzed.","And just like that, he moved forward once more.","For her.","Always for others.","And as he did, Ruination's resolve hardened even further.","A True Source was just the beginning.","She would give him so much more!"]},{"number":3663,"title":"Chapter 3663: Chapter 3662 The Complexity of the Living II","paragraphs":["As she moved with her Master from the Frequency of Blood as Ruination had obtained all the hidden pieces and spokes of the Wheel buried within that realm.","Another part of her body remained within the Infiniverse Megalos.","The ever-changing construct she'd been competing with and losing to, countless times in terms of utility and advancement over the months.","But still, they were together.","At this moment, a crimson-gold figure of Ruination floated into a small world nestled within the heart of the Infiniverse Vein.","A world where floating islands dangled in the skies like ornaments.","The ground was blanketed in sheets of snow, while the fantastical islands above spilled cascading waterfalls, each one formed from severed concepts of Dreams, Avalon, Genesis, Helios, Quantum, Prana, and many others—each unique, each vibrant in its own way.","This was a world mirrored after the Beast World, the one their Master had delved into from his original blue planet.","The same world where he had claimed a spiritual land that had evolved into the terrifying thing now known as the Infiniverse Megalos.","Amidst the many floating islands, Ruination drifted toward a simple one- a quiet island that resembled that spiritual land exactly. The same land where her Master had fought against a certain prideful penguin and other spiritual beasts to gain ownership.","Upon this island, a woman draped in white sat in a snowy field.","Her eyes shimmered like starlight—pupils swirling with countless layers of Megalos themselves.","Ruination appeared behind the Infiniverse Megalos Body, her voice calm as her feet touched down upon the snow.","\"Master is battling a psychotic Dead Thing across realities. Another part of him is stepping into the Ravines, about to face even more Dead Things, and we...we sit here.\"","...!","We sit here.","She felt ashamed just saying the words aloud.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body didn't even turn as she replied.","\"You did a decent enough job creating that Cradle of Purity just now. You're doing something.\"","...!","A decent enough job.","That's what she said about a construct designed to do what hadn't been done for eons.","A construct that allowed True Sources to be purified and absorbed without risking Fractal Collapse of Existence!","And still...she called it a decent job.","Ruination somehow agreed and nodded.","\"What are you doing?\" she asked softly.","How were they contributing?","While their Master bore the weight of countless realities—fighting, building, and protecting, what were they doing?","The stellar eyes of the Infiniverse Megalos Body blinked slowly. She continued gazing at the endless fields of snow, her fair fingers playing in the frost as she answered.","\"You are becoming a Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence. I am trying to become an Absolute Complex True Source of Existence.\"","BOOM!","Shocking words left her lips—but she continued casually, as if discussing the weather.","\"I've looked at all the avenues and possibilities. With the Singed taken to the level of a True Source, I already have the flame of a Source burning within the heart of the Infiniverse Megalos. It can serve as the fuel for a Wheel of Existence. But I need something more. Something grander. The words of that Dead Thing...they've been echoing in my mind.\"","...!","The words of a Dead Thing?","Ruination raised a brow, then settled beside the Infiniverse Megalos Body in the snow.","\"The psychotic Bob? What part of his words could possibly cause someone to reflect?\"","She didn't like the time and energy her Master had to spend on that Dead Thing.","But the Megalos replied evenly:","\"That which Innervates the Wheels of Existence. I don't know what it is. I don't even know if it exists. But maybe that's what I need before I step forward to become an Absolute Complex True Source. Or...I brute-force it. I devour all the possibilities and frequencies of this Wheel of Existence and take everything it has.\"","WAA!","Her eyes gleamed with a chilling brilliance.","Ruination didn't reply.","She simply raised her head, watching as thousands of snowflakes began to drift around them on this floating island.","Two terrifying treasures sat side by side.","One—already a form of a Wheel of Existence.","The other...something far more unfathomable.","Both of them were thinking the same terrifying thing—how to become something greater. Something worthy of a single man.","The True Severed Origin Osmontian!","At some point, in the stillness of the snow, the Infiniverse Megalos Body finally turned toward her.","\"My path is harder. Yours is more straightforward. I've gone ahead and used the Source of that Queen of Matter. I'm expanding into more and more frequencies of the Wheel.","I've begun spreading my weavings across them—gathering every Piece and Trace of the Wheel for you. It should accelerate your progression... so you can become a more complete Wheel for Master to wield.\"","She spoke about something terrifying—as if she were describing how she'd brewed tea or prepared a meal for their Master.","And yet, she was manipulating a Source so rare, it had once only existed to observe fables within the states of Matter.","Now, she was spreading her will across frequencies with it and taking exactly what she wanted.","Ruination raised a brow, then nodded, adding with a light shrug.","\"Keep that Queen of Matter away from Master, if you can. She seems like another brand of crazy that might distract him more than others.\"","...!","She remembered the woman's eyes—those mad, elated eyes when she had grabbed her throat. As if she enjoyed being choked.","Her Master didn't need that kind of chaos in his life.","But the Infiniverse Megalos Body shook her head and replied calmly:","\"Women and food are some of the few...weavings of Existence that Master still enjoys in these craziness of Existence. Food is just a hobby for his palate. Women, though... he complements them and they complement him. They help him stay sane. Even if he added a hundred more, I wouldn't be averse to it.","And that Queen of Matter? She's like us. She adores Master. Don't let her eccentricities bother you. Focus on yourself—and leave the rest to me. When you're ready for the Pieces and Traces of the Wheel I'm gathering... just say the word as they might be enough to complete you.\"","...!","Her gaze shifted onto Ruination as she continued.","\"How close are you to attaining your True Source?\"","Like an older sister offering advice to her younger sibling, the Infiniverse Megalos asked gently, powerfully, and with all the weight of power behind her words!"]},{"number":3664,"title":"Chapter 3664: Chapter 3663 The Complexity of the Living III","paragraphs":["How far was Ruination from achieving the True Source of Ruination?","Such a heavy question hung in the air as two women sat in a field of snow, atop a floating island within a world nestled inside a massive Infiniverse Vein.","Ruination answered simply.","\"Soon. But that's my surprise for Master. Do you have anything?\"","She asked with flashing, competitive eyes.","At that moment, the figure of the Infiniverse Megalos Body rose, her stellar eyes fixed on the snowstorm that had begun to intensify over the once-tranquil land.","\"The purity of the Flame of the Singed burning within me has allowed me to begin converting my vibrant complexity into refined weavings-ones nearly identical in quality to what the Affix of the Cradle of Purity can provide. I've already started collecting these weavings, and I can direct them toward the foundational Pillars of the Infiniverse Megalos to become a True Source. If you don't hurry, it might be me who gifts Master a True Source within the next hour.\"","BOOM!","Her words were outrageous.","Ruination stood too with a spark of seriousness in her expression.","\"I... will take those Pieces and Traces of the Wheel you've gathered so far starting now.\"","...!","She said it with a fire in her voice.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body smiled lightly, then waved her hand—and in an instant, the snowy skies ruptured. From above, dazzling Pieces and Spokes of the Wheel, drawn from multiple Frequencies, began gushing down.","Ruination leapt skyward to collect them all.","She felt as if she were racing against time.","—","Elsewhere, within the vast Infiniverse Vein.","Noah sat on the edge of a farm.","Wind whipped his dark hair as he looked out over acres of thriving land, clothed in simple, loose-fitting white garments that revealed his sculpted form.","All around him, countless fields shimmered with potent Waves of Existence, their crops nourished by the blood of Pioneers and Source Entities he'd once discovered within the lands of Hell Terra Firma.","But he had evolved so far... that these weavings could no longer impact him much.","His thoughts briefly drifted to Hell Terra Firma, where his satellites still roamed, seeking any lingering secrets in that mysterious land devoid of Authority.","If the Primal Flame of the Wheel had been hidden there, what else could be?","It was just a passing thought in his mind.","He raised his head, sensing the connections of Ruination and the Infiniverse Megalos as he could distinctly feel they were up to something.","But he let them be as he looked out around him.","It felt almost strange, his main body sitting calmly in a farm, while other aspects of him battled Dead Things across Frequencies or explored the Infinite Ravines.","He was stretched across the cosmos, yet somehow still grounded- always right here.","Within the protective folds of the Infiniverse Megalos.","And now, he was about to embark on another fantastical endeavor within this land he called home.","He looked down at his chest—at the True Source Atlas of Existence embedded within him. His gaze landed on the last remaining empty Mundi of Power, and he murmured.","\"Let's go ahead and complete the Atlas, why don't we?\"","HUUM!","With the quiet command of his voice, the wheel-like Atlas began to hum and vibrate. In its final Mundi, wondrous particles began to bloom.","Noah didn't yet know what kind of System of Existence would emerge...","But he was only just laying its foundation.","And the foundation would be grand.","\"Since the last system embraced Dark Matter and Anti-Matter... this final one will include all three states of existence.\"","WAA!","The foundation sparked to life in spectacular fashion.","In another Mundi of Power, he felt the Pathway to the Source of Ingeniare activate—buzzing with brilliance.","He raised a brow.","\"Oh?\"","It whispered to him—ideas, designs.","Why not do what others never could?","It spoke of the Domus of Pale Verbum Labyrinth, Absolute Fear of Existence, and the Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality.","Could a new System of Existence be forged- one built upon Verbum, Fear, and Causality?","If so, could it birth a True Source that allowed him to devour Wild True Sources as easily as that rare being the Great Beyonder once mentioned—one whose nature matched the very Wild True Source he was currently immersed in?","The idea hovered briefly in Noah's mind.","Then he nodded.","Let's see where it leads.","And so, the final System of Existence for his Atlas began.","Right there, with his main body, in the middle of a farm.","The same farm he had once dreamed of retiring in, but retirement would have to wait.","Because nothing was ever so simple.","Not when the memories of Bob delivered by the hands of the Great Usurper spoke of even more complex threats lurking beyond the Infinite Ravines of the Wheel of Existence.","There was an entity that had annihilated the initial weavings of the Wheel Bob came from.","Now, that being was seeking the same thing Bob himself was after.","If such a being existed—was it truly alone?","Were there others like it?","And if becoming a True Source was only the beginning, as the Great Beyonder warned... then Noah would have to postpone his peaceful farm life indefinitely.","But...","\"I like it.\"","WAA!","He loved the journey.","He had loved the fantastical weavings of existence ever since the first day he summoned a fireball into his hand.","He knew the future wouldn't be easy.","There would be catastrophes.","There would be enemies that might even push him to fury.","And then...there were the words of Ashmole.","The dead Wandering Alchemist had told him that across Existence, there will always be Oddities who defy all logic—who are utterly ridiculous in every way.","Ashmole stayed that he could not wait for the day when one of them—someone even more absurd than Noah came to face him.","To suffocate him. To overwhelm him. So that he could finally know what it feels like.","Noah chuckled.","Because that's exactly why he moved the way he did.","So that day would never come.","So that no existence would ever outmatch or outpace him.","And that's why...","\"Cheats. Quintessence. Paradox...you all need to get a move on.\"","...!","He whispered to the unique Pathways within him—urging them toward True Source Ascension.","So that he could remain...","A monster.","A breaker of rules.","A defier of the boundless weavings of complexity.","Because he...","He was just getting started!"]},{"number":3665,"title":"Chapter 3665: Chapter 3664 The Complexity of the Living IV","paragraphs":["He was simply getting started!","And so, he focused inward—while the last and final System of Existence was being forged in the Ninth Mundi of Power, his attention remained locked on the current battle that spanned across Frequencies.","The battle against the Dead Thing, Bob!","—","Inside the Frequency of Mana.","A blue slime floated in an endless, azure sea of pure energy, humming to itself as its bright, circular eyes scanned the surroundings. It noticed clusters of other slimes drifting nearby.","Straightening up, it aimed to approach a group of elegant female slimes to show off the purity of its mana when, all of a sudden...","BOOM...CRACK!","The once-stable waves of mana surrounding it exploded and shattered in a horrifying cascade, as if existence itself were being erased.","Everything nearby faced decimation and collapse. The blue slime found itself fragmenting into countless shards, its weavings of existence on the verge of dispersing entirely.","Just as it was about to perish, it saw them- the ones responsible.","A tentacled entity with a bald, round head glowed with purple and black light. Opposite him stood a humanoid being shimmering with stellar black brilliance. Behind him, obsidian halos spun, and wings of starlit shadow unfurled in full.","The halos above his head spun violently and gushed forth a terrifying weaving of existence. The breakdown and collapse that had stretched across light-years in the surrounding regions...","Began to reverse.","The blue slime felt its shattered weavings reform, slowly returning to what they once were. The cracks that splintered reality began to mend.","And in just a brief moment—","SAA!","Everything was back to normal.","\"...!\"","The blue slime and countless other beings in the region glanced around in shock, their trembling eyes darting nervously. And then, the bold little slime screamed first.","\"What the fuck was that?!\"","They had all felt the collapse of their very existence—only to have it restored. But the ones responsible?","Gone.","They had already disappeared into the Weave, shattering one plane of reality to reappear in another Frequency entirely.","BOOM!","Every impact was existence-shattering. The terrifying True Source of Khaos only seemed to grow stronger and more unhinged with every passing second.","It was as if Bob was regaining the fullness of his power with each beat, each breath—moving closer and closer to becoming a more complete Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.","Existence fractured faster with each clash. Noah had to keep pace, releasing his own True Source of Existence, letting it proliferate through the Frequencies, mending what was broken and restoring what once was.","The battle was a stalemate. Despite the raw power of Khaos, Noah's existence was actively adapting. With every passing moment, his complexity increased.","Bob saw this. He shook his head, and then after what felt like ages, spoke once again.","\"None of this is needed. None of this has to happen. Even now, I've kept the weavings of the two Wheels behind me mostly dormant. I don't want to taint anything. All I need... is entry into a True Frequency. You could end all of this peacefully, my friend.\"","...!","BOOM!","Their weavings clashed again. Existence cracked, twisted, distorted—and then reformed—as they plunged into the dark embrace of the Weave once more.","Noah didn't relent. His True Source of Existence permeated the space, spreading outward to overwhelm and collapse every remnant of Khaos it encountered.","But as he did this, he replied to Bob with vibrant waves of tyranny surging around him.","\"Have you heard the fable of the Scorpion and the Frog?\"","...?!","Bob blinked, clearly caught off guard. He looked at Noah, trying to determine if he'd heard him correctly, then shook his head.","He had never heard such a ridiculous tale.","Even as their True Sources continued to collide—distorting reality with each strike—Noah pressed on, his eyes radiating with cosmic brilliance that made him look like an ancient titan of stellar obsidian brilliance!","\"A Scorpion and a Frog met on the banks of a raging river. It was too treacherous for the Scorpion to cross, so he politely asked the Frog to carry him across. Do you know what the Frog did?\"","...!","Noah asked it casually. And when Bob heard the direction the story was going, a flash of anger crossed his face. Khaos around him began to bubble with seething intensity.","Still, Noah continued.","\"The Frog was suspicious as fuck. He said, 'How do I know you won't sting me?' And the Scorpion replied—completely rationally—'Because if I sting you, we'll both drown.' It made sense. The Frog hesitated but eventually agreed, letting the Scorpion ride on his back as he began to cross the river.\"","Noah's voice dropped.","\"But halfway across... the Scorpion struck. It stung the Frog, poisoning him. As they began to sink, the dying Frog asked, 'Why the fuck would you do that? Now we're both going to die!' And the Scorpion replied...\"","He paused in the eye of the storm, his voice calm amidst the crashing chaos.","\"'It's in my nature.'\"","Bob's expression soured. He didn't answer, only glanced behind him—toward the two massive Wheels, black and white, as though grappling with a difficult decision.","Noah didn't stop.","\"So what lesson do you take from that? Because to me—you're the Scorpion. Even if it kills you. Even if it destroys everything—you'll still sting. That is just your nature.\"","He exhaled sharply.","\"So no. I won't carry you across the river. I won't take you to a True Frequency of Existence.\"","His tone darkened.","\"I'll learn more about you instead. Because ever since arriving in the Infinite Ravines... things about your nature are starting to become clearer.\"","...!","BOOM!","Another clash. Their weavings collided, and the scenery shifted.","They now stood within the Frequency of Night.","Endless starlight stretched across a cosmic void.","In that moment, Bob's weaving hesitated.","\"...What did you say?\"","He hadn't cared much about the Scorpion and the Frog.","But now—at the mention of something else—his eyes narrowed with cold calculation. His voice dropped, cautious.","\"The Infinite Ravines? You arrived in the Infinite Ravines?!\"","...!"]},{"number":3666,"title":"Chapter 3666: Chapter 3665 The Complexity of the Living V","paragraphs":["The way Bob asked the question made it clear—something that should never have been done, had been done. His gaze locked onto Noah with a stern intensity as he sought confirmation.","\"You sent a part of yourself to the Infinite Ravines?!\"","He asked again, as if needing to hear it aloud.","Noah met the being's stare calmly. His silence served as a direct answer.","Bob shook his head slowly, as though the knowledge itself was a curse.","\"You... haha, fuck. I told you—every Wheel of Existence has its most unique entities. And you? You're like a fucking beacon. You shine too bright, too strange. In a place like the Infinite Ravines, where Dead Things roam... your mere presence draws them in. If even one of them catches a glimpse of you—senses the difference—they'll spread word. And then you'll face an onslaught of Dead Things, all desperate for that. The same thing I'm after.\"","...!","Bob's words came in a rush, tumbling one after another as his frustration mounted.","Noah considered them carefully. This wasn't something he dismissed easily. Coldly, he asked.","\"My presence alone in the Infinite Ravines could cause such an avalanche?\"","Bob nodded, then reached out behind him.","The illusory white Wheel began to stir, moving closer, floating toward him until it hovered at his fingertips.","\"Your presence... is not just your presence. The Dead Things in the Ravines—wandering the unknown Nullvein Gravewake Folds of collapsed Wheels—they seek sustenance from Wild True Sources. Yes. But they also search for differences. For anything new. Any anomaly.\"","A new term appeared for Noah.","Nullvein Gravewake Folds of collapsed Wheels and existence. These were the endless regions that stood outside of Infinite Ravines of Absolute Complex True Sources?","Bob paused, his voice growing graver with each word as he continued.","\"Because when they sense difference... it might mean the Wheel that the Infinite Ravines are connected to holds something more. Something unique. THAT. A pathway. A gateway. Whether it's true or not doesn't matter. If one of them suspects it, others will come. They'll come to confirm. And when they arrive, your very being will only solidify their suspicions as when I looked at you, I also became more certain that this Wheel might truly hold a great piece of a puzzle! And that's when things will spiral. Beings like me—or worse—will come. Man...\"","He exhaled deeply, as if dreading what must come next.","\"I never wanted things to reach this point.\"","But he believed they had.","\"It means I'll have to get serious now—get what I need before chaos spreads. I... didn't want to do this, Osmont. I didn't want to do this.\"","There was desperation in his eyes as, without warning, the illusory White Wheel was suddenly in his grasp. Complexity surged around him, while Noah's True Source of Existence crashed down in raging waves.","Bob's state of Khaos elevated his power even further, yet the chaos dispersed anything near him. And in his hands, the white Wheel radiated a strange, eerie splendor—its glow pierced with the screams of countless beings.","And Bob—he did the unthinkable.","\"OOOH!\"","He began to pull the Wheel apart.","He was breaking it.","Tears welled in his eyes.","At the same time, Noah's weavings received a transmission from the Great Usurper—an echo of shock and revelation.","|He's burning them... no, he's burning half of all the lifeforms within the White Wheel of Existence! And he's doing it in a way that purges even the ones I had overtaken! He's breaking the White Wheel of Existence!|","WAA!","Bob was breaking the Wheel.","And he did so with a terrible sorrow etched into his face, using Khaos as a shield against Noah's furious attacks. But then—without warning—a dazzling, stellar obsidian Pillar of Concordance erupted above him.","Brilliant.","Stellar.","Obsidian.","It pierced through the violet Khaos like a blade through silk, crashing into Bob. The obsidian light struck his skin, slamming into his bald head—half of the Pillar's brilliance shattered on contact.","But—","\"I didn't want to do this!\"","Bob roared with anguish, even as fracture lines began to crawl across the surface of the White Wheel. In the next moment, Primal Flames—drawn from Hell Terra Firma—erupted around him.","He was burning it all.","Even as Noah's True Source bore down on him, disintegrating the top half of his head, Bob continued!","His face was twisted—not with fury—but with mad sorrow.","He screamed.","\"Break!\"","...!","A shattering.","Bob...was breaking a Wheel of Existence.","BOOOM!","The dazzling White Wheel split in half. At its fracture point, the Primal Flames surged outward—releasing potent, unfamiliar waves of energy.","Unlike anything Noah had ever seen.","The energy was too pristine.","Too unfathomable.","And Bob—he harnessed all of it. He wrapped it in the flames and didn't hurl it at Noah. No—he directed it upward.","Reality itself tore open.","Existence buckled and screamed as the Weave split and warped. The force of the Wheel's destruction wasn't meant for annihilation.","It was meant for entry.","Guided by the Primal Flames, the force surged toward a distant shimmer of white-gold light.","The flames of the Singed.","But not from the Frequency of Flames.","No.","These were the True Flames.","Of the True Frequency of the Singed.","And when Bob confirmed it...","\"OOOH!\"","He completely tore the White Wheel in two, using its force to rip open a massive rift above. It was a wound in existence itself. But from it... spilled the impossible. True Flames—of a True Frequency.","With the shattered Wheel in each hand, Bob howled in despair. More than half his head was gone, along with huge portions of his complexity. Yet he soared toward the wound he had carved into reality—across the path of chaos and flame.","Noah roared in rage, his Pillar of Concordance chasing behind him. He saw Bob engulfed in the True Flames of the Singed, assaulted from every direction.","Yet...","Bob raised his left hand.","He burned the broken half of the White Wheel in his grip—sacrificing it to shield himself from annihilation.","And with that act—after the unthinkable destruction of one of the Dead Absolute Complex True Sources of Existence...","Bob crossed the threshold.","And entered a True Frequency."]},{"number":3667,"title":"Chapter 3667: Chapter 3666 Ashes I","paragraphs":["The True Frequency of the Singed.","Inside it, Noah remained atop the blistering True Heart of Existence.","The same True Heart of Existence that was considered the Source of the scattered Flames of the Wheel of Existence—and only a fraction of what made up the Absolute Complex True Source that was the Wheel of Existence.","Its gloriously pure white flames and blood continued to surge into his body as he sought to harness that unparalleled purity to elevate his other pathways, testing if they, too, could ascend to the level of True Sources.","The effectiveness had dropped significantly after he attained the True Source of the Singed, yet he remained here nonetheless as he did not stop.","He could feel the distant gaze of the Origin Singed. And at that moment, his expression shifted—eyes narrowing as he turned toward a distant region within the vast True Frequency of the Wheel. There, the brilliant white-gold space split apart and tore open as a shattered white Wheel of Existence pierced through, and it was carrying none other than...","Bob.","BOOM!","He crashed into the True Frequency of the Singed, having done the impossible.","He had shattered an Absolute Complex True Source—even if it had already been dead, just to brute force his way into a True Frequency of Existence.","...!","Noah's body, still draining the purity of the True Heart of Existence, now only contained the residual power of the True Source of the Singed. At most, he could express a fraction of its might through his form here.","But even that, magnified by the effects of the System of Existence of Ordo Ab Chao—wasn't enough to stop Bob.","And now, Bob was in a True Frequency of the Wheel, exactly where he wanted to be!","The moment he arrived, tears spilled from his eyes—eyes that shone like boundless singularities. Behind him, the other body of Noah followed, trailing an obsidian Pillar of Concordance and spinning halos of dark brilliance.","Bob clutched the remnants of a shattered half of a white Wheel of Existence—dim, fading into glimmers of ash. He'd used it not just to find the True Source of the Singed, but to bypass its protective folds—a feat that would've obliterated anyone else.","Half of an entire Wheel of Existence began to crumble into pure white ash. With its collapse came the release of countless souls.","Wailing entities—burning within the weavings of a dead True Source for what could have been centuries now perished.","Their cries ceased.","As if they had been released.","Towards the end, the ceasing cries of some even seemed to be those of relief as if they were thankful they did not have to live in death any longer!","A silence came.","And with that silence, Bob's face twisted with grief.","His bald head began to regenerate, flesh knitting back together as his eyes filled with the weight of what he had just done.","For so long, he'd heard those screams. And now...gone. Silenced.","The absence was unbearable.","He nearly screamed.","But he held it in. Because what he'd sacrificed... couldn't be in vain.","His will surged outward across the white-gold landscape of this True Frequency.","He saw the remnants of fallen wheels. He saw a terrifying, silver-white Wheel of Existence—its countless Spokes gleaming like spears.","And he saw the Origin Singed—its expression livid, its body seething with rising power.","The defender placed here within this sacred frequency to ensure that this very scenario never happened.","And yet Bob cast only a single glance toward the Origin Singed before shifting his gaze toward a distant horizon.","A direction where waves of white-gold brilliance stretched on endlessly—seemingly empty.","But Bob felt it.","An entrance.","One that led directly to the Absolute True Source of Existence—the core of the Wheel itself.","BOOM!","He surged forward.","But Noah moved just as fast.","His obsidian form, blazing with the splendor of the True Source of Existence, blinked into Bob's path. He collided with him, driving him back as a Pillar of Concordance sent Bob spiraling across the skies.","Noah turned his gaze toward the distant Origin Singed, hand outstretched, voice roaring:","\"Don't you fucking dare bring back your True Source!\"","His presence thundered with command. He could already feel it—that sliver of power within the Origin Singed was rising rapidly, nearing the Nascent Source-Bearer level of complexity.","That meant one thing.","The Origin Singed was preparing to recall its True Source from the Infinite Ravines and forcefully reintegrating it into the Wheel of Existence.","It was the same blasphemous action the Omnifather once took—an act that brought Bob, the Dead Thing, into being.","And now, it was happening again.","This ancient being, who lived for logic, purity, and precision, heard Noah's words.","But his expression remained unreadable.","His body launched forward, inserting itself between Bob and the distant entrance.","His voice, ancient and resolute, echoed like a verdict.","\"The most important priority is to stop the immediate threat—the one that seeks to disrupt or collapse the Wheel of Existence. That threat is here. It has pierced this sacred place. In its presence, all other possibilities are irrelevant.\"","...!","Pure logic radiated from him.","From his perspective, if Bob reached the heart of the Wheel, nothing else mattered.","What use was it to protect the Infinite Ravines if a Dead Thing had already broken into a True Frequency of the Wheel itself and was about to taint its Core?","If the Origin Singed's main body remained anchored within its Gateway Domus—what difference would it make?","What was he defending if the core was already compromised?","So, in the next moment—","From a Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity, a terrifying grandeur erupted.","The power of Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity surged from the Origin Singed.","His form warped, appearing before Bob.","A massive Pillar of Concordance, glowing with pure white and gold, bloomed—slamming into Bob and enveloping him completely.","The True Origin Singed had returned.","Abandoning his position. Bearing the weight of unspeakable consequences.","But he returned with his full True Source of Existence..."]},{"number":3668,"title":"Chapter 3668: Chapter 3667 Ashes II","paragraphs":["A terrifying Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity erupted before Bob.","The Pillar of Concordance it conjured lashed out, wrapping violently around Bob and burning everything he held as it was unfathomably heavy and seeking to purify and scorch entirely!","Khaos burned.","The remaining half of the white Wheel in his hands began to disintegrate in flickering, golden flames.","And Bob—Bob let out a guttural, broken howl that echoed across frequencies.","\"I. JUST. WANT. TO. SAVE. HER!\"","HUUM!","The shattered white Wheel pulsed in his grasp, unleashing the wails of countless quintillions of bound souls.","It burned with terrifying brilliance. Bob took the broken Wheel and swung it against the pillar raging around him.","BOOM!","Like a fissure tearing through the very layers of existence, the Pillar of Concordance split—flickering in and out of reality before shattering into oblivion.","Without pause, Bob seized the trembling, ruined Wheel like a spear. His arm swung back before he hurled it- tumultuous, raw, and final...toward the Origin Singed.","OOOH!","A cataclysm of complexity roared as Noah's own True Source of Existence surged forward like a tidal wave- black stellar seas howling through the void.","But it was a beat too slow.","Just a breath too far away.","Because in the moment before Noah's source could sweep the battlefield, the shattered white Wheel struck the chest of the Origin Singed.","BOOM!","A Dead Absolute Complex True Source—shattered though it was—slammed into a freshly returned Origin Singed. The impact hurled him back, his chest splitting open in a torrent of glowing, white-gold blood.","With a livid glare, the Origin Singed tried to pull the embedded Wheel from his chest—but it was like dragging the weight of endless complexity.","It anchored him.","It dragged him down.","Toward the endless white-gold seas below.","And Bob? He surged forward once more.","A Harmonized Sourcebound Icon manifested, the Origin Singed himself...only to be one-shotted by Bob in passing!","It wasn't to discredit the power of the Origin Singed—no.","He was one of the last sentinels left behind by the Wheel to stand in the face of annihilation.","But this enemy?","This enemy was obscene.","Far too obscene for the likes of common weavings to understand!","The Origin Singed had been bound by something no other enemy could conjure: a dead, half-shattered Wheel of Existence.","All he could do was raise his gaze and watch-watch as a Dead Thing neared the Wheel of Existence.","And in that moment, the Origin Singed howled.","\"O Singed! Burn all that you have for the sake of the Wheel!\"","His voice was thunder and reverence—laced with desperation. All across the void, figures of Singed in various complexities obeyed, bursting into radiant white flames that surged toward him as their expression were heavy. So, so heavy.","All... except two.","Emelline and Mysara stood frozen. Eyes wide.","Trembling.","Their strength... nowhere near enough for this battle, but the commands they followed were not of that Origin Singed!","At such a time—","Because if he didn't stop Bob now, Bob would reach the point of entry that led straight to the Wheel of Existence.","Noah turned to his dwindling seeds of stellar obsidian—the essence of his True Source of Existence.","He knew. He needed more.","More complexity. More power.","Because if he didn't stop Bob now, Bob would reach the point of entry that led straight to the Wheel of Existence.","His weavings buzzed violently—urging, summoning everything he had.","And from the depths of his soul, across all entangled paths...","|Master, I am here.|","The weavings of Ruination surged through him.","That inseparable, unbreakable connection.","And through her... he felt the birth of something terrifying.","|As a Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence, I should have already been a True Source. But my complexity was too low. After consuming the Pieces and Spokes of the Wheel, I have reached the threshold. It is sufficient. My True Source is yours, Master.|","HUUM!","Her voice—serene and filled with adoration as though she wanted to give him everything she possessed.","And in that moment, she gifted him something wondrous—a spoonful of complexity that exploded through his being.","Prompts rose from the core of his Existence.","|The Pathway to the True Source of Ruination has been traversed by Ruination herself on your behalf.|","|The True Source of Ruination is budding within your Existence as your complexity reaches new heights.|","\"...!\"","Ruination.","Wondrously crimson. Fantastically destructive.","Noah closed his eyes.","And though he wouldn't dare speak the depths of his adoration for her—this construct that had stood by him, again and again—he gave her only two words.","'Thank you.'","...!","Just two words were what he uttered!","And across their connection, he felt it.","Her entire being buzzed—as if those words were the greatest gift she had ever received.","In that instant, he was gifted a True Source.","He felt it.","He communed with it.","And though time was cruel and fleeting, he understood enough in the span of an instant.","He understood what Ruination was.","And with his eyes locked on Bob—who was already nearing the edges of his obsidian restraints of the True Source of Existence.","Noah called out.","\"Endless Ruin- Infinite Bastille.\"","...!","A whisper.","And yet, reality responded as if it had been screamed into its bones.","Reality turned red.","Existence bled.","And from every direction, crimson Pillars of Ruin bloomed, encircling Bob. And then, they were gone.","But above and below him, his reality shifted.","Bob was now sealed within a cylindrical crimson prison. No walls. No floor. No ceiling. Just a vertical tunnel of unending red—stretching forever.","Noah watched this unfold, his voice a lullaby of finality.","\"No bars. No walls. Just a descent into endless Ruination... until you forget the very notion of rising.\"","...!","Bob's figure began to fall.","And fall.","Perpetually.","Around him, the weavings of Khaos and a spinning Black Wheel of Existence raged in defiance.","But now—it wasn't all about complexity.","It was about understanding Ruination itself.","Unless one's complexity entirely eclipsed Noah's.","Unless one could shatter the source of Ruination itself.","They would never escape.","This was...","Endless Ruin—Infinite Bastille.","An eternal prison.","A recursive tapestry of existential descent where time loops, and pain multiplies, where dread grows heavier the longer you fall.","Where rising... is no longer a concept!"]},{"number":3669,"title":"Chapter 3669: Chapter 3668 Ashes III","paragraphs":["An endless prison.","Bob was falling, physically and existentially, after reaching the True Frequency of the Singed through shocking means.","Noah watched him, sensing the growing burst of complexity within and then spoke aloud.","\"You might be able to get out if you shatter the other Dead Absolute Complex True Source of Existence. Or you might not. But if you do, all the cards you have will be lost. The feasibility of even getting close to what you want will be all but gone.\"","His voice echoed with quiet dread as Bob's form continued plummeting into the Endless Ruin- Infinite Bastille.","Bob's face twisted in anguish, his voice a raw bellow.","\"I just want to save her! I...just want her back! Why must Existence itself fight me at every turn?!\"","His mind hovered at the brink of collapse, his mental state unraveling at the edges.","Noah stared, his body wrapped in the crimson allure of Ruination. Around him, a Pillar of Concordance of Ruination bloomed as he stood like a warden over the plummeting being.","Elsewhere, another of Noah's bodies that had been perched atop the True Heart of Existence devouring everything it could flashed, now wrapped in obsidian-stellar light, glowing with the True Source of Existence.","He appeared directly above the Origin Singed who was smashed against a remnant Spoke of the Wheel, his chest liquefying in a necrotizing bloom as a shattered half of a white wheel was embedded within him and suppressing his very weavings of existence.","Noah's gaze was cold.","\"Your return to the Wheel of Existence...did anything follow you? Did any Dead Thing slip through the Gateway Domus you protected?\"","His eyes burned with restrained fury.","The Origin Singed roared his answer as he felt his weavings of existence collapsing.","\"Two. Two Dead Things have entered!\"","...!","Noah's expression turned soured, his words coming out freely.","\"Fucking hell.\"","In solving one problem, they'd ushered in two more.","The Origin Singed looked to him with a face that mingled power, pain, and a strange apathy.","\"The core of the Wheel must be protected. Nothing, not even you, should enter. The Wheel weaves as the Wheel weaves. Since you've stopped that Dead Thing from advancing, perhaps you are now the latest weaving. Protect it. I will...\"","His words faltered, his existence crumbling with them.","Noah's voice cut through him like a blade.","\"Shut the fuck up and clean up the mess you made.\"","HUUM!","His hand stretched forth, tendrils of obsidian-stellar light erupting as he grasped the necrotizing shard of the Wheel of Existence.","A black Pillar of Concordance crashed down, engulfing the entire region, bathing the white wheel and the bloodied figure of the pierced Origin Singed.","\"Echoes of the Unwritten.\"","HUUM!","Noah's voice held no warmth as the weavings of Existence burst forth in magnificent wonder.","Power surged- power to undo, to redo- spilling over the Origin Singed. His horrific wounds began to reverse, the embedded white wheel slowly drawing itself out, suspended in air.","But as Noah rewound the attack, his weavings sensed something—a whisper of corruption nestled between the broken white wheel and the healing wound of the Origin Singed.","As the wound sealed, a silent, creeping infection remained- the will of the Great Usurper.","That white fragment... it held countless dead souls, their essences already fading. They had been infected- tainted by the Great Usurper.","And when that Wheel fragment embedded into the Singed, it had carried the Usurper's will straight into him.","Noah did not undo this.","As the wound sealed, a silent, creeping infection remained- the will of the Great Usurper.","Noah turned to the Origin Singed, his tone like frozen steel.","\"Let's go fix your mess. Where are the two Dead Things you let through?\"","The Origin Singed touched his chest, then cast his gaze toward the blazing crimson prison in the distance of the True Frequency of the Singed pulsing with eerie heat.","\"I must protect this frequency before anything else. That is my—\"","HUUM!","The very weavings of the True Source of Existence grew heavy around them as Noah stared, unblinking.","The undone weavings that had been vented were now being rewound. The shattered white Wheel of Existence, suspended in a sea of obsidian light, began gravitating back toward the Origin Singed's chest.","The wound reopened.","Necrotizing white bloomed again as the agony returned.","Noah repeated himself, unwavering.","\"Let us go and fix your fucking mess.\"","This time, it wasn't a suggestion.","It was a command.","The Origin Singed felt it- the threat in Noah's voice.","Far away, Emelline of the First Flame and Mysara saw this unfolding and instinctively looked away.","The Origin Singed's expression remained placid as his gaze shifted to the imprisoned Bob, who howled within the Endless folds of Ruination.","He closed his eyes.","\"The Wheel weaves as the Wheel weaves.\"","...!","A reluctant acceptance.","Noah began reversing events once more. The Singed's chest healed fully, the white Wheel fragment retreating further.","But by doing so, Noah silently allowed the will of the Usurper to dig even deeper.","That being wrapped in gold and white flame cast one final look at Bob, then tore space open with his left hand, revealing a massive rift.","He stepped through it.","Noah followed.","They were heading toward the two Dead Things that had passed into the Wheel as consequence of the Singed's return.","What they left behind was a raging stellar obsidian Pillar of Concordance of Existence, containing a shattered white wheel spinning in silence.","What remained were Emelline and Mysara, tending to the thousands of Singed whose existences had been scarred by that one suicidal command- to burn themselves for his cause.","They moved to care for the fallen as their expressions were extremely heavy as if they had to reflect and think back go everything they knew, while behind them...","Noah's other body remained.","Bathed in the crimson weavings of Ruination, standing as sentinel over the imprisoned Bob.","And upon his chest, a wondrous Affix of the Cradle of Purity bloomed, its light shining even as he stared down the Dead Thing trapped in the Endless Ruin."]},{"number":3670,"title":"Chapter 3670: Chapter 3669 Ashes IV.","paragraphs":["Every action had an equal and opposite reaction.","Every choice had a consequence.","Noah stared at the man- a being who had become a Dead Thing- someone who had made countless choices across a long life, all of them leading here.","To this.","A prison of Noah's making. And unless something drastic happened like shattering another Dead Absolute Complex True Source-getting out would be nearly impossible.","Yet Bob remained calm, surrounded by the weavings of the True Source of Ruination, his mind remarkably intact. He called out, his voice unwavering.","\"My daughter. I do all of this for my daughter. She's locked within this Absolute Complex True Source of Existence.\"","His eyes flicked to the black Wheel of Existence that hovered beside him, its weavings unbearably complex. At the center, untouched, was a soul he had never dared to disturb.","\"Others- others can be called out and turned into Faceless Lifeforms. But her... I've never touched her soul. I've never even spoken to her. I feared tainting her with death. But if I can find that... I should be able to reinvigorate the Dead Wheel of Existence. Everyone within it would be saved. It's such a simple act. Harmless. This... this is all I seek. I'm just a father seeking a sliver of hope for his daughter.\"","Bob's voice rang with conviction, as if he had built every ounce of his existence toward this moment.","Noah's expression didn't shift. Cold. Unmoved.","The fable of the Scorpion and the Frog echoed in his mind.","This man, this thing...would sting and kill them all, no matter how sweetly he spoke.","But Noah still asked.","\"What is that? The thing you and the one who destroyed your Wheel were chasing—what is it?\"","He needed to know the identity of this unknown force that powerful beings were chasing.","The reason he hadn't believed Bob wasn't just distrust—it was because the entity who had destroyed Bob's Wheel eons ago...they had come seeking the same thing. They hadn't intended to destroy. They had come for that.","And yet, destruction followed.","So how could Bob expect anything different?","Still, Noah sought answers.","Bob turned toward him, his eyes aglow with weary truth.","\"It is unknown. Many call it different names. No one knows what it truly is. But we believe that unique Absolute Complex True Sources... they act as pathways. Some call it The Loom. Others call it the Pirene of Existence. Everyone has their name for it, and yet... no one has ever found or seen it. But I believe its pathway is here. I just...\"","He trailed off.","All he needed was to reach the core weavings of the Wheel of Existence.","But Noah could never allow it. The risk was too great.","That, too, was a choice.","And because no one ever truly knew the consequences of even the smallest decisions, Noah raised the Cradle of Purity high above the endless prison of Ruination.","He was about to make a choice of his own.","He had to.","Because in this very moment, his body—traveling alongside the Origin Singed—flickered across countless frequencies of Existence until they finally arrived...","At hell.","BOOM!","BOOM!","The Frequency of Light shook violently. Its very fabric teetered on collapse. What once brimmed with vibrant auras and silver-white brilliance had now been reduced to dust.","Minutes ago, the Expanse had been filled with life. The strings of existence—tense and bright.","Now?","Fractured.","Broken.","Drained of light!","The Flow. The Weavings. The very essence of the Frequency of Light—over half of it—was gone. Devoured.","Every Pioneer. Every Existence-Severing entity. Every Source, whether it be Lesser or Prime.","Gone.","Annihilated by the two Dead Things who had arrived here after Bob.","And they revealed, in perfect clarity, the true nature of what Dead Things do.","Noah sensed them from afar.","One was a massive gray, crescent-shaped Wheel exuding tentacles lined with razor teeth. It consumed everything.","He dubbed it the Gray-Wheeled Tentacled Dead Thing.","The other... a humanoid woman.","Her figure was barely two meters tall, and yet her hair—a storm of darkness—extended across light-years, vast enough to match a Megalos.","Her strands consumed everything they touched. Noah dubbed her...the Heran Megalos Dead Thing!","Their Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity surged higher with each ounce of life drained.","White gold flames of the Wheel innately washed down like a sea to try and scorch them, but they withstood these flames with their Dead True Sources!","\"Choices, and consequences.\"","Noah's voice was quiet. Final.","Beside him, the Origin Singed stood still, watching the devastation with grim resolve. He said nothing.","Then he moved.","A streak of burning light—he launched himself toward the two Dead Things, aiming to stop their annihilation of the Frequency of Light before they moved on to consume others.","And they would.","They would devour endlessly. Satisfying their True Sources... and then continuing anyway.","Noah turned his gaze upon the collapsing landscape and spoke softly.","\"Echoes of the Unwritten.\"","HUUM!","The True Source of Existence erupted from him again—its necessity growing with each new calamity.","Stellar obsidian brilliance gushed outward, bathing light-years of space. From the torn remnants of the Frequency of Light, something began to return.","Life.","Weavings.","Form.","The destroyed and decimated structures—countless quintillions—began to reform. The Megalos of this frequency slowly returning to their former state.","As this grand process took hold, Noah turned his head toward the two distant Dead Things.","The Origin Singed had barely reached them.","The body of the Origin Singed flared, erupting with the luminous Pillar of Concordance as he shouted:","\"Moshata! Bizax! Our fight isn't over!\"","He knew their names.","He had battled them for eons.","He couldn't afford to let them persist!","Their presence alone—even without feeding—was causing the Wheel's flow to collapse. Rapidly.","They had to die. And quickly.","Noah's body radiated the profound power of the True Source of Existence as he was undoing a cataclysm and restoring a Frequency.","And then, he also began to radiate with crimson Ruination, calling out lightly.","\"Existential Unraveling.\"","...!","Ruination unfurled.","Instantly, crimson lines shot out from Noah—trillions of them—each one alive, lashing toward both Dead Things in the distance!"]},{"number":3671,"title":"Chapter 3671: Chapter 3670 Ashes V","paragraphs":["Existential Unraveling.","Noah's body burned with the True Source of Ruination as he unleashed a terrifying capability.","The True Source of Ruination could identify the foundational \"threads\" that composed a being- their memories, identities, concepts, and pull them apart with eerie precision into absolute ruin.","And so, it released those crimson threads.","Threads capable of isolating the weak points within True Sources of Existence and unraveling them, leaving the target in a state of unbeing.","And as they did, his chest radiated a terrifying white-gold brilliance- the Cradle of Purity ready to receive any unraveled threads of existence and devour them whole.","SKEEE!","The two Dead Things roared with maddened fervor, their very beings thrumming in an excited state they hadn't felt in millions of years.","Because, for the first time, they were inside the depths of the Wheel of Existence.","Until now, they had fought only within the Infinite Ravines.","This moment—this choice—was everything they had been dreaming of, coming true in the span of an instant.","The moment the Origin Singed chose to fully return to the folds of the Wheel.","The two of them had been present in the Gateway Domus he protected at the time. They'd followed his returning Weavings—like a path carved just for them.","They had left behind three other Dead Things in that Gateway Domus, unfortunate enough to not be within its folds when the Origin Singed made his return.","They would forever regret it.","Because, by now, that Gateway Domus was likely being taken—merged into another.","So, their entrance into the Wheel of Existence would not go quietly. Their Dead True Sources of Existence erupted in full, ready to stand against the Origin Singed they once knew, and...","BOOM!","Noah's Weavings arrived at that exact moment, surrounding and bombarding the two Dead Things with countless crimson threads of brilliance that sought to break down their weavings.","But it wasn't just that.","\"What...the hell?\"","The Dead Things were utterly shocked. Not by the power—the complexity felt surprisingly manageable.","No. What shocked them was that the threads were unbinding and devouring trace amounts of their Dead True Sources.","A being with a Living True Source of Existence was devouring fragments of their Dead True Sources?","They were stupefied. Because they knew how corrupted their Dead True Sources were.","Even if dispersed, they always returned. Parasitic weavings that never left.","Yet...","The crimson threads of Ruination did break down the fragments. And then... devoured them.","Their eyes watched in disbelief as dark gray threads of death and decimation flowed through crimson lines—until they were absorbed into the dazzling white-gold object spinning in the chest of a distant being.","They looked at him like he'd lost his mind. As if they wanted to say, \"Dude, are you okay? Eating our weavings will kill you, you know?\"","Even the Origin Singed turned in that moment—gaze sharp, expression unreadable—as multiple Pillars of Concordance of the Singed burst outward.","A grandiose battle began.","Shockingly, a Cradle of Purity was being wielded as a weapon!","This battle, unfolding in the Frequency of Light, had Noah facing down two Dead Things alongside the Origin Singed, even as the fallout of his past mistakes reverberated across existence.","His gaze soured as he looked up, vision crossing countless weavings until it landed on the Infinite Ravines.","—","BOOM!","The Great Beyonder, Veyl'Aethra, and Noah were unleashing their True Sources of Existence to withstand the arrival of the Dead Things. And shockingly, the situation wasn't completely dire.","Thanks to Noah.","His white-gold flames emanating from the True Source of the Singed had empowered the True Sources of both Veyl'Aethra and the Great Beyonder, allowing them to release more than double their usual complexity.","Fiery Pillars of Concordance blazed across the battlefield, stabilizing their Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexities.","But just as the trio might've found reason to breathe...","Noah sighed.","He looked up first. He had expected this.","\"It seems,\" he muttered, \"that things are about to get a little more dreadful... because of someone's stupid mistake.\"","Veyl'Aethra and the Great Beyonder followed his gaze, stunned.","A space equivalent to an entire omniverse away fractured, collapsing—as if something else was being layered atop it.","Another Domus was being merged.","The Great Beyonder gawked, shaking her head in disbelief.","\"You absolutely cannot be serious, right?\"","It wasn't even directed at Noah.","It was like she was asking the Wheel of Existence itself...","\"Really? Really???\"","Because what was happening was utterly maddening.","Noah looked on, voicing it calmly.","\"The Origin Singed left his post to protect the True Frequency of the Singed—even after I told him not to. His return to the Wheel has pulled in two more Dead Things...in addition to Bob.\"","...!","His words only brought worse news.","The others' expressions darkened, but Noah continued.","\"Bob is contained. The other two are being held off too. The merging Domus is likely what the Origin Singed left behind. But to withstand it and the Dead Things within...it's going to take far more complexity.\"","His eyes burned with quiet brilliance, contemplating countless possibilities.","His True Source of the Singed had incredible empowering potential, but the way he was using it... barely tapped even five percent of its capabilities.","His thoughts raced.","How much change could he unleash in a span of an instant?","He turned to the Great Beyonder as many possibilities came together at once, and he came to a decision.","\"I...may have a method to boost your current complexity by a tremendous degree in a short time. The environment here isn't ideal, so I'll do it through your Trace Weavings of Existence in the Amarantos Dream under the Wheel of Existence.\"","...!","He said it like it was simple.","The Great Beyonder looked at him, utterly dumbfounded.","But Noah? He was already continuing the conversation somewhere else entirely.","—","All of it contained in the span of a moment.","The span...of an instant.","Within an Amarantos Dream.","Atop a surreal landscape of obsidian-gold mountains and floating clouds, Noah stood, eyes fixed on Azzurra—now hosting the fully assimilated consciousness of the Great Beyonder as his voice echoed out to her.","\"You mentioned two methods of increasing complexity: the Mechanic of Ascension via Existential Source Trials, and the Mechanic of Ascension via Source Devouring Evolution. I...I am creating a third Mechanic of Ascension right now.\"","...!","As if it were that simple.","Right now.","The Great Beyonder just stared at him, completely incredulous!"]},{"number":3672,"title":"Chapter 3672: Chapter 3671: Ashes VI","paragraphs":["A different Mechanic of Ascension- one unlike the Existential Source Trials or the Mechanism of Ascension via Source Devouring Evolution.","Noah said this with utter seriousness. The Great Beyonder could already guess what he meant by his earlier words about the Gateway Domus not being a suitable place to use this new method. But here, in this Amarantos Dream, it was possible.","She had a suspicion about what it could be as she asked with sharp eyes just to make sure.","\"You...aren't a Fractal Being with a tendency toward things like this, right?\"","\"...\"","Noah didn't even bother responding. Around his body, multiple Sources flared to life.","Traces of the Singed.","Vibrant waves of the True Source of Existence.","Ecstatic pulses of the True Source of Ruination.","But the Singed was the critical one. The other two only amplified it, empowering what had been locked down in the Infinite Ravines.","The Great Beyonder stared at the radiant True Sources with marvel, confirming Noah's earlier claim- he truly held multiple True Sources.","And then he spoke, white-gold flames of the Singed dancing across his skin.","\"One can either undergo trials and battering to gradually strengthen their True Source, or devour the Purity and Complexity of others at the cost of becoming a Fractal Being. But the mechanism I'm about to forge... I call it Eclipse Merging—Dual Evolution.\"","WAA!","Eclipse Merging—Dual Evolution!","Noah spoke the term aloud as his body radiated an overwhelming purity without a hint of complexity.","Only Purity.","The Singed, brimming with Purity, seemed to isolate that essence from all the other Sources within him.","\"Pioneered by the True Source of the Singed, all of the Purity of my Existence is brought to the forefront. Eclipse Merging resonates with another True Source- not merely empowering it, but merging and sharing the Purity of its Existence. This merging allows for potential Evolution in both True Sources. The greatest requirement is absolute trust, as the flames of the Singed... must be allowed to flow into another's True Source.\"","As he finished, he extended his hand.","The Great Beyonder rolled her eyes as she placed hers into his.","She wanted to say this was just dual cultivation with extra steps- but she went along with it.","White-gold brilliance surged around them, clothes falling away in a flare of light. A veil descended around them. Bodies entwined. Pure flames of the Singed bloomed around them, dazzling and heavy!","And the Great Beyonder closed her eyes and felt it.","Her True Source, still bound within the Infinite Ravines, sparked to life.","More than when the Singed had once washed her and Veyl'Aethra in its power as this time, it wasn't just empowering her.","This time, the Singed flowed into her True Source.","She hesitated.","It was dangerous- deadly, even. To let someone into your True Source was to hand them your existence. If she didn't resist, if she didn't defend it, he could shatter her very foundation if he so chose.","She hesitated.","And as if sensing her fear, Noah pulled her closer. She bit her lip, and her eyes glimmered with unshakable resolve. And then, she allowed her True Source to fully open.","Countless trillions of swirling obsidian runes became bathed in the flames of the Singed-those flames now flowing into every rune, altering them to gold.","Resonance. Then, for a moment, true merging.","It was otherwise impossible to merge two True Sources.","But the terrifying purity of the Singed allowed it. It could merge with another Source seamlessly, refining and purifying it to terrifying levels- temporarily anyways!","The Great Beyonder trembled as her Purity shot upward rapidly.","And then...","The Singed took in the Purity of both the True Sources of Ruination and Existence, channeling crimson and obsidian flames into her very essence as...","BOOM!","Her body erupted with dozens of glimmering Pillars of Concordance.","Glimmering pillars that represented her skyrocketing Purity- her very Existence elevated as waves of complexity fed back into her main body in the Infinite Ravines.","Noah's voice came softly like a law written into existence.","\"Not just an Empowerment or Resonance...but an Evolution of the True Source as it's influenced by the Purity of another.\"","The Purity of the Great Beyonder's True Source surged, her eyes snapping open in disbelief.","She could feel her Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity brushing up against a wall- one she'd never thought she could cross so soon.","Her Complexity remained at the same stage.","But her Purity, spurred by Noah's method, began to exceed it.","And then it happened.","She felt it.","She felt her Purity eclipse the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity as she spoke, dazed.","\"Past the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity... one's Complexity and Purity begin to form their Mythic True Signature. From there, they become one of two things- a Converged Architect with High Complexity and Moderate Purity...or a Resplendent Monad with Moderate Complexity and High Purity.\"","...!","The stages of power among True Source entities.","Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity.","Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity.","And then...the divergence.","If one had High Purity and Moderate Complexity, they became a Resplendent Monad.","If they had High Complexity and Moderate Purity, they became a Converged Architect.","And at this very moment, the Great Beyonder's Purity rose so fast that her Mythic True Signature began to form.","Genuinely. Slowly!","\"I... I should barelt qualify as a Quasi-Resplendent Monad with this much Purity...\"","She stared at the surreal truth.","Noah listened, the flames of the Singed rising higher around them both. He asked, his voice calm but curious.","\"Any changes to the nature of your True Source?\"","His weavings moved through her True Source of Runes- swimming in them.","She had trusted him fully.","And as his Singed weavings permeated through her True Source of Runes, his Pathway to the True Source of Runes rapidly took shape as the road was built seamlessly- with him very soon attaining this True Source himself while the Purity of the Singed...became even grander!","His flames were everywhere inside her.","He could feel it.","He could sense the forming of the so called Mythic True Signature the Great Beyonder had spoken of. Her voice came to him softly as she tried to understand the purity surging within her.","\"My Runes are purer, their existence deeper, and they now carry heat. A scorching, unfathomable heat. As a Quasi-Resplendent Monad...my Mythic True Signature will be capable of suppressing any Harmonized Sourcebound Icon!\"","HUUM!","She said it with awe and barely veiled hunger.","Her terrifying Purity flowed back to her main body in the Infinite Ravines.","She didn't just want to stabilize the current chaos.","She wanted to burn away the Dead Things.","She wanted to kill!"]},{"number":3673,"title":"Chapter 3673: Chapter 3672: Ashes VII","paragraphs":["Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity, Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity... and then, Converged Architect or Resplendent Monad.","Levels that correlated low to average degrees of Complexity and Purity... to moderate levels... and then to heights of High Purity and Complexity.","The Great Beyonder had just taken her first steps into the realm of a Resplendent Monad-forming what she now called a Mythic True Signature.","But... what did that truly mean when observing the True Sources of the living and the dead?","—","In the Infinite Ravines.","Inside a Gateway Domus that held... ten Wild True Sources of Existence.","Ten Wild True Sources.","That meant nine other Gateway Domus had collapsed and been merged into this single one. Such a place should have been impossible to hold and terrifying in its Complexity and power.","It begged the question- who could possibly be standing at its forefront to defend it?","Across the inestimable waves of warped distance, the auras of more than twenty Dead Things sprawled throughout the chaotic Domus, this entire structure swirling with fractured color and brilliance as the Wild True Sources seethed, ebbed, and flowed all around.","There were crystal mountains in one direction. Layers of fiery, hellish landscapes in another.","Seas of silver and gold shimmered to one side. The skies in another blazed with purple flames.","The mere expression of ten Wild True Sources would be enough to cause any Nascent Source-Bearer to falter and collapse, even. But here, in these volatile weavings of existence, every single entity present was a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.","Well... almost every entity.","One would expect countless defenders stationed at a Gateway Domus holding ten Wild True Sources.","But there was only one.","A single figure who stood alone against more than twenty Dead Things.","At this moment, a middle-aged man with dark hair and sun-warmed skin hovered above a gray sea of ash. His figure was wrapped in a billowing robe of smoke and shadow, his entire presence emanating a serene, unshakable grace.","He appeared... relaxed.","As if the chaos didn't exist.","He floated lazily in the sea of gray-ash brilliance, utterly absorbed in the Senet board before him. He didn't even glance toward the monstrous Dead Things moving slowly, devouring and surviving within this terrifyingly converged Domus.","Above this man, seated calmly upon the gray ash sea, were over a hundred glowing Pillars of Concordance- shimmering structures designated to various points across the Domus.","Each pillar released waves of unending gray ash, carrying a sense of absolute finality.","A memory of what once was.","It felt like... if even a single fleck of that ash touched one's True Source, that Source would begin to collapse- transformed into nothing more than what the ash represented.","Untold ruin. Irrevocable destruction.","The many gray ash pillars stretched in every direction, creating a stabilizing force that hindered the Dead Things' movements.","But even they weren't the true reason for the terrifying stability of this space.","Above the ash-draped man playing Senet, an illusory figure shimmered brilliantly in the skies.","An enormous figure—gray and luminous—hovered high above, and it looked exactly like the man seated in the sea below.","But this illusion... was colossal.","Larger than even ten Omniverses combined.","Compared to his true two-meter frame floating calmly on the ashen tide, the contrast was almost absurd.","And yet, the massive being projected above wasn't just a visual trick.","It was his Mythic True Signature of Existence.","So vibrant. So vastly complex.","Its eyes alone were the size of entire Omnverses, and they gazed coldly and unforgivingly at every single Dead Thing present.","The moment any of them dared to move...","That would be their death.","There would be collapse. There would be ash.","This was the terrifying True Source of Asche, and it wrapped itself around a single man.","Still focused on his board, he smiled faintly and spoke, seemingly to no one.","\"Hey... I'm hearing a different tune of existence after all these millions of years. Sounds like something's coming.\"","...!","He spoke, but there was nobody around him!","And yet, right after...","He nodded, as though receiving a reply from someone or something only he could hear.","His head tilted toward a shifting reflection forming in the gray sea.","It showed a different Gateway Domus, one from elsewhere in the Infinite Ravines.","Multiple such reflections rippled around him- screens showing other Domus, many of them trembling, merging with one another in real time.","The man bearing the True Source of Asche gazed into them all. Then sighed.","\"Take it easy on these kids. If any more doors need merging, just bring them here. And... oh?\"","He paused.","One of the reflections caught his attention—the fourth door he recognized clearly.","His brows lifted.","\"That's the door of the Little Singed... why did he abandon it? And you're merging it into...\"","His eyes lit with sharp brilliance.","He leaned closer.","\"That's...\" he muttered, entranced as he watched an obsidian-gold Signature bloom above a certain Great Beyonder.","\"What a pleasant surprise... another Mythic True Signature on the rise. That'll ease a few burdens.\"","He paused.","\"But... much more will be needed if the tune I'm hearing turns out to be real. I'll need to step in just a bit more.\"","As he said it, his seated form began to rise slowly from the gray ash sea.","Immediately, the Dead Things stirred.","Their auras flared. Their Dead True Sources of Existence surged outward in response.","But before they could act, the man wrapped in the True Source of Asche tapped a single finger toward one of them.","A creature shaped like a million-legged insect, its body jagged and grotesque, shrieked and flew backward in terror.","And yet...","With that one tap...","A Signature, an identity of a very profound existence flickered!","And the ash came.","A wave of swirling gray- final and unfathomable, wrapped the creature in a sea of ruin.","Even as its Dead True Source screamed in defiance, its body and being destabilized, breaking down...","Until it became ash.","Within a second, a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity-level Dead Thing was reduced to flickering dust.","...!","All other Dead Things paused mid-devouring.","They roared, not in triumph, but in dread.","And the one bearing the True Source of Asche narrowed his gaze, his voice cutting through the chaos.","\"You've eaten up so much... stay behind for me.\"","WAA!","He had killed more Dead Things than he could remember over the eons.","And now...","He was simply adding to his tally."]},{"number":3674,"title":"Chapter 3674: Chapter 3673: Point of No Return I","paragraphs":["Inside a Gateway Domus swirling with ten Wild True Sources, the holder of the True Source of Asche began wiping out the Dead Things he had drawn in over the years.","They arrived at the doorways and would see his figure, knowing he was too powerful for them to attack and overcome.","But since he never attacked, and they could remain inside the Domus to devour Wild True Sources constantly... they stayed and did so.","Carefully.","Or so they believed.","But their time was limited- they were simply lambs being led to slaughter. And now, the slaughter had begun as seas of ash swirled around the Dead Things, breaking down their True Sources in terrifying ways because even that which was dead... turned to ash.","As this occurred in one Gateway Domus...","In another, a Wild True Source of Oxidation descended from above, coming to layer itself upon the Wild True Sources of Verbum, Fear, and Causality.","Wherever this True Source passed, existence degraded. Corrosion swept through anything that was or could be as if any weak True Source of Existence came close, it would rust and decay unfathomably fast.","It was a terrifying True Source to encounter, and it made its descent into the same Gateway Domus that Noah, the Great Beyonder, and Veyl'Aethra occupied.","Its arrival drew the raging auras of three Dead Things, howling with the kind of baleful fury only those who missed something vital could emit.","They had missed their chance to enter the genuine wheel of existence.","Because the protector of the previous Domus had returned to the folds of the wheel itself, and two \"lucky\" Dead Things had managed to follow the Origin Singed down that path.","But these three had not.","So they came now- late, furious, and full of spite as Noah and the Great Beyonder looked at each other.","In a distant place, their weavings intertwined as Noah continued Eclipse Merging—Dual Evolution. Their Purity surged, and the Great Beyonder pushed herself to stabilize at the threshold of a Quasi-Resplendent Monad.","And at that moment- she chose to reveal it.","She asked herself- What does it mean to step into the stage of a Quasi-Resplendent Monad?","The answer was Purity.","When the Purity of one's True Source reached a certain threshold, it shone with terrifying radiance. Deep within her, her identity crystallized into a singular emblem.","A Mythic True Signature formed entirely from her True Source of Runes.","It was as if she had crafted a second self, born of incomprehensible purity. And though it remained within her...","\"Come out.\"","She spoke with quiet command, her eyes flashing. From the depths of her being, a dazzling, illusory obsidian-gold form erupted.","It was massive- so immense that its conceptual size dwarfed understanding.","A manifestation of her identity- an illusory titan made of black-gold light hovered above her, expanding to the length of an entire Omniverse.","Next to it, her physical body seemed insignificant.","But her Mythic True Signature...was everything!","And perhaps the most astonishing part- she barely needed to exert any Authority to manifest it.","Her signature was no different than a human smiling or waving. Just a natural expression of who she was.","So the Great Beyonder let it shine.","The massive signature towered above her, taking the form of a dark-haired woman whose presence radiated unfathomable beauty and power. She gazed down upon the three oncoming Dead Things, who raged and roared, throwing out their True Sources in blind fury.","But the Great Beyonder's Mythic True Signature opened its mouth and dominance rolled out like a storm. Quintillions of Runes erupted like a beam of reality-shattering light, slamming toward all three Dead Things.","BOOM!","The Dead Things recoiled.","The Mythic Signature had formed so quickly, they couldn't dodge it. The obsidian pillar of brilliance consumed them near-instantly.","Their Dead True Sources screamed like fresh flesh sizzling in boiling oil.","Collapse surged through them.","Quintillions of Runes pierced their True Sources, unraveling everything that made them them.","And within those Runes...was heat.","The heat of Flames.","Eclipse Merging.","Dual Evolution.","The design of the True Severed Origin Osmontian wasn't just a dual cultivation method. It was a way to evolve True Sources and to transform their very essence. To evolve them!","And now, the Beyonder's True Source of Runes displayed a new quality.","It roared with a penetrating glare, cutting through all three Dead Things simultaneously. It was about to cleave them in half...until a voice stopped it.","\"Leave a shred of their Source intact. I have uses for them...\"","Noah's voice rang out with calm finality. The Great Beyonder's eyes flashed as she commanded her Mythic Signature to obey.","It cleaved their bodies, leaving them split in half- just enough of their True Sources still pulsing in the distance.","The terrifying pillar of Runes remained as from within it, a single Rune pulsed white-gold and ignited, shaping into the figure of Noah.","...!","He had warped across the span of an entire Omniverse to appear beside the three decimated Dead Things. His chest radiated as three white-gold tendrils burst out, wrapping around their crumbling forms and dragging them into his chest.","Their Dead True Sources had no resistance left. They'd been shredded by the storm of Runes, nearly collapsing into oblivion.","So from Noah, the Cradle of Purity emerged- its tendrils searing with light. They coiled around the Dead Things like celestial chains and yanked them into his chest.","Then...they vanished.","...!","It took a a while to describe.","But in reality, everything had occurred in a single second- from the Great Beyonder's signature unveiling that released a magnificent Mythic True Signature, to Noah's sudden appearance near the decimated Dead Things, to the moment the three Dead Things were dragged into his chest into the Cradle of Purity!","One second.","And the collapse of three Dead Things was complete.","\"...\"","Silence followed.","A crushing, awe-filled stillness blanketed the Gateway Domus as Veyl'Aethra- and even the other Dead Things still exerting their power around the Wild True Sources- froze and stared!"]},{"number":3675,"title":"Chapter 3675: Chapter 3674: Point of No Return II","paragraphs":["Three Dead Things- cleared in a second.","And these particular three weren't just any Dead Things. They came from a new Gateway, seething with rage- rage that stemmed from missing their chance to enter the folds of the Wheel of Existence.","But all of that fury?","It meant absolutely nothing when their Dead True Sources collapsed instantly!","Veyl'Aethra stared up, stunned, eyes locked on the impossibly massive Mythic True Signature swirling above them.","\"That... how did you manage to achieve that?\"","His voice was dazed. So were his weavings. He knew the kind of power the Great Beyonder commanded- but he had no explanation for how she had gone from releasing Pillars of Concordance... to a Mythic True Signature.","The Great Beyonder's face didn't so much as flinch. Her gaze was fixed on Noah- the distant figure who had just absorbed three Dead Things into his chest like it was the most natural thing in the world.","She couldn't explain exactly what she had done- or what she was still doing, hidden within the privacy of an Amarantos Dream deep in the Weavings of the Wheel.","But her eyes carried a sharpness. A caution.","A message pulsed outward to Noah.","\"You've revealed so many different things in such a short time that maybe I don't even need to ask. But... did you really just draw in the remnants of the Dead True Sources of those three?\"","Her voice was calm, but edged in disbelief.","\"Life and death don't mix. I've heard of many who've faced Fractal Collapse just for trying to devour incompatible Wild True Sources—much less Dead Things. But you already know that.\"","She said it because she had to. Because no matter how much she believed in the power of the one who had opened up new pathways of power, what he was doing defied reason.","And if he didn't speak up before doing things like this, it could come off as nothing short of absurd.","She didn't wait for his reply. After all they'd shared, she already knew the answer.","\"You're not going to tell me that what happens to others- collapse, corruption, taint- won't apply to you, even though you just devoured the remnants of three Dead True Sources of Existence, right?\"","...!","She said it anyway.","And from the distance, Noah's only reply was a smile.","The Great Beyonder sighed as silence hung between them. Then, her Mythic True Signature turned toward the other Dead Things still prowling their Gateway Domus.","\"Since someone unfathomable and impossible to understand has arrived... it's time this Gateway was cleared of all Dead Things that have been plaguing it for far too long.\"","...!","Her Mythic True Signature glared down with glacial resolve and brilliant cold fury.","No matter what their Dead True Sources represented.","No matter how many millions of years they had wandered across Infinite Ravines- or what lay beyond them.","In that moment, the Great Beyonder, newly ascended, struck to annihilate.","Meanwhile, the one who had set all of this in motion was facing wonders of his own, deep within the Weavings of Existence.","His main body was etching the final and most powerful System of Existence within the Ninth Mundi of Power.","Something else hadn't been planned, but it was happening as thanks to his design of a third Mechanic of Ascension through Eclipse Merging- Dual Evolution, he achieved something even faster.","|The Pathway to the True Source of Runes has been thoroughly walked and understood through the merging of true flames into the definition of Runes within the Great Beyonder.|","|Your own definition of Runes has been completed.|","|The True Source of Runes blooms to fruition.|","HUUM!","Who said Dual Cultivation held no power?","Who said one couldn't attain a True Source through it?","Well, there were many prerequisites. But Noah had met them. And in this moment, through a new companionship, he attained another True Source of Existence.","His Weavings burned anew, stepping forward in complexity once more.","And that wasn't all.","A newly born Affix began to bloom.","|Three Dead True Sources of Existence have been pulled into the Cradle of Purity.|","|The Dead True Sources are deemed Moderate in Complexity, and Below Average in Purity.|","|Refinement and Purification of the Three Dead True Sources has begun.|","The Cradle of Purity lit up with fantastical brilliance. And while this process unfolded, Noah was also devouring two more Dead True Sources- those he'd battled alongside the Origin Singed.","But there was one more his Weavings were reaching for.","A being far stronger than any Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Noah had faced.","This one was returning to power.","He was healing- regaining strength and edging closer and closer past Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.","His name was Bob!","Trapped in the True Frequency of the Singed, his body bound inside an endless prison of Ruination. Noah's tendrils had already pierced the prison's walls—nibbling at the brilliance of Khaos.","Bob's cold eyes turned toward them.","He wasn't like other enemies- ones that could be overpowered and discarded easily in a single fight. Bob held the True Source of Khaos and, horrifyingly, an Absolute Complex True Source- even if it was a Dead one.","A black Wheel of Existence floated behind him.","His final card. His last move.","And if he used it to break free from this prison....he knew. Even Bob knew he would forfeit his right to fight for the depths of the Wheel of Existence where he believed an answer to where The Loom was existed!","His journey... would end.","The realization cut through him like truth. And Bob spoke.","\"Many, many dangerous things happen...when someone's pushed to desperation.\"","...!","His voice always had weight.","Even now, he made the norm feel unnatural and dangerous.","And as he spoke, obsidian stellar seas of the True Source of Existence intruded upon the prison of Ruination. Alongside them, a new True Source bloomed as billions of golden Runes exploded into reality.","Runes.","Gold and glorious.","Gold and resplendent.","Bob's eyes widened as the Runes crashed down around him. He understood once more that Noah was coming for everything- to devour and take everything he held!","All paths.","All exits.","And that... drove him to the edge of true desperation.","\"You're pulling out True Sources from your arse like it's the easiest thing in the world,\" Bob voiced out. \"More and more signs that this Wheel of Existence might actually be the one that holds that piece of the puzzle. And since I can't reach it, since you've pushed me this far...I can only say that whatever comes next...you engineered it. You made it possible.\"","...!","Three True Sources of Existence clashed around him.","And at that moment, Bob's black Wheel of Existence materialized. His body overlapped with it, settling in its very core, tentacle-like limbs gripping the outer rims of the Dead Absolute Complex True Source.","He closed his eyes.","Tears fell.","And in a voice cracked with time and longing, he called out to a soul nestled within the Wheel.","\"Wait just a little bit longer for Dad to get you, okay?\"","...!","A small soul stirred at the center of the Wheel, hearing a voice for the first time in millions of years.","And after that... incandescent brilliance erupted all around him."]},{"number":3676,"title":"Chapter 3676: Chapter 3675: Point of No Return III","paragraphs":["With tears streaming from his eyes, Bob became transfused onto the black Wheel of Existence.","The Dead Absolute Complex True Source!","He sensed the terrifying complexity radiating from all around the bindings of the crimson prison. Apart from this True Source, he felt the stellar obsidian-black True Source that could revert existence, and now, a third True Source that displayed billions of golden runes.","\"With every passing second, you grow stronger and stronger. A new True Source seems to bud from you as easily as breathing. My fate... is likely to face imprisonment and the gradual breakdown of my Existence with your increasing complexity. So let me take myself out of the equation.\"","...!","Bob uttered these words as Noah moved even faster.","All of his True Sources held Average Complexity, with only his Purity surging at the Moderate level!","Against Bob, who had likely once surpassed the level of a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity before the collapse of his weavings...it wasn't enough to bring him down quickly.","Not against someone whose True Source of Khaos burned with a high level of complexity.","Not against someone who held a genuine Dead Absolute Complex True Source!","A black wheel, which he currently grasped by its rims, erupted with black brilliance that covered him entirely in its light. That same light pushed away Noah's billions of runes, seas of dark brilliance, and the crimson of Ruination!","\"You have made me a desperate man, Noah Osmont.\"","WAA!","Bob's voice held no emotion or friendliness.","\"And with desperation... comes pain on both sides. I know pain. I understand pain. I hope you are ready for it too... Friend. I will be back with the means necessary to obtain what I need.\"","...!","Friend.","When he had said it before, multiple times, it carried a trace of weavings that it might have been true.","That he had considered it a possibility.","But at this moment, the word was unfathomably cold and filled with apathy. From the Black Wheel of Existence, Bob's figure became entirely bathed in black brilliance as he... disappeared from the endless prison of Ruination!","Khaos vanished, leaving behind faint remnants.","The glimmer of the Black Wheel of Existence remained as it flashed. Noah looked upon it with heaviness as he bellowed out.","\"ECHOES OF THE UNWRITTEN!\"","HUUM!","His seas of the True Source of Existence pulsed and seethed as he sought to undo an event!","But...","BZZT!","The Black Wheel of Existence, still present, spun heavily as it released waves of Complexity that resisted the reversal of this event!","\"Echoes! Of! The! Unwritten!\"","...!","Noah's eyes shone with brilliance as he bellowed again, his True Source of Existence burning brightly, but the result was the same.","The first event he could not undo stood before him, with Bob having left behind a glimmer of the Black Wheel of Existence to prevent it.","And he called it a glimmer because with every passing second, the Dead Absolute Complex True Source of Existence became more and more illusory, as if it might fade at any moment.","\"...\"","Noah gazed at it with utter coldness. He despised the idea of an enemy escaping and prolonging conflict. He sought closure at every turn. But when it came to Bob- and the literal Absolute Complex True Source he wielded- what could be done?","He had come infinitely close to the core of the Wheel of Existence, closer than ever before. But even then, he couldn't reach it, not while Noah continued to display increasingly greater Complexity.","Unlike other maddened entities who would despair and go all out, Bob had done the rational thing- he left.","And he didn't just leave the True Frequency of the Singed.","He left the Wheel of Existence entirely.","Noah could confirm this with his current Complexity. When he tried to undo the event, he felt the push and pull leading toward the Infinite Ravines themselves!","\"...\"","He floated gloriously in the white-gold brilliance of the True Frequency of the Singed, his expression heavy.","True Sources swirled around him, but he felt no joy. This result could be considered both a success and a failure.","The threat of Bob was eliminated...","But only temporarily.","What would a man driven to desperation do to ensure that, when he returned, things would play out differently?","Especially one who understood Noah's rapid rate of progression, and knew the more time that passed, the stronger Noah would become, and the harder it would be to face him.","What would such an entity do to achieve his goals?","\"...\"","The possibilities were many.","And none of them were good!","Noah remained floating in the True Frequency of the Singed, his weavings continuing to press down on the illusory Black Wheel of Existence. Remnant tendrils of Khaos moved to devour anything they could, the Cradle of Purity buzzing softly at his chest.","But at this moment, only remnant weavings of Bob remained- everything else about him was gone!","This meant that now, only two Dead Things remained within the weavings of the Wheel. Noah's weavings, burning with frustration, turned fully upon them!","—","In the Frequency of Light.","The Gray-Wheeled Tentacled Dead Thing and the Heran Megalos Dead Thing were still facing the Pillars of Concordance of the Origin Singed, alongside countless tendrils of Ruination conducting Existential Unraveling.","But now, Noah's gaze carried a weight of livid determination as he called out coldly.","\"Existential Engraving.\"","WAA!","Billions of golden runes unfurled from him, rushing toward the Two Dead Things already surrounded by multiple True Sources.","And unlike Bob, these Two Dead Things lacked the backing of an Absolute Complex True Source of Existence. So when the golden runes descended, they couldn't push them away so easily!","One golden rune after another became bound to their bodies while the tendrils of Ruination ran rampant, dividing their attention further.","Slowly, thousands of golden runes became branded into their bodies- their Weavings of Existence- as they became engraved!","Existential Engraving.","At that moment, Noah was beginning to understand that Runes were not just a language, but living codes.","Living, breathing codes of existence itself... and of what it could become."]},{"number":3677,"title":"Chapter 3677: Chapter 3676: Point of No Return IV","paragraphs":["Codes of Existence.","Living, breathing weavings of Existence- that was how he saw Runes. And if he engraved his Runes of Existence onto the True Source of another...","He could rewrite their living code.","He could alter their living record.","Or, in the case of the Dead Things, their Dead Records.","When the Dead Things had thousands of Runes engraved across their bodies, they realized- too late- that the output of their True Sources was gradually being cut off. Their bodies could no longer express it freely.","Which gave the tendrils of Ruination more freedom to unravel their existence, as even more golden Runes latched onto their Dead True Sources.","When a million Runes were branded into their forms, more than half of their True Source output was severed.","\"OOOH!\"","They roared in maddened defiance, while opposite them, the figure of the Origin Singed watched Noah, his expression carved from stone.","Once over half of their True Sources were bound and suppressed, the unraveling through Ruination intensified. Their bodies were consumed—wrapped in countless crimson tendrils.","And then, hundreds of millions of golden Runes locked into their essence. Soon after, their Dead True Sources ceased all expression.","...!","What they could express was no longer their own.","The Codes of Existence themselves bound to their essence, rewriting their very function-sealing their ability to even spread their weavings.","It was a horrifying act.","And as it took form, Noah floated toward the two bound Dead Things.","Their forms shimmered, incandescent golden Runes glowing across their surfaces, engraved deep into the framework of their existence.","He stood before them, eyes cold, hands clenched. The Runes binding them flickered and began to tear them apart.","Noah was literally ripping them to pieces.","He was furious.","He was livid!","\"Give me your memories.\"","HUUM!","\"Give me your records.\"","WAA!","\"Give me everything.\"","...!","He hadn't gotten what he needed from Bob.","So he took it out on these two.","And in doing so, he scattered their remnants into the Cradle of Purity, officially and personally destroying two Dead Things almost entirely by his own power as the wary Origin Singed floated nearby, gaze sharp.","Even then, his eyes flickered again. Changed and altered.","He looked inward.","And what he sensed stopped his weavings cold.","Something was devouring his True Source.","A sensation so vast and terrible that it should have been impossible not to notice—yet here it was, eclipsing over half his True Source before he even felt it.","This had been happening for some time.","Likely ever since...","Ever since his weavings of existence had been rewound. Healed.","When...!","His eyes flared with light. He looked at the back of the entity tearing the Dead Things apart.","One man. Against a half-shattered white Wheel of Existence sunken to his chest, nearly collapsed- had managed to reverse the unraveling.","But in that act of reversal, he had done something.","\"What did you do to me?\"","The Origin Singed's eyes burned as he shouted the question across the space between them.","What had Noah done?","Noah didn't turn. Didn't glance back at the flaming white-gold body of the being whose weavings he disapproved of. His reply came low and sharp.","\"I did nothing. I simply didn't move to correct anything.\"","He had seen the Great Usurper's weavings within the Wheel- had seen him use Bob's necrotizing strike, the one that shattered an Absolute Complex True Source of Existence. A strike that should've ended someone like the Origin Singed.","And Noah...had simply let it happen.","He might have even helped.","Because...","\"You don't seem to be using the True Source of the Singed well enough. Let someone else do it on your behalf.\"","...!","His words, cold as the abyss, landed like blades.","The Origin Singed's face twisted, knowing over half of his weavings were no longer his own- commandeered by something else.","\"The Wheel weaves as the Wheel weaves,\" he said stiffly, maintaining a hold on his composure. \"But the Wheel will not stand for this.\"","A threat. Thinly veiled.","The Wheel would not allow one of its Protectors to be usurped.","But Noah never looked back. He kept ripping apart the weavings of two Dead Things.","His reply?","\"What could you possibly know of what the Wheel wants... and doesn't want?\"","HUUM!","With that, the body of the Origin Singed began to tremble.","Behind him, the illusion of a flickering white Wheel of Existence pulsed, then blinked in and out of view.","A moment passed.","Then his body went completely still.","Seconds later, his head rose.","His expression shifted.","And then...","A wide grin bloomed on his face.","\"Holy shit.\"","The voice was not the Origin Singed's.","It belonged to someone else.","To the Great Usurper.","He lifted his hands, staring at them—at the vibrant True Source bubbling inside him. Then turned toward the shattered illusion of the white Wheel behind him.","And grinned wider.","\"Even if it's broken,\" he said, awed, \"the remnants of an Absolute Complex True Source are fantastic. I used a shred of their last authority to conduct the quickest and most thorough Subjugation of a Source.\"","His voice surged with power.","In mere moments, he had seized one of the mightiest True Source entities born of the Wheel—and made it his.","A radiant True Source, flickering with corruption and purity alike, danced across his fingertips. Remnants of a Dead Absolute Complex True Source still burned within his soul.","Noah finally turned, looking at his old friend.","His voice came calm.","\"The living and the dead don't mix... so how do your weavings feel?\"","The Great Usurper stood within the body of the Origin Singed, cloaked in dead souls from Bob's weavings. Bathed in the True Source of another.","He smiled.","\"My existence remains living. And with these pure flames of the Origin Singed, I can purge all traces of Dead Sources. But...\" he tilted his head slightly, eyes distant, \"All weavings of Dead Things are calling to me now. I'm getting faster. More precise at usurping the souls of the Dead. It's like they're missing something vital—something that makes it easier for my weavings to spread. I think...\"","He paused, then nodded.","\"I think I'll chase more Dead Things. Head to the Infinite Ravines, where this guy just was. You good down here?\"","...!","The Great Usurper's path shimmered into existence before him.","And as Noah finished clearing the Wheel of Existence of all remaining Dead Things—the only ones that remained were already waiting... in the Infinite Ravines."]},{"number":3678,"title":"Chapter 3678: Chapter 3677: Point of No Return V","paragraphs":["The living and the dead did not mix.","This statement seemed to be an absolute truth that remained staunch, and yet, as always- exceptions existed!","That which used to be the Origin Singed was struck by a half-shattered Dead Absolute Complex True Source, nearly causing his existence to collapse. But at that critical moment, the intervention of Noah and the weavings of the Great Usurper striking at the same time allowed something fantastical to be born.","The old Origin Singed, who had lived for millions of years, was no more. His pure flames were now under the control of the Great Usurper, who found a surprising connection and calling to the Dead Things.","The living was being drawn toward the dead, and for reasons unknown, it was unfathomably easier for him to expand his efforts of usurpation upon them than anyone else.","Noah looked at the figure of the Great Usurper as he acclimated to his new body and gave a light nod.","\"No other Dead Things exist in these weavings of the wheel. At this moment, the only possible source of trouble remains the Infinite Ravines. Be careful there.\"","He offered the warning to his old friend, who smiled toward him and gave a light nod as his body began to burn with white-gold flames.","\"To this day, I can never quite get a handle on the progression of power. When I took over the body of an Existence Severing entity, I looked at the very concept of existence they severed and thought to myself- wow, this is absolutely incredible. Then I took over a Pioneer, then a Lesser Source, a Greater Source, a Prime Source... every single one made me feel and see more. Now, I've got my hands on a True Source- someone at the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity stage, apparently... and who knows what lies beyond this?\"","The Great Usurper spoke with a smile full of melancholy, as if he was both expectant and cautious of what the future held.","Noah looked toward him, his calm weavings settling, as he replied.","\"True Sources are the apex of complexity in existence, yet they are also stages filled with countless wonders. They rely on both the Purity and Complexity of Existence. You'll gain complexity fairly easily; the main issue is Purity. But you did take over the body of the Origin Singed- one of the purest existences due to his concept. So maybe you'll be okay in that field as well. For the Infinite Ravines- do you want to come to the same region where I am with a few others, or...\"","Noah posed the question, but the Great Usurper shook his head vehemently.","\"The same Gateway Domus as you? Not in a million years. I assume you'll clear it fairly soon—it might be empty of Dead Things right after. Ashmole had a point when he spoke about you and your Flow. It's far too massive...you absorb everything around you. Your Flow is bigger than mine as you're the one person I never wanted to compete against when it comes to resources. When there's an overabundance of them, I'll be there. And with the memories of the Origin Singed... what lies beyond the Infinite Ravines may be even more confounding, with countless opportunities waiting. But, one step at a time... one step at a time.\"","The Great Usurper made his decision. Noah nodded, watching as his old friend returned the gesture. His body began to flicker with a terrifying array of complexity as he took a step and disappeared.","\"I'll keep in touch. And I'll keep looking for Bob. He completely isolated me in the White Wheel of Existence, which he then destroyed—as if he knew that, someday, he would need to do that to deal with me and multiple other issues. Among all the enemies we've faced... this one is different. He feels like us—like someone supported by the very weavings of reality and existence...\"","The words of the Great Usurper resonated across the restoring frequency of light as Noah gave a light nod, watching as the weaving of his old friend vanished into the Weave and headed toward the Infinite Ravines.","Bob was like them.","This became more and more true over time. Of all the beings in his entire wheel-law of existence, Bob was the only one whose Flow exceeded all others.","A singular product of an entire Absolute Complex True Source.","Their first clash had ended, but he would return. When he did, Noah wanted to eliminate the sense of competition completely—to become so advanced in both Purity and Complexity of Existence that even if Bob was ten or a hundred times stronger than before, there would be ultimate closure by the time they met again.","He affirmed this silently as he examined his own existence.","The True Sources of the Singed, Existence, Ruination, and Runes burned within him.","Four True Sources of Existence!","Within his Cradle of Purity, he was drawing in multiple Dead Things, as they offered immense purity and complexity—resources he would soon allocate with purpose.","And his Last Mundi of Power... was nearly finished forming a new System of Existence. Once complete, his True Source Atlas of Existence would be whole.","There was much left to do, but he progressed steadily, ensuring the very weavings of existence around him didn't collapse.","Ruination would continue journeying across multiple frequencies of the wheel to obtain whatever shattered remnants and pieces remained—moving toward becoming a full Ruined Miniare Wheel of Existence.","If she could become an Absolute Complex True Source, it would mean another burst of complexity—ensuring Noah could handle any future battles effortlessly.","And then, there was the Infiniverse Megalos.","A wonder with complexity larger than any Frequency he had experienced so far—perhaps rivaled only by the true Frequency of the Singed.","Within this construct resided his family and his people.","Whenever he made tremendous leaps in complexity and power, they followed. At this moment, they had entire Frequencies of Existence as their playground.","It would be a time of preparation and of savoring the wonders that came with the complexity of existence as they readied themselves for whatever Bob or any other Dead Thing dared to throw their way."]},{"number":3679,"title":"Chapter 3679: Chapter 3678: Point of No Return VI","paragraphs":["One body of his finished up in the Frequency of Light.","Another body of his remained in the True Frequency of the Singed.","He looked at the necrotizing, shattered piece of a white Wheel of Existence that floated within his constraints and bindings as he surveyed this Frequency.","It no longer had its Origin Singed.","He looked at the many Singed who were gravely injured, as well as the figures of Emelline and Mysara.","They no longer had an Origin Singed to rely on at this moment, and Noah was all they had left.","Did that make him the True Origin Singed?","His gaze sharpened at such a weaving of an idea as he turned and looked toward the direction Bob had been trying so hard to reach.","Toward where the very core weavings of the Wheel of Existence should be!","—","As one man gazed over the endless weavings of the Wheel and what could possibly lie at their very center...","Across the endless Weave, where one could cross to enter countless Frequencies or step into the Infinite Ravines.","Within the Infinite Ravines themselves, inside a Gateway Domus filled with shattered mirrors reflecting absolutely nothing...","In here, the Omnifather could be seen sitting atop a fractured mirror, his form brilliantly massive and so vast that his sunken head alone had once been mistaken for a dying star.","His body was etched with ever-changing glyphs, ancient symbols of possible existences long collapsed. His flesh gleamed with multicolored brilliance- not like a rainbow, but like refracted stardust from a billion different parallel weavings of existence, constantly shifting in hue, tone, and density as if he were made from every plane of existence stitched together!","Yet... he looked truly worn.","Tired.","Sunken eyes, vast enough to hold the reflections of galaxies, stared downward, weighed by the burden of eons. His face was aged- wrinkled by gravity itself, time folding over it like paper too long exposed to the elements. His back was hunched, shoulders curled inward, as if the pressure of existence still rested upon them!","The Omnifather was the singular wielder of the True Source of Versality...was.","The Origin of variation, a source of infinite possibility and adaptation. Versality was the power to embody, merge, or reinterpret every other possibility out there. It had limitless fluidity. However, this blessing was also a curse. Versality never ceases. It shifts endlessly, pulling on him, draining him, never allowing rest, as even his existence must change. Thus, he appeared fractured and weary- a being endlessly rewriting himself, bearing the totality of all the possible forms he could be!","It was why, when he failed Existence Severing, he did not perish.","There were countless other possibilities of him that did not fail.","So he simply pulled upon them.","He made his mistakes.","A great deal of them, in fact.","His sunken eyes thought about the Dead Thing he had let in countless years ago, because he simply wanted to return into the weavings of the Wheel.","The Dead Thing...","HUUUM!","In his thoughts, the massive figure of the Omnifather was forced to raise his head as he felt the terrifying glow of a Dead Thing's complexity erupting across the Gateway Domus he protected!","And when he looked, he found this Dead Thing looking back at him.","Shooting across the Domus as if it were coming from the direction of... the Wheel of Existence itself.","As if it was leaving the Wheel of Existence, crossing the Gateway Domus, and heading out toward the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","The Omnifather looked at the Dead Thing, his eyes trembling in incredulity and shock.","The Dead Thing—Bob—surrounded by a dazzling Dead Absolute Complex True Source of Existence, looked back at him. Their gazes locked briefly before Bob's cold, apathetic eyes turned away from the Omnifather, as if he had merely observed someone inconsequential.","But the Omnifather was shaken. That... was Bob!","A Watcher of the Wheelomachy. The Disciple of the First Watcher!","But he was a Dead Thing?","And as the Omnifather looked at the Black Wheel of Existence around Bob, he went ashen as he recognized that Wheel—it was the same one that had wrapped around a tentacled creature...","A Dead Thing he had once let into the Wheel and hunted down himself to kill and eradicate, as it had ruined his tremendous Purity and prevented him from becoming a Resplendent Monad!","But... they were one and the same?","And now it was leaving the Wheel of Existence?!","The more the Omnifather thought about it, the more ashen he became as he imagined disastrous consequences!","\"STOP!\"","He roared, his billowing True Source of Versality erupting, but the blinding black brilliance covering Bob was far too intricate and complex. Bob did not even glance behind him as he continued to tear across the Gateway Domus until he flickered out of existence!","...!","The Omnifather breathed heavily as he stared at the scene.","His eyes pulsed with lividity and rage as he roared, his body splitting apart as one of him surged ahead.","Following where Bob had vanished—into the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, where rare were the entities of the Wheel of Existence who dared to go...","Unless they had abandoned their posts.","Past a Gateway Domus.","And into the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","BOOM!","The unmaking of existence thundered out as the figure of Bob crossed a doorway and made a clean exit—appearing in an area filled with overlapping folds of existence and non-existence stretching out endlessly in all directions!","From where he came, one could barely make out a flicker of life amid all the death.","It looked like a shattered mirror barely discernible amidst the obsidian folds of collapse, paradox, and fragmented existence—hidden between the folds of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, where the entrance to the Gateway Domus he had just exited lay!","The moment he arrived in the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, his body began to brim with a terrifying sense of Complexity as if unshackled. Black and white brilliance erupted from the Absolute Complex True Source of Existence that bathed over Bob, and in the next moment...","WAP!","Black and white separated.","In the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, two Bobs- one white, one black—appeared.","The White Bob looked weary and tired, while the Black Bob met his eyes with a cold gaze, his voice echoing out.","\"You tried things your way for millions of years, and look where that brought us.\"","...!","The Black Bob shone with interminable luminosity.","His Complexity was rising ever higher, while his Purity remained constant. His voice echoed, resonating with the weavings of collapse all around.","\"I'll take it from here.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":3680,"title":"Chapter 3680: Chapter 3679: Point of No Return VII","paragraphs":["He would take it from here.","The version of Bob that shone with an obsidian luster spoke, his voice low and final, as a terrifying level of complexity radiated from his body in waves.","The other Bob, bathed in white light and brilliance, said nothing. His silence felt ancient, as if it carried the weight of millions of years spent drifting through the Nullvein Gravewake Folds and the Wheel of Existence. He simply floated, silent, as the obsidian Bob reached out and grasped the black Absolute Complex True Source of Existence.","With a slow breath, he clutched it tightly. Then, using his left hand- now transformed into a crescent-shaped blade- he cleaved open his own chest in one swift strike.","No blood spilled. There was none left to give.","Bob pushed the black wheel of existence into the gaping wound, inch by agonizing inch, until the entirety of the Dead Absolute Complex True Source of Existence was sealed inside him.","Into his being.","It was a choice with no return.","Even if he found what he was searching for- the one thing whose presence was rumored to be hidden deep in the Wheel of Existence- even if he discovered The Loom, this act made certain he could never reclaim the status of the living.","\"I will ensure her weavings remain untouched. I will find THAT at all costs, and I will bring her back from the fate of a Dead Thing. I will see her smile again. No matter what.\"","For her.","He would give up everything for her.","Even this- the irreversible union with a Dead Absolute Complex True Source of Existence.","He had passed the threshold.","A point of no return!","There would be no going back.","But this...this was only the beginning.","The obsidian Bob turned to the white Bob, his complexity rising in terrifying bursts of light as he spoke, his voice cold and resolute.","\"Rest.\"","WAA!","\"You've worked hard all these years,\" he added, softer now. \"You can rest.\"","...!","The expression on the white Bob was heavy, worn. He closed his eyes like a soldier laying down his sword, and in the next breath, his body dissolved into radiant light- disappearing into the obsidian form of the other Bob.","His form now shimmered with layers of radiant waves, and as he exhaled, he turned his gaze toward a far-off direction, speaking aloud-though more to himself than anyone else.","\"You shattered my home looking for answers about The Loom—the Pirene of Existence. You know more about it than anyone I've ever encountered. But what would you do... if you knew where its Weavings might be hidden?\"","...!","His words carried the weight of choices his other self would have never made.","Because the one he spoke of- that entity- was something else entirely. A being that had laid waste to entire Frequencies with nothing but a thought in his Wheel of Existence.","A creature that, when disappointed by what lay at the core of an Absolute Complex True Source of Existence, had simply devoured its Coressence and shattered it.","What if that being entered the scene?","Another irreversible point.","And—","\"STOP!\"","A booming roar thundered from a shimmering doorway buried within the Nullvein Gravewake Folds. The Omnifather emerged.","A furious giant.","His multicolored brilliance flared with rage, Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity blazing from his form as he stared down Bob.","\"You! Have you been active in the Wheel all these years? What have you done? What have you done?!\"","BOOM!","Versality exploded into existence- a brilliance of infinite possibilities and cascading variations.","And still, Bob stared back coldly... and tapped.","A single tap.","As if the very Folds themselves- the paradox, the collapse, the unknown- answered to him.","A wave of terrifying complexity surged forward, wrapping around the Omnifather's radiant power.","In a blink...","Possibilities vanished.","Variations shattered.","The weavings of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds crushed the Omnifather's might, until all that remained was a glimmering Crystallized True Source.","The obsidian Bob raised his hand, drew the crystal in- and swallowed it.","...!","Then, his gaze turned to the shattered, mirror-like doorway that led into the Infinite Ravines of the Wheel of Existence- a place where the Weavings of Noah Osmont lingered.","He spoke coldly, his words laced with timeworn gravity.","\"Existence is but a stage. All the living and the dead are merely players. Each has their entrance, and each- an exit. Each has a role before they fade. It's not a matter of if. Only when.\"","Heavy. Ancient.","His form flickered, and then he vanished, a streak of light swallowed by the immeasurable depth of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","He had just decimated a True Source that had reached the height of Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity.","Even if it was merely half- a body conjured through the hands of the Omnifather- it had still fallen.","The reasons were layered.","Partly because of the terrifying transformation Bob had undergone.","Partly... because the Folds themselves favored the Dead.","In this realm of collapse and paradox, the weavings of Dead Things surged with twice, even thrice the power compared to the living.","So yes- extinguishing a True Source happened in an instant.","And moments after the Omnifather fell...","WAP!","A new burst of multicolored brilliance lit the air.","A weakened, worn visage of the Omnifather emerged, trembling.","He had less than a tenth of his original complexity and purity. Still, he lived.","He inhaled ragged breaths, his body trembling from death's touch, and stared at the shattered entrance of his Domus.","Without a word, he flew back into it.","\"...\"","Silence reigned.","Only the eerie howls of complexity echoed across the region of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","Until...","BZZT.","From the darkness, an illusory nine-pointed star bloomed.","And a man stepped forth.","His face was peaceful- but troubled.","He had waited here, guided by the whisper of his own Weavings, believing he would find peace.","Instead, he had witnessed a force he could not comprehend.","He had watched a being he could not see through... walk away after speaking utterly ominous words!"]},{"number":3681,"title":"Chapter 3681: Chapter 3680: Point of No Return VIII","paragraphs":["[Existence is but a stage. All the living and the dead are merely players on this stage. Every single one will have their entrance—and their exit...]","...!","Those words echoed in the Peacemaker's mind as he sighed, eyes drifting down to the Enneagram pulsing on his chest.","\"This was supposed to bring me peace? I don't like it. Where are the last remnants that'll complete you? A full Absolute Complex True Source...that's the only thing that'll give me peace when facing someone like him. And he's leaving, probably to return with reinforcements. We need to get you ready. Fast.\"","He spoke to the Enneagram as it began to hum, glowing with brilliance that poured across his form before his illusory image vanished, swallowed by the folds of the Nullvein Gravewake.","—","Within the weavings of the Wheel's flow.","In the Prime Frequency of the End.","The Infiniverse Megalos.","The Infiniverse Megalos could shrink to the size of a grain of sand, yet span across uncharted light-years.","There, in a far-flung corner, the Queen of Matter hovered, studying the massive Vein in the shape of an infinity symbol.","Books spun excitedly around her- each one alive with pulsing light- as she floated in a white dress that shimmered like the remnants of forgotten stars.","\"Where to start? Where to start! The lost Harem members? The only Son of the True Emperor of Quintessence? The left-behind Primogenitors? The hot beach boy, Erikson? Ayame? Ugh, I can't choose!\"","She smiled, twirling. So many fables she'd only read about and now, she could finally meet them.","But then, her laughter faded into a sigh.","\"I know the fate of existence is kind of... hanging by a thread. Is now really the time to meet my heroes?\"","What she wanted to do and what she should do clashed inside her.","And yet... her resolve hardened.","\"The True Emperor of Quintessence will handle Bob and any other existential messes. I'll help in my own way. I don't need to change who I am, do I? Especially since I have this...\"","She turned, glancing over her shoulder.","Behind her dress stretched illusory strings-vast, radiant threads connecting her to the very Infiniverse Megalos. Her Source had been altered permanently by its power.","Her Complexity and Purity surged upward. She was rising into the realm of those she'd once called legends...eventually anyways.","And if that was the case-","\"I'll meet all those I only read about before. And I'll start with...\"","She opened a glowing book. Her hand pressed a name that lit up in starlit gold.","Shadow Guard, Night.","\"Huhu... huhu! She must have written volumes on Queen Adelaide and the others! You're first.\"","She shot forward like a comet, her Source guiding her straight to the Fable she longed to meet.","A short distance away, still within the Megalos...","An illusory figure- the Infiniverse Megalos Body, watched it all with calm poise. Her expression thoughtful, her eyes shifted to a distant corner of reality before she spoke aloud.","\"Master, I wish to come with you. To see what you are about to see.\"","...!","Her voice sent a message across Existence.","To Noah.","What he was about to witness?","It was located within the True Frequency of the Singed.","The Absolute Complex True Source.","The Wheel of Existence.","She didn't have to wait long.","Noah replied simply.","\"Come, then.\"","...!","Existence buzzed.","Complexity pulsed.","And then, she disappeared.","—","In the True Frequency of the Singed.","Noah flew forward, streaking across seas of flames- waves growing more intense and more concentrated with every mile.","White-gold gave way to pure white. The color of the Heart of Existence itself.","The further he went, the more condensed and pure the flames became.","Until...","A rift appeared in the distance.","Nothing grand—just a simple white tear in space, exuding terrifying purity.","Just as he neared, space warped.","And the Infiniverse Megalos Body appeared beside him.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body was akin to an embodiment of boundless reality as she stood like an existential empress woven from the threads of existence itself.","She wore a flowing dress of radiant white and gold, its fabric seemingly spun from the starlight of collapsed Megalos. Inlaid across the dress were countless gems shaped like endless loops- symbols of infinity that shimmered with shifting hues, each gem echoing a different Pantheonic Megalos within the Infiniverse.","Her hair, a cascading waterfall of white brilliance, fell past her shoulders like the remnants of forgotten mana. Her gaze was ageless as her eyes exuded wisdom, command, and unshakable poise.","She had come entirely ready to see the core of the Absolute Complex True Source!","Noah smiled, extending his hand.","She took it, serene and steady.","Together, they walked forward.","Past waves of roaring complexity.","And into the white rift that only revealed itself in the deepest core of the True Frequency of the Singed.","Together... they stepped through.","HUUM!","Their very weavings trembled and vibrated as purity and complexity slammed against them like tidal waves.","Had they come without the protection of a True Source, they would have perished instantly.","As the barrage settled, Noah opened his eyes.","Before him lay an endless sea of white and gold, glowing with impossible brilliance and larger than many Frequencies of Existence combined.","And within this sea...floated fragments.","Remnants of a shattered Wheel.","White spokes. Gold spokes. Silver spokes. Scattered traces and ancient pieces- drifting, suspended, across the existential tide.","Yet in the far distance...","He saw it.","A smidge of something enormous.","Something whole.","Not shattered.","Not fractured.","A corner- just a glimpse- of an intact white-gold Wheel. A genuine Wheel of Existence.","But even that was not what held his gaze.","At the very center of the white-gold sea...between them and the Wheel...","Stood a man.","An old man, with wisps of white hair.","He wore a simple robe of white. A golden blindfold veiled his face- his wrinkled skin glowing faintly with serenity and age.","A blindfolded elder, standing where the core of the Wheel of Existence should be.","Noah's eyes narrowed.","Because the Purity radiating from this being...","It surpassed anyone he had ever encountered so far!"]},{"number":3682,"title":"Chapter 3682: Chapter 3681: The Breaking of The Wheel I","paragraphs":["An old man with white hair and a white robe, with a golden blindfold on his face.","Noah looked at such a being as they floated serenely in a sea of white-gold brilliance.","Everything around seemed filled with waves of radiant purity, and this being himself seemed to account for more than half of all that purity.","It was an existence that stood in an area which contained the core weavings of the very Wheel of Existence.","So what exactly could such a being represent?","Noah was not a fan of riddles as he and the Infiniverse Megalos Body moved closer across the vast white-gold sea while Noah's voice echoed out.","\"An old man with a blindfold where the very core of the weavings of the Wheel is... who might Sir be?\"","His tone was that of calm, regal dignity blooming as he asked such a question.","And opposite them, the old man did not raise his gaze or look toward them, as if he were truly blind.","He simply remained in his current position, floating while standing within an endless sea of purity.","His lips moved as he replied with an ancient voice, and if one heard it, they could distinctly notice the fact that such a voice... had not been used frequently.","As if the speaker had not opened his mouth for millions—or billions—of years.","It carried that sense of age and profundity!","\"I am The Witness.\"","...!","The Witness!","A grandiose distinction for any entity that would be in a place deeper than even the Origin Singed had been.","Noah was focused on this being, as his own distinction as the Weaver of Existence sought to unravel and understand the identity... of everything before him.","Meanwhile, the figure of the Infiniverse Megalos Body wasn't even looking at the old man, as her gaze was on the distant, massive section of the white-gold Wheel of Existence swimming in this vast and endless sea of purity.","This was her main focus, as she was here to see and understand what it meant to be an Absolute Complex True Source of Existence!","\"The Witness...\"","Noah said these words with care as he proceeded to continue.","\"And what exactly does The Witness... witness? I deal with a great deal of mysteries and complexities every single day—lately, I find myself liking simplicity and answers to mysteries more than anything.\"","His words echoed out as he affirmed that the being he was looking at... had a level of purity that exceeded the Quasi-Resplendent Monad that was the Great Beyonder at this moment.","If their power was so high, were they the actual final defender of the Wheel of Existence?","If Bob had managed to get through, would this be the final safeguard the Wheel of Existence had to stop everything?","After the old man was asked such a question, his lips formed a wizened, crescent smile as he waved his hands.","\"I see histories old and young. I see weavings of existence that occur, and countless others that do not occur. I witness the flow of the Wheel of Existence, as well as the entities swimming within this flow, making up an interconnected web of existence. I witness the feats of men and women across countless Frequencies of the Wheel. I witness the feats of... Noah Osmont and all the possibilities he could be. I witness the feats of the Infiniverse Megalos and all that she could be. Would you like to see all the possibilities that I witness?\"","HUUUM!","Grandiose words that caused Noah's mind to buzz echoed out from this being as he asked whether Noah would like to see the countless possibilities he witnessed.","And at such a question, Noah became stern as he replied calmly:","\"Humor me.\"","The old man who could not see, The Witness, nodded as he waved his hands, causing the eruption of countless illusory screens to fill everything around him.","The illusory screens showed a great deal of things, but at this moment, the face of the Infiniverse Megalos Body filled the screens!","One screen showed her in the Expanses, as she alone stood against Watchers of the Wheelomachy while devouring everything around her.","One screen showed her in the Megalos Beyond, standing before a massive Pantheon that swallowed everything—countless Outerversal Morphons standing against her.","Another screen showed the Infiniverse Megalos Body radiating a terrifying level of power, her mouth wide open, akin to an existential vacuum, as she swallowed an entire Frequency of Existence.","...!","In many of the illusory screens displaying variations of the Infiniverse Megalos, she was conducting different versions of actions—but for the most part... the vast majority showed her devouring the very weavings of existence themselves into her being.","\"I witness the Echoes of Existence of the one you brought here.\"","The Witness spoke as he waved his hand and the illusory screens changed.","\"I witness the Echoes of Existence of the one you walk with across Frequencies, right now devouring Shattered Remnants of the Wheel.\"","The many illusory screens shifted to now display... Ruination.","Now they displayed her figure in multiple forms. In one screen, she was waving her hands toward an entire Frequency of Existence as it was painted red and began to descend into ruin.","In another illusory screen, she sat upon a crimson throne inside Megalos Nihilos, as legions of creatures born of anti-matter swirled around her.","In many other screens, she was shown within the lands of Hell Terra Firma, her figure crossing through while followed by countless races of beings.","In one screen, she was a Primordial Cosmic Treasure that remained floating inside the universe—imposing cycles of ruin again and again... and again.","It showed countless possibilities and variations, as Noah looked at all of them with a cold gaze and spoke out.","\"Echoes of Existence?\"","The Witness had called them Echoes of Existence.","And he nodded at Noah's question as he replied.","\"Yes. Echoes. Possibilities of what was, or what could be. For some, they are parallel versions of the existence they are. You might even possibly see or observe them within the Veiled Frequencies of Existence. In the Unstable Frequencies of Possibilities. Would you like to see your own possibilities? Your own Echoes of Existence?\"","The Witness asked such a question as Noah's gaze became unfathomably stern, and yet... he still nodded!"]},{"number":3683,"title":"Chapter 3683: Chapter 3682: The Breaking of the Wheel II","paragraphs":["The old man with the blindfold waved his hands again, as the screens proceeded to change one more time.","Countless screens—by the thousands—flickered and changed from displaying variations of Ruination. And yet when they changed to display Noah's variations...","The countless screens were actually blank.","They showed nothing.","There was only a single screen reflecting the same image of him at this very moment!","All of the other screens had absolutely nothing.","...!","The scene was heart-shaking.","The Witness held an impassive gaze as he revealed a singular screen of variation—a singular screen of possibility.","\"Out there, across the endless threads of reality, there are countless possibilities and parallel weavings of existence. And yet for you... your possibilities seem to be dragged in and contained within a single weaving of existence. Why is that?\"","...!","The Witness asked that question.","Out there, across the parallel weavings of existence—across the Frequencies of Existence—one might find different versions of Barbatos, Adelaide, Athena... even Echoes of Existence for the Infiniverse Megalos and Ruination.","Reflections of what they could be, based on their current weavings of complexity.","But they wouldn't be able to find Noah.","And as the question settled like thunder in the silence, Noah's eyes flashed with sharp brilliance, his words slicing through the moment like a tyrannical blade.","\"Should the Witness not be the one to tell me why and explain these mysteries? You stand at the very core of the Wheel of Existence. The things you see and know should be innumerable, right? So tell me—what theories do you have? What possibilities can I ponder myself?\"","He asked with a cold gaze and the old man in the blindfold simply... shook his head.","\"I do not know.\"","HUUM!","\"The Wheel of Existence does not know.\"","WAA!","\"You rose and entered the flow of the Wheel in a way that forced even the Wheel to look at you, recognize you...to accept you. I believe you were always there. You were born of its weavings...and yet somehow, your possibilities and variations were nowhere to be found. I do not know. And neither does the Wheel. There was a time I worked very, very hard to Witness where those possibilities might have been as you began to encompass a dense flow of Existence...\"","...!","As he spoke, the old man with the golden blindfold waved his hand—and three of the once-empty screens filled with life.","They showed...Noah on his Blue Planet.","One screen showed him living peacefully with his mother and father. A harmonious, happy family. It showed him growing up... becoming a doctor.","No apocalypse.","No Beasts or Demons.","Another screen showed him burying his parents while still very young. The weight of loss forging him into a tyrant—an underground boss who lived for control.","A third screen revealed him with a family of his own. A woman with golden hair. A pet eagle. Three children gathered around a dining table—laughing, eating, living.","The Witness displayed these as he slowly shook his head.","\"The amount of weavings required just to pull up these three... could birth a thousand Frequencies.\"","...!","\"And these possibilities... they only existed before you ever touched Mana. After that, not even the Wheel could find a single Echo of your Existence. Even those of immense power leave variants—trails of Echoes. Look around you. They all do. But you... don't. Are you...\"","Now the old man hesitated, as if unsure how to ask the question that weighed down his chest.","Noah remained still.","And after a pause that echoed across Existence, the question finally fell.","\"Are you... alive?\"","BOOM!","The Witness, who stood at the core of the Wheel of Existence, was asking Noah... if he was alive.","BZZZT!","The figure of the Infiniverse Megalos Body turned cold at the question. A terrifying complexity radiated from her, pressing down on The Witness like a storm. Her energy whispered one simple thing- How dare you?!","And still, The Witness bore it, shaking his head slowly.","\"Don't misunderstand me. It's a genuine question. Look at the Living... and the Dead. The Dead have fewer possibilities—just faint Echoes. But before they were dead, they brimmed with potential. Because all Dead Things... were once alive. All broken Wheels of Existence... were once whole. Do you know why they died? Do you know the true nature of the Wheels of Existence?\"","The true nature of the Wheels of Existence.","Noah's mind buzzed with the weight of it, his thoughts vibrating as he answered coldly.","\"Then enlighten me.\"","The old man smiled.","His golden blindfold flickered as he waved his hand once more- causing the countless screens to vanish, replacing them with what had always surrounded them- the endless white-gold sea and the shattered Remnants of the Wheel.","The Spokes. The Traces. The Pieces.","And far away... the distant white-gold Wheel, only a single section of it visible.","The Witness extended a hand to all of it, speaking with a voice carved from utter majesty.","\"For there to be remnants... something must have broken. For there to be shattered pieces of the Wheel of Existence... the Wheel itself must have fractured.\"","WAA!","The Wheel of Existence had to be shattered... for Traces and Pieces to drift across Frequencies.","Noah's weavings pulsed.","His very distinction as the Weaver of Existence whispered that these words... were truth.","And yet...","He turned his head to stare at the distant white-gold Wheel, still so pristine. Still so whole. And the blindfold on The Witness shimmered as he spoke again—serene and powerful.","\"Shall I show you... the first breaking of the Wheel?\"","HUUM!","As those words rang out, a colossal screen of brilliance bloomed behind him—stretching the length of an entire Omniverse.","Lesser minds would have shattered just trying to comprehend it.","But for Noah... and the Infiniverse Megalos...","It was but a glance.","A glance that held everything.","And on that screen—spanning stars and systems and the spaces between...","He saw...","A radiant, verdant Wheel of Existence.","Unfathomably vast.","Floating serenely in an endless emerald sea.","Its colossal spokes blazed with quintillions of ancient runes, and towering waves of complexity rippled around it—each surge humming with dense concentrations of impossibly pure existence.","It pulsed.","With life.","With serenity.","With transcendence.","With power that defied all reason.","A Green Wheel of Existence.","And The Witness simply said...","\"This... was the first breaking of the Wheel.\""]},{"number":3684,"title":"Chapter 3684: Chapter 3683: The Breaking of the Wheel III","paragraphs":["The First Breaking of the Wheel!","The Witness uttered those words just as, behind him, a massive screen the size of an Omniverse bloomed into existence.","But it didn't feel like any random screen.","It felt real.","It felt like they were looking at a grand record etched into the very fabric of existence.","And as if to confirm it, Noah and the Infiniverse Megalos Body locked eyes with the golden-blindfolded figure of the Witness. In his ancient voice, he called out to them, green-gold tendrils emanating from his hands, floating mere inches away.","\"If you allow me... you can experience the Record of the First Breaking of the Wheel yourself.\"","...!","\"As the Witness, I have seen it. I have preserved it. And at this moment, I can show it in a true sense by allowing you to experience it yourselves.\"","To experience the First Breaking of the Wheel.","Even the idea was terrifying. Noah's weavings of existence burned brilliantly, his True Sources analyzing the green-gold tendril before him as he coldly reached for it.","That tendril radiated a terrifying purity and complexity far beyond the Mythic Signature of the Great Beyonder.","It held a True Source Noah hadn't yet fully understood, but he recognized it with a sense of familiarity.","He gave a light nod to his Construct beside him. As he grabbed the tendril, an incandescent green-gold brilliance bathed everything nearby.","And then, part of his consciousness was pulled elsewhere.","To another weaving of existence entirely.","To the flow of an age lost to eons.","To the record of the First Breaking of the Wheel!","—","\"Haha, Little Witness, are you really dozing off right now? Shouldn't you act out your name and title and be here to witness this grandiose event?\"","The voice stirred Noah from what felt like a deep reverie, an impossibly long dream.","HUUUM!","In the depths of his existence, the stellar obsidian radiance of his True Source of Existence buzzed, anchoring him. He knew who he was. This was a record. This was the dream.","He spread his senses outward.","He was in a small body- young, maybe a teenager. But his eyes couldn't see.","A green blindfold wrapped around them, tied neatly at the back of his head. His robe was simple—white and green—covering him from top to bottom.","Even when he looked inward, he found a calm, silent True Source at the Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity level.","It was... the True Source of Continuity.","This was the True Source of the Witness!","But the real shock was his surroundings.","An endless green sea.","Scattered across it like radiant archipelagos were Frequency Havens—self-contained micro-frequencies tethered to the sea's flow, all converging toward a resplendent, green Wheel of Existence.","The Frequency Havens pulsed with their own unique Source structures. One was a floating citadel of harmonic crystal and firelight. Another, a storm reef of volatile plasma and temporal sand. Some shimmered with lunar ice that sang waves of complexity. Others swirled through labyrinths of compressed gravity and spectral flora of existence.","And they were guarded not by ordinary entities, but by those who burned with the light of True Sources.","The most powerful of them were Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects.","Monads and Architects.","Though Noah's eyes were blind, his senses- his True Source- saw clearly. He could feel the presence and expressions of dozens of these entities.","An overwhelming intensity of Purity. A staggering depth of Complexity.","Some sat calmly atop their Frequency Havens. Others talked among themselves or with those of lower standing. On many havens, Noah sensed Resplendent Monads smiling and conversing with Harmonized Sourcebound Icons and Nascent Source-Bearers, who gazed at them with respect.","This was a different age.","A different record, a different weaving of existence- one where beings of Average, Moderate, and High Purity and Complexity existed in breathtaking abundance.","Even the Frequency Haven he stood upon spanned the size of a standard Omniverse- its complexity exponentially greater.","Waves of verdant-gold light shimmered around him. Complexity...was everywhere.","Even the one who woke him...","Noah turned to find a burly, muscular man in a loose, stellar green robe. His body burned with green flames, vibrant with life and vitality.","When he clapped Noah on the back- lightly, the tremors threatened to fracture his source if it had been any harder.","Profundity radiated from him. His eyes, expectant and vibrant, glowed with High Purity and Complexity. He was both a Resplendent Monad and a Converged Architect.","\"All who wanted to be here to witness the Wheel's change are here,\" he said. \"Many came from the Infinite Ravines- trading places to witness this moment themselves. What do you think, Little Witness? What are we about to witness with the Wheel of Existence?\"","The terrifying existence posed the question, and Noah found his lips moving as though this young body were playing out a perfect record.","\"How should I know? We're all just watching the First of Existence. And Monad Romulus... I know you know exactly what level of purity and complexity your source has reached. If you keep hitting me like that, you'll shatter my weavings next time.\"","His voice was laced with annoyance and grumbling- completely unlike the deep, ancient tone of the Witness he and the Infiniverse Megalos Body had observed not long ago.","And still, despite the grumblings, Monad Romulus only laughed and beckoned to others gathered in the distance.","\"Hey, Monad Gideon, Architect Reyna! Come give this kid a few more smacks. He doesn't seem to know what's good for him. I was helping his True Source grow stronger with every slap- and he complains about it!\"","Laughter rippled through the Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects as the Witness turned toward them with a mixture of fondness and frustration.","They were his mentors. His teachers. The ones who had guided him across existence.","He knew they meant well. And now?","Now, he had to take this moment seriously.","He had to Witness.","Time passed as those terrifyingly complex entities communicated, a display of harmony and wonder in this forgotten age... until finally...","\"Oh... it begins!\""]},{"number":3685,"title":"Chapter 3685: Chapter 3684: The Breaking of the Wheel IV","paragraphs":["The voice of Resplendent Monad Romulus rang out from this Frequency Haven, echoing across the vibrant, stellar-green sea.","His gaze and the gaze of many others turned toward the distant, verdant Wheel of Existence that had begun to radiate a terrifying brilliance.","The transformation of the Wheel of Existence.","With their level of power, they all felt the shift coming, but none of them knew what it truly meant, or what would come next.","They only knew that the Wheel of Existence, the very force that had shouldered and sheltered them since their youth like an umbrella woven from stars as they grew in power and complexity- had to transform.","It wasn't even a matter of choice. This change... whatever it was... had to happen.","It was bound to happen.","And they were here to witness it. To support it.","Would it hold the answer to the Infinite Ravines and the unending assaults of the Living and the Dead?","None of them knew.","So, they watched.","And then...","HUUUM!","Everything began to tremble. The Wheel of Existence became suffused with a terrifying magnitude of complexity.","The Wheel seemed to gather all that it was- all that it had been- as it surged with a brilliance far greater than anything it had shown before.","Beside him, Resplendent Monad Romulus chuckled softly, casting his gaze toward a distant point where a lone entity floated unaccompanied, untouchable.","\"Even that guy couldn't stay away, huh?\"","He spoke casually, but his words held weight. Noah turned to look, his eyes pulsing because even though this figure didn't radiate outward light or display overwhelming power...","When one's gaze truly landed on him, the purity and complexity that being held... exceeded that of any living Resplendent Monad or Converged Architect.","A man in a stellar-green robe. His face was mostly obscured, yet from this far distance, Noah could see his eyes.","Eyes holding a deep, ancient sadness.","As if... he already knew what was coming.","His deeply green eyes pulsed with an intensity Noah couldn't withstand for long.","The transformation had begun.","The Wheel was changing.","A storm of complexity bloomed and converged from every direction as the booming sound of the Wheel turning echoed out.","The Wheel of Existence... was turning.","And even the Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects fell silent.","All watched as the verdant Wheel completed a full turn. The spokes, the surface, every intricate rune etched onto it glowed—each one alive with a level of complexity unattainable by any entity. A complexity that only an Absolute Complex True Source could reach.","And then, the Wheel- overflowing with unimaginable complexity- could no longer hold it in.","In a brief, breathless moment...","It flashed.","A wave of blinding brilliance burst outward, revealing quintillions upon quintillions of green threads extending from the Wheel- threads that touched every True Source in this place, and countless more across frequencies and realities.","As if it was borrowing the blessing and complexity of all those it once shielded... and those still seeking shelter beneath it.","Noah watched as a pillar of verdant light erupted around the Wheel. Its surface began to change. Thick green lines formed—intricate and deliberate—as if the Wheel was forging something grander than itself.","Every observer felt it. Their complexities buzzed. Their souls stirred. The gains they could draw from this moment... they would ponder for eons.","Then, in the next moment...","BZZT!","The brilliant green pillar of light distorted and fizzled.","Something was...missing.","The complexity wasn't enough.","Something hadn't been achieved.","And then...","Everything turned.","It happened far too fast for anyone to stop it.","The pillar fizzled out—and a massive fissure split the Wheel of Existence from top to bottom.","...!","CRACK!","\"Ah...\"","As if his soul had been split, Noah whispered in the body of the Witness.","\"AAH!\"","\"NO!\" Beside him, Romulus and the others roared in horror. Their bodies ignited with power as they surged toward the Wheel.","But it was too late.","The crack became an unraveling.","And in the next instant, the verdant Wheel of Existence shattered—splintering into countless fragments!","It was...the breaking.","The Breaking of the Wheel.","Noah saw it all.","The Witness stood frozen, anchored atop the Frequency Haven, watching as the impossible unfolded.","No one had expected this.","They had all anticipated a transformation. A rebirth. Something greater.","But never this.","The full breaking of the Wheel was too immense.","It unleashed a blinding brilliance—raw complexity surging outward with a light that blinded even the Witness.","He felt it.","The existence around him vanished. He couldn't see. Couldn't feel.","Even the blindfold over his eyes—he couldn't sense it.","Seconds. Minutes. Days. Eons.","Time lost all meaning.","And then...","Sensation returned.","The Witness inhaled—foreign air filling his lungs. His chest burned, his True Source strained under the weight of new, unfamiliar changes.","Familiar, yet not.","And when his senses returned fully...","His body trembled.","He looked around.","Nothing.","No one.","He was alone.","Even the green sea...","No- it was no longer green.","Before his very eyes, the sea shifted from verdant purity to a crimson hue of brilliance.","He turned, and where the great Wheel had once stood majestic and glorious...","A new crimson Wheel bloomed.","A newborn Wheel, glowing faintly.","Its complexity was far less than the one before. A fraction of the verdant titan that came before it.","But none of that mattered.","The Witness wept.","Tears streamed down his face as his senses reached across the sea, over shattered pieces of the Wheel, broken remnants of Frequency Havens, and wild pulses of incomplete True Sources.","\"Monad Romulus?! Monad Gideon?!\"","The Witness cried out with all the complexity of his True Source of Continuity.","But there was no answer.","He had seen the Breaking of the Wheel—and now... every person he'd ever known was gone.","He could still sense the echoes of their lives.","He, who had never seen since the day he was born, felt the truth. He instinctively knew.","They weren't dead.","Their True Sources hadn't collapsed.","So where were they?","And why was he the only one left?","\"Monad Romulus...!\"","A deep, broken cry tore from his soul—but no answer came.","Only a blooming, crimson Wheel of Existence remained.","The prior form...","Had undergone the Breaking."]},{"number":3686,"title":"Chapter 3686: Chapter 3685: The Breaking of the Wheel V","paragraphs":["Green turned to crimson.","Vast stretches of sea adopted that crimson allure of brilliance as the hum of a silent, glowing Wheel stretched out across existence.","Everything looked altered- and yet, somehow, not. Inside the Witness, Noah felt it all.","He felt the Breaking of the Wheel with his very existence as his mind surged with static and wonder, the scene replaying over his existence again and again as it was both horrific and beautiful at the same time.","A failed transformation.","But a transformation into what?","And if it failed, how many times had this happened before? Because in this moment, there wasn't just a crimson Wheel of Existence... but a white-gold one.","So just how many Breakings had there been?","How many failures?","And where had all the powerful Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects gone? Where had those beneath them in power gone?","The Breaking didn't destroy them. But it was as if the strongest beings tied to the Wheel were displaced—flung to unknown realms every time a Breaking occurred.","As these questions churned, Noah felt the same desolation and quiet grief the Witness carried.","The green blindfold, shaped by the surrounding sources, slowly changed—its verdant hue bleeding into the crimson shade of the sea around them.","The Witness was completely blind, relying only on his source. His head turned in the direction of the slowly spinning crimson Wheel as he wondered.","As he grieved.","As he cried.","And from then on, he continued to Witness.","HUUUM!","Other weavings of existence thrummed in the moments that followed as the surrounding weavings fractured and broke.","The record of an age—one far older than comprehension—came to an end.","It showed glimpses of beings who had existed before the First Breaking of the Wheel.","Beings far more powerful than anything currently within the flow of the Wheel of Existence.","And because he had Witnessed this... Noah's weavings of existence began to spark with grand possibilities.","As the ancient record shattered, his essence snapped back into the present—and even as it did, he could still feel the changes and wonder from what he'd just experienced.","|The True Source of Continuity has been understood under a different definition from the True Source of the Witness.|","...!","He had lived the First Breaking of the Wheel by merging with the body of the Witness.","And the burning True Source of this being was open to him—his to explore—because for that brief span of time, it felt like his own body. He'd understood the very definition of Continuity from someone else's eyes.","Noah's continuity stemmed from the very pillars that held up the foundation of the Infiniverse Megalos.","Pillars like Entropy, Relativity, Manadynamics, and more.","And now, his Pathway toward the True Source of Continuity absorbed a new definition, reshaping itself.","But that wasn't all.","|You Witnessed the weavings of the Resplendent Monad Romulus and gazed upon his True Source of Entropy.|","|A possible definition of Entropy tracing back to the First Breaking of the Wheel has been obtained by your weavings of existence.|","HUUM!","His essence thrummed with new potential. His gains weren't singular.","But still contained.","Because in the next moment, his weavings awoke once more—this time in the radiant, white-gold seas of brilliance.","Beside him, the Infiniverse Megalos Body released a slight tremble. Her eyes shimmered with returning light—her weavings reigniting with terrifying brilliance. Noah had no clue what truths she'd faced in the vision of the First Breaking.","But then... his mind buzzed again as she began to share her knowledge and memory of it.","Noah had taken over the Witness to observe—but where had she been?","That question lingered until the unthinkable happened.","The Witness had layered the weavings of the Infiniverse Megalos Body... onto the First Wheel of Existence.","The Verdant Wheel.","Unlike Noah—who only observed—she had lived the First Breaking.","Her weavings trembled. Noah's expression turned grim as his gaze shifted to the distant Witness. Even with his golden blindfold, the ravines of sadness surrounding him were palpable.","His power was immense. He had chosen Noah to descend into his younger body to observe that cataclysmic moment. And somehow, he had also allowed the Infiniverse Megalos Body's weavings to be projected onto the Wheel that broke.","And whatever repercussions or catastrophes might result from this were completely unknown. Because in that moment... the Infiniverse Megalos Body stood frozen.","As if observing and feeling the Breaking had done something unexplainable to her!","Amid it all, the Witness spoke again.","\"That was the first Breaking of the Wheel. Back then, none of us knew what the change would bring...or what the transformation would birth. All those who were there to witness it vanished—except me. Where they went, I can only theorize. But after watching a brand-new Wheel spin and turn, I believed the failure to evolve... released a surge of unfathomable complexity that wiped the slate clean. Yet the Breaking didn't decimate those tied to the former Wheel. It didn't kill. It sent them—to other signatures of life.\"","...!","\"I told myself they had been scattered across different weavings. Different Wheels of Existence. I can not say if it is true, but... it comforted me back then. Since that day, I have Witnessed. After the First Breaking, I stayed. I watched the Wheel turn and weave. I witnessed new True Sources bloom under the threads of an Absolute Complex Source.\"","\"And during all that time... my greatest fear remained the Infinite Ravines. But when I visited their many Gateway Domus... I found no Living. No Dead. For years...for countless years.\"","...!","When the Witness said that, Noah's weavings pulsed violently.","He remembered something crucial mentioned in the record of the First Breaking.","That there were beings left behind in the Ravines... to defend- and they were even capable of easily switching their position with those inside the Wheel of Existence and going back and forth...since there were many of them to defend.","To defend against both the Living and the Dead.","Entities tied to Living True Sources... and those bound to Dead ones had all been attacking the Infinite Ravines!"]},{"number":3687,"title":"Chapter 3687: Chapter 3686: The Breaking of the Wheel VI","paragraphs":["After the First Breaking of the Wheel, there was a disappearance of everything within the Infinite Ravines, and nothing appeared again for countless years that followed.","When it seemed like the Witness was about to continue speaking on his own accord, Noah stopped him gently with a question.","\"In the previous records I observed,\" he said softly, \"it was mentioned that there was a defense against both the Living and the Dead in the Infinite Ravines. Why is that?\"","It was a critical question.","The Witness smiled before responding.","\"Even we did not understand it then. We would battle Harmonized Sourcebound Icons... and occasionally Converged Architects and Monads—brimming with life—who had crossed the Nullvein Gravewake Folds. They seemed drawn to our Infinite Ravines. Many of them fought with everything they had, saying they simply sought entry into the weavings of the Wheel. But we allowed neither the Living nor the Dead. For even the Dead could mimic the Living... and corrupt all they touched. Yet the reason both were drawn into the Ravines... was due to the brilliant complexity the First Wheel of Existence emanated.\"","...!","The Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","Scattered memories of that place—collapsed weavings and folded threads of existence—had already begun budding within Noah, even as he shredded records and purified Dead True Sources in the present.","And the Witness's voice pressed on.","\"Before its First Breaking, it drew every entity toward it simply because of the immense Purity it held. Before the Breaking. Before the failed transformation. Afterward... there were no more visitors in the Infinite Ravines. It was as if the light from the Wheel was no longer strong enough to draw in anything from the Folds. Only after millions of years—when the Wheel's complexity and purity began rising again—did Dead Things start appearing. No Living ones. And even the Dead were weaker. This... along with my Witnessing of the Second and Third Breakings of the Wheel... allowed me to form a few undeniable conclusions.\"","...!","Noah's expression shifted at the mention of the Second and Third Breakings.","It hadn't happened just once. It had happened again—and again.","The Witness continued.","\"By the time the Dead began being pulled into the Infinite Ravines, new True Sources had begun to bud and rise. They kept the Dead at bay. And because I knew so little at the time, I even descended into the Infinite Ravines myself to ensure all remained as it should. After the First Breaking... the number of beings who could attain the level of Monad or Converged Architect was pitifully small compared to those who existed before the First Breaking. Then came a time I sensed a change. Others sensed it too. They came to the core weavings of the Wheel to observe—curious, but unaware of what was coming.\"","The Witness's blindfold seemed to grow heavier, his burden too great to name.","\"And I was there... when the Second Breaking of the Wheel occurred. And again—I was the only one left. All others were scattered and sent away. The defenders and Dead Things within the Ravines were also expelled. The crimson Wheel cracked and broke... and in its place, a Violet Wheel of Existence bloomed. It was less pure, less complex than the First Verdant Wheel. This time, it took many more millions of years for its purity to rise again. And again, weaker Dead Things came. Even fewer entities could rise to the level of Monad or Converged Architect. None—not a single one—came close to that being who exceeded even Monads before the First Breaking.\"","Noah remembered.","The green-haired man—the one Monad Romulus had pointed to. A man whose gaze carried the weight of sadness and inevitability, as if he knew what would happen to the Wheel of Existence.","No entity like him had ever risen again.","The Witness's blindfold buzzed softly as he spoke.","\"The Third Breaking. The Fourth. The Fifth. Sixth. Seventh. Eighth... They all occurred, one after the other. And each time... the Wheel of Existence lost more of the purity and complexity it had once held during the era of the First Verdant Wheel. Every transformation it attempted afterward failed. I came to understand something: the transformation had to succeed the first time. If the Wheel undergoes a Breaking... then the chances of transformation succeeding after that are nearly nonexistent. And the more it Breaks... the more impossible it becomes. Until...\"","He swept his arms across the golden sea around them.","And Noah's eyes widened as he looked out at the countless shattered pieces of the Wheel floating across the horizon... and the distant, white-gold brilliance of the current Wheel of Existence.","\"We never knew what the transformation would've brought. But it had to succeed the first time. Since it didn't... I understood that the Wheel was doomed to repeat Breakings. Again and again. And not long ago, I felt it again. The level of complexity and purity of the Wheel behind us... has once more reached a threshold. One that is calling transformation. It could occur in a million years. A thousand. A year. A month. I don't know.\"","The words he said next nearly made Noah curse aloud.","\"I do not know when it will happen. But I do know this—after all the Breakings I have Witnessed, one truth has become clear. This coming Ninth Transformation of the Wheel... is the final one.\"","HUUM!","\"If this transformation is not passed successfully—and I say again, it is nearly impossible—then the Wheel of Existence will Break for the ninth time. And when that happens... it will no longer be a Living Absolute Complex True Source.\"","...!","\"It will finally—and irrevocably—become a Dead Absolute Complex True Source. No more chances. No more transformations. No more Living.\"","BOOM!","The words were horrific even to hear—and yet, they were spoken.","Noah's eyes gleamed with a fierce, terrifying light as a question surfaced again in his mind.","The question of the Living and the Dead.","Where did the Dead come from?","They were the same.","They were all the products... of the Breakings of the Wheel of Existence!"]},{"number":3688,"title":"Chapter 3688: Chapter 3687: Infiniverse I","paragraphs":["A Wheel of Existence actually undergoes a series of transformations—again and again—across its infinite weavings.","The first transformation was meant to succeed.","But when it failed, the Wheel shattered like a shell far too intricate to remain whole. In shedding that immense complexity, another version of itself bloomed—but it was a dim echo. Less pure. Less vast.","Logically, if the transformation couldn't succeed when the Wheel held its peak brilliance and complexity, how could it possibly succeed in a lesser state? The second time. The third. The eighth.","And now, it stood on the edge of a ninth transformation—its final one!","Failure was almost written into its fate.","The Ninth Breaking of the Wheel was bound to happen, and this time with finality!","Noah's eyes simmered, lit with the terrible glow of existence as he thought through it all.","Before the first breaking, the Wheel radiated such complexity, such purity, that it gave rise to Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects. And when that happened, both the living and the dead from the Nullvein Gravewake Folds came for it.","Now? Only a scattered handful of Dead Things drifted toward this fading, depleted golden Wheel—its luster dulled, its complexity diminished.","Even its protectors now mirrored that decay as they weren't that powerful compared to before!","Everything was connected.","Every action met an equal and opposite reaction.","And Noah now stood before the reality that the Ninth Breaking of the Wheel wasn't spoken of as a \"transformation\" anymore. No. The transformation had become a myth, a laughable impossibility. What remained was collapse.","The collapse of the Wheel of Existence... and with it, everything it held. Every life. Every source. Doomed to fall under the weavings of a Dead Absolute Complex True Source.","He...would not allow it!","His gaze lifted- sharp, burning, unyielding- toward the Witness.","That ancient figure who had been there from the very beginning. From the First Breaking.","The one who had watched it all.","So Noah asked, voice steady, \"Across thousands, millions, and billions of years through every breaking—you've just watched. The Ninth and final one is coming. Did you try to stop any of it?\"","Did he try?","Such a question cracked the silence. The being in the golden blindfold trembled, ever so slightly. He took a slow, heavy breath—and answered with aching calm.","\"I have tried more than you can imagine. I've experimented with Dead Things, their memories, their echoes, all in search of the origin—trying to learn what went wrong. I ventured to the perilous, collapsed weavings of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds... searching, begging for an answer. Over the eons, I've asked myself endlessly—how could the impossible be overcome? And always, the answer circled back to one truth: something must change. A new variable must rise. Whether from within... or from outside the Wheel.\"","WAA!","As those words hung in the air, his sightless eyes, seeing so much even though they were blind, locked onto Noah.","And the old man continued.","\"In the Third Breaking, I observed hopeful possibilities. Entities with curious complexities. I asked myself—Could they be the variable? But no. They weren't.","The Fourth Breaking came. I waited. I watched. And again—nothing.","The Fifth. The Sixth. The Seventh. No true change. No spark.\"","His voice softened, distant with memory.","\"Not until the Eighth. Then... one appeared. A Holder of a True Source of Asche. He reached the Resplendent Monad level. He wasn't cast away like the others—just like me. But even he, in the end, wasn't enough.\"","He took a moment, then looked into the present.","\"And now? This final weaving. This last desperate chance. I asked again—Is there any hope? Or will the Wheel perish into obscurity... while I become the Witness of its final fall... just another Dead Thing?","I asked. I pondered. I witnessed. Waiting for anything... for anyone...\"","His voice faltered. Then grew strong.","\"And out of nowhere, they appeared.","A Dead Thing...carrying two Dead Absolute Complex True Sources.","A Living Native... with a budding False Absolute Complex True Source.","And then... two Constructs capable of becoming Wheels themselves.\"","...!","Behind him, illusory screens lit up—massive and otherworldly—revealing the images of Bob, the Peacemaker, Ruination, and the Infiniverse Megalos Body.","\"Variables,\" the Witness whispered, his voice reverent.","\"They came from nowhere. The first two were easier to understand. The other two...were not of this weaving. Not even bound to their own paths. They were... controlled by something else. Something even the Wheel itself could not comprehend. An Anomaly that had no echoes. No probabilities. Just impossibility.\"","...!","His blind gaze fixed fully on Noah.","But Noah remained calm. Cold. Watching.","Variables. Possibilities.","The Witness had watched across eons— and he looked at Bob or the Peacemaker as possibilities. He stood, wondering if Infiniverse Megalos or Ruination were the answer.","But then...","Noah's gaze sharpened.","\"You thought Bob might be the Variable? Just because he carried two Dead Absolute Complex True Sources? You continued to watch all he did because of that?\"","\"...\"","Silence fell. The Witness could feel the disdain bleeding from Noah's words.","He looked down at his hands as he spoke again—softly.","\"I have witnessed quintillions of deaths across these breakings. You and I see the world differently. We act differently. I don't expect you to agree with my choices... but they are my weavings, just as your actions are yours. I may not approve of them... but I would never hold them against you.\"","...!","Differences. Viewpoints. Actions. Weavings!","Noah's eyes glinted.","\"And what actions of mine do you not approve of?\"","WAA!","It was a knife-sharp question—and the Witness paused before answering with that same calm, ancient tone.","\"It's not a single action. It's your very existence. Your state of being. You are...incomprehensible. As an Anomaly, you add chaos when we need clarity. You birth paradoxes. And binding yourself to the brightest Variables... only deepens the uncertainty.","When the final breaking nears, I believe what is needed is certainty.","Not Anomalies.","But again... I don't hold it against y—\"","\"You've talked enough.\"","HUUM!","A new voice rang out—cutting cleanly through the moment.","It wasn't Noah.","And it wasn't the Witness.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body stepped forward, standing tall beside Noah. Her eyes shimmered—glorious and unfathomable—brimming with the cold, unrelenting brilliance of Megalos.","And they were locked entirely on the Witness."]},{"number":3689,"title":"Chapter 3689: Chapter 3688: Infiniverse II","paragraphs":["The character of entities that had lived for an unfathomably long time always carried a certain apathy—especially when gazing across the weavings of Existence.","Because when you've witnessed quintillions of deaths, the birth and end of weavings across eons, watching a few trillion—or even more quintillions—fade becomes nothing more than a flicker. A process that once unfolded over millennia now happens in seconds.","And so... they could watch Megalos collapse.","They could witness Frequencies of Existence—intricate expanses laced with Matter, Anti-Matter, and Dark Matter—burst into ruin, their inhabitants screaming silently into oblivion.","And still... feel nothing.","But if Noah stood there, watching as a Frequency began to fall—its Megalos imploding, quintillions about to die—what would he do?","The answer wasn't theoretical. It had already happened. When Bob shattered an entire Frequency by manipulating its Node... what did Noah do?","He restored it.","Even as the Echoes of the Unwritten unfolded, Noah reached through and pulled that Frequency back, reviving the quintillions of beings within it. Every time their battle spilled into another Frequency, he did the same.","Just because he was powerful... just because he'd seen endless death... didn't mean he would stand idle when it stared him in the face.","But not everyone was like him.","The Witness was something else entirely—a being shaped by a Complexity that saw the weavings of Existence through a colder lens.","And now, here he was—speaking of Variables. Of things that could shift the impossible fate of the Wheel. But all he saw in Noah... was an anomaly. A being he couldn't understand. A being tied to the very Variables the Witness prayed would appear.","It was then the Infiniverse Megalos Body stirred. She rose, her expression sharp as steel, her voice slicing through the silence like a drawn blade.","\"Just because your weavings can't understand something doesn't make it an anomaly. It simply means... you're lesser.\"","WAA!","Her voice cracked through the dazzling seas!","\"You watched the Wheel break again and again—and did nothing. You had countless years, and still, you never became a Variable, only waited for one. Now, on the eve of the Ninth Breaking, you sulk in solemnity, bemoaning fate. And when one Variable finally arises—one you can't grasp—this is your response? Pathetic.\"","BOOM!","Her words cut deep.","Her Complexity surged like a storm, rising with her fury.","She turned toward the one she called Master. Her presence quieted... and she dropped to her knees.","\"Master, this Variable has been preparing something for you.\"","...!","Noah moved to raise her gently, smiling.","\"You never need to kneel to me. You know that.\"","\"I know,\" she replied softly. \"And I still choose to. What others don't understand... is never an anomaly to me. What they fear, I've always been connected to. And now, I wish to give back—to offer even a fraction of what's been given to me. I want to present you with an Absolute Complex True Source. A Wheel of Existence unlike any other.\"","HUUM!","As she spoke, her form radiated with a brilliance that pulsed with unspoken power. Noah felt it in his chest and through their grand connection- something calm, something pure!","He nodded.","Then, lifting her hand in his, he looked toward the distant Wheel of Existence and asked.","\"What of the Wheel? What of the Witness?\"","...!","The one who'd shown them the Breaking. The one who claimed he was waiting for Variables to alter the impossible.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body turned her gaze to him, voice cold as glass.","\"He can continue to Witness.\"","WAA!","\"As for the Wheel... I benefited from its First Breaking. And so, I will repay it—by saving it from annihilation.\"","BOOM!","Words spoken with staggering simplicity... and devastating weight.","She had just declared she would save the Wheel.","And the certainty in her voice made the Witness tremble.","But then her gaze drifted from the Wheel... to Noah.","\"It no longer holds meaning for us. I will not touch its Frequencies or its weavings. I will construct my own—on my own foundation—ensuring a purity untainted by any flaw. Complexity will follow. Come, Master. Let me show you.\"","...!","They were still within the sacred region of the pristine Wheel of Existence. A vast white-gold sea surrounded them—endless and silent. And the Witness, who had been there since the First Breaking, still waited.","Still searching for a Variable.","But the Infiniverse Megalos Body... she turned away from it all. As though it no longer mattered.","Noah nodded.","Then he looked at the distant Wheel, motionless and yet spinning—a contradiction etched in golden fractals.","Bob had come here, searching for something.","Something connected to what he called... The Loom.","Was it hidden within this dying Wheel, now on the brink of its Ninth and Final Breaking?","Noah held that question for only a moment.","Then he took her hand—and together, they vanished.","Leaving the Witness standing alone.","Again.","The white-gold sea stretched in all directions. The shattered fragments of the Wheel drifted endlessly, orbiting a still center. The Witness stood, blind yet somehow dazed.","\"They just... left?\"","He had waited. Waited to see what would happen if the Infiniverse Megalos Body touched the Wheel.","And yet—she hadn't.","She refused it. Rejected it. Said she'd make her own.","And now...","Even without a Breaking, the Witness was once again... alone.","—","In the Prime Frequency of the End.","Noah and the Infiniverse Megalos Body returned—hovering before the radiant, multicolored infinity-shaped Infiniverse Vein. The skies rippled with celestial light, Havens floating in the distance.","Her form pulsed—Complexity bleeding from every fiber of her being.","\"Since Master is about to comprehend Continuity and Entropy—drawing from the definitions of the Witness and Romulus and forging our own from their definitions...I will begin my advancement with them. Without external interference. Without impurities. I will construct the True Frequency of Continuity and the True Frequency of Entropy—from the foundation of their True Sources.\"","HUUM!","Her decision ignited something. A storm of purpose built on everything she had become.","And from that moment... the Infiniverse Megalos Body began forging True Frequencies of Existence.","Not borrowed.","Not inherited.","But born from her own making!","Unfathomably grand.","Unfathomably pure.","Unfathomably...magisterial!"]},{"number":3690,"title":"Chapter 3690: Chapter 3689: Infiniverse III","paragraphs":["Within the Infiniverse Megalos.","Unique waves of wonder spread outward, the sensations rippling through existence and causing the most perceptive ones to quickly look up, as if sensing the coming changes.","The Queen of Matter, who had been excitedly speaking to a Shadow Guard, froze. Around her, chains connected to golden Books foretelling the grandest Fables came to a halt, even the one in the hands of the Shadow Guard, Night, who was reading them as if judging and evaluating!","The Queen of Matter raised her head in shock. The one she was communicating to did the same.","Inside the intricate vein that held the tremendous weavings of existence, the main bodies of multiple important personages also looked up.","Smiles touched their faces. Some shook their heads, amused.","They stood atop a small haven of obsidian-gold Dreams, shimmering with Dark Matter and Matter. Above them, golden auroras painted the skies. Beneath their feet, brilliant black and gold mountains rolled across the land.","In such a place—","Kazuhiko stopped in front of Henry, pausing their spar. He sheathed his katana, the blade glimmering with the light of Omniverses, and asked lightly.","\"Which advancement do we think he's making now? It's happening just as we can't find any more Faceless Lifeforms across frequencies...\"","Kazuhiko's words hung in the air. Henry steadied his waves and complexity, shimmering blue and gold, the silent flame of the Singed flickering near him. He shook his head and answered.","\"Your guess is as good as mine. But whatever change is coming... feels too significant. Too widespread.\"","...!","Others heard. Across the haven, beings who were comparing their weavings through sparring looked up, pausing their matches.","Erikson, adorned in blue beach attire, gold flippers clutched in his hands as weapons, spoke out boisterously.","\"A transformation of the Infiniverse itself? Maybe he'll take my idea and make a whole frequency of beaches! Endless waves of the sea, white sandy beaches stretching forever!\"","A few rolled their eyes.","Nearby, Ayame shimmered gold and added wistfully.","\"I wish we could see it happening on the grander scale. I'd love to know—\"","Space distorted.","Her words cut off as the figure of the Infiniverse Megalos Body appeared.","Her weavings buzzed with immense complexity and purity. She cast her gaze over those who had gathered here, those using the space to compare their existence through battle.","A blinding illusory screen then erupted above her.","\"It will be good for you all,\" she said, \"to observe the emergence of True Frequencies based on the True Sources of Existence. It will make it easier for you to grasp your own True Sources—or to follow the path of the True Severed Origin Osmontian.\"","...!","It would be a positive thing for them to watch the emergence of True Frequencies of Existence.","Fantastical words. Yet real enough that the screen above them shifted, displaying a scale few could fathom.","A view that stretched across countless light-years. Vast enough to cover multiple Omniverses and still, it was only a zoomed-out image of the massive Infiniverse Vein and the havens surrounding it.","And at that moment—","A violet-purple river of brilliance bloomed from the Infiniverse Vein, stretching outward.","At its base, countless tendrils of complexity and purity intertwined. Growth, happening on a conceptual scale the size of multiple Omniverses.","It contained the budding, terrifying musings of the True Source of Entropy.","The first-ever True Frequency of Existence to be built within the Infiniverse...was Entropy.","Chaos and wonder, woven together.","Maybe it had meaning. Maybe it didn't.","But as many watched, they could not help but ask questions.","Dr. Hall stepped forward, his voice cutting through the awed silence.","\"You said True Frequencies of Existence...we've gone into and observed Normal Frequencies and Prime Frequencies. How are they different from True Frequencies?\"","A question that caused minds to buzz, thoughts racing.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body, shining with stellar white brilliance, answered calmly:","\"Everything is based on Purity and Complexity. In this age of the Wheel of Existence, there are many average Frequencies of Existence and a few Prime Frequencies. But the number of True Frequencies is very low.\"","...!","She continued.","\"Normal Frequencies of Existence are the foundational oceans of weavings that make up the flow of the Wheel. Vast fields containing countless Megalos Domains- Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter- alongside endless seas of the Expanse, acting as the fulcrum of their complexity and purity. A Normal Frequency holds Average Purity and layered Complexity, but often in a chaotic, unstable, and weak form. Within them, life evolves, decays, and cycles endlessly. Those born within will find it arduous to elevate their existence. The number of Existence Severing, Pioneers, or Source Entities that could emerge... is abysmally low. The Frequency barely expresses what it stands for. Having a True Source emerge from such a place is rare.\"","She lifted her hand, pointing outward- beyond the haven, toward the grander scale.","The Megalos Ynnere they were within... was contained in the Prime Frequency of the End.","\"Prime Frequencies of Existence,\" she said, \"are rarer. They are weavings born from the convergence and refinement of multiple Nodes of Normal Frequencies into singular, higher states. Here, Purity increases sharply as they hold Moderate Purity and Complexity. Contradictions are resolved. Structures of existence grow more resilient and organized. Complexity deepens, forming multi-layered domains that are self-sustaining and potent. The identity of the Frequency becomes actualized. Inhabitants aligned with a Prime Frequency can attain a True Source in time.\"","Her gaze hardened.","\"The Prime Frequency of the End... its inhabitants experience constant apocalypses, dangers, and catastrophes. They must overcome them. And through that struggle, their complexity and purity grow stronger.\"","...!","They heard such words as they thought back to their own lives and records.","A history of... apocalypses?","Catastrophes?","They thought of everything they had gone through as their expressions could not help but change.","All of that was simply because they were based inside a frequency geared toward expressing itself?","And its expression was what allowed the many life forms within it to increase in power—as through a constant grinding and waves of catastrophe...powerful entities would be born!"]},{"number":3691,"title":"Chapter 3691: Chapter 3690: Infiniverse IV","paragraphs":["The gaze of the Infiniverse Megalos Body was calm as she continued.","\"The Prime Frequency of Flames bathes everything in a terrifying essence of fire. Only unique lifeforms capable of withstanding the heat of suns are born there. They live their records based on this, and eventually, they too hold the chance of becoming Entities capable of obtaining a True Source. Frequencies of moderate Purity and Complexity—even within them, there are few True Sources capable of being born. But above Prime Frequencies... there are Frequencies born of an established and brilliant True Source of Existence itself.\"","She paused, her eyes drifting toward the budding True Frequency of Entropy.","All eyes turned upward.","The violet-purple river... had begun to take on the form of a massive pillar.","A pillar- but truly, it was a Spoke, stretching outward from the Infiniverse Vein.","And a Spoke... could only belong to a budding Wheel of Existence.","\"True Frequencies of Existence are creations birthed directly from a True Source of Existence,\" she said, \"making them incomparably pure and harmoniously complex. High in Complexity. High in Purity. Unlike Prime or Normal Frequencies, every atom within a True Frequency embodies the fundamental principle of its Source—such as Entropy, Continuity, or Manadynamics. Those born and living within a True Frequency are truly blessed. They gain unique boons, including Existential Transcendence, Existential Immunity, and Limited Absolute Evolution based on the Source's concept. True Frequencies allow for complex beings to rise. From them, powerful True Sources can emerge- giving birth to Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity Entities, Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Entities, even Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects.\"","She spoke at length. And as she did, the massive pillar...the Spoke—grew larger.","It jutted across light-years of distance, stretching the conceptual size of 1,000 Omniverses... and still expanding.","From it, waves of violet brilliance gushed outward, washing across the surrounding space, even bathing the Infiniverse Vein itself.","Moments later...","BOOM!","An incandescent violet brilliance washed over them all.","The True Source of Entropy.","Had it been a Wild True Source, even the strongest among them would have broken down and collapsed instantly.","But this one had an owner.","It was controlled.","It nurtured rather than destroyed.","They felt it—their weavings of existence reacting, the distant calling of chaos and disorder resonating through their cores.","\"True Frequencies,\" the Infiniverse Megalos Body said, \"were abundant before the First Breaking of the Wheel of Existence.\"","WAA!","Terrifying words.","Words none of them knew—yet!","The First Breaking of the Wheel?","The Wheel broke?","Shock rippled through them. The Infiniverse Megalos Body simply continued.","\"There were even Frequency Havens filled with isolated True Sources. Back then, the True Frequencies of Existence exceeded even the high parameters of Purity and Complexity. Their nature approached Limited Absolute levels of Purity and Complexity. From these Frequencies, many Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects were born—beings of tremendously high Purity and Complexity.\"","...!","\"Among them, a single being even exceeded those stages—born from the True Frequency of Lifefyre. But after the First Breaking of the Wheel, progressively lesser True Frequencies bloomed. They lost the luster of Limited Absolute Purity and Complexity. After the Second Breaking, the Third, even the Eighth... very few True Frequencies emerged. Even those that did were mere fractions of what once existed.\"","She smiled faintly.","\"Can you guess... what level of Purity and Complexity we seek for the first True Frequency built under the banner of the True Severed Origin Osmontian?\"","...!","Could they guess?","The question hung over them, heavy and profound.","RAA!","An Emperor Penguin thumped its chest with its flippers. A sharp voice rang out","\"Limited Absolute! What else could it be under the banner of the True Emperor of Quintessence but this?!\"","Its golden eyes radiated pride, fierce and overwhelming.","The Infiniverse Megalos Body turned her gaze to it, and the Penguin's pride wavered slightly under her stare.","Yet she smiled, a rare and brilliant thing to see on her who was serious 99% of the time!","She turned back toward the massive forming Spoke.","Her first Spoke.","The backbone of a new Wheel.","\"Yes.\"","...!","And she gave the affirmation.","\"We will forge something unforged since before the First Breaking of the Wheel. A Limited Absolute Purity and Complexity True Frequency of Existence.","It will not only shape itself but spread across the Infiniverse.","It will be the first...of many.\"","She paused, voice like existential thunder layered beneath weavings of silk.","\"In this Infiniverse... there will no longer be Normal or Prime Frequencies.","There will only be True.\"","HUUM!","Her words resonated profoundly through existence.","They watched as the massive Spoke continued to grow, extending over 5,000 Omniverses in conceptual size.","And inwardly, it was even vaster.","\"The True Frequency of Entropy, born from the True Source of Entropy, embodies the elegant dissolution and disorder of existence,\" she said.","\"It is not chaos—it is a return to the Zero-State. The absolute foundation of potential.\"","The Infiniverse Megalos Body waved her hand, summoning a swirling vortex of violet brilliance, a serpent coiling around her fingers.","HUUM!","The moment the True Source of Entropy appeared in her hands, the world around her shuddered.","Even the obsidian-gold sandy mountains of Dreams were painted violet.","\"Beings aligned with this True Frequency can gain the ability to unravel constructs, existence, even memories,\" she said.","\"The unique boon of this True Frequency—the one that will be potent inside of it, but still prevalent across the Infiniverse Megalos as a whole—is Existential Reset.\"","Her words struck like a hammer.","\"The capacity to deconstruct oneself entirely and reforge from pure Zero-State—without losing their existence.","Within this Frequency, destruction and chaos will become sacred rites.","Nothing false will endure the presence of one who undergoes cycles of chaotic unraveling and reformation...until they become Pure and Complex enough to seize the True Source of Entropy itself.","Or even evolve into new meanings of Entropy-Chaos, Disorder, and more.\"","She smiled, her aura crackling violet with magisterial radiance!","\"And mind you...this is just the first True Frequency of the Infiniverse.\"","Just...the first!","—","Entropy bloomed as a True Source and as a Spoke of a Wheel.","And yet, as this occurred, silent and unseen waves that represented the birth of an unfathomable Wheel of Existence with its first Spoke spread.","Setting into motion Echoes that even the Infiniverse Megalos could not yet predict the eventual outcomes of!"]},{"number":3692,"title":"Chapter 3692: Chapter 3691: Infiniverse V","paragraphs":["Echoes of Existence.","Some were echoes that stretched across Frequencies.","Others were of a different kind- types that many couldn't even begin to fathom.","But as the first Spoke representing a True Frequency of Entropy bloomed within the Infiniverse Megalos and caused unknown echoes to spread...","Previously scattered echoes that had bloomed from a Domus were about to make their return at this moment.","Old echoes.","Not the new echoes spreading out right now.","What the new echoes that were now spreading would bring...remained unknown.","—","Outside the umbrella of the Wheel of Existence.","Past its Infinite Ravines and the Gateway Domus.","Beyond a silver rift flickering within the endless layers of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","HUUM!","The folds of collapse, existence, and nonexistence quaked as terrifying auras emerged, one after another.","Each more dreadful than the last.","At the forefront stood a childlike humanoid, its weavings actively devouring the surrounding strands of existence.","A grin stretched permanently from ear to ear. Its eyes were pure obsidian. Cold. Merciless.","Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw.","He had been alerted by Vha'Nekrul, the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon who had watched Noah empower the Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra within a certain Gateway Domus.","Veltraxis appeared, his eerie smile sharpened with purpose. His body grew- dead skin tearing and expanding as waves of obsidian death and wonder rippled across him.","Now, he stood as a towering skeletal silhouette cloaked in shadow-threaded robes that flowed like liquefied void. Spiked bone protrusions crowned his head like a twisted halo, and his maw stretched unnaturally wide, filled with serrated, smiling teeth. His limbs tapered into tendrils, swaying as if whispering secrets to the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","His Complexity... was High.","High!","Not Average. Not Moderate.","High!","Around him, massive Dead Things of similar Complexity manifested one after another, each more unstable than the last. Their weavings barely held together by Sorrowglass True Source Panaceas- without which, they would become Fractal Beings.","Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, stood before the gateway- its infinite edges flickering with threads of decayed stars and devoured timelines. His hollow smile widened as his voice rang out- a paradox of elegance and entropy.","\"For cycles uncounted, we have wandered...half-things, hollow, converged into this mockery of form. And why? Because we believed. Because we hoped. Because we hunted the Loom. Each Wheel whispered fragments, echoes of a pattern... but never the whole. Some gave us strands. Others? Silence. Absolutely fucking nothing. But this one... this Wheel of Existence... it sings of vibrant True Sources. It might hold a melody. And if it hides a piece of the Loom within its Spokes...\"","\"Then we shall strip it bare. Burn its Frequencies. Shatter its weavings until it bleeds the truth we were denied. We are tired of being Dead Things pretending to live. I want my True Source alive again- bright, burning, unforgotten! The rest of you feel the same, yes?!\"","HUUM!","His weavings buzzed as monstrous forms of beings with Below Average Purity but High Complexity seethed behind him. One stepped forward-","a hunchback giant composed entirely of writhing worms.","\"O 77th Mawbearer of Recursive Hunger, shall I alert nearby Mawbearers of this possibility?\"","...!","The worm-entity asked as Veltraxis turned his cold gaze upon it.","He, Veltraxis, was the 77th Mawbearer of the One Hundred Mawbearers of the Hollow Concord of Nullity.","A legion of beings. Of Dead Things. United under a singular cause in this region of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","The Concord of Hollow Nullity was a dreadful pantheon of Dead Things—forgotten champions, broken Architects, and failed Monads—bound by an agonizing purpose: to become alive again.","Scattered across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, these entities once held True Sources now lost to collapse and death. They clawed through shattered timelines in search of the Loom.","At their heart stood the One Hundred Mawbearers—horrors of vast intellect and warped might. They sought not salvation.","They sought reclamation—of essence, of memory, of meaning. They were not born to be hollow.","They would not remain so.","Veltraxis shook his head.","\"It is merely a single Wheel of Existence—one that already bears the stench of multiple Breakings. At best, there will be a Resplendent Monad or two. If it were a Wheel yet untouched... unbroken... it would be teeming with Monads and Converged Architects, and more of the One Hundred would be summoned. But this? This will be our feast. Let us go.\"","WAA!","Their bodies pulsed with heavy Dead True Sources.","Without delay, they dove into the Gateway Domus—now an overlap of four Wild True Sources: Causality, Fear, Verbum, and Oxidation.","The Hollow Cascade of Reversed Causality, the Pale Verbum Labyrinth, and the Domus of Absolute Fear of Existence twisted and collided with the fourth—once guarded by the Origin Singed—the Domus of Oxidation.","In that moment, Veltraxis, a Converged Architect, and fourteen other Dead Things of similar power stepped through the veiled Domus doorway and into the Infinite Ravines.","Among the 14, Vha'Nekrul who had reported to him could also be seen!","—","Within a certain Gateway Domus.","The Mythic Signature of the Great Beyonder brought down her hand. Upon impact, eighty-one Pillars of Concordance bloomed all at once, converging upon a single Dead Thing whose True Source nearly shattered.","Almost.","But a sliver remained.","From nowhere, tendrils of gold wrapped around it, dragging its weavings toward the chest of none other than Noah.","Into his Cradle of Purity.","There, its Complexity would be dismantled and consumed.","\"Haha... that's the last of the Dead Things! We actually cleared all the Gateway Domus!\"","The expression on the Great Beyonder's vast Mythic Signature radiated triumph- the power of a Quasi-Resplendent Monad alive in her gaze, swirling with trillions of runes.","With the efforts of Noah and Veyl'Aethra beside her, every Dead Thing in the region—each only Harmonized Sourcebound Icons of Moderate Complexity and Below Average Purity—had either fled or perished.","Some, like this one, were preserved. Noah had gathered a total of nine Dead Things and their True Sources into his Cradle of Purity.","The rest were erased beneath the relentless force of the Great Beyonder's Mythic Signature.","She was becoming more and more familiar with her power as she turned towards Noah at this moment with shining eyes, her voice firm and filled with power.","\"It seems like your arrival has changed many things. More and more dead things will keep falling as the dire situation of the Infinite Ravines will soon be turned.\"","...!"]},{"number":3693,"title":"Chapter 3693: Chapter 3692: Infiniverse VI","paragraphs":["The Great Beyonder once again spoke with positivity.","And Noah heard it- and instantly, alarm bells rang in his mind.","Because the last time she had spoken with such optimism, it was right before another Gateway Domus had emerged, forcing itself upon the others already present, followed by a downpour of Dead Things.","And now she spoke in a similarly hopeful tone, even going so far as to mention that the dire nature of the Infinite Ravines had shifted because of him.","Noah glanced around as he heard this, his expression stern, as if bracing for an imminent shift the moment her words ended.","She noticed and harrumphed, rolling her eyes.","\"Do you think I'm some kind of jinx? That every time I talk about things getting better, something comes crashing down to prove me wrong? The Weavings of Existence don't work like that. There are coincidences, and then there are-...!\"","She stopped.","Veyl'Aethra, who had been watching them both, suddenly froze.","His smile faded into something quiet. Something sorrowful.","The face of the Great Beyonder turned pale. Her eyes trembled with a mixture of shock and fury as both her gaze and the gaze of her Mythic Signature snapped toward the distance.","And Noah sighed.","He knew it had nothing to do with her words.","He knew.","But still, every time she made a positive comment, existence itself seemed determined to prove her wrong.","At that moment, all of them turned toward a distant region of the twisting, overlapping Gateway Domus.","From there... a pressure surged.","Terrifying and heavy, eclipsing even the Quasi-Resplendent Monad aura of the Great Beyonder.","And there was more than one.","Vile and saturated with the weavings of the dead.","Sensing it, Veyl'Aethra's sorrow deepened. He shook his head solemnly- and then, his body flickered and distorted, as if his very existence were lagging or shifting into something else.","Noah caught this anomaly with his current perception just as his attention shifted toward the approaching auras- now becoming visible.","The veiled threshold of the Gateway Domus tore open with a thunderous hum.","A Dead Thing of horrifying complexity stepped through first.","Noah's eyes flared with a blinding light, bursting with complex, exceedingly pure power as his distinction as the Weaver of Existence surged forth.","And above this newcomer, a name appeared:","[Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw (Converged Architect)]","Clear and undeniable.","And it only made Noah's expression harden further.","Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, strode forward like death incarnate clothed in splendor. His skeletal frame loomed tall, draped in shadow-threaded robes that rippled like liquefied void. A twisted halo of bone spires crowned his head, and his grinning maw revealed serrated teeth in an unending smile.","Behind him came the Fourteen Dead Things—monstrosities of ruin, from titanic worm-hives to void-armored husks, each pulsing with raw, unstable Dead True Sources.","They stood in a perfect, menacing semi-circle.","The air bent and bled around them, their presence rupturing the wild weavings of True Sources across the Domus.","Noah, Veyl'Aethra, and the Great Beyonder grew even more somber, their eyes narrowing.","Collapse itself had entered the battlefield-heralded by Veltraxis, whose cold, endless grin stretched as he calmly uttered...","\"Hello.\"","BOOM!","The sound echoed like a divine decree.","The Gateway Domus trembled violently. And then—suddenly—it surged upward, folding and unraveling across countless layers of existence.","It wasn't that another region was being drawn into theirs.","It was their Gateway Domus...being forcibly merged into another.","A judgment had been made: the three of them alone weren't enough to face what was coming.","And truly, when faced with fourteen Converged Architects, failed Resplendent Monads, and even a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon- what could the Wheel do but yield?","Noah kept his gaze fixed on the other Dead Things accompanying Veltraxis. Though their power was slightly less than his, it was still far too complex for even a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon-level being to stand against.","Even with his current complexity, Noah knew he could not harm their True Sources for now.","But that might not remain true even an hour from now, as the Infiniverse Megalos underwent a terrifying ascension.","BOOOM!","Reality split apart.","The Domus shattered and reformed with a loud, jarring bang—and when it reassembled, it was no longer in the same place.","Now, they were somewhere else entirely.","A place dominated by a single, terrifying aura.","Structures of fractured brilliance swirled around them.","Ten Wild True Sources flowed freely, clashing and weaving in chaotic majesty.","Crystal mountains glittered in one direction. Fiery hellscapes churned in another.","Colors and wonder bled through every crevice of the air.","And yet... most striking of all was an endless gray sea, its waters thick with ash.","There were no Dead Things here.","Only this ash-covered expanse, surrounded by hundreds of radiant gray pillars.","Floating above the gray sea was a solitary figure—a middle-aged man with dark hair and tan skin. A robe of smoke and shadow billowed around him, and he radiated nothing but calm and quiet awe.","Noah locked eyes with him.","And he remembered the words of the Witness—about a Resplendent Monad who had survived since the Eighth Breaking of the Wheel.","The holder of the True Source of Asche.","At that moment, their Gateway Domus had fully merged into his, bringing along fifteen Dead Things—most of them on par with Resplendent Monads.","\"...\"","Noah breathed through the chaos and turned inward.","To his own power.","Because no matter what the outer weavings did, he could count on himself.","On his weavings.","And now, with monstrosities arriving from every corner, he focused inwards—on the Infiniverse Megalos.","On his True Source Atlas of Existence, on Ruination, and the complex Dead Things of the Cradle of Purity that he would one day devour.","From deep within, the Infiniverse Megalos spoke to him.","\"Through any Weavings of Existence... I will be here, Master.\"","HUUM!","Her voice rang with serenity and solemn resolve.","She could see what he saw.","She understood what now stood before them.","And so, she accelerated her transformation.","Her voice echoed again, reassuring him:","\"Master, others will gain their own boons from the True Frequencies of the Infiniverse Megalos. But you... you will have something else entirely.\"","WAA!","\"For you, the entire True Frequency of Entropy—newly constructed—is available to grasp and wield. It will allow you to channel its intricate weavings and the full complexity of the Infiniverse... into a single, focused point, expressed through the True Source of Entropy- through the Spoke of Entropy.\"","\"I will begin working on Continuity next... followed by Manadynamics, and all the rest... until the Infiniverse Megalos takes its final step- becoming the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence.\"","...!"]},{"number":3694,"title":"Chapter 3694: Chapter 3693: One After Another I","paragraphs":["The Infiniverse Wheel of Existence.","That was the end goal. The destination. The apex the Infiniverse strained toward!","And it had to be enough.","Because Noah couldn't fail- not now, and not ever.","Others could stumble. Others could break. But him? Even his worst mistakes were victories in disguise. He thought of Bob, and how things had played out. A failure, maybe. But only by his impossible standards.","Anyone else would've seen it for what it was: a successful stand against a monstrous Dead Thing, denying him at every turn until he was finally forced to withdraw.","Now, another challenge had risen.","This time? It was multiple Dead Things. Entities on the level of Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects.","They towered in complexity, vastly beyond him. But they were far inferior in purity.","Noah's mind raced, turning over the dynamic interplay between power, purity, and complexity.","What happens when someone of extreme purity collides with someone of massive complexity?","Which would prevail?","If his current purity was at the \"Moderate\" level, could the presence of multiple pure True Sources tip the scale- even against something like a Dead Thing Converged Architect?","He hadn't known the answer. Not before.","But now... now, he had test subjects.","If he survived the clash with them, that is.","At that moment, within the Infiniverse Megalos, a radiant violet Spoke surged from the Infiniverse Vein and stretched outward- farther and farther- until it reached the very edge of what was visible.","And there, from the tip, a ring began to form.","It curved, arcing outward, until it wrapped the Infiniverse itself in a luminous outline.","The outer ring...","Of a Wheel of Existence.","Unfathomable. Impossible.","And yet it was happening- right here before his eyes!","|The True Source of Entropy has bloomed within your Weavings of Existence.|","|The True Source of Entropy is connected to the True Frequency of Entropy, holding Limited Absolute Purity at its core. The True Source itself has been forged with Moderate Complexity and Quasi-High Purity.|","...!","He hadn't even moved yet, and answers were already arriving.","Others climbed slowly- they chose a path, forged a single True Source, and walked a careful line.","But Noah? His path was never meant to be like anyone else's. He didn't forge a True Source.","He forged multiple.","And the Infiniverse... it didn't just help him create more of them, it linked them to True Frequencies of Existence!","It gave him access to forces no other existence could ever hope to touch.","Like now, Entropy. A freshly forged True Source.","And because it was connected to a True Frequency of Limited Absolute Purity...","His own True Source of Entropy emerged with Quasi-High Purity and Moderate Complexity.","Moderate alone could crown someone a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.","High could elevate them to a Resplendent Monad or Converged Architect.","But Quasi-High?","That placed him right in between- exactly like the Great Beyonder.","And this? This was just the first True Source the Infiniverse had birthed.","More were coming. Each tethered to its own True Frequency and each adding its own Quasi-High Purity to him.","How many would he need?","How long until he reached a state to rival- or even surpass- a Resplendent Monad?","He didn't have that answer yet.","But soon, he would!","HUUM!","As violet flames of Entropy raged in his Weavings of Existence, Noah stood motionless, absorbing it all.","Entropy.","Entropy!","|Through the Weavings of the True Source of Entropy, Echoes of Finality may now be utilized.|","|Fractured Echoes obtained from your Records will be randomly unleashed, granting them Fractured Echo Forms imbued with the unraveling chaos of Entropy. Their presence alone can slowly deteriorate the True Source of any opposition. When a Mythic True Signature is used to channel the Echoes of Finality, their potency escalates exponentially.|","|Existential Reset is also now possible, allowing your Weavings to revert to a Zero-State. However, this is not recommended as your current state is the most optimal, and it is not guaranteed you will return to it should you Reset.|","...!","This was what the others in his Infiniverse could wield.","And while he could, technically... he didn't need to.","His outcome was already the best one possible.","Even as he adjusted to the burning weight of Entropy, something new was also beginning as the Infiniverse moved relentlessly.","|The True Frequency of Continuity has begun to be forged.|","From a point on the opposite end of the Infiniverse Vein, a white-green brilliance sparked to life.","Another Spoke was forming.","Another True Source was on its way.","And in the middle of it all...","\"Let me wield your first Spoke of Entropy in this newly merging Domus. I want to see if I can smack a Converged Architect around with it...\"","...!","Noah's eyes glowed with the quiet light of tyranny of a man who had already decided the outcome.","And the answer, as always...","\"Yes, Master.\"","Affirmation.","Obedience.","The violet Spoke of the Infiniverse Wheel shimmered.","Its weavings surged across dimensions, connecting to his construct through an unshakable bond.","It would cross countless realities to arrive...in the depths of the Infinite Ravines.","—","The Infinite Ravines.","Inside a Gateway Domus where over a dozen Wild True Sources converged and flared, their Weavings of Existence thrashing violently.","Any Harmonized Sourcebound Icon would struggle here.","There were too many forces. Too much pressure.","It was almost too much for Veyl'Aethra- his face pale, his True Source wrapped tight around him just to survive.","The Great Beyonder stood steady.","Her purity, on its way to becoming truly High, insulated her from the worst of it.","Noah?","He stood still, his body bubbling with power.","He matched the Great Beyonder now- purity for purity. Complexity for complexity.","And as he stared across the expanse, his gaze found the source of the rising dread.","A congregation of Dead Things loomed, watching.","Their attention turned sharply toward a single figure.","The holder of the True Source of Asche.","A man with gray hair and a beard of the same. His robes, billowing shadow-ash gray, flowed as he sat atop a sea of gray ash.","Everything around him whispered with the same color, the same finality.","Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, had fixed his monstrous gaze on this man- believing him the only threat.","But he was wrong!","Because while the Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra were frozen, tense and uncertain, Noah stepped forward, calm and composed.","His voice sliced through the stillness like a Quintessential blade.","\"Before all the craziness kicks off... would you all mind introducing yourselves? Maybe tell me why, exactly, you've chosen now to enter the Infinite Ravines? Because this doesn't look like a random appearance...this looks coordinated. So tell me, what brings you all to our home?\"","...!","His voice was calm.","Measured.","But behind it throbbed power. Unapologetic. Unrelenting. Tyrannical. Quintessential!","And suddenly, every eye, alive and not, turned to him."]},{"number":3695,"title":"Chapter 3695: Chapter 3694: One After Another II","paragraphs":["What brings you all to our home?","He asked it plainly- at a moment soaked in tension, when most would've struggled to breathe, let alone speak.","But Noah, even with the storm of destruction and chaos looming over them all, stood there- fearless and unshaken, as if making small talk over the weavings of existence","Far ahead, just beyond a row of fourteen Dead Things, Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, turned his attention from the ashen horizon and grinned. Edge to edge. That smile deepened as he looked between Noah and the holder of the True Source of Asche.","And then, he spoke.","\"If you were any other Harmonized Sourcebound Icon, I might've glanced at that Resplendent Monad standing beside you and asked why he let something so fragile speak for him. But since you are directly responsible for our arrival here... I'll indulge your disrespectful little question. It was you.\"","...!","It was him?","Noah blinked, disbelieving.","What the fuck did he mean it was him?","The Great Beyonder's gaze sharpened, her eyes narrowing as Veltraxis's grin widened further—so wide now it seemed his entire face was a smile carved into dead flesh.","He lifted a dead hand, motioning to the side—toward the only Harmonized Sourcebound Icon among his monstrous entourage.","\"This one here saw you. In your Gateway. From a distance. He witnessed you ignite a white-gold flame that could actually empower and fortify other True Sources.\"","...!","\"You see... the alteration of any True Source, whether it's one's own or someone else's, is nearly impossible. When it does occur, it's the result of something... singular. A presence standing beyond conventional power. Something tied to a special kind of Wheel of Existence. That's why I came. To confirm whether what you wield is that kind of Wheel. In truth... us being here? It's your fault. Your existence, the uniqueness of it, called us. Isn't it beautiful?\"","HUUM!","Heavy words.","But the words weren't admiration.","They were psychotic, laced with manic glee—spoken by something that didn't just want to watch the existence burn, but wanted to dance in the ashes.","Noah's gaze sharpened, glowing brighter with each breath.","They came because of him?","Because of the Singed?","He wanted to call it bullshit, but...at the same time, looking at his long history, was he actually the thing that invited apocalypses, catastrophes, and destruction?","\"...\"","Before he could speak, another voice rose- ancient, amused, and unmistakably alive.","\"Oh, come on. A white-gold flame that empowers True Sources? Is that all it takes to make Dead Things giddy these days?\"","...!","The voice of the Holder of the True Source of Asche echoed like a song from the grave- timeless and unbothered, even here, in the maw of chaos.","A slow smile tugged at his ageless face.","Veltraxis turned toward the Sea of Ash, answering curtly.","\"These days? Everything makes Dead Things jumpy. Every day, we inch closer to True Death.","I am the 77th Mawbearer of Recursive Hunger—part of the Concord of Hollow Nullity...","There are others like us...Dead Things searching for the same answer. For the same thing. Even Living Things clawing to stop the Last Breaking of their Wheels are looking for it. Tell me... can you blame our desperation?\"","WAA!","He dropped words that could unhinge a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon.","The 77th Mawbearer?","That meant there were at least seventy-six more like him.","And more, if the number wasn't symbolic.","The Concord of Hollow Nullity wasn't alone.","There were other factions of Dead Things like it.","Other nightmares moving across existence like cancer through stars.","And...","\"Fucking hell...\"","Noah cursed aloud, his eyes burning with tyranny as his thoughts snapped into focus.","These monsters could not be allowed to leave.","Not one.","Somehow, some way—they all had to die.","A strange light began to rise from within him—a bloom of power so complex it seemed to bend the space around him.","Without a word, he stepped forward, flames already flickering across his skin.","The Great Beyonder moved, almost reached for him, but Noah brushed her hand aside with a small, reassuring pat.","He didn't stop.","From his right hand, violet flames ignited—layered with the familiar brilliance of white-gold, the signature of the Singed.","To the outside world, it looked like a crystallized pillar of white-gold light was forming—a spear wrapped in entropy, impossibly dense.","He was summoning the Spoke of Entropy, hidden behind the veil of his white gold flame.","He couldn't reveal his weavings too freely, after all.","Then, he turned back to Veltraxis and the others, nodding casually.","\"So... you all came here with grand intentions. Trying to break through to the Wheel of Existence, right? Anyone feel like a quick warm-up? Just me, a humble little Harmonized Sourcebound Icon...Versus, let's say... not your weakest, but your only Harmonized Sourcebound Icon. That'd be you, right? Vha'Nekrul?\"","...!","The Weaver of Existence made names clear.","The pillar in his hand—sleek and razor-edged—snapped into position, the point aimed directly at the Dead Thing who had once observed him in silence.","The skeletal being's eyes flared in rage at being called the weakest.","Noah didn't even acknowledge it.","He kept going.","\"Actually... no. Let's skip that. I'll fight a Converged Architect instead.\"","His smile returned, calm and filled with tyranny.","\"The weakest among them.\"","And then...","The Spoke moved.","It pointed.","Dead silence followed.","It landed on a towering, hunchbacked Dead Thing.","A grotesque creature made entirely of sleek, writhing worms—each one twitching in unison, like a hive that wore a corpse as armor.","A ripple of recognition passed through Noah's eyes as the distinction of the Weaver of Existence worked freely.","\"M'gorrhaal, The Crawling Colossus. Holder of the Dead True Source of Infestation.\"","...!","\"Think you can handle someone as tiny as me?\"","Noah's voice dripped with majesty now, each syllable stabbing at the pride of the Dead Things across from him.","M'gorrhaal trembled.","Not in fear, but in hunger—barely holding himself back.","And then, Veltraxis raised a hand—silent and fluid—and gave the command.","Go.","The Crawling Colossus moved.","Towering. Slouching. Writhing.","The battlefield shifted with each thunderous step.","A 1 v 1.","A Harmonized Sourcebound Icon versus a Converged Architect.","On paper, the result should've been clear.","But none of them—not even Veltraxis—understood what Noah held.","In his hand wasn't just a True Source.","It was a Spoke.","A fragment of a Wheel.","A weight of existence itself.","And now, the outcome?","Was unknown."]},{"number":3696,"title":"Chapter 3696: Chapter 3695: One After Another III","paragraphs":["M'gorrhaal, the Crawling Colossus. Holder of the Dead True Source of Infestation.","This was his title- a distinction that, in this moment, stood as he faced the singular figure of Noah.","It was as if every other Source of Existence, dead or living, had vanished.","And beneath the weave of their Existences, only the two of them remained.","Even though the Great Beyonder and Veyl'Aethra warred behind Noah, their gazes were solemn and turbulent as they tried desperately to find a way out.","Even in the far distance, the figure holding the True Source of Asche watched in silence, his face carved with a smile that barely veiled the intensity and seriousness behind his eyes.","Even farther, across from them, near the grotesque creature that held the Dead True Source of Infestation- Veltraxis hovered in a manner that inspired dread. The surrounding weavings of Existence were passively drawn and devoured by him, including the many wild True Sources.","But all of that faded.","Only the two of them seemed to exist now.","And Noah...","\"You're one ugly fucker, aren't you? What exactly were you when you were alive? Do you even remember?\"","His words caused M'gorrhaal to pulse violently, his True Source of Infestation flaring.","The Dead Thing didn't answer- not immediately. It simply stared at Noah with a bottomless hunger, drawn to his purity as if it carried a divine aroma.","The millions of worms writhing across its face wiggled, salivating, as its ancient, dead voice echoed out.","\"The Blooming Womb of Rot.\"","HUUM!","The surroundings pulsed, their colors rotting into a diseased green and ashen gray.","The True Source of Infestation bloomed wildly, and above M'gorrhaal, a Dead Mythic True Signature materialized with virulent malice.","It appeared as a dead, skeletal worm composed of trillions of lesser worms. Its height towered over a hundred Omniverses, crowned with serrated bony jaws and a grotesquely pulsing, stomach-like core that split open like a wound, spewing verdant-gray tides of madness.","The True Source of Infestation had fully unfolded.","The Blooming Womb of Rot bloomed.","This plague-forged biome pulsed like living flesh—birthing bio-organic spires, twitching tendrils, and eyeless larvae that exhaled pestilence into the air.","Noah read its nature clearly as he gripped the Spoke in his hand tighter.","Once this Source was activated, every wound, pore, and orifice in any Living or Dead Thing within range could become a potential birthing point for parasitic Infestlings—limb-wrapped horrors that gestated at an accelerated rate of existence.","They would spread across the opposing True Sources and devour their hosts from within...unless purged.","Only cleansing from a True Source of High Purity or High Complexity could counter them.","That was the only real path to resistance- the only way one could hope to overcome such infestation.","The eyeless larvae and virulent seas surged toward Noah like a pestilent tide.","And opposite him, M'gorrhaal's deep, guttural voice echoed again:","\"You...are mighty.\"","WAA!","\"You...are tasty.\"","...!","\"Let me feed, O Living True Source filled with Purity.\"","Its voice radiated authority, and the festering sea beneath it seemed to salivate, drawn toward Noah's terrifyingly radiant essence.","But Noah only gripped the spear-shaped Spoke and thrust it forward as he spoke:","\"Echoes of Finality.\"","...!","Echoes.","Of Finality.","He invoked them.","Fractured Echoes gathered from his Records surged outward, manifesting in Echo Forms imbued with Entropy's unraveling chaos.","And at that instant—","Noah's eyes flared with violet light.","|Echoes of Finality have scoured your Records and randomly selected the Fractured Echo Form of Quintessential Emperor's Annihilation Technique – First Form: The Descent of the Ascendant Severing Soul Star.|","...!","An old weaving. A piece of him.","Part of his Record.","|The Echo of Finality: Shattered Entropic Wheel is blooming.|","Behind and above him, a violet \"star\" bloomed—though it wasn't truly a star. And it was covered by the flames of the Singed.","It was the True Source of Entropy, transformed into a Mythic True Signature.","A Shattered Wheel, its sole Spoke stretching the size of 1,000 Omniverses, bloomed with violent grace.","Yet it burned with white-gold flames.","The Wheel appeared as a broken celestial structure—its lone Spoke pointed directly at the onrushing tide of infestation.","But it didn't move.","It didn't need to.","Because the original Record of the Ascendant Severing Soul Star was deceptively simple.","[Quintessential Emperor's Annihilation Technique – First Form]: ...The Assassin Emperor of Severance becomes a multi-target effect against all who gaze upon the Star of Illumination. It can only chain once under multi-target status....","A forgotten power.","Yet under the influence of Entropy, it became something far more magnificent—reforged into a white-gold Wheel of severing judgment.","And when the trillions of eyes making up M'gorrhaal gazed upon the Wheel...","SUUU!","From the broken Wheel, unfathomable flashes of existence surged toward the grotesque gray-green tide!","Toward the very sea birthed from a Dead True Source of Infestation!","These radiant severing lights carried more than Entropy. Disguised as white-gold, they bore the force of the Spoke itself.","They bore the weight of the Infiniverse Megalos.","\"...\"","Entropy alone—Quasi-High Purity and Moderate Complexity, was staggering.","But now it merged with the Spoke, a literal anchor of the True Frequency of Entropy, and the heavy burden of the Infiniverse's Complexity.","It was weighty.","It was overwhelming.","His own Purity, the Spoke, the very framework of Complexity—merged into a singular, fantastical strike.","Against the Mythic True Signature of a Converged Architect with High Complexity—Noah's Severing Lights of Existence flashed.","And the horrid tide of pestilence that spread so widely...","Was cut.","Shredded apart as if it had never been.","The corruption disintegrated in white-gold fire—there one instant, gone the next.","Only M'gorrhaal remained.","\"...\"","Above him, the massive skeletal worm writhed—then shattered beneath the brilliance of Purity and Complexity.","M'gorrhaal himself...","CUT!","Split down the center.","CUT! CUT!","More pieces followed, his High Complexity flaring wildly—his end nearing True Death as space warped.","And the final severing strike dragged what was left of his body before Noah.","Golden tendrils erupted from Noah's chest and devoured everything that remained of the Dead Thing.","Instantly.","Too fast!","The weakest Converged Architect among the Dead Things...had been erased.","But...","That wasn't all.","The Shattered Entropic Wheel, which drew from the Quintessential Emperor's Annihilation Technique – First Form...","Was multi-target.","And behind M'gorrhaal...","There were many more targets."]},{"number":3697,"title":"Chapter 3697: Chapter 3696: One After Another IV","paragraphs":["The Weakest Converged Architect among those who entered was decimated as his True Source of Infestation was overwhelmed by something it didn't even understand!","And above Noah, the massive Mythic True Signature of a Shattered Entropic Wheel with a single spoke remained. Its tremendously fast attacks—based on the record of the Quintessential Emperor's Annihilation Technique, First Form—swept out at this moment on all enemies that gazed upon it!","The weavings of existence where only Noah and the Holder of the True Source of Infestation were contained seemingly broke down, as everyone in the surroundings became visible once more.","And the effects of the Shattered Entropic Wheel spread as they seemed like unfathomably fast blades of existence, seeking to cut down every Dead Thing in sight.","But...","The figure of Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, stepped forward.","He stood before all of the Dead Things as the attacks surging toward them—and those hurtling toward him—converged in his direction.","His smile deepened.","And in the next instant, existence itself began to fold, constrict, and collapse around them.","Near them all, the possible weavings of the living True Sources of Existence ceased to exert their effects.","In his hands, Noah felt the terrifying True Source of Entropy he held—his Spoke—vibrate as he received a horrific backlash. The weavings, Wild True Sources, and existence around him began to fold and collapse in a terrifying manner, threatening to bring down all Complexity!","For the first time in a while, he felt a threat.","He felt his Moderate Complexity and Quasi-High Purity here in danger!","He prepared to exert even more power and even call his other True Sources here, when in the next moment...","WHOOSH!","Ash began to spread around him as a man surrounded by endless ash appeared.","WAA!","The Mythic True Signature of the Great Beyonder released trillions of obsidian-gold runes around him.","Veyl'Aethra radiated a wonder of white as his left hand trembled.","And around him, the terrific collapse seeking to pressure his existence itself was forcefully paused, with an erupting gray sea of ash even pushing it away!","\"And here I thought there was still honor in Dead Things...\"","The voice of the Holder of the True Source of Asche rang out as he stood before Noah, the Great Beyonder, and Veyl'Aethra.","The scene cleared.","In the region where Veltraxis was, the entire Domus had changed—as if everything nearby had collapsed and filled with paradoxes. Extreme obsidian foldings spread out, resembling the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","Within them, the figures of the Dead Things became even more empowered. The power they radiated seemed twice as potent.","In front of all this, Veltraxis stood, his smiling expression never fading.","He floated toward the spot where M'gorrhaal, The Crawling Colossus, once stood. His obsidian-clawed hand reached out and tapped the area, as if struck by remembrance.","And his aged voice echoed out.","\"He returns to the everlasting silence between pulses, where no weavings dare shimmer and all hungers are finally still. Let his rot sing with glory, for even decay remembers greatness.\"","...!","Was he... honoring the decimation of M'gorrhaal?","Afterward, he turned to look toward the direction of Noah.","His gaze bypassed even the ancient figure surrounded by gray ash.","\"Honor? Honor? Is that tasty? Can I wipe my arse with it? You see, when you are a Dead Thing, you have to be adaptable. You have to be like... what was that saying? Ah yes, you have to be like water, my friend.\"","HUUM!","\"And I am a very constantly changing stream of water at this moment. I have to adapt.\"","His complexity was terrifying.","Even though it was deemed... High, it was terrifyingly so.","He alone had done something unfathomable—as this Gateway Domus was no longer simply filled with Wild True Sources... but the weavings of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds themselves had been inserted here by Veltraxis!","The Smiling Empty Maw shook his head as he looked toward Noah with eyes pulsing with obsidian death and continued.","\"The one whose True Source you just collapsed... do you know what he was asking me just moments ago before we arrived?\"","...!","\"He was asking me whether we should alert and let the other Mawbearers of the Hollow Concord of Nullity know what we were doing—and whether we needed support. I told him no. Because if there was a clue to that which so many of us seek, I wanted it for myself. And if there was no clue, I would've simply feasted on the weavings of a living Wheel of Existence. But now... to honor him, my mind has changed.\"","WAA!","Noah's expression became stern.","The Holder of the True Source of Asche's calm smile faded away entirely as he began to move, a massive Mythic True Signature of himself blooming above him!","\"Haha, I've already done it. I've alerted all 100 Mawbearers of the Hollow Concord of Nullity about a possible Wheel of Existence I may want support on. Your location—unalterable across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds—is now known to all. And I do this not because I believe I cannot wipe you all here... but out of an overabundance of caution and efficiency. I am old. Truly old, and I have seen many things.\"","...!","\"Did you expect fairness? Did you expect that after asking for a one-versus-one battle and then destroying a Converged Architect, I'd be dismayed—have my pride hurt—and send another Converged Architect one after another? No. No, no, no!\"","His eyes and weavings brimmed with death and madness.","\"No.\"","Around him, the terrifying weavings of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds continued to spread!","\"No... this is not a fairytale. This is not some fantasy. This is real. Too many things are at stake—and you don't even have the capacity to understand what existence for Dead Things is like. Today, you'll get a glimpse of how that feels. A glimpse of pain. A glimpse of death.\"","BOOM!","Countless weavings collapsed all around as this entire Gateway Domus became filled with the weavings of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","And Veltraxis looked coldly at the four of them.","The Great Beyonder was ashen, her eyes trembling with rage and horror.","Veyl'Aethra sighed, his gaze one of desolation.","And the Holder of the True Source of Asche sighed with ageless solemnity.","Things... seemed utterly dire.","The Smiling Empty Maw's outstretched smile became even more jagged as he continued.","\"It seems all available Mawbearers of the Hollow Concord of Nullity who aren't tied up by other Wheels will be here soon. Tell me—has your Wheel of Existence not undergone multiple Breakings already? How many Resplendent Monads and Converged Architects does it have? Because unless you've dozens... things do not look well for you.\"","Its words were taunting.","\"Oh, and speaking of which...\"","And as if things couldn't possibly get worse...","\"It seems the first one has arrived.\"","Veltraxis looked behind him- and in the next moment, the folded, collapsed weavings of paradoxes, existence, and nonexistence erupted as brand new auras of... 26 Dead Things bloomed.","Half Converged Architects. Half Harmonized Sourcebound Icons.","And in the lead...","\"Haha, my brother—the 63rd Mawbearer of Endless Paradox—is the first to arrive, it seems.\"","At the forefront, a terrifying entity led the group of 26 newly arriving Dead Things. It radiated a level of Complexity eclipsing even the 77th Mawbearer of Recursive Hunger, Veltraxis!","It was an unfolding of existence that spelled doom and decimation.","Weavings that caused Noah's eyes to burn with tyrannical lividity!"]},{"number":3698,"title":"Chapter 3698: Chapter 3697: Everything I","paragraphs":["At a certain point in time, one simply wanted to be left alone.","To do what they wished and accomplish what they wanted, without having to worry about large-scale events.","At this moment, that was what Noah desired.","He wanted to complete his Atlas of Existence, to let Ruination consume as many shattered pieces of the Wheel as she pleased, and for his Infiniverse Megalos to smoothly continue its transformation—becoming the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence.","He wanted all of this, but as always, there was the factor of Time.","And it seemed that with every passing moment, Time only spelled complexity and catastrophe.","The catastrophe right now? It stemmed from the arrival of a terrifying group of Dead Things, drawn here by a single being-Vha'Nekrul, who had observed Noah while the white flames of the True Source of the Singed empowered others.","Because of this, a monstrous entity had been alerted. Veltraxis, the Smiling Empty Maw, the 77th Mawbearer of Recursive Hunger.","And such a being, already beyond unfathomable, had called upon more like it. Others even more powerful had already begun to arrive. And they would keep arriving!","One after another.","One. After. Another!","At a time like this, when tyrannical lividity coursed through him, Noah instead found himself calm. Unfathomably calm. Eyes closed, calculating.","He took a breath, closed his eyes for a heartbeat. When he opened them again... they pulsed with clarity, as he sent a thought to the Infiniverse Megalos.","'The future that may unfold from here will be a difficult one. I need you to begin preparations just in case.'","...!","He saw several possibilities.","He examined the complexity of the enemies before him and those to come, and compared them to his own evolving Complexity and Purity. He measured his potential once the Atlas was complete and as the Infiniverse Megalos continued forming Spokes of the Wheel.","He calculated. He judged. And the conclusions were... not ideal!","Because of this, he had to prepare.","|What do you need me to do, Master?|","The Infiniverse Megalos responded with her usual calm, measured tone.","Noah answered succinctly, even as the form of the 63rd Mawbearer of Endless Paradox began to materialize.","'Other parts of me will move with you. Start the process—traverse from Frequency to Frequency. Convert all Channelers to connect with you. The goal is all Frequencies and all possibilities.'","...!","A heavy step.","And if one considered why Noah would begin such a process...they would dread the future he must have foreseen!","The Infiniverse Megalos didn't speak for a moment. Then, firmly.","|Understood, Master.|","A command given. A command followed.","Noah turned his gaze to the newly emerging figure- a thing of death, like all the others, but this one drew the attention of even Veltraxis.","The 63rd Mawbearer of Endless Paradox.","Veltraxis looked toward them as the new Mawbearer arrived, its form a massive obsidian bone-cross, an X-shaped skeleton of ruin with a crimson eye glaring at its center.","It was a vile thing to behold. And behind it, even more monstrosities appeared- each having reached the terrifying stage of Converged Architect.","|Oh 77th... This is the Wheel you found? Its taste already seems exquisite.|","\"Haha, 63rd... Xhurrel. The Wheel itself will be interesting, yes. But the purity of a certain creature within this Wheel? That may be even more appetizing.\"","...!","As he said this, Veltraxis turned a grim, ravenous smile toward Noah.","And even as they spoke, the surrounding weavings, still connected to the Infinite Ravines, trembled.","They had to tremble.","Because at this moment, Noah and everyone else could feel it.","The descent of a few dozen Wild True Sources of Existence.","A few dozen.","Enough to overwhelm even Harmonized Sourcebound Icons. Yet, it was... understandable.","Before Noah, the figure of the holder of the True Source of Asche sighed as he looked up.","\"I didn't expect this day to come. All this time, I lingered, waited, did all that I could—hoping for a miracle. But like all things...it all turns to ash. Endless, unfathomable ash...\"","His voice carried the weight of helplessness, even from one as powerful as a Resplendent Monad.","Noah looked up and confirmed it as well- multiple Gateway Domus were merging into theirs.","Continuously.","Without pause.","As if the Wheel of Existence had deemed it necessary to converge its defenses. Across many fractured doorways, a singular Gateway Domus was forming!","A unified... Infinite Ravines.","One doorway for the entire Wheel of Existence.","And that brought both wonder and dread.","Because from those fused gates...","HUUM!","Auras of power surged as defenders began to descend, their faces shocked.","They were numerous.","Dozens of beings at the level of Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity and the less complex Nascent Source-Bearer entities appeared from above, below, and behind.","Among them, Noah saw the figure of the Omnifather- his expression grave.","Apart from him, he also saw a woman!","He saw someone he had only glimpsed in the weavings of records, in dreams tied to Bob.","She stepped forth...the Watcher of the Wheelomachy.","The First Watcher. A radiant woman with flowing red hair that shimmered like molten dusk.","She stood beyond time's grasp, her eyes pulsing with a power close to that of a Resplendent Monad, her presence reflecting every revolution of the Infinite Wheel.","Noah squinted.","But as the Weaver of Existence, clarity came to him faster than to most as he was able to glimpse her True Source.","The True Source of Chronohedra- the very Axis of Temporal Balance!","A fearsome True Source. One that anchored reality while preserving the sequence of all positive time.","Among the defenders, she was among the purest, most intricate, and yet even she was not a true Resplendent Monad.","Men. Women. Entities with no clear race or gender.","Noah counted 77 Legends.","Protectors only spoken of in whispers across Frequencies. Some remembered. Most forgotten.","The Great Beyonder studied them all and confirmed what they already feared.","\"All of the Gateway Domus... are merging here...\"","Yes.","One of the worst possible scenarios was unfolding. All defenders were gathered in one place.","At the same time, more Dead Things emerged—some from the very same gateways the defenders had guarded all this time.","And those Dead Things, arriving one by one, looked in awe at the blazing auras of Veltraxis and the 63rd Mawbearer of Endless Paradox.","At the same time, behind those two beings, within the folds of Nullvein Gravewake that Veltraxis conjured, a tremor ran through, and...eighteen more Dead Things appeared.","Led by yet another Mawbearer of the Hollow Concord of Nullity.","\"Ah...\"","It felt like an endless incursion.","And despair began rising like a flood!"]},{"number":3699,"title":"Chapter 3699: Chapter 3698: Everything II","paragraphs":["Despair was rising like a flood, and this wasn't happening to just some weak entities with lesser complexity who did not have the capability to shift the scale of power... this was happening to beings who had lived for millions of years.","Because the scene they were witnessing was utterly horrendous to behold.","Just now, in this moment, there were quite literally dozens of Converged Architects who were Dead Things.","Even without mentioning or acknowledging the Harmonized Sourcebound Icon Complexity Dead Things.","The Converged Architects alone were equivalent to Resplendent Monads, and on the side of the Living, they had... a single one so far.","A few with extremely Pure or uniquely complex weavings were somewhat close to Resplendent Monads, but they could be counted on a single hand.","\"What in fresh hell is this, my friend?\"","From above the merging Gateway Domus, the figure of none other than the Origin Singed appeared, of course controlled by the mind of the Great Usurper.","He had just recently delved into the Infinite Ravines, and in this moment, he was already drawn into a singular, unified doorway, where he now stared at a number of terrifying entities.","The only one he recognized was Noah. And so he moved toward him, while the other arriving legends also gathered near the Holder of the True Source of Asche.","Near the only Resplendent Monad here.","Noah gave the Great Usurper a glance and shook his head as if even words could not explain this, continuing to survey the gathering legends. His gaze landed on a woman clad in weavings of Anti-Matter and Dark Matter, her eyes serpentine- was this... the Stellar Weaver?","The question lingered only a moment before another familiar presence stepped forward.","The Omnifather, though ashen, recognized Noah and came forward to ask.","\"You... you were in the weavings of the Wheel. Do you know what Bob did within? Are these Dead Things his doing—invited by him after he left for the Nullvein Gravewake Folds?!\"","The Omnifather looked injured as he echoed the question.","Noah gave him a glance and calmly replied,","\"The chaos Bob caused has been dealt with as these Dead Things...have nothing to do with him.\"","They had nothing to do with him. But they were here.","They had caused the entire Wheel of Existence to exert its effort, merging every single doorway within the Infinite Ravines. The entire Wheel could now only be accessed through a singular, central focus point.","All defenders were present, and any Living Things that still existed would arrive here too.","The positives and negatives swirled. Even as the descent of a few dozen True Sources continued, the arrival of Dead Things never ceased. After the appearance of three Mawbearers...","BOOM!","Another shattered the folds of collapse and complexity as they appeared.","The 71st Mawbearer.","The 50th Mawbearer.","The 47th Mawbearer.","The 88th Mawbearer!","Noah looked from one to the next, watching them appear in seconds, each leading groups with at least twelve Dead Things, some as many as twenty-seven as his distinction as the Weaver of Existence continued to go crazy!","The more that appeared, the heavier the despair settled into the hearts of the Living who stood opposite them.","And all the while, Veltraxis stood at the forefront, his demonic grin, already stretched from ear to ear, somehow growing wider.","He was looking at Noah and the Holder of the True Source of Asche as if waiting.","Waiting for that face.","That face of despair.","That face of rage and pain.","And yet, even as the expressions of the living legends behind Noah became ashen... Noah remained calm.","His eyes did not so much as flutter.","Veltraxis took that as a challenge.","From the side of the Living...","\"Haha... Haha! Just... Haha!\"","Veyl'Aethra, the old man, was laughing madly.","His left hand flickered, trembling as it began to phase in and out of existence, as if it were lagging.","His Fractal Collapse... now visible. Everyone around him stepped back slightly.","Some didn't care. Their eyes showed only tiredness and waves of hopelessness as they looked up- not at the Dead Things, but beyond them.","An entity in the form of a massive white spider, seas of Anti-Matter surging around her, the True Source of Nihilos itself pulsing at her core, looked toward the distant dead with a despotic tone.","\"We defended for eons. We left everything behind to battle Dead Things that at least matched us in strength—or were weaker. Through them, we grew stronger. We hoped for a distant future where none of this would be needed. And yet, the final result...\"","She didn't finish.","Holding only Nascent Source-Bearer Complexity, her voice still carried a hopeless weight. Even existing in this chaotic space—layered with multiple Wild True Sources, took everything she had. And still... ash was spreading, forming a sea around them. It was the only bastion protecting the weaker defenders here, preventing their weavings from collapsing entirely under the pressure.","No one answered the hopelessness in the White Spider's voice.","Because what was there to say?","Beside Noah, the Great Beyonder had tears streaming down her face.","Not because she was weak. She was strong. And because she would keep fighting, that was why she cried. She wept wondering if it would all end like this- if all of it had ever truly meant something.","And then...","BOOM!","Behind them, an illusion of a radiant white-gold wheel bloomed to life.","...!","From it, an entity with a golden blindfold stepped out.","An entity that could not see.","The Witness.","Even with the blindfold, desolation and sadness emanated from him. His very presence stabilized the wild True Sources, their terrifying effects suddenly drawn inward—focused on the region of collapsed paradoxes and existence where the Dead Things had gathered.","But his appearance was more than just symbolic!","Two Resplendent Monads now stood by their side.","And further behind them, many turned toward the illusory brilliance of the white-gold Wheel of Existence.","They saw the massive flow that had led them all here. And in this moment, when their eyes met it, the gazes of many were not filled with warmth.","They held grief. Even fury.","Some had left the Infinite Ravines long ago.","They had abandoned it.","But not them!","They still stood to defend it as now, a little less than one hundred Defenders of the Wheel remained here.","And yet—what reward did they earn for their loyalty?","Their only recompense was legions of powerful Dead Things appearing one after another in this sealed space.","\"What do you think, O Bearer of the White-Gold Flame?\"","The voice sliced through the hopelessness, Veltraxis speaking directly.","He looked toward Noah, his dead smile widening, his obsidian hands brimming with decay and death as he raised them, roaring with malicious laughter.","\"There are already sixteen Mawbearers here and one hundred forty-three Converged Architects! Meanwhile, you have two flimsy Resplendent Monads to our 143! Tell me, what outcome do you think will bloom from all this?!\"","HUUM!","His voice echoed, piercing and heavy. He wanted it.","He wanted that look of hopelessness and despair that had claimed so many faces among the Living.","But most of all, he wanted to see it on Noah.","But he...would never see it.","Because even now, in this woven storm of despair- where even defenders of the Wheel wept and faltered...Noah grasped a Spoke and replied, utterly void of emotion.","\"The more of you that come, the more of you there are to kill.\"","...!","Despair never touched Noah's face.","And he had no intention of letting it.","Because in this very moment...","He continued his preparations!"]},{"number":3700,"title":"Chapter 3700: Chapter 3699: Everything III","paragraphs":["As Noah made his preparations, so did others.","In a unique mental frequency of existence utilized by the Dead.","Folds of collapse and dead True Sources scattered here and there, in such a unique space where only the signatures of certain Dead Things could enter...","\"Veltraxis, why call us in here?\"","The voice of the 63rd Mawbearer of Endless Paradox called out toward the horrific figure of Veltraxis, who wore a wide smile on his face.","Around them, the other Mawbearers that had also arrived stood watchful, as Veltraxis looked at them all before he began to speak in an eerie tone.","\"I want you all to keep a lookout and focus on this being right here...\"","As he spoke, he waved the weavings of the dead around them, displaying the image of none other than Noah.","\"This is the Living who drew me here in the first place. He held a True Source of Existence that could empower others. I know, that's nothing too crazy. We've seen it once or twice before. And when we investigated those Wheels of Existence, only a single one had anything that related to the Loom. So I came to check this one out—and this Living creature, who I can affirm is at the level of a Harmonized Sourcebound Icon, had a battle against M'gorrhaal, and was able to collapse his weavings in one shot.\"","...!","The words raised the brows of the terrifyingly powerful and Complex Mawbearers.","Meanwhile, the horrid smile of Veltraxis only grew wider and darker.","\"A Harmonized Sourcebound Icon who not only holds a True Source that empowers others, but can also skip past the staunch demarcations of Purity and Complexity to erupt with a power that can erase the weavings of a Converged Architect. Given that we are weaker in these Infinite Ravines, I'll give him a break, but still...\"","He seemed to be indicating something.","And as if the others already knew what he meant, the 81st Mawbearer, a creature made entirely of muscular tissue, spoke out in a rumble.","\"You don't mean to say... he is one of the True Favored Living Things?\"","...!","A True Favored Living Thing.","A creature born within the weavings of the Wheel, as inside their Existence, a mutation occurred and they gained a tremendous amount of weavings from the collective essence of the Breakings of the Wheel!","Such beings were akin to tonics to Dead Things as even a single one exceeded the value of thousands of Sorrowglass True Source Panaceas.","But they were always tricky.","And they were powerful.","Veltraxis only smiled deeper, shaking his head and raising his hands as if he could not be sure.","\"Who knows? But any True Favored Living Thing from a Wheel indicates even more that the Wheel holds something special. Watch his weavings closely from here on out. If he can kill one Converged Architect in a single blow—even though I have begun bringing in the dreaded Nullvein Gravewake Folds—he may suddenly display power to kill multiple Converged Architects. All I ask for bringing you all here... is one fourth of him and this Wheel.\"","...!","He was bargaining.","\"Oh, and to ensure there is no chance of failure, I'll continue to call a few other Mawbearers—we know how tricky True Favored Living Things can be, where they can turn the tides even in impossible odds. Right now, their chances of withstanding us are less than 1%, and I want to bring that to 0 if I can. Even if it's overkill—but it will mean what you all can devour will be less. This, I apologize for.\"","...!","The 63rd Mawbearer of Endless Paradox waved his hand at this.","\"It is okay. If the Wheel also ends up having something relating to the Loom, it will be well worth it in the end. Alright—how do you all want to do it?\"","How did they want to do it?","What exactly did he mean by such a thing?","Even though others might not know or understand, the Mawbearers of the Hollow Concord of Nullity knew very well.","Veltraxis smiled while looking at the others as he voiced out.","\"I was thinking... the Symphony of the True Dead. The resonance of all our Dead True Sources permeating out will take out any Harmonized Sourcebound Icons, and only the Resplendent Monads and the True Favored Living Thing would be able to withstand it—though heavily bound. And of course, the one to lead it is just arriving... I greet thee.\"","...!","Veltraxis bowed toward a newly arriving figure in this mental frequency.","It was... a humanoid entity in his early 30s, neither handsome nor ugly, but surrounded by musical instruments.","\"I greet thee, O 9th Mawbearer of the Dissonant Echo, Melodrass. We are humbled that you answered our call to come, when we know you are attending to multiple things.\"","...!","Veltraxis and all other Mawbearers bowed toward the newly arriving being.","The 9th!","A Single-Numbered Mawbearer!","Veltraxis and the others were already unfathomably complex—but this being... his weavings had already begun to surpass the level of a Converged Architect.","Better yet, he was also a Resplendent Monad as unlike many Dead Things, he had managed to bring his Purity to a high level!","A nigh impossible task for the Dead!","But his Complexity... was already nearing the level far past High, as he was simply looking for that spark.","\"With you here, we may not even need to do anything.\"","...!","Another Mawbearer smiled as he said this while rising up.","The 9th Mawbearer of the Dissonant Echo did not say anything—he only smiled while shaking his head.","He did not speak.","As if he could not speak!","Veltraxis shook his head, as if he understood everything from just that head shake, and he was the one to reply.","\"We have to be methodical with any Wheel of Existence. Anything forced to death will fight like mad—to the extent that its last flare of death could eradicate any Resplendent Monad or Converged Architect. We don't want that to be any of us, right? The last time a Mawbearer truly died was a billion years ago—let's not change that too soon...\"","His deep voice echoed out as the others agreed.","Just like this, the Dead Things convened and got ready to unleash decimation!","—","Noah looked out toward the eyes of the Dead that were seeking dread and despair—especially the cruel figure of Veltraxis, who seemed ready to move at any moment, and the ever-increasing numbers of Mawbearers coming through!","He looked at all of this and began to move with more and more certainty—as right away, he raised his hands and released flickers of white-gold flames that looked like small, glorious, spinning, flaming Omniverses.","They bloomed to cover multiple areas all around him while he voiced out to the Legends here.","\"The white-gold flames around you will empower your True Source should you accept them. They will make you even purer and allow you to express grander complexity.\"","He spoke in a calm tone and described everything slowly.","And yet—even after he spoke—one of the Legends turned to look at him and shook their head.","\"What use will it be? Their Converged Architects grow more and more in number with every passing second. Unless, behind me, the weavings of the Wheel of Existence have so drastically changed that Resplendent Monads are going to rise out by the dozens soon—I ask you again, how the fuck does this change anything?!\"","And the Legend was nearly shouting as he said this.","It was an entity with the True Source of Pride.","His body shone black and gold, and in this moment, its very construct seemed to be breaking as its core Source shook!","In the midst of his negativity—which could not really be dismissed, because it was true, the figure of the Holder of the True Source of Asche reached out to grasp the dazzling white-gold flame in front of him as his voice echoed out.","\"So long as we are alive, there is always use in fighting.\"","...!"]}]);
